     5	# The Arrival Substrate
     6	
     7	 Loops is rebuilding its store around a single canonical artifact: an append-only,
     8	 per-custodian arrival log. Everything else — the sqlite index, full-text
     9	 search, fold state, and the shared file people actually read — becomes a declared,
    10	 rebuildable projection of it. This document lays out the model, the five laws
    11	 that freeze it, the empirical evidence that the current design fails in ways the new one
    12	 cannot express, and the shipping plan: a 1.0.0 contract break, a one-time migration
    13	 sidecar, and a CLI rebuilt from scratch over the SDK.
    14	
    15	 Converged over five cross-family review passes, 2026-08-16 → 17 ·
    16	 Kyle Gruel with Claude Opus 5, Claude Fable 5, and GPT 5.6 “Sol” ·
    17	 grounded by a 22-agent code audit, an 81-row consumer census, and the first live merge experiment
    18	
    19	Contents
    20	
    21	Loops, for the cold reader
