   270	## 7Rotation, revocation, taint
   271	
   272	Rotation was already ruled. The compromise case was the one true gap, closed this session.
   273	
   274	 The cooperative cases were settled by the 2026-08-14 custody arc and the meta-schema ruling
   275	 before it: rotation within an observer’s key set is invisible to everyone else’s
   276	 grants; removal is a forward-only epoch rekey (“stops seeing new, never unsees
   277	 old”); delegate revocation is certificate expiry, never a registry event; and registry
   278	 mutations must be signed facts, verified before honoring. What no prior pass unpacked:
   279	 what a revocation means for records signed between a key’s compromise and the
   280	 revocation’s position.
   281	
   282	Ruled — arm one, the default
   283	
   284	 Taint stays in place. The records were legitimately admitted — at
   285	 admission time the key was valid, so the receipt was and remains true. Compromise degrades
   286	 the attribution (signature no longer implies author for the span), never the
   287	 receipt; excising records would delete true history to fix a false inference. Excision is
   288	 also the operation arrival exists to forbid — a rebuild-with-holes renumbers every
   289	 later witness position, breaks every seal over the span, and establishes that custody history
   290	 is editable, capping the log’s evidentiary value permanently. The revocation fact gives
   291	 every projection a position-bounded predicate — “signed by K in
   292	 (introduction, revocation)” — to discount, exclude, or flag per purpose,
   293	 reversibly if the compromise window is later re-assessed. Tainted-span disposition
   294	 is interpretation policy: admission records observation, not semantic eligibility, applied to
   295	 keys. The taint is also the forensic record of the incident itself.
   296	
   297	Ruled — arm two, content destruction
   298	
   299	 When tainted content must genuinely cease to exist — a live secret or
   300	 poisonous payload written into the log — the operation is the single re-custody
   301	 ceremony, never an in-place rebuild: a new lineage, genesis receipted with source
   302	 hashes, classification facts recording exactly what was excised and why. Old positions die
   303	 honestly because their lineage is retired, not silently renumbered. Second instance of the
   304	 ceremony beside the 0.x→1.0 sidecar; nothing is built for revocation at all.
