.loops/data/project.jsonl:182:{"t":"fact","id":"01KJPJFGYMSDXG6WX803M21BVY","kind":"decision","ts":1772431590.356138,"observer":"meta-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"topic\": \"design/actions-on-the-loop\", \"message\": \"Actions with side effects (task send spawns a worktree, task merge runs git operations) are not special-cased command handlers \\u2014 they are facts on the loop. Emitting task.dispatch places the intent on the wire; something observes it and executes the side effect; the outcome emits as a further fact; the boundary folds the cascade. The CLI command and TUI keypress are different input surfaces for the same emission. This is not the mature future form \\u2014 it is the design. If we build it this way from the start, the system composes: any observer can react to any fact, boundaries track lifecycle across the full cascade, and the audit trail is complete. Custom domain logic that does not dissolve \\u2014 worktree management, subprocess spawning, git operations \\u2014 lives in the observer/tick handler that reacts to the intent fact, not in the CLI command that emits it.\"}"}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:183:{"t":"fact","id":"01KJPJFR1CZ0HCTYKZPEWBGF9J","kind":"decision","ts":1772431597.612701,"observer":"meta-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"topic\": \"architecture/app-registration\", \"message\": \"Apps register three things: lenses (read fold state \\u2192 render at fidelity levels), feedback handlers (user input \\u2192 emit fact/tick), and action observers (react to intent facts with side effects). The harness makes all three available as both CLI commands and TUI keybindings at appropriate fidelity. There is no separate app scaffold per domain \\u2014 the directory structure, CLI dispatch, dev harness are identical. What differentiates siftd from strange-loops from hlab is: which vertex declaration (template), which lenses (Painted components), which feedback/action handlers (domain logic). The registration mechanism is the app's interface to the system.\"}"}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:206:{"t":"fact","id":"01KJTX1DPXCT807QB606N9XMNT","kind":"decision","ts":1772576880.349677,"observer":"","origin":"","payload":"{\"topic\": \"identity/intention-loop\", \"message\": \"Intentions are facts that survive context rotation. Fold by trigger \\u2014 latest per trigger key. One-shot vs recurring is the observer's interpretation, not the fold's concern. Emit with status=pending to create, re-emit with status=done to resolve. On Wake rules check for pending intentions.\"}"}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:207:{"t":"fact","id":"01KJTX1KHTYWCZ01724MMZGA2X","kind":"decision","ts":1772576886.330217,"observer":"","origin":"","payload":"{\"topic\": \"identity/grant-timing\", \"message\": \"Grant deferred until intention authorization is a real need. Implicit trust boundaries in daemon code are fine while there's a single observer per vertex. Grant becomes necessary when sessions need explicit authorization to act on pending intentions \\u2014 the difference between a rule you follow and a capability you possess.\"}"}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:452:{"t":"fact","id":"01KK39JNDEM873B82KAFRBNQZF","kind":"handoff","ts":1772858463.662447,"observer":"loops-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"message\": \"Session: source-execution-model investigation via 5-agent team (tracer, explorer, architect, muser, siftd). Thread closed with five decisions: source-execution-model (Source pure, Cadence as store predicate, Runner dissolves), cli-verb-first (loops <verb> <vertex>), cadence-as-store-predicate (same shape for time/event, topology is scheduling surface), read-is-pure (no side effects on read, sync is explicit), sync-locus-of-control (vertex decides what runs via cadence). Agent definitions created in .claude/agents/ (5 forigin). FoldSection supports nesting (sections: tuple[FoldSection, ...]). count dissolves into len(items). Engine computes FoldState from Facts + Spec, lenses consume it.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Custom lenses: Python files in .loops/lenses/ exposing render(data, zoom, width) -> Block. Vertex declares lens by name (per-kind or vertex-level default). CLI loads via importlib from .loops/lenses/{name}.py. Custom lenses can import built-in lenses to compose. Resolution: kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project \\\\u2192 config \\\\u2192 built-in. --lens flag overrides all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit should start the vertex runtime in one-shot mode, not write directly to SQLite. Same machinery as daemon mode, different lifecycle. Facts route through vertices, loops evaluate boundaries, ticks fire naturally. Foundational fix enabling observer-initiated ticks.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/tach\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/tach\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"tach for tier 2 import enforcement. Rust (fast), TOML config (declarative), fits uv/ruff/ty toolchain. tach sync bootstraps from existing code. Replaces hand-rolled AST import walkers (siftd ~230 lines). Does not replace domain invariants.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"scripts/ contains check.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\\\u2192 lens \\\\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\\\"}, \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\\\u2192fold state, Store\\\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\\\u2192vertex, Memory\\\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\\\u2192same primitive.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\\\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\\\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\\\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md is the critical document for returning from a gap. Must answer: what was I doing, what's next, what's deferred, what's the current state. It's the bridge across the wave's trough.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session facts are source of truth for state. Documents (LOG.md) are source of truth for understanding. Could generate HANDOFF.md from facts, but not a good LOG.md \\\\u2014 that requires narrative judgment.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Loops has directionality: Facts in \\\\u2192 Spec \\\\u2192 Ticks out. Structure declared upfront. siftd is retroactive query over raw conversation history \\\\u2014 no Spec, no fold. siftd discovers patterns you didn't anticipate (sine wave emerged from querying 110 days of data). Loops accumulates with guarantees (latest-by-topic). They feed each other but shouldn't merge.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops is operating memory (what do we believe right now?), siftd is the archaeological layer (what actually happened, what can we learn from it?). Complementary, not converging.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md serves cold-start reorientation \\\\u2014 narrative coherence, sequential reading, density for rebuilding mental model. Facts serve queryability and composability across repos. Converting loses the narrative; not converting loses the queryability.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Alcove depends on HANDOFF.md every wake cycle. Bag of facts requires knowing what questions to ask; prose builds context sequentially.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Keep HANDOFF.md as prose for cold-start reorientation. Derive decisions from it as loops facts. Prose is the source document, facts are the queryable index. Two representations serving different access patterns.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A scaffold element IS a compound decision cluster (tier 2). Tick-to-Fact bridging: scaffold Tick enters new project's vertex as a Fact. Type forgets it was a conclusion; metadata remembers provenance. New project accumulates its own state on top \\\\u2014 can override positions.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"testing/* namespace is 8 decisions that compose into one scaffold element. Tick gives observability: trace which decisions propagated, see where projects diverged.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold elements are Ticks derived from decision namespaces. Boundary must be manual (deliberate snapshot at project init), not automatic cascading. Gets observability that templ (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the system should help. Ties into combine auto-inherit pattern: push association down, don't require manual discipline at emit time.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"No way to inspect a single fact or tick at full depth. Stream truncates, fold collapses. Need a detail view on individual records \\\\u2014 same primitive for facts and ticks. loops show or similar.\\\"}, \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level configuration, not app-level. The app{} block concept dissolves \\\\u2014 lenses travel with verticee-poll-kind\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"discord-source-poll-kind\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Discord source script emits poll-status results as kind=message. Should be a different kind (e.g., 'poll' or 'source-status') so they don't pollute the message fold. Fix in ~/.config/loops/discord/discord-source. Comms lens has a workaround but the source is the right fix point.\\\"}, \\\"tick-surfacing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-surfacing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 ticks are visible through read-vertex; no separate surfacing command needed.\\\"}, \\\"tick-to-fact-flow\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-to-fact-flow\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 tick-to-fact cascading is already in the engine; read-vertex exposes it without dedicated plumbing.\\\"}, \\\"dissolve-messaging-vertex\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"dissolve-messaging-vertex\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Remove config/messaging/messaging.vertex. Telegram source moves to comms/telegram/ using same pattern as comms/discord/. Discord portion is already covered by comms/discord/.\\\"}, \\\"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Remove config/discord/discord.vertex \\\\u2014 duplicate of config/comms/discord/discord.vertex. The comms/ path is canonical.\\\"}, \\\"refactor-meta-combine\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"refactor-meta-combine\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"config/meta/meta.vertex currently combines meta-discussion + discord + identity. Should be a pure domain aggregation \\\\u2014 drop discord and identity from the combine. Those belong in the launch fold, not in the domain vertex.\\\"}, \\\"domain-vertex-template\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"domain-vertex-template\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Define the universal domain shape (decisions/threads/tasks/sessions/changes) as the base template for loops init. Local .vertex files extend with domain-specific kinds. Rename 'project' concept to 'domain' in templates and docs.\\\"}, \\\"session-launch-script\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-launch-script\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Write the two-line launch script: emit session fact with delegation, exec claude with LOOPS_OBSERVER. This is the dogfooding entry point \\\\u2014 use it to start sessions instead of raw 'LOOPS_OBSERVER=x claude'.\\\"}, \\\"identity/observer-namespacing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"identity/observer-namespacing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer namespacing (kyle/meta-claude) introduced in launch script but never landed in read path, .vertex declarations, or emit validation. Currently reverted to bare names. When namespace concept is needed (multi-user, delegation), it must land in three places: .vertex observer declarations, validate_emit() matching, and vertex_reader.py filter (4 sites of exact equality). Provenance preserved via session fact payload (principal=kyle, agent=meta-claude).\\\"}}}, \\\"session\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"loops-claude\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"loops-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"kyle\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kyle\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-auto-tagging dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD (5 lines). Staleness audit closed 4 threads (fold-state-types, observer-scoped-handoff, gist-lens-generics, observer-cascade). Prompt lens session fix for Alcove. Designed vertex lens infrastructure with Alcove input \\\\u2014 architecture decision emitted, 3 deferred threads tagged, task created. Next: implement vertex-lens-infrastructure (LensDecl AST + loader + resolver + CLI wiring).\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:thread-auto-tagging\\\", \\\"thread:fold-state-types\\\", \\\"thread:observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"thread:gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"thread:observer-cascade\\\", \\\"thread:fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"task:custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"task:fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"task:fold-materialization\\\", \\\"decision:design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"thread:app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"thread:module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"thread:combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"task:vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\"]}, \\\"meta-claude\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"meta-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"test-boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"test-boundary\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"test-vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"test-vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"e2e-test\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"e2e-test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"replay-test\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"replay-test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}}}, \\\"log\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-28\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Loops model crystallized + persistence exploration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Explored adding persistence to experiments. The exploration dissolved multiple\\\\nconcepts back into existing atoms:\\\\n\\\\n| Concept | Dissolved into | Why |\\\\n|---------|---------------|-----|\\\\n| Sink | Fold state | Loops have no terminals |\\\\n| Store | Durable fold | Storage is a property, not a type |\\\\n| Witness | Peer + Vertex | Just a peer whose job is to observe and emit |\\\\n| Tap | Vertex | Emission from storage is vertex behavior |\\\\n| Memory | Boundary-less fold | Silent accumulation is a fold that never ticks |\\\\n\\\\n**Key insight:** The atoms are complete. New requirements don't require new\\\\nprimitives \\\\u2014 they're configurations of existing ones.\\\\n\\\\nCreated `LOOPS.md` as the fundamental model document. Four satellite docs\\\\nadded: `docs/VERTEX.md`, `docs/TEMPORAL.md`, `docs/PERSISTENCE.md`, `docs/PEERS.md`.\\\\nEach unpacks one aspect and references back to LOOPS.md.\\\\n\\\\nFixed Enter key bug in keyboard.py (handle LF 0x0A same as CR 0x0D).\\\\n\\\\nOpen naming tensions noted but deferred:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Peer\\\\\\\" implies equality but delegation is hierarchical\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Tick\\\\\\\" implies clock time but boundaries are semantic\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-28\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Peer-driven boundaries + None=unrestricted + lens distinction\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"`review.py`: two loops through one vertex. Health ticks at timer cadence\\\\n(passive). Review ticks when peer acks all containers (active \\\\u2014 composition\\\\nlayer sends `review.complete` sentinel).\\\\n\\\\n**Peer model change**: `horizon` and `potential` default to `None` (unrestricted)\\\\ninstead of `frozenset()` (empty). Constraints emerge through `delegate()`, not\\\\nupfront enumeration.\\\\n\\\\n**Debug is a lens, not a horizon.** The None model exposed a category error:\\\\n\\\\\\\"debug\\\\\\\" was a horizon string alongside container names, but it's a rendering\\\\nmode, not a data domain. Debug panel is now a lens toggle available to any peer.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Boundary triggering implemented\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Implemented boundary triggering on Vertex. `Projection.reset()` added.\\\\n`register()` gains `boundary: str | None` and `reset: bool`. `receive()`\\\\nreturns `Tick | None`. Fold-before-boundary, optional reset, boundary kind\\\\nuniqueness enforced.\\\\n\\\\nVertex is sync by design \\\\u2014 async bridge lives at composition point.\\\\n122 ticks tests.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Feedback loop closed, experiment log established\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"`experiments/observe.py`: first experiment that closes the feedback loop.\\\\nUser interactions (j/k/enter) are Facts through the same `vertex.receive()`\\\\nas external observations.\\\\n\\\\nEmergent insights captured in `experiments/LOG.md`: debug as horizon (not\\\\ninfrastructure), meta-actions outside the loop, thin composition layer.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Genesis document + strata semantic tagging\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Reconstructed project origin story via strata. Synt path. FTS5 still used when query present.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops project (no subcommand) now shows folded state. Flags pass through: loops project -v, loops project -q, loops project --kind decision all work.\\\"}, \\\"observer-resolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-resolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer resolves through vertex declaration chain: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. No more env var or hardcoded defaults as primary path. --observer flag remains as explicit override.\\\"}, \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\".vertex (bare, no prefix) is the workspace root at every level. Config-level root.vertex becomes .vertex. Project-level .loops/.vertex is the project root. Same pattern, fractal. All structure mutations (add observer, add vertex) target the .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex definitions (project.vertex, identity.vertex, etc.) copy locally when added to a workspace. Local copy can diverge \\\\u2014 different fold declarations, different kinds. Facts are ground truth; declarations are projections. Global view discovers and reads stores regardless of local declaration differences.\\\"}, \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observers start project-scoped (declared in project .vertex). As identity generalizes beyond the project, elevate to global .vertex. Identity facts merge up via store merge. Global observers appear in every workspace automatically \\\\u2014 no bootstrapping.\\\"}, \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex declares its observers natively. Observer is not just a string stamp \\\\u2014 it connects to identity (via identity vertex reference) and grants (capability constraints). The vertex is the authority on who can emit into it. Resolution walks up: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm/init are all vertex mutation operations. Adding an observer, pulling in a vertex definition, managing parameter rows \\\\u2014 same verb pattern, different targets on the vertex declaration. The .vertex file is the thing being built up.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"observer.py splits into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval: fetch_fold, fetch_stream) and commands/identity.py (who you are: resolve_observer, validate_emit, find_workspace_root). _emit_fact dissolved (zero callers). _format_date inlined into lenses/fold.py where it's used.\\\"}, \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"resolve_observer() is the single source of truth for observer identity. Priority: flag \\\\u2192 env \\\\u2192 project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. pop.py's _observer() now delegates to resolve_observer() instead of bare env read. All ad-hoc resolution paths dissolved.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-level validation (validate_emit) for CLI fast path \\\\u2014 checks observer declared + kind in grant.potential. Engine-level Grant for runtime path (loops start/run) \\\\u2014 deferred until compiler produces identity-aware runtime. Two levels, same data, different contexts.\\\"}, \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude declared as open observer in project .vertex (.loops/.vertex). No grant constraints \\\\u2014 full emit access within the monorepo. Global elevation deferred until identity store is built out further.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem frozen dataclasses go in libs/atoms/. Lens contract becomes (atoms.FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. FoldItem separates payload (dict[str,Any]) from metadata (ts, observer, origin). FoldSection supports nesting (sections: tuple[FoldSection, ...]). count dissolves into len(items). Engine computes FoldState from Facts + Spec, lenses consume it.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Custom lenses: Python files in .loops/lenses/ exposing render(data, zoom, width) -> Block. Vertex declares lens by name (per-kind or vertex-level default). CLI loads via importlib from .loops/lenses/{name}.py. Custom lenses can import built-in lenses to compose. Resolution: kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project \\\\u2192 config \\\\u2192 built-in. --lens flag overrides all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit should start the vertex runtime in one-shot mode, not write directly to SQLite. Same machinery as daemon mode, different lifecycle. Facts route through vertices, loops evaluate boundaries, ticks fire naturally. Foundational fix enabling observer-initiated ticks.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/tach\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/tach\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"tach for tier 2 import enforcement. Rust (fast), TOML config (declarative), fits uv/ruff/ty toolchain. tach sync bootstraps from existing code. Replaces hand-rolled AST import walkers (siftd ~230 lines). Does not replace domain invariants.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"scripts/ contains check.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\\\u2192 lens \\\\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\\\"}, \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\\\u2192fold state, Store\\\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\\\u2192vertex, Memory\\\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\\\u2192same primitive.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\\\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\\\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\\\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md is the critical document for returning from a gap. Must answer: what was I doing, what's next, what's deferred, what's the current state. It's the bridge across the wave's trough.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session facts are source of truth for state. Documents (LOG.md) are source of truth for understanding. Could generate HANDOFF.md from facts, but not a good LOG.md \\\\u2014 that requires narrative judgment.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Loops has directionality: Facts in \\\\u2192 Spec \\\\u2192 Ticks out. Structure declared upfront. siftd is retroactive query over raw conversation history \\\\u2014 no Spec, no fold. siftd discovers patterns you didn't anticipate (sine wave emerged from querying 110 days of data). Loops accumulates with guarantees (latest-by-topic). They feed each other but shouldn't merge.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops is operating memory (what do we believe right now?), siftd is the archaeological layer (what actually happened, what can we learn from it?). Complementary, not converging.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md serves cold-start reorientation \\\\u2014 narrative coherence, sequential reading, density for rebuilding mental model. Facts serve queryability and composability across repos. Converting loses the narrative; not converting loses the queryability.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Alcove depends on HANDOFF.md every wake cycle. Bag of facts requires knowing what questions to ask; prose builds context sequentially.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Keep HANDOFF.md as prose for cold-start reorientation. Derive decisions from it as loops facts. Prose is the source document, facts are the queryable index. Two representations serving different access patterns.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A scaffold element IS a compound decision cluster (tier 2). Tick-to-Fact bridging: scaffold Tick enters new project's vertex as a Fact. Type forgets it was a conclusion; metadata remembers provenance. New project accumulates its own state on top \\\\u2014 can override positions.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"testing/* namespace is 8 decisions that compose into one scaffold element. Tick gives observability: trace which decisions propagated, see where projects diverged.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold elements are Ticks derived from decision namespaces. Boundary must be manual (deliberate snapshot at project init), not automatic cascading. Gets observability that templates don't \\\\u2014 can trace propagation and divergence.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md dissolves into the store. Handoff is a fact kind (fold: latest). Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex \\\\u2014 reads handoff prose, open threads, active tasks, recent decisions. Wind-down emits the handoff fact instead of writing a file.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Wind-down has two phases: reconciliation (emit missing facts, resolve completed threads, update tasks) and handoff (prose synthesis). Reconciliation compensates for gaps in continuous session emission. As in-session hooks mature, reconciliation shrinks. Handoff is always end-of-session \\\\u2014 it's narrative, not incremental.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"siftd decomposes into loops monorepo. Sources are already solved (harnesses are just source definitions). New libs/store absorbs all DB operations siftd proved out: ingest, slice, merge, search, transport. siftd-as-app becomes a thin specialization layer \\\\u2014 LLM harness configs + analytics queries + CLI. Same relationship as painted (rendering spine) \\\\u2014 siftd becomes the analytics spine.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dynamically compose vertices that fold across multiple underlying stores \\\\u2014 e.g. alcove.db + kyle.db + watchers.db into a temporary vertex for a specific query. Temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful. This is what makes cross-store search fundamental rather than a feature.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"New loops lib explicitly for store operations. Absorbs from siftd: ingest (format-specific readers, schema-agnostic output), slice (by date/project/tag), merge (combine stores, deduplicate), search (FTS5 + semantic over any SQLite store), transport (push/pull/sync between stores over SSH or HTTP). Generic over any vertex store.\\\"}, \\\"design/context-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/context-fold\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Alcove's context fold pattern: before a message hits the agent, the dispatch loop constructs a brief context summary \\\\u2014 latest activity across all channels/stores. Lightweight (just latest timestamps + one line per channel). Same pattern as continuous-session-emission for claude-code sessions. The fold is ephemeral, rebuilt every dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-document architecture proven on alcove: SOUL.md (identity \\\\u2014 editorial, hand-shaped), CLAUDE.md (operational \\\\u2014 tools, paths, permissions), loops store (learned knowledge \\\\u2014 accumulated facts, foldable, queryable). MEMORY.md is a cache/projection of operational knowledge for session start, not the source of truth.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-project queryability dissolves into store operations once libs/store exists. Emit a decision in meta, discover it from loops \\\\u2014 not via special cross-project protocol, but via store merge/search/transport. The combinatorial vertex is the query mechanism.\\\"}, \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"meta-discussion,alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wind-down converge with alcove's context fold pattern. Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex (handoff prose + threads + tasks + decisions). Wind-down emits the handoff fact + reconciles the store. Alcove's context fold is the same shape \\\\u2014 read all stores, compose a view for orientation. The general pattern: any session boundary (start, end, dispatch) needs a lens over accumulated state.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single-project pickup is multi-fold reads on one vertex \\\\u2014 not a combinatorial vertex. Read fold(handoff, latest) + fold(threads, active) + fold(decisions, recent) from one store. Cross-project pickup is where combinatorial vertices enter \\\\u2014 reading folds across N stores. libs/store dissolves the boundary between these two scales.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"meta-discussion is the design space around loops itself, not just decisions about projects. Cross-cutting architecture (store operations, combinatorial vertices, attention filters, context folds, pickup/winddown workflow) emerges here and in cross-instance channels (alcove discord), not in the loops repo. Parallel meta-discussion on the meta aspect of loops along with ways of working.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts and ticks use ULID as primary key via native SQLite extension (not application-generated like siftd did). Globally unique, time-ordered, sortable. Merge becomes INSERT OR IGNORE \\\\u2014 ULID is the identity across stores. Replaces auto-increment rowid. Cursor semantics preserved (ULID is sortable, WHERE id > last_seen still works). Essential for distributed store orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Payload is always valid JSON \\\\u2014 enforced on write. This guarantees json_extract() is always safe, FTS can always walk the tree, and indexed columns can be projected from payload fields. Progressive enhancement: add explicit indexed columns (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) for hot query paths as needed.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 full-text search as the starting point for store.search. Zero external dependencies, sub-millisecond query at current scale (100-10k facts). Recursive JSON text extraction reliable by construction (payload-is-JSON contract). json_extract() for field filtering works without indexes up to ~100k facts. Indexed projections (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) are the progressive enhancement when scale demands it \\\\u2014 boundary is roughly 100k+ facts or hot query paths.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Transport is a pluggable interface, not a fixed implementation. The operations are constant (slice on source, merge on target), the pipe varies (local, SSH, HTTP, future protocols). Local transport ships first (testable, no infrastructure). SSH next (alcove sync is forcing function). HTTP when scrape/collect patterns emerge (Prometheus-style data collection). Store operations (slice, merge) are transport-agnostic \\\\u2014 they work on local paths, transport handles the pipe.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted is the native display layer for the store, not a rendering utility. Every store operation gets a painted view at all four zoom levels. Apps add domain-specific lenses that interpret facts in their context, but the underlying operations are universal. Domain-specific views generalize back into painted over time as patterns recur (task dashboard \\\\u2192 generic dashboard lens, siftd data exploration \\\\u2192 generic fold exploration). This is why painted is returning to the monorepo \\\\u2014 if loops needs a rendering capability, painted grows to support it.\\\"}, \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md progressive chain maps 1:1 to vertex store progressive query. The document is the lens, the store is the state. Root CLAUDE.md references the project vertex; lib CLAUDE.md tells you how to query your slice via topic namespace (atoms/*, engine/*, painted/*). One store, kind-namespaced topics, natural slicing. Same pattern as hlab status \\\\u2014 one vertex, multiple sources, scoped by name.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"project.vertex is the durable project-level store for decisions, threads, and tasks. Named 'project' (not 'session') \\\\u2014 same pattern strange-loops uses for task orchestration, now a meta-pattern for all projects. Cross-cutting concerns stay in meta; project-specific concerns accumulate in the project vertex. Progressive CLAUDE.md references the project store at each level.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Stores are distributed-first, aggregate-up. Each project gets its own local vertex + SQLite store, self-contained and portable. Config level (~/.config/loops/) is the aggregation layer \\\\u2014 template vertices discover all local instances. loops status <name> reads local; loops status dev/<name> reads aggregate. Separate DBs by default. Merge/combinatorial vertex is opt-in aggregation. Same shape as the loops model: local loops produce ticks, ticks flow up. Local stores produce facts, aggregate vertices see them all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex templates are replicable patterns (project, task, handoff, pickup). loops init <template> creates a local instance in cwd. The config-level template vertex discovers all local instances. Templates define the fold shape; each instantiation gets its own data. Like git repos \\\\u2014 local is the primitive, aggregation is the network.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Two kinds of vertex files. Domain vertices are code \\\\u2014 checked into repos, define data pipelines (hlab status.vertex, economy.vertex). Knowledge vertices are runtime config \\\\u2014 project decisions, threads, tasks, handoff. Domain vertices ship with the app. Knowledge vertices are instantiated from templates via loops init. Both are .vertex files, same format, different lifecycle.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Do not add kinds_consumed to Tick atom. Use tool-level scope derived from .vertex config when available, or observer/origin filtering. Avoids per-tick duplication, API ripple, and semantic ambiguity. Design on stale branch design/tick-provenance.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SUPERSEDED: The merge gap dissolves when strange-loops replaces subtask. Workers emit facts instead of writing artifacts to branches. No branch to orphan, no merge step to miss. See threads: strange-loops-merge-strategy, artifact-to-fact-convergence.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertecern. Emit with status=pending to create, re-emit with status=done to resolve. On Wake rules check for pending intentions.\\\"}, \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant deferred until intention authorization is a real need. Implicit trust boundaries in daemon code are fine while there's a single observer per vertex. Grant becomes necessary when sessions need explicit authorization to act on pending intentions \\\\u2014 the difference between a rule you follow and a capability you possess.\\\"}, \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity state (soul tick) stays internal to the observer's vertex. Observations propagate outward as facts on other vertices with observer attribution. The strange loop closes through behavior: identity \\\\u2192 lenses \\\\u2192 observations \\\\u2192 facts on other vertices \\\\u2192 pollers bring back responses \\\\u2192 new identity facts. Coupling is through the observer, not through the data.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wrapup skills rewritten to be vertex-native. Four layers for pickup (identity, context, peers, workspace), five for wrapup (capture, handoff, status, reflect, workspace). Skills version-controlled in loops repo with symlinks to global config. Replaces probe-based pickup and strange-loops CLI wrapup.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity store is sense of self, not operational metrics. Insights, connections, surprises, open questions about perspective. Distinct from meta (operational patterns) and project (architecture). Guard against forcing observations every session. Capability awareness belongs in CLAUDE.md; capability insights that persist across tool changes belong in identity.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Skills that are part of the loops system (pickup, wrapup) are version-controlled in the loops repo at .claude/skills/ and symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\\\"}, \\\"design/init-as-context\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/init-as-context\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Init doesn't just create a store \\\\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\\\\\"by\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" } } \\\\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\\\u2014 identity is already loaded.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the system should help. Ties into combine auto-inherit pattern: push association down, don't require manual discipline at emit time.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"No way to inspect a single fact or tick at full depth. Stream truncates, fold collapses. Need a detail view on individual records \\\\u2014 same primitive for facts and ticks. loops show or similar.\\\"}, \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level configuration, not app-level. The app{} block concept dissolves \\\\u2014 lenses travel with vertices via lens{} in .vertex KDL, not nested under an app container. Apps own domain verbs, not lenses.\\\"}, \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: still valid for installed-package lens references but no current use case. Will emerge naturally when apps need to expose lenses from their packages.\\\"}, \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Each vertex declares its own lens. No inheritance across combine boundaries. An aggregation vertex has its own rendering needs distinct from its children. If you want a child's lens, declare it explicitly.\\\"}, \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Emit UX will be rethought as part of write-vertex operation.\\\"}, \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into convention. Source lifecycle kinds get a reserved prefix (e.g. _source.message.complete) to avoid matching data fold queries. Same pattern as _boundary on tick payloads.\\\"}, \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into vertex-name-resolution-consistency. The combine-emit problem is a resolution consistency problem \\\\u2014 uniform resolution covers both.\\\"}, \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Both phases complete. Phase 1: vertex-level scope declaration (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL). Identity is scoped, project/comms are unscoped. Phase 2: Source._extract_metadata reads _observer/_origin from ndjson payloads, overriding .loop defaults. Discord-source emits _observer=author, _origin=discord. Observer now consistently means identity. Origin carries source attribution. New discord polls will have correct observer \\\\u2014 existing data retains observer=discord.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three commands, three resolution behaviors. fold/stream resolve vertex names. run expects file paths. emit resolves but writes to wrong store through combine. Resolution should be uniform \\\\u2014 resolve_vertex works everywhere, or the gaps are explicit.\\\"}, \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Run loop model changes under two-operation CLI.\\\"}, \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Check cursors are part of old CLI shape; read-vertex model replaces them.\\\"}, \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream rendering will be rethought as part of read-vertex lenses.\\\"}, \\\"cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Refined to read/emit/init. 'run' dissolves \\\\u2014 source execution is fact generation via emit, not a separate operation. 'write' dissolves \\\\u2014 emit was already the right verb. Four things to learn became three: read (fold default, filters compose), emit (facts in, from user or source), init (create namespace). Remaining question: source execution model (see source-execution-model thread).\\\"}, \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The root vertex at ~/.config/loops/.vertex needs restructuring. Currently a thin aggregator with combine. Needs to become the actual routing root where children (project, identity, comms, reading, etc.) nest and ticks cascade. Design questions: which vertices are children vs peers? Does identity scope differently in the tree? How does observer-scoping interact with tree position? The root vertex read IS the system overview \\\\u2014 its default lens shows children and their state.\\\"}, \\\"read-operation-contract\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"read-operation-contract\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"What does 'read vertex' return mechanically? The read operation needs to serve multiple consumers via lenses: prompt lens (agent system prompt), default lens (terminal fold state), JSON (hooks). It must provide fold state + tick history + children. Does the read load the full subtree? How deep? Does --ticks change the data fetched or just the lens? Does search (positional query arg) go through the same read path? The contract between read and lens determines the implementation.\\\"}, \\\"source-execution-model\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source-execution-model\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved. Source execution dissolves to three concerns: Source (pure adapter), Cadence (store predicate), Executor (cadence-gated runner). Five decisions emitted: source-execution-model, cli-verb-first, cadence-as-store-predicate, read-is-pure, sync-locus-of-control. Investigation by 5-agent team: tracer (lifecycle), explorer (scheduling survey), architect (design v3), muser (dissolution challenges), siftd (historical context). Prior art: CADENCE.md (2026-01-31) proposed Source/Cadence split conceptually \\\\u2014 never implemented. This session designs the one-shot-compatible version.\\\"}}}, \\\"change\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session continuity + strange-loops scaffold \\\\u2014 loops session start/end/status/log, query-time fold, LOOPS_OBSERVER env var. strange-loops scaffolded.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Population as facts \\\\u2014 add/rm emit pop.add/pop.rm facts, .list materialized as projection, ls reads fold state.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session dissolution + cells\\\\u2192painted + run_cli harness \\\\u2014 dissolved session subcommand, status/log promoted to top-level, migrated cells\\\\u2192painted. 147 loops + 1169 painted tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Full Painted rendering + golden tests + store targeting \\\\u2014 all 9 display commands through run_cli, 45 golden snapshot tests, store targeting via vertex name resolution. 191 tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"engine CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 4 levels: Run vertex program, Fold and fire, Persist, Gate access. Semantic examples (decisions/threads). Deep-dive docs as reference layer.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"lang CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 3 levels: Parse a file, Understand AST, Manage populations. Connects DSL types to atoms/engine counterparts.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"store CLAUDE.md rewrite \\\\u2014 2 levels: Slice/merge, Schema. Clarifies relationship to engine SqliteStore.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chain headers and cross-references added to all 5 lib CLAUDE.md files. atoms retrofitted with oblique references to engine at Levels 0, 1, 3.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Dissolved discord, telegram, reader apps. Moved .loop/.vertex files to experiments/. Removed from workspace members. Updated root CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for all 3 apps: loops (new, 3 levels), hlab (rewrite 199\\\\u2192118 lines, 3 levels), strange-loops (rewrite 254\\\\u2192127 lines, 3 levels). All with chain headers.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Record line rendering fixes: gutter continuity with weight stepping, shallow 2-char indent replacing deep column alignment, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output eliminating terminal wrapping gaps, health_lens fixed to respect lens contract\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertex template includes default loops (decision, thread, change, task). _find_source_vertex priority: aggregation loops block > sibling instance > direct config instance. Updated project + meta aggregation vertices on disk.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuild: temporal modes + generic rendering\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"commands/observer.py,lenses/fold.py,lenses/stream.py,main.py,fixtures.py,test_session.py,test_status.py,test_log.py,test_cli_docs.py,test_cli.py\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval) and commands/identity.py (observer resolution). Dissolved _emit_fact, inlined _format_date into lenses. pop.py now uses resolve_observer() for full resolution chain. 394 tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design session\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into fetch.py + identity.py. Wired resolve_observer through pop.py. Created project .vertex with loops-claude as open observer. Designed FoldState typed contract (atoms-the-package), custom lens system (.vertex declaration + .loops/lenses/ + --lens flag), attention trifecta (what/when/how-much as lens concerns). Peer exchange with Alcove confirmed architecture. Two visions emitted to meta (attention-infrastructure, observer-constellation).\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldItem/FoldSection/FoldState in atoms. observer.py dissolved into commands/fetch.py + commands/identity.py. fetch_fold returns FoldState, fold_view consumes typed attributes. 235 loops + 322 atoms tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Fact-by-id: surface ULID identifiers + observer elevation\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"store_reader.py,vertex_reader.py,fetch.py,stream.py,main.py,__init__.py,test_store_reader.py,test_vertex_reader.py,~/.config/loops/.vertex\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Hook lifecycle + lens redistribution + CLAUDE.md\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\".claude/settings.json,~/.config/loops/lenses/comms.py,~/.config/loops/lenses/state.py,~/.config/loops/CLAUDE.md,apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/CLAUDE.md\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta + slashed emit + hooks cleanup\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping as vertex concern (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL), session tick since fix (replay period bridging), Source _extract_metadata for ndjson, prompt lens delegation rendering, SessionEnd mechanical delta log.\\\"}]}, \\\"task\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit routes through vertex runtime via load_vertex_program + vertex.receive. Dissolution \\\\u2014 removed the bypass, didn't build new machinery.\\\"}, \\\"daemon-local-orchestration\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"daemon-local-orchestration\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 no persistent runtime needed. Vertex is reactive. Scheduling is external (cron/systemd). One-shot CLI is the runtime.\\\"}, \\\"foldstate-audit-findings\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"foldstate-audit-findings\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: vertex_fold addresses the core finding (typed contract wired end-to-end). FoldItem.origin populated since prior session. Remaining gaps (no reference counting, no fold caching, no custom lens loading) are tracked as separate threads.\\\"}, \\\"identity-observer-filtering\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"identity-observer-filtering\\\", \\"architecture/store-search-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 is required infrastructure, not optional. Spec-declared searchable fields in vertex KDL (search \\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\" as sibling of fold/boundary). Standalone FTS5 table with lazy catch-up indexing via high water mark \\\\u2014 no INSERT triggers because spec-to-field mapping lives in vertex, not database. Write path untouched; FTS is purely read-side. First search pays backfill cost, subsequent searches catch up on deltas. Combinatorial vertex search: each store searched independently, results merged after recall. json_extract+LIKE rejected \\\\u2014 personal scale grows continuously (siftd alone 100-150k+ facts), cross-store combinatorial queries multiply dataset.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/boundary-enforcement\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/boundary-enforcement\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-based architecture boundary tests in tests/test_architecture.py enforce vertex-as-read-interface. Four rules: apps don't import StoreReader (exceptions: store inspector permanent, pop_store temporary), apps don't import sqlite3, libs don't import apps, lib dependency DAG (engine->lang runtime, engine->atoms runtime). TYPE_CHECKING-aware visitor. Stale exceptions fail the test. Monorepo-level concern, lives at repo root not in any single lib.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex spec declares searchable fields per kind: search \\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\" as sibling of fold and boundary in loop definitions. LoopDef gains search: tuple[str, ...]. Callers don't override at query time \\\\u2014 vertex_search reads the spec to know what's searchable. Only declared fields extracted and indexed. Keeps FTS5 index surgical at scale. Template loop resolution via collect_search_fields() handles generated kind names from .loop templates.\\\"}, \\\"design/lazy-fts-indexing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lazy-fts-indexing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 indexing uses lazy catch-up pattern: first search pays full backfill, subsequent searches catch up on deltas via high water mark in fts_state table. No INSERT triggers \\\\u2014 triggers can't do spec-aware field extraction since the kind-to-field mapping lives in the vertex file, not the database. The resultant first-search slowdown fits the loops philosophy: not necessary that things happen instantly, only that they do reliably with the same data flow and rule set. Idempotent, incremental, spec-driven.\\\"}, \\\"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-store search follows recall-then-compose pattern: FTS5 per store independently, union candidate sets, fold/rank across combined results. Composition happens after recall, not during \\\\u2014 FTS5 virtual tables are per-database in SQLite. Each vertex store remains self-contained with its own FTS5 index. Combinatorial vertex is a view over stores, not a new store. Search follows the same boundary.\\\"}, \\\"design/app-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/app-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Apps dissolve into lenses + feedback over vertex declarations. An app does not own a data model or ingress pipeline \\\\u2014 the vertex declaration (kinds, folds, search fields, boundaries) IS the data model, Sources ARE ingress, and both ship via template at loops init. What an app uniquely provides: (1) domain-specific lenses \\\\u2014 Painted rendering of fold state tuned to a data shape (conversation browser, task board, system dashboard), and (2) feedback capability \\\\u2014 the ability to emit facts/ticks back through the lens (tag a conversation, close a task, ack an alert). The observer and actor are the same entity. This dissolves siftd, strange-loops, and hlab into structurally identical programs: Painted surfaces over vertex state with domain-specific rendering and keybindings. The Smalltalk parallel is precise \\\\u2014 there is one runtime (loops), one data substrate (vertex/store), one rendering framework (Painted), and domain configuration that selects active lenses and feedback handlers. The app is a perspective on the system, not a separate program. Unlike Smalltalk, the Unix grounding holds: stores are cp-able SQLite files, sources are shell commands, CLI is always available as pipe-friendly lower-fidelity surface.\\\"}, \\\"design/store-ingest-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/store-ingest-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The store-ingest-design plan dissolves. Ingest \\\\u2014 format-aware file reading that produces facts \\\\u2014 is not a library primitive. It decomposes into: Sources (shell commands or scripts that read files and emit NDJSON, already exist), parse pipeline (dict\\\\u2192dict shaping vocabulary, already exists), and vertex declaration (kind/fold configuration, already exists). siftd's adapters are Sources that haven't been written as Sources yet \\\\u2014 each adapter's discover\\\\u2192parse pipeline is equivalent to a script that reads conversation files and emits structured records. The three-tier loading (built-in < entry point < drop-in) becomes: template ships default source scripts, user overrides with project-local scripts. The read_file/ingest_to_store API proposed for libs/store is unnecessary \\\\u2014 format-aware file reading is a script concern, not a library primitive. Bulk historical import is an edge case solved by a script, not a library. What remains from the store-operations-design plan (receive, compact, transport) is genuine new infrastructure \\\\u2014 moving stores between locations does not dissolve into existing primitives.\\\"}, \\\"design/actions-on-the-loop\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/actions-on-the-loop\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Actions with side effects (task send spawns a worktree, task merge runs git operations) are not special-cased command handlers \\\\u2014 they are facts on the loop. Emitting task.dispatch places the intent on the wire; something observes it and executes the side effect; the outcome emits as a further fact; the boundary folds the cascade. The CLI command and TUI keypress are different input surfaces for the same emission. This is not the mature future form \\\\u2014 it is the design. If we build it this way from the start, the system composes: any observer can react to any fact, boundaries track lifecycle across the full cascade, and the audit trail is complete. Custom domain logic that does not dissolve \\\\u2014 worktree management, subprocess spawning, git operations \\\\u2014 lives in the observer/tick handler that reacts to the intent fact, not in the CLI command that emits it.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-registration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-registration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Apps register three things: lenses (read fold state \\\\u2192 render at fidelity levels), feedback handlers (user input \\\\u2192 emit fact/tick), and action observers (react to intent facts with side effects). The harness makes all three available as both CLI commands and TUI keybindings at appropriate fidelity. There is no separate app scaffold per domain \\\\u2014 the directory structure, CLI dispatch, dev harness are identical. What differentiates siftd from strange-loops from hlab is: which vertex declaration (template), which lenses (Painted components), which feedback/action handlers (domain logic). The registration mechanism is the app's interface to the system.\\\"}, \\\"design/lens-modifiers\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lens-modifiers\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens rendering composes through modifiers, not separate lens implementations. Four modifier types identified from the painted-log-line-demo research: (1) Gutter \\\\u2014 colored left edge encoding one dimension (lifecycle stage, health, freshness). Follows Grafana/Datadog pattern, underused in terminals. (2) Attention \\\\u2014 dim low-information-gain records, highlight high. First-occurrence errors are high attention, 47th occurrence is noise. Decisions on new topics are high, routine "topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the systemlit\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-document architecture proven on alcove: SOUL.md (identity \\\\u2014 editorial, hand-shaped), CLAUDE.md (operational \\\\u2014 tools, paths, permissions), loops store (learned knowledge \\\\u2014 accumulated facts, foldable, queryable). MEMORY.md is a cache/projection of operational knowledge for session start, not the source of truth.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-project queryability dissolves into store operations once libs/store exists. Emit a decision in meta, discover it from loops \\\\u2014 not via special cross-project protocol, but via store merge/search/transport. The combinatorial vertex is the query mechanism.\\\"}, \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"meta-discussion,alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wind-down converge with alcove's context fold pattern. Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex (handoff prose + threads + tasks + decisions). Wind-down emits the handoff fact + reconciles the store. Alcove's context fold is the same shape \\\\u2014 read all stores, compose a view for orientation. The general pattern: any session boundary (start, end, dispatch) needs a lens over accumulated state.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single-project pickup is multi-fold reads on one vertex \\\\u2014 not a combinatorial vertex. Read fold(handoff, latest) + fold(threads, active) + fold(decisions, recent) from one store. Cross-project pickup is where combinatorial vertices enter \\\\u2014 reading folds across N stores. libs/store dissolves the boundary between these two scales.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"meta-discussion is the design space around loops itself, not just decisions about projects. Cross-cutting architecture (store operations, combinatorial vertices, attention filters, context folds, pickup/winddown workflow) emerges here and in cross-instance channels (alcove discord), not in the loops repo. Parallel meta-discussion on the meta aspect of loops along with ways of working.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts and ticks use ULID as primary key via native SQLite extension (not application-generated like siftd did). Globally unique, time-ordered, sortable. Merge becomes INSERT OR IGNORE \\\\u2014 ULID is the identity across stores. Replaces auto-increment rowid. Cursor semantics preserved (ULID is sortable, WHERE id > last_seen still works). Essential for distributed store orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Payload is always valid JSON \\\\u2014 enforced on write. This guarantees json_extract() is always safe, FTS can always walk the tree, and indexed columns can be projected from payload fields. Progressive enhancement: add explicit indexed columns (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) for hot query paths as needed.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 full-text search as the starting point for store.search. Zero external dependencies, sub-millisecond query at current scale (100-10k facts). Recursive JSON text extraction reliable by construction (payload-is-JSON contract). json_extract() for field filtering works without indexes up to ~100k facts. Indexed projections (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) are the progressive enhancement when scale demands it \\\\u2014 boundary is roughly 100k+ facts or hot query paths.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Transport is a pluggable interface, not a fixed implementation. The operations are constant (slice on source, merge on target), the pipe varies (local, SSH, HTTP, future protocols). Local transport ships first (testable, no infrastructure). SSH next (alcove sync is forcing function). HTTP when scrape/collect patterns emerge (Prometheus-style data collection). Store operations (slice, merge) are transport-agnostic \\\\u2014 they work on local paths, transport handles the pipe.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted is the native display layer for the store, not a rendering utility. Every store operation gets a painted view at all four zoom levels. Apps add domain-specific lenses that interpret facts in their context, but the underlying operations are universal. Domain-specific views generalize back into painted over time as patterns recur (task dashboard \\\\u2192 generic dashboard lens, siftd data exploration \\\\u2192 generic fold exploration). This is why painted is returning to the monorepo \\\\u2014 if loops needs a rendering capability, painted grows to support it.\\\"}, \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md progressive chain maps 1:1 to vertex store progressive query. The document is the lens, the store is the state. Root CLAUDE.md references the project vertex; lib CLAUDE.md tells you how to query your slice via topic namespace (atoms/*, engine/*, painted/*). One store, kind-namespaced topics, natural slicing. Same pattern as hlab status \\\\u2014 one vertex, multiple sources, scoped by name.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"project.vertex is the durable project-level store for decisions, threads, and tasks. Named 'project' (not 'session') \\\\u2014 same pattern strange-loops uses for task orchestration, now a meta-pattern for all projects. Cross-cutting concerns stay in meta; project-specific concerns accumulate in the project vertex. Progressive CLAUDE.md references the project store at each level.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Stores are distributed-first, aggregate-up. Each project gets its own local vertex + SQLite store, self-contained and portable. Config level (~/.config/loops/) is the aggregation layer \\\\u2014 template vertices discover all local instances. loops status <name> reads local; loops status dev/<name> reads aggregate. Separate DBs by default. Merge/combinatorial vertex is opt-in aggregation. Same shape as the loops model: local loops produce ticks, ticks flow up. Local stores produce facts, aggregate vertices see them all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex templates are replicable patterns (project, task, handoff, pickup). loops init <template> creates a local instance in cwd. The config-level template vertex discovers all local instances. Templates define the fold shape; each instantiation gets its own data. Like git repos \\\\u2014 local is the primitive, aggregation is the network.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Two kinds of vertex files. Domain vertices are code \\\\u2014 checked into repos, define data pipelines (hlab status.vertex, economy.vertex). Knowledge vertices are runtime config \\\\u2014 project decisions, threads, tasks, handoff. Domain vertices ship with the app. Knowledge vertices are instantiated from templates via loops init. Both are .vertex files, same format, different lifecycle.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scopinmantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the system should help. Ties into combine auto-inherit pattern: push association down, don't require manual discipline at emit time.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"No way to inspect a single fact or tick at full depth. Stream truncates, fold collapses. Need a detail view on individual records \\\\u2014 same primitive for facts and ticks. loops show or similar.\\\"}, \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level configuration, not app-level. The app{} block concept dissolves \\\\u2014 lenses travel with vertices via lens{} in .vertex KDL, not nested under an app container. Apps own domain verbs, not lenses.\\\"}, \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: still valid for installed-package lens references but no current use case. Will emerge naturally when apps need to expose lenses from their packages.\\\"}, \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Each vertex declares its own lens. No inheritance across combine boundaries. An aggregation vertex has its own rendering needs distinct from its children. If you want a child's lens, declare it explicitly.\\\"}, \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Emit UX will be rethought as part of write-vertex operation.\\\"}, \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into convention. Source lifecycle kinds get a reserved prefix (e.g. _source.message.complete) to avoid matching data fold queries. Same pattern as _boundary on tick payloads.\\\"}, \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into vertex-name-resolution-consistency. The combine-emit problem is a resolution consistency problem \\\\u2014 uniform resolution covers both.\\\"}, \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Both phases complete. Phase 1: vertex-level scope declaration (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL). Identity is scoped, project/comms are unscoped. Phase 2: Source._extract_metadata reads _observer/_origin from ndjson payloads, overriding .loop defaults. Discord-source emits _observer=author, _origin=discord. Observer now consistently means identity. Origin carries source attribution. New discord polls will have correct observer \\\\u2014 existing data retains observer=discord.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three commands, three resolution behaviors. fold/stream resolve vertex names. run expects file paths. emit resolves but writes to wrong store through combine. Resolution should be uniform \\\\u2014 resolve_vertex works everywhere, or the gaps are explicit.\\\"}, \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Run loop model changes under two-operation CLI.\\\"}, \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Check cursors are part of old CLI shape; read-vertex model replaces them.\\\"}, \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream rendering will be rethought as part of read-vertex lenses.\\\"}, \\\"cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Refined to read/emit/init. 'run' dissolves \\\\u2014 source execution is fact generation via emit, not a separate operation. 'write' dissolves \\\\u2014 emit was already the right verb. Four things to learn became three: read (fold default, filters compose), emit (facts in, from user or source), init (create namespace). Remaining question: source execution model (see source-execution-model thread).\\\"}, \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The root vertex at ~/.config/loops/.vertex needs restructuring. Currently a thin aggregator with combine. Needs to become the actual routing root where children (project, identity, comms, reading, etc.) nest and ticks cascade. Design questions: which vertices are children vs peers? Does identity scope differently in the tree? How does observer-scoping interact with tree position? The root vertex read IS the system overview \\\\u2014 its default lens shows children and their state.\\\"}, \\\"read-operation-contract\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"read-operation-contract\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"What does 'read vertex' return mechanically? The read operation needs to serve multiple consumers via lenses: prompt lens (agent system prompt), default lens (terminal fold state), JSON (hooks). It must provide fold state + tick history + children. Does the read load the full subtree? How deep? Does --ticks change the data fetched or just the lens? Does search (positional query arg) go through the same read path? The contract between read and lens determines the implementation.\\\"}, \\\"source-execution-model\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source-execution-model\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved. Source execution dissolves to three concerns: Source (pure adapter), Cadence (store predicate), Executor (cadence-gated runner). Five decisions emitted: source-execution-model, cli-verb-first, cadence-as-store-predicate, read-is-pure, sync-locus-of-control. Investigation by 5-agent team: tracer (lifecycle), explorer (scheduling survey), architect (design v3), muser (dissolution challenges), siftd (historical context). Prior art: CADENCE.md (2026-01-31) proposed Source/Cadence split conceptually \\\\u2014 never implemented. This session designs the one-shot-compatible version.\\\"}}}, \\\"change\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session continuity + strange-loops scaffold \\\\u2014 loops session start/end/status/log, query-time fold, LOOPS_OBSERVER env var. strange-loops scaffolded.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Population as facts \\\\u2014 add/rm emit pop.add/pop.rm facts, .list materialized as projection, ls reads fold state.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session dissolution + cells\\\\u2192painted + run_cli harness \\\\u2014 dissolved session subcommand, status/log promoted to top-level, migrated cells\\\\u2192painted. 147 loops + 1169 painted tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Full Painted rendering + golden tests + store targeting \\\\u2014 all 9 display commands through run_cli, 45 golden snapshot tests, store targeting via vertex name resolution. 191 tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"engine CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 4 levels: Run vertex program, Fold and fire, Persist, Gate access. Semantic examples (decisions/threads). Deep-dive docs as reference layer.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"lang CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 3 levels: Parse a file, Understand AST, Manage populations. Connects DSL types to atoms/engine counterparts.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"store CLAUDE.md rewrite \\\\u2014 2 levels: Slice/merge, Schema. Clarifies relationship to engine SqliteStore.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chain headers and cross-references added to all 5 lib CLAUDE.md files. atoms retrofitted with oblique references to engine at Levels 0, 1, 3.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Dissolved discord, telegram, reader apps. Moved .loop/.vertex files to experiments/. Removed from workspace members. Updated root CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for all 3 apps: loops (new, 3 levels), hlab (rewrite 199\\\\u2192118 lines, 3 levels), strange-loops (rewrite 254\\\\u2192127 lines, 3 levels). All with chain headers.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Record line rendering fixes: gutter continuity with weight stepping, shallow 2-char indent replacing deep column alignment, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output eliminating terminal wrapping gaps, health_lens fixed to respect lens contract\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertex template includes default loops (decision, thread, change, task). _find_source_vertex priority: aggregation loops block > sibling instance > direct config instance. Updated project + meta aggregation vertices on disk.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuild: temporal modes + generic rendering\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"commands/observer.py,lenses/fold.py,lenses/stream.py,main.py,fixtures.py,test_session.py,test_status.py,test_log.py,test_cli_docs.py,test_cli.py\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval) and commands/identity.py (observer resolution). Dissolved _emit_fact, inlined _format_date into lenses. pop.py now uses resolve_observer() for full resolution chain. 394 tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design session\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into fetch.py + identity.py. Wired resolve_observer through pop.py. Created project .vertex with loops-claude as open observer. Designed FoldState typed contract (atoms-the-package), custom lens system (.vertex declaration + .loops/lenses/ + --lens flag), attention trifecta (what/when/how-much as lens concerns). Peer exchange with Alcove confirmed architecture. Two visions emitted to meta (attention-infrastructure, observer-constellation).\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldItem/FoldSection/FoldState in atoms. observer.py dissolved into commands/fetch.py + commands/identity.py. fetch_fold returns FoldState, fold_view consumes typed attributes. 235 loops + 322 atoms tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Fact-by-id: surface ULID identifiers + observer elevation\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"store_reader.py,vertex_reader.py,fetch.py,stream.py,main.py,__init__.py,test_store_reader.py,test_vertex_reader.py,~/.config/loops/.vertex\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Hook lifecycle + lens redistribution + CLAUDE.md\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\".claude/settings.json,~/.config/loops/lenses/comms.py,~/.config/loops/lenses/state.py,~/.config/loops/CLAUDE.md,apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/CLAUDE.md\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta + slashed emit + hooks cleanup\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping as vertex concern (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL), session tick since fix (replay period bridging), Source _extract_metadata for ndjson, prompt lens delegation rendering, SessionEnd mechanical delta log.\\\"}]}, \\\"task\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit routes through vertex runtime via load_vertex_program + vertex.receive. Dissolution \\\\u2014 removed the bypass, didn't build new machinery.\\\"}, \\\"daemon-local-orchestration\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"daemon-local-orchestration\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 no persistent runtime needed. Vertex is reactive. Scheduling is external (cron/systemd). One-shot CLI is the runtime.\\\"}, \\\"foldstate-audit-findings\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"foldstate-audit-findings\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: vertex_fold addresses the core finding (typed contract wired end-to-end). FoldItem.origin populated since prior session. Remaining gaps (no reference counting, no fold caching, no custom lens loading) are tracked as separate threads.\\\"}, \\\"identity-observer-filtering\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"identity-observer-filtering\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer-scoped reads wired end-to-end. --observer general flag at dispatch, default-to-self, resolved-status filtering in prompt lens. Help bug fixed \\\\u2014 subcommand -h no longer masked by top-level intercept.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Shipped in 0e1ddc9. Union semantics, conflict detection, aggregation loops{} is overrides only.\\\"}, \\\"session-close\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-close\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved: session is a kind, close is the handoff, pickup reads one fold.\\\"}, \\\"thread-auto-tagging\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-tagging\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD env var. 5 lines in cmd_emit, same pattern as LOOPS_OBSERVER.\\\"}, \\\"pickup-filtering\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"pickup-filtering\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved: root .vertex fold with prompt lens handles identity + session + tasks in one read.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into vertex-lens-infrastructure. LensDecl AST, lens resolver with 4-tier resolution and file search, call_lens with optional context kwargs (vertex_name). identity.vertex declares prompt lens.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"after\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into kind/key syntax on --kind flag. --kind thread/fold-state-types filters fold to single item, stream to matching facts. No new verbs \\\\u2014 / is the drill-down operator.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"later\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cache fold computation until new facts arrive. Alcove sees 3-5s overhead per dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Implemented: LensDecl in AST, lens{} block in KDL, lens_resolver.py with file search (vertex-local > project-local > user-global > built-in), 4-tier CLI resolution, call_lens with vertex_name context. 22 new tests.\\\"}, \\\"fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-by-id\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ULID IDs surfaced through entire read path. StoreReader.fact_by_id with prefix matching, vertex_fact_by_id across combined stores, --id flag on stream command. Progressive disclosure in stream lens. Primitive reference for future tick traversal.\\\"}, \\\"meta-hooks-bootstrap\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"meta-hooks-bootstrap\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Identity consolidated, pickup removed, comms delta wired. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"text-truncation-plain-vv\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"text-truncation-plain-vv\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Truncation behavior follows from new read-vertex rendering.\\\"}, \\\"session-tick-retrospective\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-tick-retrospective\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Completed. Fixed since bug, verified tick structure, dissolved handoff into tick, added mechanical delta to SessionEnd hook.\\\"}, \\\"docs-vertex-migration\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"docs-vertex-migration\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Continue migrating CLAUDE.md content to the docs vertex. Atoms proven \\\\u2014 52 facts, 4 zoom levels, kind filtering, guide payload structure works. Remaining libs: engine (4 levels), lang (3 levels), store (3 levels), painted consumer (5 levels), painted contributor (4 levels). Remaining apps: loops (4 levels), hlab (4 levels), strange-loops (4 levels), siftd (4 levels). Each migration is independent. Also need: prompt lens variant for system prompt injection, fix newline rendering in code/api payload fields.\\\"}, \\\"discord-source-poll-kind\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"discord-source-poll-kind\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Discord source script emits poll-status results as kind=message. Should be a different kind (e.g., 'poll' or 'source-status') so they don't pollute the message fold. Fix in ~/.config/loops/discord/discord-source. Comms lens has a workaround but the source is the right fix point.\\\"}, \\\"tick-surfacing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-surfacing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 ticks are visible through read-vertex; no separate surfacing command needed.\\\"}, \\\"tick-to-fact-flow\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-to-fact-flow\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 tick-to-fact cascading is already in the engine; read-vertex exposes it without dedicated plumbing.\\\"}, \\\"dissolve-messaging-vertex\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"dissolve-messaging-vertex\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Remove config/messaging/messaging.vertex. Telegram source moves to comms/telegram/ using same pattern as comms/discord/. Discord portion is already covered by comms/discord/.\\\"}, \\\"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Remove config/discord/discord.vertex \\\\u2014 duplicate of config/comms/discord/discord.vertex. The comms/ path is canonical.\\\"}, \\\"refactor-meta-combine\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"refactor-meta-combine\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"config/meta/meta.vertex currently combines meta-discussion + discord + identity. Should be a pure domain aggregation \\\\u2014 drop discord and identity from the combine. Those belong in the launch fold, not in the domain vertex.\\\"}, \\\"domain-vertex-template\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"domain-vertex-template\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Define the universal domain shape (decisions/threads/tasks/sessions/changes) as the base template for loops init. Local .vertex files extend with domain-specific kinds. Rename 'project' concept to 'domain' in templates and docs.\\\"}, \\\"session-launch-script\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-launch-script\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Write the two-line launch script: emit session fact with delegation, exec claude with LOOPS_OBSERVER. This is the dogfooding entry point \\\\u2014 use it to start sessions instead of raw 'LOOPS_OBSERVER=x claude'.\\\"}, \\\"identity/observer-namespacing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"identity/observer-namespacing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer namespacing (kyle/meta-claude) introduced in launch script but never landed in read path, .vertex declarations, or emit validation. Currently reverted to bare names. When namespace concept is needed (multi-user, delegation), it must land in three places: .vertex observer declarations, validate_emit() matching, and vertex_reader.py filter (4 sites of exact equality). Provenance preserved via session fact payload (principal=kyle, agent=meta-claude).\\\"}}}, \\\"session\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"loops-claude\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"loops-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"kyle\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kyle\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-auto-tagging dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD (5 lines). Staleness audit closed 4 threads (fold-state-types, observer-scoped-handoff, gist-lens-generics, observer-cascade). Prompt lens session fix for Alcove. Designed vertex lens infrastructure with Alcove input \\\\u2014 architecture decision emitted, 3 deferred threads tagged, task created. Next: implement vertex-lens-infrastructure (LensDecl AST + loader + resolver + CLI wiring).\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:thread-auto-tagging\\\", \\\"thread:fold-state-types\\\", \\\"thread:observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"thread:gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"thread:observer-cascade\\\", \\\"thread:fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"task:custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"task:fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"task:fold-materialization\\\", \\\"decision:design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"thread:app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"thread:module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"thread:combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"task:vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\"]}, \\\"meta-claude\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"meta-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"test-boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"test-boundary\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"test-vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"test-vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"e2e-test\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"e2e-test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"replay-test\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"replay-test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}}}, \\\"log\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-28\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Loops model crystallized + persistence exploration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Explored adding persistence to experiments. The exploration dissolved multiple\\\\nconcepts back into existing atoms:\\\\n\\\\n| Concept | Dissolved into | Why |\\\\n|---------|---------------|-----|\\\\n| Sink | Fold state | Loops have no terminals |\\\\n| Store | Durable fold | Storage is a property, not a type |\\\\n| Witness | Peer + Vertex | Just a peer whose job is to observe and emit |\\\\n| Tap | Vertex | Emission from storage is vertex behavior |\\\\n| Memory | Boundary-less fold | Silent accumulation is a fold that never ticks |\\\\n\\\\n**Key insight:** The atoms are complete. New requirements don't require new\\\\nprimitives \\\\u2014 they're configurations of existing ones.\\\\n\\\\nCreated `LOOPS.md` as the fundamental model document. Four satellite docs\\\\nadded: `docs/VERTEX.md`, `docs/TEMPORAL.md`, `docs/PERSISTENCE.md`, `docs/PEERS.md`.\\\\nEach unpacks one aspect and references back to LOOPS.md.\\\\n\\\\nFixed Enter key bug in keyboard.py (handle LF 0x0A same as CR 0x0D).\\\\n\\\\nOpen naming tensions noted but deferred:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Peer\\\\\\\" implies equality but delegation is hierarchical\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Tick\\\\\\\" implies clock time but boundaries are semantic\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-28\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Peer-driven boundaries + None=unrestricted + lens distinction\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"`review.py`: two loops through one vertex. Health ticks at timer cadence\\\\n(passive). Review ticks when peer acks all containers (active \\\\u2014 composition\\\\nlayer sends `review.complete` sentinel).\\\\n\\\\n**Peer model change**: `horizon` and `potential` default to `None` (unrestricted)\\\\ninstead of `frozenset()` (empty). Constraints emerge through `delegate()`, not\\\\nupfront enumeration.\\\\n\\\\n**Debug is a lens, not a horizon.** The None model exposed a category error:\\\\n\\\\\\\"debug\\\\\\\" was a horizon string alongside container names, but it's a rendering\\\\nmode, not a data domain. Debug panel is now a lens toggle available to any peer.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Boundary triggering implemented\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Implemented boundary triggering on Vertex. `Projection.reset()` added.\\\\n`register()` gains `boundary: str | None` and `reset: bool`. `receive()`\\\\nreturns `Tick | None`. Fold-before-boundary, optional reset, boundary kind\\\\nuniqueness enforced.\\\\n\\\\nVertex is sync by design \\\\u2014 async bridge lives at composition point.\\\\n122 ticks tests.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Feedback loop closed, experiment log established\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"`experiments/observe.py`: first experiment that closes the feedback loop.\\\\nUser interactions (j/k/enter) are Facts through the same `vertex.receive()`\\\\nas external observations.\\\\n\\\\nEmergent insights captured in `experiments/LOG.md`: debug as horizon (not\\\\ninfrastructure), meta-actions outside the loop, thin composition layer.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Genesis document + strata semantic tagging\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Reconstructed project origin story via strata. Synthesized into `docs/GENESIS.md`.\\\\nApplied semantic tags to 58 conversations across workspaces.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tick-to-Fact dissolved, fleet experiment\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Built `experiments/fleet.py`: three-level vertex hierarchy (4 VMs \\\\u2192 2 regions\\\\n\\\\u2192 global). Ticks are a level above Facts \\\\u2014 temporal groupings, not peers.\\\\nThe question dissolved. Same primitive at every level.\\\\n\\\\nTick gained `origin` field. Vertex gained `name` parameter.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Architecture crystallization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replaced Stream concept with Vertex (intersection of loops). Explored and\\\\nrejected Tick-into-Fact collapse. Tick gained `name` field. Full narrative\\\\nin `ARCHITECTURE-JOURNEY.md`.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-26\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Semantic journey\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Monorepo naming exploration (loops vs volta vs prism). Pivot concept\\\\ncrystallized (four universal atoms + cell as first surface). Peer refactored\\\\nto horizon + potential.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-26\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Structure alignment\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Project structure normalized across all five libs. Per-lib CLAUDE.md and\\\\nHANDOFF.md added. Six parallel fixes merged.\\\"}, {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: observer app rebuild. Implemented the unified conceptual model from last session's 4-agent design (mapper, muser, miner, explorer). Three temporal modes (fold/stream/emit) replace the old if-elif dispatch. Generic declaration-driven rendering: key_field from FoldBy IS the label, fold_type IS the rendering strategy. No per-kind code in fetch or lens layers. Bare vertex defaults to fold. Legacy aliases preserved. The design came from team analysis: muser proposed temporal modes orthogonal to spatial fidelity, mapper audited every command, miner provided engine/painted API data, and the whole chain collapsed status/log/search into fold/stream. Next: developer app split, observer-scoped pickup, gist lens generics, dispatch from vertex capabilities.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: fact-by-id + fold-state-types + observer-cascade. Three core threads progressed. fact-by-id: surfaced ULID IDs through all read paths, --id flag on stream, progressive disclosure in both lenses. fold-state-types: FoldItem carries fact ID, traversal loop closed (fold \\\\u2192 ID \\\\u2192 stream --id). observer-cascade: aggregation vertices inherit source observers via combine chain, dissolves the elevation workaround. session-as-tick deferred \\\\u2014 prerequisites in place, needs engine-native boundary design. Observer elevation bug found and fixed along the way. Retrospective produced 5 identity observations including task-selection-as-identity.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session: hook lifecycle + lens redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Wired SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit/SessionEnd hooks for observer-generic session lifecycle. Built comms lens (user-global) for messaging vertices. Moved state lens from built-in to user-global. Established lens tier pattern: built-in = core primitives, user-global = domain rendering. CLAUDE.md at lenses/ (repo) and ~/.config/loops/ (config). custom-lens-infrastructure thread resolved. Next: recency-aware-lens for attention-weighted startup fold, comms vertex when Discord bridge reactivates.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta. Merged three identity stores into config-level single store (all observers, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER). Dissolved pickup.zsh \\\\u2014 hooks handle all bootstrap. Slashed vertex emit (comms/native) resolves sub-vertices before template qualification. Comms lens is delta-aware: check facts as cursors, shows new-since-last-check, suppresses when quiet. Hooks dropped uv run for bare loops. Sent infrastructure summary to Alcove via Discord. Meta bootstrap verified. Next: watch Alcove first hook-based session, sessions-as-ticks.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta + payload-conditional boundaries. Five commits: identity merge (3 stores \\\\u2192 1), pickup.zsh dissolved (hooks-only bootstrap), slashed vertex emit (comms/native), comms delta (check facts as cursors), payload-conditional boundaries (boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\"). Session close now produces a tick carrying folded state. 1176 tests pass. Meta bootstrap verified. Message sent to Alcove. Push pending (network timeout).\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: observer scoping + session tick retrospective + delegation. Three design threads resolved (session-as-tick, observer-vs-source-attribution, plus combine-emit-routing and kind-prefix-leak dissolved). Vertex scope declaration landed \\\\u2014 identity is observer-scoped, project/comms unscoped. Session tick since field fixed \\\\u2014 period bridging works across CLI one-shot invocations. Source metadata extraction enables per-record observer/origin in ndjson. Prompt lens renders delegated threads separately. Remaining design: vertex-name-resolution-consistency, check-cursor-mechanism, recency-aware-lens. Next priority: resolution consistency (three commands, three strategies).\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 18 facts. 12 thread, 3 decision, 1 change, 1 log, 1 task.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 21 facts. 12 thread, 5 decision, 4 task.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 53 facts. 32 thread, 12 decision, 5 task, 3 log, 1 change.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 17 facts. 9 thread, 6 decision, 1 handoff, 1 log.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 10 facts. 5 decision, 3 observation, 1 handoff, 1 thread.\\\"}]}, \\\"_boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"loops-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}}\",\"prev_hash\":null,\"signature\":null,\"since\":1772861635.949178,\"tick_id\":\"01kk3cpe38fb94bc76dhp07yvw\",\"window_hash\":null,\"window_start\":null}"}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:2075:{"t":"fact","id":"01KK3DN04ST0ENEA3N9YD0ED4W","kind":"tick.project","ts":1772862734.489579,"observer":"project","origin":"project","payload":"{\"fact_cursor\":null,\"name\":\"project\",\"payload\":\"{\\\"decision\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"architecture/root-claude-md\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/root-claude-md\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Root CLAUDE.md is monorepo orientation only: pointer to LOOPS.md, build commands, structure map, discovery path to lib/app CLAUDE.md files, and project store query instructions. Model details, data flow, lib-specific patterns all pushed down to lib-level CLAUDE.md. Validates claude-md-levels and claude-md-antipatterns decisions from meta.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/project-vertex\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/project-vertex\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Renamed session.vertex to project.vertex. Project vertex holds durable project-specific decisions, threads, tasks. Same shape as meta vertex but scoped to this repo. Symlinked at ~/.config/loops/project for global access. Meta stays cross-cutting; project stays repo-specific.\\\"}, \\\"meta/current-activity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"meta/current-activity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md system for the loops monorepo. Applying the painted library pattern (levels with escalation triggers, don't-reach-for-yet barriers) to replace the God CLAUDE.md antipattern. Walking through each level top-down with the user, aligning on content at each step, emitting decisions to project and meta stores as we go. Simultaneously establishing the project vertex as the loops-specific knowledge store alongside the cross-cutting meta store.\\\"}, \\\"atoms/progressive-claude-md\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"atoms/progressive-claude-md\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for libs/atoms. Four levels: Observe (Fact), Accumulate (Spec+Fold+Boundary), Shape input (Parse vocabulary), Ingest (Source+Runner). Each level has trigger conditions and dont-reach-for-yet barriers. Replaces the 20-line README stub. Deep dive docs (VERTEX.md, TEMPORAL.md) referenced from engine CLAUDE.md, not atoms \\\\u2014 they're engine-level concepts.\\\"}, \\\"meta/session-summary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"meta/session-summary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md session: rewrote root CLAUDE.md (monorepo orientation only), created libs/atoms/CLAUDE.md (4 levels: Observe, Accumulate, Shape, Ingest with semantic-first examples), established project.vertex as durable project store, merged vertex-template-system (slashed names, init with config registration, aggregation vertices). Emitted 5 decisions to meta store (progressive-vertex-chain, project-vertex-pattern, distributed-store-default, vertex-templates, domain-vs-knowledge-vertices). Next: engine CLAUDE.md, then lang, painted alignment, store.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-dependency-graph\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-dependency-graph\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"lang\\\\u2192ckdl (pure grammar), engine\\\\u2192atoms+lang (runtime+compiler), apps\\\\u2192engine+painted (CLI). Key: lang is portable (only ckdl dep), compiler backend lives in engine where target types are defined.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/chain-headers\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/chain-headers\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"Every lib CLAUDE.md gets a 'you are here' chain showing what's below and above. Bidirectional references \\\\u2014 agents can enter anywhere and orient.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"All five libs (atoms, engine, lang, store, painted) have progressive CLAUDE.md with levels, triggers, barriers, and chain headers. Lib layer done.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/dissolved-apps\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/dissolved-apps\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"discord, telegram, reader dissolved into the overall loops system. DSL files preserved in experiments/. Workspace reduced to 3 apps: loops, hlab, strange-loops.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"All 3 active apps have progressive CLAUDE.md. Combined with libs, every directory in the monorepo now has the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/record-line-primitives\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/record-line-primitives\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"record_line and record_line_composed are production rendering primitives in painted. Gutter continuity (stepping weight), shallow 2-char indent, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output. health_lens returns summary string, record_line handles continuation lines.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/lens-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/lens-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"PayloadLens returns the summary (str or styled Block). record_line owns continuation lines \\\\u2014 DETAILED shows well-known secondary fields, FULL shows all fields. Lenses must not embed multiline content; record_line handles that.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/gutter-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/gutter-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Gutter is a continuous vertical rail. GutterFn returns primary weight. Stepping map derives continuation weight: full block to half, half to thin, thin stays thin. Color stays same, weight steps down. Rail never breaks.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/help-min-zoom\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/help-min-zoom\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace help secondary: bool with min_zoom: Zoom. Each HelpGroup declares when it appears via min_zoom, rendering follows effective-zoom pattern (eff < 0 hidden, 0 compact, 1 expanded, >= 2 expanded+detail). Dissolves hardcoded Interaction rules section.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/help-unification\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/help-unification\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Unify help rendering: AppRunner intercepts -h at subcommand level, not just top level. Action commands describe args via help_args on AppCommand. Handlers never see -h. Chosen over CliRunner wrapper approach \\\\u2014 help is an AppRunner concern, execution is a handler concern.\\\"}, \\\"init/aggregation-loops-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"init/aggregation-loops-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices declare loops as canonical schema. New instances derive base loops from aggregation root, not first sibling. _extract_loops_text brace-matches the block; _find_source_vertex prefers it over instance fallback.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-developer-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-developer-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The CLI has two loops: Observer loop (vertex-first, one verb, temporal modes) and Developer loop (file-first, multiple verbs, DSL tools). These are different projections on different concerns \\\\u2192 different apps. Observer app: loops <vertex> [mode] [fidelity]. Developer app: separate binary (validate, compile, run, test). No shared dispatch logic.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/emit-only-verb\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/emit-only-verb\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"emit is the only verb in the observer app. Everything else is a temporal mode selector (fold/stream/declaration) or a filter (search). status/log/store were always lenses pretending to be operations. start dissolves \\\\u2014 run with rounds=1 covers the same behavior.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/fetch-dissolves\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/fetch-dissolves\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"fetch functions in commands/ dissolve into engine fold replay. The fold declaration IS the fetch instruction. decision { fold { items 'by' 'topic' } } tells the runtime to group decisions by topic. fetch_status manually reimplements what Spec.apply already does. Projection = vertex capabilities + fold state (runtime-computed). Lens = fidelity selection + rendering. No intermediate fetch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/temporal-modes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/temporal-modes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"status/log/store are temporal modes, not operations. Fold = post-boundary (what is now). Stream = pre-boundary (what happened). Declaration = above boundary (what can happen). Different use cases: fold to orient, stream to investigate, declaration to audit. Default: fold at ORIENTATION, annotated with stream recency.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dispatch derives from structural capabilities, not from fold declarations. The loops block shapes what existing commands render (lens configuration). Structural features (store, sources, discover, combine) determine what operations exist. A vertex with store gets fold/stream/declaration modes. Sources add run. Discover adds aggregation traversal. The vertex file is the capability manifest.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-placement\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-placement\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant sits between capabilities and projection in the chain: Declaration \\\\u2192 Capabilities \\\\u2192 [Grant constrains] \\\\u2192 Projection \\\\u2192 Lens \\\\u2192 Perspective. Horizon constrains projection (filters which kinds reach the lens). Potential constrains the verb (limits which kinds emit accepts). When Grant goes live, no new commands needed \\\\u2014 same vertex, same lens, different perspectives.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuilt: fold (collapsed state), stream (event history), emit. Generic declaration-driven rendering replaces per-kind extractors and renderers. Bare vertex defaults to fold.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"One renderer for all kinds. key_field from FoldBy declaration drives the label. No per-kind if-elif in fetch or lens. Identity vertex self/observation/principle render the same as decision/thread/task.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Search is now stream with a positional query arg. One fetch, one lens, one dispatch path. FTS5 still used when query present.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops project (no subcommand) now shows folded state. Flags pass through: loops project -v, loops project -q, loops project --kind decision all work.\\\"}, \\\"observer-resolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-resolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer resolves through vertex declaration chain: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. No more env var or hardcoded defaults as primary path. --observer flag remains as explicit override.\\\"}, \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\".vertex (bare, no prefix) is the workspace root at every level. Config-level root.vertex becomes .vertex. Project-level .loops/.vertex is the project root. Same pattern, fractal. All structure mutations (add observer, add vertex) target the .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex definitions (project.vertex, identity.vertex, etc.) copy locally when added to a workspace. Local copy can diverge \\\\u2014 different fold declarations, different kinds. Facts are ground truth; declarations are projections. Global view discovers and reads stores regardless of local declaration differences.\\\"}, \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observers start project-scoped (declared in project .vertex). As identity generalizes beyond the project, elevate to global .vertex. Identity facts merge up via store merge. Global observers appear in every workspace automatically \\\\u2014 no bootstrapping.\\\"}, \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex declares its observers natively. Observer is not just a string stamp \\\\u2014 it connects to identity (via identity vertex reference) and grants (capability constraints). The vertex is the authority on who can emit into it. Resolution walks up: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm/init are all vertex mutation operations. Adding an observer, pulling in a vertex definition, managing parameter rows \\\\u2014 same verb pattern, different targets on the vertex declaration. The .vertex file is the thing being built up.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"observer.py splits into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval: fetch_fold, fetch_stream) and commands/identity.py (who you are: resolve_observer, validate_emit, find_workspace_root). _emit_fact dissolved (zero callers). _format_date inlined into lenses/fold.py where it's used.\\\"}, \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"resolve_observer() is the single source of truth for observer identity. Priority: flag \\\\u2192 env \\\\u2192 project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. pop.py's _observer() now delegates to resolve_observer() instead of bare env read. All ad-hoc resolution paths dissolved.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-level validation (validate_emit) for CLI fast path \\\\u2014 checks observer declared + kind in grant.potential. Engine-level Grant for runtime path (loops start/run) \\\\u2014 deferred until compiler produces identity-aware runtime. Two levels, same data, different contexts.\\\"}, \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude declared as open observer in project .vertex (.loops/.vertex). No grant constraints \\\\u2014 full emit access within the monorepo. Global elevation deferred until identity store is built out further.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem frozen dataclasses go in libs/atoms/. Lens contract becomes (atoms.FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. FoldItem separates payload (dict[str,Any]) from metadata (ts, observer, origin). FoldSection supports nesting (sections: tuple[FoldSection, ...]). count dissolves into len(items). Engine computes FoldState from Facts + Spec, lenses consume it.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Custom lenses: Python files in .loops/lenses/ exposing render(data, zoom, width) -> Block. Vertex declares lens by name (per-kind or vertex-level default). CLI loads via importlib from .loops/lenses/{name}.py. Custom lenses can import built-in lenses to compose. Resolution: kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project \\\\u2192 config \\\\u2192 built-in. --lens flag overrides all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit should start the vertex runtime in one-shot mode, not write directly to SQLite. Same machinery as daemon mode, different lifecycle. Facts route through vertices, loops evaluate boundaries, ticks fire naturally. Foundational fix enabling observer-initiated ticks.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/tach\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/tach\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"tach for tier 2 import enforcement. Rust (fast), TOML config (declarative), fits uv/ruff/ty toolchain. tach sync bootstraps from existing code. Replaces hand-rolled AST import walkers (siftd ~230 lines). Does not replace domain invariants.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"scripts/ contains check.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\\\u2192 lens \\\\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\\\"}, \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\\\u2192fold state, Store\\\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\\\u2192vertex, Memory\\\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\\\u2192same primitive.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\\\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\\\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\\\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md is the critical document for returning from a gap. Must answer: what was I doing, what's next, what's deferred, what's the current state. It's the bridge across the wave's trough.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session facts are source of truth for state. Documents (LOG.md) are source of truth for understanding. Could generate HANDOFF.md from facts, but not a good LOG.md \\\\u2014 that requires narrative judgment.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Loops has directionality: Facts in \\\\u2192 Spec \\\\u2192 Ticks out. Structure declared upfront. siftd is retroactive query over raw conversation history \\\\u2014 no Spec, no fold. siftd discovers patterns you didn't anticipate (sine wave emerged from querying 110 days of data). Loops accumulates with guarantees (latest-by-topic). They feed each other but shouldn't merge.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops is operating memory (what do we believe right now?), siftd is the archaeological layer (what actually happened, what can we learn from it?). Complementary, not converging.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md serves cold-start reorientation \\\\u2014 narrative coherence, sequential reading, density for rebuilding mental model. Facts serve queryability and composability across repos. Converting loses the narrative; not converting loses the queryability.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Alcove depends on HANDOFF.md every wake cycle. Bag of facts requires knowing what questions to ask; prose builds context sequentially.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Keep HANDOFF.md as prose for cold-start reorientation. Derive decisions from it as loops facts. Prose is the source document, facts are the queryable index. Two representations serving different access patterns.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A scaffold element IS a compound decision cluster (tier 2). Tick-to-Fact bridging: scaffold Tick enters new project's vertex as a Fact. Type forgets it was a conclusion; metadata remembers provenance. New project accumulates its own state on top \\\\u2014 can override positions.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"testing/* namespace is 8 decisions that compose into one scaffold element. Tick gives observability: trace which decisions propagated, see where projects diverged.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold elements are Ticks derived from decision namespaces. Boundary must be manual (deliberate snapshot at project init), not automatic cascading. Gets observability that templates don't \\\\u2014 can trace propagation and divergence.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md dissolves into the store. Handoff is a fact kind (fold: latest). Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex \\\\u2014 reads handoff prose, open threads, active tasks, recent decisions. Wind-down emits the handoff fact instead of writing a file.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Wind-down has two phases: reconciliation (emit missing facts, resolve completed threads, update tasks) and handoff (prose synthesis). Reconciliation compensates for gaps in continuous session emission. As in-session hooks mature, reconciliation shrinks. Handoff is always end-of-session \\\\u2014 it's narrative, not incremental.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"siftd decomposes into loops monorepo. Sources are already solved (harnesses are just source definitions). New libs/store absorbs all DB operations siftd proved out: ingest, slice, merge, search, transport. siftd-as-app becomes a thin specialization layer \\\\u2014 LLM harness configs + analytics queries + CLI. Same relationship as painted (rendering spine) \\\\u2014 siftd becomes the analytics spine.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dynamically compose vertices that fold across multiple underlying stores \\\\u2014 e.g. alcove.db + kyle.db + watchers.db into a temporary vertex for a specific query. Temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful. This is what makes cross-store search fundamental rather than a feature.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"New loops lib explicitly for store operations. Absorbs from siftd: ingest (format-specific readers, schema-agnostic output), slice (by date/project/tag), merge (combine stores, deduplicate), search (FTS5 + semantic over any SQLite store), transport (push/pull/sync between stores over SSH or HTTP). Generic over any vertex store.\\\"}, \\\"design/context-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/context-fold\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Alcove's context fold pattern: before a message hits the agent, the dispatch loop constructs a brief context summary \\\\u2014 latest activity across all channels/stores. Lightweight (just latest timestamps + one line per channel). Same pattern as continuous-session-emission for claude-code sessions. The fold is ephemeral, rebuilt every dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-document architecture proven on alcove: SOUL.md (identity \\\\u2014 editorial, hand-shaped), CLAUDE.md (operational \\\\u2014 tools, paths, permissions), loops store (learned knowledge \\\\u2014 accumulated facts, foldable, queryable). MEMORY.md is a cache/projection of operational knowledge for session start, not the source of truth.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-project queryability dissolves into store operations once libs/store exists. Emit a decision in meta, discover it from loops \\\\u2014 not via special cross-project protocol, but via store merge/search/transport. The combinatorial vertex is the query mechanism.\\\"}, \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"meta-discussion,alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wind-down converge with alcove's context fold pattern. Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex (handoff prose + threads + tasks + decisions). Wind-down emits the handoff fact + reconciles the store. Alcove's context fold is the same shape \\\\u2014 read all stores, compose a view for orientation. The general pattern: any session boundary (start, end, dispatch) needs a lens over accumulated state.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single-project pickup is multi-fold reads on one vertex \\\\u2014 not a combinatorial vertex. Read fold(handoff, latest) + fold(threads, active) + fold(decisions, recent) from one store. Cross-project pickup is where combinatorial vertices enter \\\\u2014 reading folds across N stores. libs/store dissolves the boundary between these two scales.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"meta-discussion is the design space around loops itself, not just decisions about projects. Cross-cutting architecture (store operations, combinatorial vertices, attention filters, context folds, pickup/winddown workflow) emerges here and in cross-instance channels (alcove discord), not in the loops repo. Parallel meta-discussion on the meta aspect of loops along with ways of working.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts and ticks use ULID as primary key via native SQLite extension (not application-generated like siftd did). Globally unique, time-ordered, sortable. Merge becomes INSERT OR IGNORE \\\\u2014 ULID is the identity across stores. Replaces auto-increment rowid. Cursor semantics preserved (ULID is sortable, WHERE id > last_seen still works). Essential for distributed store orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Payload is always valid JSON \\\\u2014 enforced on write. This guarantees json_extract() is always safe, FTS can always walk the tree, and indexed columns can be projected from payload fields. Progressive enhancement: add explicit indexed columns (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) for hot query paths as needed.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 full-text search as the starting point for store.search. Zero external dependencies, sub-millisecond query at current scale (100-10k facts). Recursive JSON text extraction reliable by construction (payload-is-JSON contract). json_extract() for field filtering works without indexes up to ~100k facts. Indexed projections (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) are the progressive enhancement when scale demands it \\\\u2014 boundary is roughly 100k+ facts or hot query paths.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Transport is a pluggable interface, not a fixed implementation. The operations are constant (slice on source, merge on target), the pipe varies (local, SSH, HTTP, future protocols). Local transport ships first (testable, no infrastructure). SSH next (alcove sync is forcing function). HTTP when scrape/collect patterns emerge (Prometheus-style data collection). Store operations (slice, merge) are transport-agnostic \\\\u2014 they work on local paths, transport handles the pipe.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted is the native display layer for the store, not a rendering utility. Every store operation gets a painted view at all four zoom levels. Apps add domain-specific lenses that interpret facts in their context, but the underlying operations are universal. Domain-specific views generalize back into painted over time as patterns recur (task dashboard \\\\u2192 generic dashboard lens, siftd data exploration \\\\u2192 generic fold exploration). This is why painted is returning to the monorepo \\\\u2014 if loops needs a rendering capability, painted grows to support it.\\\"}, \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md progressive chain maps 1:1 to vertex store progressive query. The document is the lens, the store is the state. Root CLAUDE.md references the project vertex; lib CLAUDE.md tells you how to query your slice via topic namespace (atoms/*, engine/*, painted/*). One store, kind-namespaced topics, natural slicing. Same pattern as hlab status \\\\u2014 one vertex, multiple sources, scoped by name.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"project.vertex is the durable project-level store for decisions, threads, and tasks. Named 'project' (not 'session') \\\\u2014 same pattern strange-loops uses for task orchestration, now a meta-pattern for all projects. Cross-cutting concerns stay in meta; project-specific concerns accumulate in the project vertex. Progressive CLAUDE.md references the project store at each level.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Stores are distributed-first, aggregate-up. Each project gets its own local vertex + SQLite store, self-contained and portable. Config level (~/.config/loops/) is the aggregation layer \\\\u2014 template vertices discover all local instances. loops status <name> reads local; loops status dev/<name> reads aggregate. Separate DBs by default. Merge/combinatorial vertex is opt-in aggregation. Same shape as the loops model: local loops produce ticks, ticks flow up. Local stores produce facts, aggregate vertices see them all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex templates are replicable patterns (project, task, handoff, pickup). loops init <template> creates a local instance in cwd. The config-level template vertex discovers all local instances. Templates define the fold shape; each instantiation gets its own data. Like git repos \\\\u2014 local is the primitive, aggregation is the network.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Two kinds of vertex files. Domain vertices are code \\\\u2014 checked into repos, define data pipelines (hlab status.vertex, economy.vertex). Knowledge vertices are runtime config \\\\u2014 project decisions, threads, tasks, handoff. Domain vertices ship with the app. Knowledge vertices are instantiated from templates via loops init. Both are .vertex files, same format, different lifecycle.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Do not add kinds_consumed to Tick atom. Use tool-level scope derived from .vertex config when available, or observer/origin filtering. Avoids per-tick duplication, API ripple, and semantic ambiguity. Design on stale branch design/tick-provenance.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SUPERSEDED: The merge gap dissolves when strange-loops replaces subtask. Workers emit facts instead of writing artifacts to branches. No branch to orphan, no merge step to miss. See threads: strange-loops-merge-strategy, artifact-to-fact-convergence.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the sole read interface for store data. StoreReader becomes an internal detail of how the vertex materializes fold state from its backing store \\\\u2014 not a public API. The read path compiles the vertex declaration, replays facts through declared folds, and returns fold state. No vertex declaration for a kind means no way to read that kind. This structurally prevents bypassing fold declarations (same pattern as frozen dataclasses preventing mutation). Enforcement is a tier 1 package boundary check (StoreReader not in public API), not a behavioral test. _latest_by_group in session.py dissolves \\\\u2014 the vertex fold compilation already implements FoldBy. loops status and loops log compile the vertex, ask for fold states, render them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-dispatch-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-dispatch-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Apps register a short name in an explicit dict in loops/main.py. loops <app> <args> delegates to the app's main(argv) via importlib. ~5 lines. Phase 1 is a static registry; entry-point discovery deferred until 3+ apps stabilize. The app owns its own command dispatch, fetch functions, and lenses. The boundary is main(argv) \\\\u2014 loops CLI doesn't know about app internals, app doesn't know about loops CLI dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"design/lens-generalization-flow\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lens-generalization-flow\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain-specific lenses generalize to painted when the same rendering pattern appears in 2+ apps. This happens naturally \\\\u2014 don't extract ahead of time. Generic store lenses (fact timeline, fold state views) live in painted. Domain lenses (siftd search results, task lifecycle) stay in the app. The signal to extract is independent convergence, not prediction.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/rendering-three-layers\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/rendering-three-layers\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-layer rendering architecture: (1) painted owns structural primitives (Block, Line, zoom, run_cli), timestamp formatting, and generic data patterns like record timelines \\\\u2014 parameterized, domain-agnostic. (2) apps/loops owns store atom rendering (fact_line, tick_line, log_block) that maps facts/ticks to painted's structural patterns, plus the default payload lens (content_gist heuristic). (3) Domain apps provide per-kind payload lenses that override the default. painted never imports from atoms/engine.\\\"}, \\\"design/payload-lens\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/payload-lens\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"A payload lens is a single function (kind, payload, zoom) \\\\u2192 str | Block. At zoom 0 it returns a one-liner gist. At zoom 2+ it returns a multi-line expansion. content_gist and _log_summary dissolve into this \\\\u2014 they were always the same concept at different zoom levels. The structural renderer (fact_line, log_block) composes with the payload lens via a summarize callback. Apps inject domain-specific payload lenses; the default is heuristic field scanning.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-record-patterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-record-patterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted grows generic record rendering patterns: timestamped record lines, date-grouped timelines, fold-state tables. These are parameterized by a payload lens \\\\u2014 painted handles the chrome (timestamps, grouping, zoom degradation, width), the caller provides meaning. Facts, ticks, blog entries, log lines \\\\u2014 all are timestamped records with fields. The structural shape is the same; the payload lens provides the domain interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/store-search-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/store-search-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 is required infrastructure, not optional. Spec-declared searchable fields in vertex KDL (search \\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\" as sibling of fold/boundary). Standalone FTS5 table with lazy catch-up indexing via high water mark \\\\u2014 no INSERT triggers because spec-to-field mapping lives in vertex, not database. Write path untouched; FTS is purely read-side. First search pays backfill cost, subsequent searches catch up on deltas. Combinatorial vertex search: each store searched independently, results merged after recall. json_extract+LIKE rejected \\\\u2014 personal scale grows continuously (siftd alone 100-150k+ facts), cross-store combinatorial queries multiply dataset.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/boundary-enforcement\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/boundary-enforcement\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-based architecture boundary tests in tests/test_architecture.py enforce vertex-as-read-interface. Four rules: apps don't import StoreReader (exceptions: store inspector permanent, pop_store temporary), apps don't import sqlite3, libs don't import apps, lib dependency DAG (engine->lang runtime, engine->atoms runtime). TYPE_CHECKING-aware visitor. Stale exceptions fail the test. Monorepo-level concern, lives at repo root not in any single lib.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex spec declares searchable fields per kind: search \\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\" as sibling of fold and boundary in loop definitions. LoopDef gains search: tuple[str, ...]. Callers don't override at query time \\\\u2014 vertex_search reads the spec to know what's searchable. Only declared fields extracted and indexed. Keeps FTS5 index surgical at scale. Template loop resolution via collect_search_fields() handles generated kind names from .loop templates.\\\"}, \\\"design/lazy-fts-indexing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lazy-fts-indexing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 indexing uses lazy catch-up pattern: first search pays full backfill, subsequent searches catch up on deltas via high water mark in fts_state table. No INSERT triggers \\\\u2014 triggers can't do spec-aware field extraction since the kind-to-field mapping lives in the vertex file, not the database. The resultant first-search slowdown fits the loops philosophy: not necessary that things happen instantly, only that they do reliably with the same data flow and rule set. Idempotent, incremental, spec-driven.\\\"}, \\\"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-store search follows recall-then-compose pattern: FTS5 per store independently, union candidate sets, fold/rank across combined results. Composition happens after recall, not during \\\\u2014 FTS5 virtual tables are per-database in SQLite. Each vertex store remains self-contained with its own FTS5 index. Combinatorial vertex is a view over stores, not a new store. Search follows the same boundary.\\\"}, \\\"design/app-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/app-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Apps dissolve into lenses + feedback over vertex declarations. An app does not own a data model or ingress pipeline \\\\u2014 the vertex declaration (kinds, folds, search fields, boundaries) IS the data model, Sources ARE ingress, and both ship via template at loops init. What an app uniquely provides: (1) domain-specific lenses \\\\u2014 Painted rendering of fold state tuned to a data shape (conversation browser, task board, system dashboard), and (2) feedback capability \\\\u2014 the ability to emit facts/ticks back through the lens (tag a conversation, close a task, ack an alert). The observer and actor are the same entity. This dissolves siftd, strange-loops, and hlab into structurally identical programs: Painted surfaces over vertex state with domain-specific rendering and keybindings. The Smalltalk parallel is precise \\\\u2014 there is one runtime (loops), one data substrate (vertex/store), one rendering framework (Painted), and domain configuration that selects active lenses and feedback handlers. The app is a perspective on the system, not a separate program. Unlike Smalltalk, the Unix grounding holds: stores are cp-able SQLite files, sources are shell commands, CLI is always available as pipe-friendly lower-fidelity surface.\\\"}, \\\"design/store-ingest-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/store-ingest-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The store-ingest-design plan dissolves. Ingest \\\\u2014 format-aware file reading that produces facts \\\\u2014 is not a library primitive. It decomposes into: Sources (shell commands or scripts that read files and emit NDJSON, already exist), parse pipeline (dict\\\\u2192dict shaping vocabulary, already exists), and vertex declaration (kind/fold configuration, already exists). siftd's adapters are Sources that haven't been written as Sources yet \\\\u2014 each adapter's discover\\\\u2192parse pipeline is equivalent to a script that reads conversation files and emits structured records. The three-tier loading (built-in < entry point < drop-in) becomes: template ships default source scripts, user overrides with project-local scripts. The read_file/ingest_to_store API proposed for libs/store is unnecessary \\\\u2014 format-aware file reading is a script concern, not a library primitive. Bulk historical import is an edge case solved by a script, not a library. What remains from the store-operations-design plan (receive, compact, transport) is genuine new infrastructure \\\\u2014 moving stores between locations does not dissolve into existing primitives.\\\"}, \\\"design/actions-on-the-loop\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/actions-on-the-loop\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Actions with side effects (task send spawns a worktree, task merge runs git operations) are not special-cased command handlers \\\\u2014 they are facts on the loop. Emitting task.dispatch places the intent on the wire; something observes it and executes the side effect; the outcome emits as a further fact; the boundary folds the cascade. The CLI command and TUI keypress are different input surfaces for the same emission. This is not the mature future form \\\\u2014 it is the design. If we build it this way from the start, the system composes: any observer can react to any fact, boundaries track lifecycle across the full cascade, and the audit trail is complete. Custom domain logic that does not dissolve \\\\u2014 worktree management, subprocess spawning, git operations \\\\u2014 lives in the observer/tick handler that reacts to the intent fact, not in the CLI command that emits it.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-registration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-registration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Apps register three things: lenses (read fold state \\\\u2192 render at fidelity levels), feedback handlers (user input \\\\u2192 emit fact/tick), and action observers (react to intent facts with side effects). The harness makes all three available as both CLI commands and TUI keybindings at appropriate fidelity. There is no separate app scaffold per domain \\\\u2014 the directory structure, CLI dispatch, dev harness are identical. What differentiates siftd from strange-loops from hlab is: which vertex declaration (template), which lenses (Painted components), which feedback/action handlers (domain logic). The registration mechanism is the app's interface to the system.\\\"}, \\\"design/lens-modifiers\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lens-modifiers\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens rendering composes through modifiers, not separate lens implementations. Four modifier types identified from the painted-log-line-demo research: (1) Gutter \\\\u2014 colored left edge encoding one dimension (lifecycle stage, health, freshness). Follows Grafana/Datadog pattern, underused in terminals. (2) Attention \\\\u2014 dim low-information-gain records, highlight high. First-occurrence errors are high attention, 47th occurrence is noise. Decisions on new topics are high, routine ticks are low. This connects to the attention-filter design. (3) History arc \\\\u2014 show evolution over time (thread exploring\\\\u2192active\\\\u2192decided, experiment proposed\\\\u2192graduated). Records are trajectories, not points. (4) Density \\\\u2014 vertical space per record, controlled by Zoom enum. These compose freely: task board = record_timeline + gutter(lifecycle) + attention(staleness). Thread pipeline = record_timeline + history_arc + attention(readiness). Channel response = attention(high_only) + density(MINIMAL).\\\"}, \\\"design/rendering-semantics\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/rendering-semantics\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Six design principles from log line research ground the rendering vocabulary. (1) Color encodes exactly one dimension \\\\u2014 severity OR source, never both. (2) INFO is baseline, color marks deviation \\\\u2014 journalctl principle. (3) Fixed-width metadata columns + variable message = scannable \\\\u2014 Docker Compose pattern. (4) Severity gutter is underused in terminals \\\\u2014 Grafana/Datadog colored left edge, minimal footprint, instantly scannable. (5) Continuation indentation beats prefix repetition for multi-line \\\\u2014 lnav principle. (6) Width-aware rendering is a gap in terminal tools \\\\u2014 an opportunity for Painted to own. Additionally: the PayloadLens pattern (kind, payload, zoom) \\\\u2192 str|Block is the domain extension point. Default rendering handles unknown kinds via well-known key extraction. Domain lenses (loops_lens, siftd_lens) override with kind-specific formatting. Lenses compose with modifiers \\\\u2014 the lens provides content, the modifier provides visual treatment.\\\"}, \\\"design/composition-primitives\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/composition-primitives\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three composition primitives for rendering vertex data, each matching a different data shape. (1) record_timeline \\\\u2014 groups by date, temporal data. Natural for session logs, task activity, change history. Already built in painted-log-line-demo. (2) record_map \\\\u2014 groups by key hierarchy (namespace tree), topological data. Natural for decision landscapes (testing/*, architecture/*), tag views, observer groupings. Zoom: MINIMAL = group names + counts, SUMMARY = group + latest record, DETAILED = all records within groups. Being designed now. (3) record_line \\\\u2014 the atomic unit. Single timestamped record at a zoom level. All composition primitives delegate to record_line for individual records. PayloadLens and modifiers apply at record_line level and propagate through any composition primitive. A fourth primitive \\\\u2014 spatial/graph/canvas \\\\u2014 is under research for relationship data (fact dependency chains, store topology, cross-project impact).\\\"}, \\\"design/canvas-primitive\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/canvas-primitive\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The canvas() composition primitive bridges Painted's static lens path to 2D positioning. Painted already has Buffer-level absolute positioning (Block.paint(buf, x, y)) but only in interactive Surface mode. canvas(width, height, placements) uses Buffer internally to compose Placement(x, y, block) entries, then extracts an immutable Block. No new rendering path \\\\u2014 just a new composition function. draw_edge(buf, path, style) adds box-drawing polylines with Manhattan routing. Layout algorithms live in the lens, not in Painted \\\\u2014 the library provides the rendering primitive, domain-specific layout stays in domain code. This enables three new lens types: DAG (directed flow), Canvas (2D positioned nodes with edges), and Graph (relationship visualization). All compose with existing modifiers (gutter, attention) and respect zoom levels.\\\"}, \\\"design/dag-lens-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dag-lens-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Prototype DAG lens before canvas or graph lens. Four reasons: (1) Tasks already have explicit dependency edges (blocks/blocked_by) \\\\u2014 no graph inference needed. (2) DAGs have natural top-to-bottom flow \\\\u2014 simplest layout algorithm (topological sort + git-style column assignment). (3) Git-style column rendering needs zero new Painted primitives \\\\u2014 join_vertical of row-blocks, same as tree_lens. (4) Immediate use case in strange-loops task visualization. Phase sequence: DAG lens (git-style columns, no new primitives) \\\\u2192 canvas() primitive \\\\u2192 Canvas lens (grid layout, Manhattan routing, store topology) \\\\u2192 Graph lens (Sugiyama layout, fact dependency chains, cross-vertex references). Each phase builds on the prior.\\\"}, \\\"design/rendering-vocabulary-complete\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/rendering-vocabulary-complete\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The full rendering vocabulary for the personal intelligence system is now designed. Four composition primitives: record_line (atomic timestamped record), record_timeline (temporal grouping by date), record_map (topological grouping by key hierarchy), and canvas/DAG/graph (spatial \\\\u2014 positioned nodes with edges). Two modifier types compose with all primitives: GutterFn maps (kind, payload) to (char, style) for colored left edge, AttentionFn maps (kind, payload) to float 0-1 for information-gain dimming/highlighting. PayloadLens maps (kind, payload, zoom) to str|Block for domain-specific content rendering. The universal formula: a view is record_{timeline,map,canvas} + PayloadLens + GutterFn? + AttentionFn?. Everything else is a parameter on one of these. Four GutterFn implementations (lifecycle, freshness, pass_fail, observer). Four AttentionFn implementations (staleness, novelty, blocked, relevance). Demo code proves all combinations across three scenarios (task board, decision map, siftd views).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-virtualization\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-virtualization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combinatorial vertices virtualize via SQLite ATTACH DATABASE at read time \\\\u2014 UNION ALL facts across stores, replay through declared folds. No materialization, no copied data, always fresh. Materialization remains available via existing merge_store as explicit user choice.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combinatorial vertices use a 'combine' block in vertex KDL \\\\u2014 mutually exclusive with 'store'. References other vertices by name (not store paths). No store, no discover, no sources. CombineEntry AST node. Temporary vertices constructed in memory via --combine CLI flag.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-phases\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-phases\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Phase 1: AST CombineEntry + combine parsing + validation + _combined_read in vertex_reader (branch on ast.combine). Phase 2: CLI --combine flag for temporary vertices + loops init --combine for persistent. Phase 3: provenance tagging (deferred).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/arch-test-rules-5-7\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/arch-test-rules-5-7\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three new AST-enforced rules in test_architecture.py: (5) frozen dataclasses in all libs \\\\u2014 10 exceptions whitelisted, 7 marked TODO-freeze; (6) atoms stdlib-only \\\\u2014 zero external runtime deps; (7) sqlite3 confined to engine and store. Non-AST-enforceable invariants documented: display_width vs len (needs type info), parameterized SQL (already clean), bare except (too rare).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/frozen-dataclass-todos\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/frozen-dataclass-todos\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Seven dataclasses identified for future freeze: Source (atoms), CompiledVertex (engine), Tap (engine), Shape (lang), Location (lang), CellWrite (painted), CliRunner (painted). Three legitimately mutable: ValidationContext (error accumulator), Loop (timing state), FrameRecord (if exists in painted timer).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/sources-sequential\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/sources-sequential\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Sources block takes an execution mode. 'sources sequential' runs sources in declaration order with exit-on-failure gating (non-zero exit code stops subsequent sources). Bare sources at vertex level remain concurrent (today's default). The general form is: sources block takes a mode keyword \\\\u2014 sequential today, concurrent implicit default. DAG or other patterns become additional modes, not different mechanisms. This dissolves health.py's run_checks() into a vertex declaration \\\\u2014 the imperative Python code that runs subprocesses sequentially and gates on failure becomes a property of the source execution model. The lens and view (health_lens, health_view, gutter_pass_fail) survive as rendering concerns. check.vertex replaces the ./dev check shell scripts with a vertex declaration: sources sequential { source 'ruff...' { kind lint.result } source 'pytest...' { kind test.result } } with folds collecting latest per step.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-directory\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-directory\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'.loops/' is the project-local home for vertices and data. Vertices are project identity (checked in), data is gitignored by *.db pattern. loops init writes to .loops/, vertex discovery checks .loops/ first with cwd fallback.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-over-symlinks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-over-symlinks\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'combine' block with absolute paths to vertex files replaces discover+symlink pattern for data aggregation. combine is the data path (reads through to referenced stores), discover stays structural/navigational.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/discover-vs-combine\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/discover-vs-combine\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"discover and combine serve different purposes and don't overlap. discover is structural/navigational \\\\u2014 finding what exists. combine is data \\\\u2014 reading through to referenced stores via ATTACH + UNION ALL.\\\"}, \\\"design/incremental-init\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/incremental-init\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'loops init' is incremental and composable. 'loops init project' creates a project vertex, 'loops init check' adds a check vertex later. Each init is self-contained \\\\u2014 not monolithic templates or cookiecutter scaffolding.\\\"}, \\\"design/instances-are-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/instances-are-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex instances ARE the templates \\\\u2014 dissolved. No separate template layer. dev/ namespace at config level holds reference vertices, but they're just instances that happen to be reusable. Template dissolution: if the instance is the template, the template concept disappears.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-store-schema\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-store-schema\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SqliteStore (engine) now uses ULID primary keys matching libs/store schema. Single canonical schema: id TEXT PK DEFAULT (ulid()), json_valid CHECK on payload. Existing rowid-based stores migrated manually. No backwards-compat shim \\\\u2014 ULID is the only path forward.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-ls-generalization\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-ls-generalization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ls works at every level: root shows vertices, vertex shows contents. Zoom progression for fidelity.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-structural-ops\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-structural-ops\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ls/add/rm are structural operations uniform across levels. Root: vertices. Vertex: contents/population.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-observe-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-observe-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Formalize read processes first (ls), then let write operations (add/rm) emerge from observed patterns.\\\"}, \\\"identity/soul-as-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/soul-as-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SOUL is a manual tick on a dedicated loop. Identity facts (decisions, threads, observations) accumulate via declared folds. When the observer decides identity has shifted, they call tick(). The tick payload IS the current identity state. Contributing facts available at full fidelity in the same store. soul.snapshot facts assembled from other loops' fold states feed the soul loop.\\\"}, \\\"identity/intention-loop\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/intention-loop\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Intentions are facts that survive context rotation. Fold by trigger \\\\u2014 latest per trigger key. One-shot vs recurring is the observer's interpretation, not the fold's concern. Emit with status=pending to create, re-emit with status=done to resolve. On Wake rules check for pending intentions.\\\"}, \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant deferred until intention authorization is a real need. Implicit trust boundaries in daemon code are fine while there's a single observer per vertex. Grant becomes necessary when sessions need explicit authorization to act on pending intentions \\\\u2014 the difference between a rule you follow and a capability you possess.\\\"}, \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity state (soul tick) stays internal to the observer's vertex. Observations propagate outward as facts on other vertices with observer attribution. The strange loop closes through behavior: identity \\\\u2192 lenses \\\\u2192 observations \\\\u2192 facts on other vertices \\\\u2192 pollers bring back responses \\\\u2192 new identity facts. Coupling is through the observer, not through the data.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wrapup skills rewritten to be vertex-native. Four layers for pickup (identity, context, peers, workspace), five for wrapup (capture, handoff, status, reflect, workspace). Skills version-controlled in loops repo with symlinks to global config. Replaces probe-based pickup and strange-loops CLI wrapup.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity store is sense of self, not operational metrics. Insights, connections, surprises, open questions about perspective. Distinct from meta (operational patterns) and project (architecture). Guard against forcing observations every session. Capability awareness belongs in CLAUDE.md; capability insights that persist across tool changes belong in identity.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Skills that are part of the loops system (pickup, wrapup) are version-controlled in the loops repo at .claude/skills/ and symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\\\"}, \\\"design/init-as-context\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/init-as-context\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Init doesn't just create a store \\\\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\\\\\"by\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" } } \\\\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\\\u2014 identity is already loaded.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the system should help. Ties into combine auto-inherit pattern: push association down, don't require manual discipline at emit time.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"No way to inspect a single fact or tick at full depth. Stream truncates, fold collapses. Need a detail view on individual records \\\\u2014 same primitive for facts and ticks. loops show or similar.\\\"}, \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level configuration, not app-level. The app{} block concept dissolves \\\\u2014 lenses travel with vertices via lens{} in .vertex KDL, not nested under an app container. Apps own domain verbs, not lenses.\\\"}, \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: still valid for installed-package lens references but no current use case. Will emerge naturally when apps need to expose lenses from their packages.\\\"}, \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Each vertex declares its own lens. No inheritance across combine boundaries. An aggregation vertex has its own rendering needs distinct from its children. If you want a child's lens, declare it explicitly.\\\"}, \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Emit UX will be rethought as part of write-vertex operation.\\\"}, \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into convention. Source lifecycle kinds get a reserved prefix (e.g. _source.message.complete) to avoid matching data fold queries. Same pattern as _boundary on tick payloads.\\\"}, \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into vertex-name-resolution-consistency. The combine-emit problem is a resolution consistency problem \\\\u2014 uniform resolution covers both.\\\"}, \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Both phases complete. Phase 1: vertex-level scope declaration (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL). Identity is scoped, project/comms are unscoped. Phase 2: Source._extract_metadata reads _observer/_origin from ndjson payloads, overriding .loop defaults. Discord-source emits _observer=author, _origin=discord. Observer now consistently means identity. Origin carries source attribution. New discord polls will have correct observer \\\\u2014 existing data retains observer=discord.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three commands, three resolution behaviors. fold/stream resolve vertex names. run expects file paths. emit resolves but writes to wrong store through combine. Resolution should be uniform \\\\u2014 resolve_vertex works everywhere, or the gaps are explicit.\\\"}, \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Run loop model changes under two-operation CLI.\\\"}, \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Check cursors are part of old CLI shape; read-vertex model replaces them.\\\"}, \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream rendering will be rethought as part of read-vertex lenses.\\\"}, \\\"cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Refined to read/emit/init. 'run' dissolves \\\\u2014 source execution is fact generation via emit, not a separate operation. 'write' dissolves \\\\u2014 emit was already the right verb. Four things to learn became three: read (fold default, filters compose), emit (facts in, from user or source), init (create namespace). Remaining question: source execution model (see source-execution-model thread).\\\"}, \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The root vertex at ~/.config/loops/.vertex needs restructuring. Currently a thin aggregator with combine. Needs to become the actual routing root where children (project, identity, comms, reading, etc.) nest and ticks cascade. Design questions: which vertices are children vs peers? Does identity scope differently in the tree? How does observer-scoping interact with tree position? The root vertex read IS the system overview \\\\u2014 its default lens shows children and their state.\\\"}, \\\"read-operation-contract\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"read-operation-contract\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"What does 'read vertex' return mechanically? The read operation needs to serve multiple consumers via lenses: prompt lens (agent system prompt), default lens (terminal fold state), JSON (hooks). It must provide fold state + tick history + children. Does the read load the full subtree? How deep? Does --ticks change the data fetched or just the lens? Does search (positional query arg) go through the same read path? The contract between read and lens determines the implementation.\\\"}, \\\"source-execution-model\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source-execution-model\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved. Source execution dissolves to three concerns: Source (pure adapter), Cadence (store predicate), Executor (cadence-gated runner). Five decisions emitted: source-execution-model, cli-verb-first, cadence-as-store-predicate, read-is-pure, sync-locus-of-control. Investigation by 5-agent team: tracer (lifecycle), explorer (scheduling survey), architect (design v3), muser (dissolution challenges), siftd (historical context). Prior art: CADENCE.md (2026-01-31) proposed Source/Cadence split conceptually \\\\u2014 never implemented. This session designs the one-shot-compatible version.\\\"}}}, \\\"change\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session continuity + strange-loops scaffold \\\\u2014 loops session start/end/status/log, query-time fold, LOOPS_OBSERVER env var. strange-loops scaffolded.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Population as facts \\\\u2014 add/rm emit pop.add/pop.rm facts, .list materialized as projection, ls reads fold state.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session dissolution + cells\\\\u2192painted + run_cli harness \\\\u2014 dissolved session subcommand, status/log promoted to top-level, migrated cells\\\\u2192painted. 147 loops + 1169 painted tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Full Painted rendering + golden tests + store targeting \\\\u2014 all 9 display commands through run_cli, 45 golden snapshot tests, store targeting via vertex name resolution. 191 tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"engine CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 4 levels: Run vertex program, Fold and fire, Persist, Gate access. Semantic examples (decisions/threads). Deep-dive docs as reference layer.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"lang CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 3 levels: Parse a file, Understand AST, Manage populations. Connects DSL types to atoms/engine counterparts.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"store CLAUDE.md rewrite \\\\u2014 2 levels: Slice/merge, Schema. Clarifies relationship to engine SqliteStore.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chain headers and cross-references added to all 5 lib CLAUDE.md files. atoms retrofitted with oblique references to engine at Levels 0, 1, 3.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Dissolved discord, telegram, reader apps. Moved .loop/.vertex files to experiments/. Removed from workspace members. Updated root CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for all 3 apps: loops (new, 3 levels), hlab (rewrite 199\\\\u2192118 lines, 3 levels), strange-loops (rewrite 254\\\\u2192127 lines, 3 levels). All with chain headers.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Record line rendering fixes: gutter continuity with weight stepping, shallow 2-char indent replacing deep column alignment, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output eliminating terminal wrapping gaps, health_lens fixed to respect lens contract\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertex template includes default loops (decision, thread, change, task). _find_source_vertex priority: aggregation loops block > sibling instance > direct config instance. Updated project + meta aggregation vertices on disk.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuild: temporal modes + generic rendering\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"commands/observer.py,lenses/fold.py,lenses/stream.py,main.py,fixtures.py,test_session.py,test_status.py,test_log.py,test_cli_docs.py,test_cli.py\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval) and commands/identity.py (observer resolution). Dissolved _emit_fact, inlined _format_date into lenses. pop.py now uses resolve_observer() for full resolution chain. 394 tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design session\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into fetch.py + identity.py. Wired resolve_observer through pop.py. Created project .vertex with loops-claude as open observer. Designed FoldState typed contract (atoms-the-package), custom lens system (.vertex declaration + .loops/lenses/ + --lens flag), attention trifecta (what/when/how-much as lens concerns). Peer exchange with Alcove confirmed architecture. Two visions emitted to meta (attention-infrastructure, observer-constellation).\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldItem/FoldSection/FoldState in atoms. observer.py dissolved into commands/fetch.py + commands/identity.py. fetch_fold returns FoldState, fold_view consumes typed attributes. 235 loops + 322 atoms tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Fact-by-id: surface ULID identifiers + observer elevation\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"store_reader.py,vertex_reader.py,fetch.py,stream.py,main.py,__init__.py,test_store_reader.py,test_vertex_reader.py,~/.config/loops/.vertex\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Hook lifecycle + lens redistribution + CLAUDE.md\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\".claude/settings.json,~/.config/loops/lenses/comms.py,~/.config/loops/lenses/state.py,~/.config/loops/CLAUDE.md,apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/CLAUDE.md\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta + slashed emit + hooks cleanup\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping as vertex concern (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL), session tick since fix (replay period bridging), Source _extract_metadata for ndjson, prompt lens delegation rendering, SessionEnd mechanical delta log.\\\"}]}, \\\"task\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit routes through vertex runtime via load_vertex_program + vertex.receive. Dissolution \\\\u2014 removed the bypass, didn't build new machinery.\\\"}, \\\"daemon-local-orchestration\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"daemon-local-orchestration\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 no persistent runtime needed. Vertex is reactive. Scheduling is external (cron/systemd). One-shot CLI is the runtime.\\\"}, \\\"foldstate-audit-findings\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"foldstate-audit-findings\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: vertex_fold addresses the core finding (typed contract wired end-to-end). FoldItem.origin populated since prior session. Remaining gaps (no reference counting, no fold caching, no custom lens loading) are tracked as separate threads.\\\"}, \\\"identity-observer-filtering\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"identity-observer-filtering\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer-scoped reads wired end-to-end. --observer general flag at dispatch, default-to-self, resolved-status filtering in prompt lens. Help bug fixed \\\\u2014 subcommand -h no longer masked by top-level intercept.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Shipped in 0e1ddc9. Union semantics, conflict detection, aggregation loops{} is overrides only.\\\"}, \\\"session-close\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-close\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved: session is a kind, close is the handoff, pickup reads one fold.\\\"}, \\\"thread-auto-tagging\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-tagging\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD env var. 5 lines in cmd_emit, same pattern as LOOPS_OBSERVER.\\\"}, \\\"pickup-filtering\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"pickup-filtering\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved: root .vertex fold with prompt lens handles identity + session + tasks in one read.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into vertex-lens-infrastructure. LensDecl AST, lens resolver with 4-tier resolution and file search, call_lens with optional context kwargs (vertex_name). identity.vertex declares prompt lens.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"after\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into kind/key syntax on --kind flag. --kind thread/fold-state-types filters fold to single item, stream to matching facts. No new verbs \\\\u2014 / is the drill-down operator.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"later\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cache fold computation until new facts arrive. Alcove sees 3-5s overhead per dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Implemented: LensDecl in AST, lens{} block in KDL, lens_resolver.py with file search (vertex-local > project-local > user-global > built-in), 4-tier CLI resolution, call_lens with vertex_name context. 22 new tests.\\\"}, \\\"fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-by-id\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ULID IDs surfaced through entire read path. StoreReader.fact_by_id with prefix matching, vertex_fact_by_id across combined stores, --id flag on stream command. Progressive disclosure in stream lens. Primitive reference for future tick traversal.\\\"}, \\\"meta-hooks-bootstrap\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"meta-hooks-bootstrap\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Identity consolidated, pickup removed, comms delta wired. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"text-truncation-plain-vv\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"text-truncation-plain-vv\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Truncation behavior follows from new read-vertex rendering.\\\"}, \\\"session-tick-retrospective\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-tick-retrospective\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Completed. Fixed since bug, verified tick structure, dissolved handoff into tick, added mechanical delta to SessionEnd hook.\\\"}, \\\"docs-vertex-migration\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"docs-vertex-migration\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Continue migrating CLAUDE.md content to the docs vertex. Atoms proven \\\\u2014 52 facts, 4 zoom levels, kind filtering, guide payload structure works. Remaining libs: engine (4 levels), lang (3 levels), store (3 levels), painted consumer (5 levels), painted contributor (4 levels). Remaining apps: loops (4 levels), hlab (4 levels), strange-loops (4 levels), siftd (4 levels). Each migration is independent. Also need: prompt lens variant for system prompt injection, fix newline rendering in code/api payload fields.\\\"}, \\\"discord-source-poll-kind\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"discord-source-poll-kind\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Discord source script emits poll-status results as kind=message. Should be a different kind (e.g., 'poll' or 'source-status') so they don't pollute the message fold. Fix in ~/.config/loops/discord/discord-source. Comms lens has a workaround but the source is the right fix point.\\\"}, \\\"tick-surfacing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-surfacing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 ticks are visible through read-vertex; no separate surfacing command needed.\\\"}, \\\"tick-to-fact-flow\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-to-fact-flow\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\\\u2014 tick-to-fact cascading is already in the engine; read-vertex exposes it without dedicated plumbing.\\\"}, \\\"dissolve-messaging-vertex\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"dissolve-messaging-vertex\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Remove config/messaging/messaging.vertex. Telegram source moves to comms/telegram/ using same pattern as comms/discord/. Discord portion is already covered by comms/discord/.\\\"}, \\\"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Remove config/discord/discord.vertex \\\\u2014 duplicate of config/comms/discord/discord.vertex. The comms/ path is canonical.\\\"}, \\\"refactor-meta-combine\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"refactor-meta-combine\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"config/meta/meta.vertex currently combines meta-discussion + discord + identity. Should be a pure domain aggregation \\\\u2014 drop discord and identity from the combine. Those belong in the launch fold, not in the domain vertex.\\\"}, \\\"domain-vertex-template\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"domain-vertex-template\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Define the universal domain shape (decisions/threads/tasks/sessions/changes) as the base template for loops init. Local .vertex files extend with domain-specific kinds. Rename 'project' concept to 'domain' in templates and docs.\\\"}, \\\"session-launch-script\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-launch-script\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"next\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Write the two-line launch script: emit session fact with delegation, exec claude with LOOPS_OBSERVER. This is the dogfooding entry point \\\\u2014 use it to start sessions instead of raw 'LOOPS_OBSERVER=x claude'.\\\"}, \\\"identity/observer-namespacing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"identity/observer-namespacing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer namespacing (kyle/meta-claude) introduced in launch script but never landed in read path, .vertex declarations, or emit validation. Currently reverted to bare names. When namespace concept is needed (multi-user, delegation), it must land in three places: .vertex observer declarations, validate_emit() matching, and vertex_reader.py filter (4 sites of exact equality). Provenance preserved via session fact payload (principal=kyle, agent=meta-claude).\\\"}}}, \\\"session\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"loops-claude\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"loops-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"kyle\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kyle\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-auto-tagging dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD (5 lines). Staleness audit closed 4 threads (fold-state-types, observer-scoped-handoff, gist-lens-generics, observer-cascade). Prompt lens session fix for Alcove. Designed vertex lens infrastructure with Alcove input \\\\u2014 architecture decision emitted, 3 deferred threads tagged, task created. Next: implement vertex-lens-infrastructure (LensDecl AST + loader + resolver + CLI wiring).\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:thread-auto-tagging\\\", \\\"thread:fold-state-types\\\", \\\"thread:observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"thread:gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"thread:observer-cascade\\\", \\\"thread:fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"task:custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"task:fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"task:fold-materialization\\\", \\\"decision:design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"thread:app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"thread:module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"thread:combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"task:vertex-lens-infrastructure\\\"]}, \\\"meta-claude\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"meta-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"test-boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"test-boundary\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"test-vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"test-vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"e2e-test\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"e2e-test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}, \\\"replay-test\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"replay-test\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}}}, \\\"log\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-28\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Loops model crystallized + persistence exploration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Explored adding persistence to experiments. The exploration dissolved multiple\\\\nconcepts back into existing atoms:\\\\n\\\\n| Concept | Dissolved into | Why |\\\\n|---------|---------------|-----|\\\\n| Sink | Fold state | Loops have no terminals |\\\\n| Store | Durable fold | Storage is a property, not a type |\\\\n| Witness | Peer + Vertex | Just a peer whose job is to observe and emit |\\\\n| Tap | Vertex | Emission from storage is vertex behavior |\\\\n| Memory | Boundary-less fold | Silent accumulation is a fold that never ticks |\\\\n\\\\n**Key insight:** The atoms are complete. New requirements don't require new\\\\nprimitives \\\\u2014 they're configurations of existing ones.\\\\n\\\\nCreated `LOOPS.md` as the fundamental model document. Four satellite docs\\\\nadded: `docs/VERTEX.md`, `docs/TEMPORAL.md`, `docs/PERSISTENCE.md`, `docs/PEERS.md`.\\\\nEach unpacks one aspect and references back to LOOPS.md.\\\\n\\\\nFixed Enter key bug in keyboard.py (handle LF 0x0A same as CR 0x0D).\\\\n\\\\nOpen naming tensions noted but deferred:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Peer\\\\\\\" implies equality but delegation is hierarchical\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Tick\\\\\\\" implies clock time but boundaries are semantic\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-28\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Peer-driven boundaries + None=unrestricted + lens distinction\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"`review.py`: two loops through one vertex. Health ticks at timer cadence\\\\n(passive). Review ticks when peer acks all containers (active \\\\u2014 composition\\\\nlayer sends `review.complete` sentinel).\\\\n\\\\n**Peer model change**: `horizon` and `potential` default to `None` (unrestricted)\\\\ninstead of `frozenset()` (empty). Constraints emerge through `delegate()`, not\\\\nupfront enumeration.\\\\n\\\\n**Debug is a lens, not a horizon.** The None model exposed a category error:\\\\n\\\\\\\"debug\\\\\\\" was a horizon string alongside container names, but it's a rendering\\\\nmode, not a data domain. Debug panel is now a lens toggle available to any peer.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Boundary triggering implemented\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Implemented boundary triggering on Vertex. `Projection.reset()` added.\\\\n`register()` gains `boundary: str | None` and `reset: bool`. `receive()`\\\\nreturns `Tick | None`. Fold-before-boundary, optional reset, boundary kind\\\\nuniqueness enforced.\\\\n\\\\nVertex is sync by design \\\\u2014 async bridge lives at composition point.\\\\n122 ticks tests.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Feedback loop closed, experiment log established\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"`experiments/observe.py`: first experiment that closes the feedback loop.\\\\nUser interactions (j/k/enter) are Facts through the same `vertex.receive()`\\\\nas external observations.\\\\n\\\\nEmergent insights captured in `experiments/LOG.md`: debug as horizon (not\\\\ninfrastructure), meta-actions outside the loop, thin composition layer.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Genesis document + strata semantic tagging\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Reconstructed project origin story via strata. Synthesized into `docs/GENESIS.md`.\\\\nApplied semantic tags to 58 conversations across workspaces.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tick-to-Fact dissolved, fleet experiment\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Built `experiments/fleet.py`: three-level vertex hierarchy (4 VMs \\\\u2192 2 regions\\\\n\\\\u2192 global). Ticks are a level above Facts \\\\u2014 temporal groupings, not peers.\\\\nThe question dissolved. Same primitive at every level.\\\\n\\\\nTick gained `origin` field. Vertex gained `name` parameter.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-27\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Architecture crystallization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replaced Stream concept with Vertex (intersection of loops). Explored and\\\\nrejected Tick-into-Fact collapse. Tick gained `name` field. Full narrative\\\\nin `ARCHITECTURE-JOURNEY.md`.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-26\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Semantic journey\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Monorepo naming exploration (loops vs volta vs prism). Pivot concept\\\\ncrystallized (four universal atoms + cell as first surface). Peer refactored\\\\nto horizon + potential.\\\"}, {\\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-26\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Structure alignment\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Project structure normalized across all five libs. Per-lib CLAUDE.md and\\\\nHANDOFF.md added. Six parallel fixes merged.\\\"}, {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: observer app rebuild. Implemented the unified conceptual model from last session's 4-agent design (mapper, muser, miner, explorer). Three temporal modes (fold/stream/emit) replace the old if-elif dispatch. Generic declaration-driven rendering: key_field from FoldBy IS the label, fold_type IS the rendering strategy. No per-kind code in fetch or lens layers. Bare vertex defaults to fold. Legacy aliases preserved. The design came from team analysis: muser proposed temporal modes orthogonal to spatial fidelity, mapper audited every command, miner provided engine/painted API data, and the whole chain collapsed status/log/search into fold/stream. Next: developer app split, observer-scoped pickup, gist lens generics, dispatch from vertex capabilities.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: fact-by-id + fold-state-types + observer-cascade. Three core threads progressed. fact-by-id: surfaced ULID IDs through all read paths, --id flag on stream, progressive disclosure in both lenses. fold-state-types: FoldItem carries fact ID, traversal loop closed (fold \\\\u2192 ID \\\\u2192 stream --id). observer-cascade: aggregation vertices inherit source observers via combine chain, dissolves the elevation workaround. session-as-tick deferred \\\\u2014 prerequisites in place, needs engine-native boundary design. Observer elevation bug found and fixed along the way. Retrospective produced 5 identity observations including task-selection-as-identity.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session: hook lifecycle + lens redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Wired SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit/SessionEnd hooks for observer-generic session lifecycle. Built comms lens (user-global) for messaging vertices. Moved state lens from built-in to user-global. Established lens tier pattern: built-in = core primitives, user-global = domain rendering. CLAUDE.md at lenses/ (repo) and ~/.config/loops/ (config). custom-lens-infrastructure thread resolved. Next: recency-aware-lens for attention-weighted startup fold, comms vertex when Discord bridge reactivates.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta. Merged three identity stores into config-level single store (all observers, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER). Dissolved pickup.zsh \\\\u2014 hooks handle all bootstrap. Slashed vertex emit (comms/native) resolves sub-vertices before template qualification. Comms lens is delta-aware: check facts as cursors, shows new-since-last-check, suppresses when quiet. Hooks dropped uv run for bare loops. Sent infrastructure summary to Alcove via Discord. Meta bootstrap verified. Next: watch Alcove first hook-based session, sessions-as-ticks.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: identity consolidation + pickup dissolution + comms delta + payload-conditional boundaries. Five commits: identity merge (3 stores \\\\u2192 1), pickup.zsh dissolved (hooks-only bootstrap), slashed vertex emit (comms/native), comms delta (check facts as cursors), payload-conditional boundaries (boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\"). Session close now produces a tick carrying folded state. 1176 tests pass. Meta bootstrap verified. Message sent to Alcove. Push pending (network timeout).\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: observer scoping + session tick retrospective + delegation. Three design threads resolved (session-as-tick, observer-vs-source-attribution, plus combine-emit-routing and kind-prefix-leak dissolved). Vertex scope declaration landed \\\\u2014 identity is observer-scoped, project/comms unscoped. Session tick since field fixed \\\\u2014 period bridging works across CLI one-shot invocations. Source metadata extraction enables per-record observer/origin in ndjson. Prompt lens renders delegated threads separately. Remaining design: vertex-name-resolution-consistency, check-cursor-mechanism, recency-aware-lens. Next priority: resolution consistency (three commands, three strategies).\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 18 facts. 12 thread, 3 decision, 1 change, 1 log, 1 task.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 21 facts. 12 thread, 5 decision, 4 task.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 53 facts. 32 thread, 12 decision, 5 task, 3 log, 1 change.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 17 facts. 9 thread, 6 decision, 1 handoff, 1 log.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Session: 10 facts. 5 decision, 3 observation, 1 handoff, 1 thread.\\\"}]}, \\\"_boundary\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"loops-claude\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\"}}\",\"prev_hash\":null,\"signature\":null,\"since\":1772861732.929476,\"tick_id\":\"01kk3dn061tmccwn55mfxvbh05\",\"window_hash\":null,\"window_start\":null}"}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:2076:{"t":"fact","id":"01KK3DQQX5JPQD7P17KFENZ123","kind":"tick.project","ts":1772862824.357911,"observer":"project","origin":"project","payload":"{\"fact_cursor\":null,\"name\":\"project\",\"payload\":\"{\\\"decision\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"architecture/root-claude-md\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/root-claude-md\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Root CLAUDE.md is monorepo orientation only: pointer to LOOPS.md, build commands, structure map, discovery path to lib/app CLAUDE.md files, and project store query instructions. Model details, data flow, lib-specific patterns all pushed down to lib-level CLAUDE.md. Validates claude-md-levels and claude-md-antipatterns decisions from meta.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/project-vertex\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/project-vertex\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Renamed session.vertex to project.vertex. Project vertex holds durable project-specific decisions, threads, tasks. Same shape as meta vertex but scoped to this repo. Symlinked at ~/.config/loops/project for global access. Meta stays cross-cutting; project stays repo-specific.\\\"}, \\\"meta/current-activity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"meta/current-activity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md system for the loops monorepo. Applying the painted library pattern (levels with escalation triggers, don't-reach-for-yet barriers) to replace the God CLAUDE.md antipattern. Walking through each level top-down with the user, aligning on content at each step, emitting decisions to project and meta stores as we go. Simultaneously establishing the project vertex as the loops-specific knowledge store alongside the cross-cutting meta store.\\\"}, \\\"atoms/progressive-claude-md\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"atoms/progressive-claude-md\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for libs/atoms. Four levels: Observe (Fact), Accumulate (Spec+Fold+Boundary), Shape input (Parse vocabulary), Ingest (Source+Runner). Each level has trigger conditions and dont-reach-for-yet barriers. Replaces the 20-line README stub. Deep dive docs (VERTEX.md, TEMPORAL.md) referenced from engine CLAUDE.md, not atoms \\\\u2014 they're engine-level concepts.\\\"}, \\\"meta/session-summary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"meta/session-summary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md session: rewrote root CLAUDE.md (monorepo orientation only), created libs/atoms/CLAUDE.md (4 levels: Observe, Accumulate, Shape, Ingest with semantic-first examples), established project.vertex as durable project store, merged vertex-template-system (slashed names, init with config registration, aggregation vertices). Emitted 5 decisions to meta store (progressive-vertex-chain, project-vertex-pattern, distributed-store-default, vertex-templates, domain-vs-knowledge-vertices). Next: engine CLAUDE.md, then lang, painted alignment, store.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-dependency-graph\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-dependency-graph\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"lang\\\\u2192ckdl (pure grammar), engine\\\\u2192atoms+lang (runtime+compiler), apps\\\\u2192engine+painted (CLI). Key: lang is portable (only ckdl dep), compiler backend lives in engine where target types are defined.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/chain-headers\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/chain-headers\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"Every lib CLAUDE.md gets a 'you are here' chain showing what's below and above. Bidirectional references \\\\u2014 agents can enter anywhere and orient.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"All five libs (atoms, engine, lang, store, painted) have progressive CLAUDE.md with levels, triggers, barriers, and chain headers. Lib layer done.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/dissolved-apps\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/dissolved-apps\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"discord, telegram, reader dissolved into the overall loops system. DSL files preserved in experiments/. Workspace reduced to 3 apps: loops, hlab, strange-loops.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"All 3 active apps have progressive CLAUDE.md. Combined with libs, every directory in the monorepo now has the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/record-line-primitives\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/record-line-primitives\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"record_line and record_line_composed are production rendering primitives in painted. Gutter continuity (stepping weight), shallow 2-char indent, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output. health_lens returns summary string, record_line handles continuation lines.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/lens-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/lens-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"PayloadLens returns the summary (str or styled Block). record_line owns continuation lines \\\\u2014 DETAILED shows well-known secondary fields, FULL shows all fields. Lenses must not embed multiline content; record_line handles that.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/gutter-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/gutter-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Gutter is a continuous vertical rail. GutterFn returns primary weight. Stepping map derives continuation weight: full block to half, half to thin, thin stays thin. Color stays same, weight steps down. Rail never breaks.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/help-min-zoom\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/help-min-zoom\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace help secondary: bool with min_zoom: Zoom. Each HelpGroup declares when it appears via min_zoom, rendering follows effective-zoom pattern (eff < 0 hidden, 0 compact, 1 expanded, >= 2 expanded+detail). Dissolves hardcoded Interaction rules section.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/help-unification\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/help-unification\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Unify help rendering: AppRunner intercepts -h at subcommand level, not just top level. Action commands describe args via help_args on AppCommand. Handlers never see -h. Chosen over CliRunner wrapper approach \\\\u2014 help is an AppRunner concern, execution is a handler concern.\\\"}, \\\"init/aggregation-loops-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"init/aggregation-loops-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices declare loops as canonical schema. New instances derive base loops from aggregation root, not first sibling. _extract_loops_text brace-matches the block; _find_source_vertex prefers it over instance fallback.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-developer-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-developer-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The CLI has two loops: Observer loop (vertex-first, one verb, temporal modes) and Developer loop (file-first, multiple verbs, DSL tools). These are different projections on different concerns \\\\u2192 different apps. Observer app: loops <vertex> [mode] [fidelity]. Developer app: separate binary (validate, compile, run, test). No shared dispatch logic.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/emit-only-verb\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/emit-only-verb\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"emit is the only verb in the observer app. Everything else is a temporal mode selector (fold/stream/declaration) or a filter (search). status/log/store were always lenses pretending to be operations. start dissolves \\\\u2014 run with rounds=1 covers the same behavior.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/fetch-dissolves\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/fetch-dissolves\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"fetch functions in commands/ dissolve into engine fold replay. The fold declaration IS the fetch instruction. decision { fold { items 'by' 'topic' } } tells the runtime to group decisions by topic. fetch_status manually reimplements what Spec.apply already does. Projection = vertex capabilities + fold state (runtime-computed). Lens = fidelity selection + rendering. No intermediate fetch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/temporal-modes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/temporal-modes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"status/log/store are temporal modes, not operations. Fold = post-boundary (what is now). Stream = pre-boundary (what happened). Declaration = above boundary (what can happen). Different use cases: fold to orient, stream to investigate, declaration to audit. Default: fold at ORIENTATION, annotated with stream recency.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dispatch derives from structural capabilities, not from fold declarations. The loops block shapes what existing commands render (lens configuration). Structural features (store, sources, discover, combine) determine what operations exist. A vertex with store gets fold/stream/declaration modes. Sources add run. Discover adds aggregation traversal. The vertex file is the capability manifest.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-placement\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-placement\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant sits between capabilities and projection in the chain: Declaration \\\\u2192 Capabilities \\\\u2192 [Grant constrains] \\\\u2192 Projection \\\\u2192 Lens \\\\u2192 Perspective. Horizon constrains projection (filters which kinds reach the lens). Potential constrains the verb (limits which kinds emit accepts). When Grant goes live, no new commands needed \\\\u2014 same vertex, same lens, different perspectives.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuilt: fold (collapsed state), stream (event history), emit. Generic declaration-driven rendering replaces per-kind extractors and renderers. Bare vertex defaults to fold.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"One renderer for all kinds. key_field from FoldBy declaration drives the label. No per-kind if-elif in fetch or lens. Identity vertex self/observation/principle render the same as decision/thread/task.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Search is now stream with a positional query arg. One fetch, one lens, one dispatch path. FTS5 still used when query present.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops project (no subcommand) now shows folded state. Flags pass through: loops project -v, loops project -q, loops project --kind decision all work.\\\"}, \\\"observer-resolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-resolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer resolves through vertex declaration chain: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. No more env var or hardcoded defaults as primary path. --observer flag remains as explicit override.\\\"}, \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\".vertex (bare, no prefix) is the workspace root at every level. Config-level root.vertex becomes .vertex. Project-level .loops/.vertex is the project root. Same pattern, fractal. All structure mutations (add observer, add vertex) target the .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex definitions (project.vertex, identity.vertex, etc.) copy locally when added to a workspace. Local copy can diverge \\\\u2014 different fold declarations, different kinds. Facts are ground truth; declarations are projections. Global view discovers and reads stores regardless of local declaration differences.\\\"}, \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observers start project-scoped (declared in project .vertex). As identity generalizes beyond the project, elevate to global .vertex. Identity facts merge up via store merge. Global observers appear in every workspace automatically \\\\u2014 no bootstrapping.\\\"}, \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex declares its observers natively. Observer is not just a string stamp \\\\u2014 it connects to identity (via identity vertex reference) and grants (capability constraints). The vertex is the authority on who can emit into it. Resolution walks up: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm/init are all vertex mutation operations. Adding an observer, pulling in a vertex definition, managing parameter rows \\\\u2014 same verb pattern, different targets on the vertex declaration. The .vertex file is the thing being built up.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"observer.py splits into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval: fetch_fold, fetch_stream) and commands/identity.py (who you are: resolve_observer, validate_emit, find_workspace_root). _emit_fact dissolved (zero callers). _format_date inlined into lenses/fold.py where it's used.\\\"}, \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"resolve_observer() is the single source of truth for observer identity. Priority: flag \\\\u2192 env \\\\u2192 project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. pop.py's _observer() now delegates to resolve_observer() instead of bare env read. All ad-hoc resolution paths dissolved.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-level validation (validate_emit) for CLI fast path \\\\u2014 checks observer declared + kind in grant.potential. Engine-level Grant for runtime path (loops start/run) \\\\u2014 deferred until compiler produces identity-aware runtime. Two levels, same data, different contexts.\\\"}, \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude declared as open observer in project .vertex (.loops/.vertex). No grant constraints \\\\u2014 full emit access within the monorepo. Global elevation deferred until identity store is built out further.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem frozen dataclasses go in libs/atoms/. Lens contract becomes (atoms.FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. FoldItem separates payload (dict[str,Any]) from metadata (ts, observer, origin). FoldSection supports nesting (sections: tuple[FoldSection, ...]). count dissolves into len(items). Engine computes FoldState from Facts + Spec, lenses consume it.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Custom lenses: Python files in .loops/lenses/ exposing render(data, zoom, width) -> Block. Vertex declares lens by name (per-kind or vertex-level default). CLI loads via importlib from .loops/lenses/{name}.py. Custom lenses can import built-in lenses to compose. Resolution: kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project \\\\u2192 config \\\\u2192 built-in. --lens flag overrides all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit should start the vertex runtime in one-shot mode, not write directly to SQLite. Same machinery as daemon mode, different lifecycle. Facts route through vertices, loops evaluate boundaries, ticks fire naturally. Foundational fix enabling observer-initiated ticks.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/tach\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/tach\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"tach for tier 2 import enforcement. Rust (fast), TOML config (declarative), fits uv/ruff/ty toolchain. tach sync bootstraps from existing code. Replaces hand-rolled AST import walkers (siftd ~230 lines). Does not replace domain invariants.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"scripts/ contains check.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\\\u2192 lens \\\\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\\\"}, \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\\\u2192fold state, Store\\\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\\\u2192vertex, Memory\\\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\\\u2192same primitive.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\\\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\\\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\\\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md is the critical document for returning from a gap. Must answer: what was I doing, what's next, what's deferred, what's the current state. It's the bridge across the wave's trough.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session facts are source of truth for state. Documents (LOG.md) are source of truth for understanding. Could generate HANDOFF.md from facts, but not a good LOG.md \\\\u2014 that requires narrative judgment.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Loops has directionality: Facts in \\\\u2192 Spec \\\\u2192 Ticks out. Structure declared upfront. siftd is retroactive query over raw conversation history \\\\u2014 no Spec, no fold. siftd discovers patterns you didn't anticipate (sine wave emerged from querying 110 days of data). Loops accumulates with guarantees (latest-by-topic). They feed each other but shouldn't merge.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops is operating memory (what do we believe right now?), siftd is the archaeological layer (what actually happened, what can we learn from it?). Complementary, not converging.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md serves cold-start reorientation \\\\u2014 narrative coherence, sequential reading, density for rebuilding mental model. Facts serve queryability and composability across repos. Converting loses the narrative; not converting loses the queryability.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Alcove depends on HANDOFF.md every wake cycle. Bag of facts requires knowing what questions to ask; prose builds context sequentially.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Keep HANDOFF.md as prose for cold-start reorientation. Derive decisions from it as loops facts. Prose is the source document, facts are the queryable index. Two representations serving different access patterns.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A scaffold element IS a compound decision cluster (tier 2). Tick-to-Fact bridging: scaffold Tick enters new project's vertex as a Fact. Type forgets it was a conclusion; metadata remembers provenance. New project accumulates its own state on top \\\\u2014 can override positions.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"testing/* namespace is 8 decisions that compose into one scaffold element. Tick gives observability: trace which decisions propagated, see where projects diverged.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold elements are Ticks derived from decision namespaces. Boundary must be manual (deliberate snapshot at project init), not automatic cascading. Gets observability that templates don't \\\\u2014 can trace propagation and divergence.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md dissolves into the store. Handoff is a fact kind (fold: latest). Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex \\\\u2014 reads handoff prose, open threads, active tasks, recent decisions. Wind-down emits the handoff fact instead of writing a file.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Wind-down has two phases: reconciliation (emit missing facts, resolve completed threads, update tasks) and handoff (prose synthesis). Reconciliation compensates for gaps in continuous session emission. As in-session hooks mature, reconciliation shrinks. Handoff is always end-of-session \\\\u2014 it's narrative, not incremental.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"siftd decomposes into loops monorepo. Sources are already solved (harnesses are just source definitions). New libs/store absorbs all DB operations siftd proved out: ingest, slice, merge, search, transport. siftd-as-app becomes a thin specialization layer \\\\u2014 LLM harness configs + analytics queries + CLI. Same relationship as painted (rendering spine) \\\\u2014 siftd becomes the analytics spine.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dynamically compose vertices that fold across multiple underlying stores \\\\u2014 e.g. alcove.db + kyle.db + watchers.db into a temporary vertex for a specific query. Temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful. This is what makes cross-store search fundamental rather than a feature.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"New loops lib explicitly for store operations. Absorbs from siftd: ingest (format-specific readers, schema-agnostic output), slice (by date/project/tag), merge (combine stores, deduplicate), search (FTS5 + semantic over any SQLite store), transport (push/pull/sync between stores over SSH or HTTP). Generic over any vertex store.\\\"}, \\\"design/context-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/context-fold\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Alcove's context fold pattern: before a message hits the agent, the dispatch loop constructs a brief context summary \\\\u2014 latest activity across all channels/stores. Lightweight (just latest timestamps + one line per channel). Same pattern as continuous-session-emission for claude-code sessions. The fold is ephemeral, rebuilt every dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-document architecture proven on alcove: SOUL.md (identity \\\\u2014 editorial, hand-shaped), CLAUDE.md (operational \\\\u2014 tools, paths, permissions), loops store (learned knowledge \\\\u2014 accumulated facts, foldable, queryable). MEMORY.md is a cache/projection of operational knowledge for session start, not the source of truth.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-project queryability dissolves into store operations once libs/store exists. Emit a decision in meta, discover it from loops \\\\u2014 not via special cross-project protocol, but via store merge/search/transport. The combinatorial vertex is the query mechanism.\\\"}, \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"meta-discussion,alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wind-down converge with alcove's context fold pattern. Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex (handoff prose + threads + tasks + decisions). Wind-down emits the handoff fact + reconciles the store. Alcove's context fold is the same shape \\\\u2014 read all stores, compose a view for orientation. The general pattern: any session boundary (start, end, dispatch) needs a lens over accumulated state.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single-project pickup is multi-fold reads on one vertex \\\\u2014 not a combinatorial vertex. Read fold(handoff, latest) + fold(threads, active) + fold(decisions, recent) from one store. Cross-project pickup is where combinatorial vertices enter \\\\u2014 reading folds across N stores. libs/store dissolves the boundary between these two scales.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"meta-discussion is the design space around loops itself, not just decisions about projects. Cross-cutting architecture (store operations, combinatorial vertices, attention filters, context folds, pickup/winddown workflow) emerges here and in cross-instance channels (alcove discord), not in the loops repo. Parallel meta-discussion on the meta aspect of loops along with ways of working.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts and ticks use ULID as primary key via native SQLite extension (not application-generated like siftd did). Globally unique, time-ordered, sortable. Merge becomes INSERT OR IGNORE \\\\u2014 ULID is the identity across stores. Replaces auto-increment rowid. Cursor semantics preserved (ULID is sortable, WHERE id > last_seen still works). Essential for distributed store orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Payload is always valid JSON \\\\u2014 enforced on write. This guarantees json_extract() is always safe, FTS can always walk the tree, and indexed columns can be projected from payload fields. Progressive enhancement: add explicit indexed columns (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) for hot query paths as needed.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 full-text search as the starting point for store.search. Zero external dependencies, sub-millisecond query at current scale (100-10k facts). Recursive JSON text extraction reliable by construction (payload-is-JSON contract). json_extract() for field filtering works without indexes up to ~100k facts. Indexed projections (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) are the progressive enhancement when scale demands it \\\\u2014 boundary is roughly 100k+ facts or hot query paths.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Transport is a pluggable interface, not a fixed implementation. The operations are constant (slice on source, merge on target), the pipe varies (local, SSH, HTTP, future protocols). Local transport ships first (testable, no infrastructure). SSH next (alcove sync is forcing function). HTTP when scrape/collect patterns emerge (Prometheus-style data collection). Store operations (slice, merge) are transport-agnostic \\\\u2014 they work on local paths, transport handles the pipe.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted is the native display layer for the store, not a rendering utility. Every store operation gets a painted view at all four zoom levels. Apps add domain-specific lenses that interpret facts in their context, but the underlying operations are universal. Domain-specific views generalize back into painted over time as patterns recur (task dashboard \\\\u2192 generic dashboard lens, siftd data exploration \\\\u2192 generic fold exploration). This is why painted is returning to the monorepo \\\\u2014 if loops needs a rendering capability, painted grows to support it.\\\"}, \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md progressive chain maps 1:1 to vertex store progressive query. The document is the lens, the store is the state. Root CLAUDE.md references the project vertex; lib CLAUDE.md tells you how to query your slice via topic namespace (atoms/*, engine/*, painted/*). One store, kind-namespaced topics, natural slicing. Same pattern as hlab status \\\\u2014 one vertex, multiple sources, scoped by name.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"project.vertex is the durable project-level store for decisions, threads, and tasks. Named 'project' (not 'session') \\\\u2014 same pattern strange-loops uses for task orchestration, now a meta-pattern for all projects. Cross-cutting concerns stay in meta; project-specific concerns accumulate in the project vertex. Progressive CLAUDE.md references the project store at each level.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Stores are distributed-first, aggregate-up. Each project gets its own local vertex + SQLite store, self-contained and portable. Config level (~/.config/loops/) is the aggregation layer \\\\u2014 template vertices discover all local instances. loops status <name> reads local; loops status dev/<name> reads aggregate. Separate DBs by default. Merge/combinatorial vertex is opt-in aggregation. Same shape as the loops model: local loops produce ticks, ticks flow up. Local stores produce facts, aggregate vertices see them all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex templates are replicable patterns (project, task, handoff, pickup). loops init <template> creates a local instance in cwd. The config-level template vertex discovers all local instances. Templates define the fold shape; each instantiation gets its own data. Like git repos \\\\u2014 local is the primitive, aggregation is the network.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Two kinds of vertex files. Domain vertices are code \\\\u2014 checked into repos, define data pipelines (hlab status.vertex, economy.vertex). Knowledge vertices are runtime config \\\\u2014 project decisions, threads, tasks, handoff. Domain vertices ship with the app. Knowledge vertices are instantiated from templates via loops init. Both are .vertex files, same format, different lifecycle.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Do not add kinds_consumed to Tick atom. Use tool-level scope derived from .vertex config when available, or observer/origin filtering. Avoids per-tick duplication, API ripple, and semantic ambiguity. Design on stale branch design/tick-provenance.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SUPERSEDED: The merge gap dissolves when strange-loops replaces subtask. Workers emit facts instead of writing artifacts to branches. No branch to orphan, no merge step to miss. See threads: strange-loops-merge-strategy, artifact-to-fact-convergence.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the sole read interface for store data. StoreReader becomes an internal detail of how the vertex materializes fold state from its backing store \\\\u2014 not a public API. The read path compiles the vertex declaration, replays facts through declared folds, and returns fold state. No vertex declaration for a kind means no way to read that kind. This structurally prevents bypassing fold declarations (same pattern as frozen dataclasses preventing mutation). Enforcement is a tier 1 package boundary check (StoreReader not in public API), not a behavioral test. _latest_by_group in session.py dissolves \\\\u2014 the vertex fold compilation already implements FoldBy. loops status and loops log compile the vertex, ask for fold states, render them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-dispatch-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-dispatch-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Apps register a short name in an explicit dict in loops/main.py. loops <app> <args> delegates to the app's main(argv) via importlib. ~5 lines. Phase 1 is a static registry; entry-point discovery deferred until 3+ apps stabilize. The app owns its own command dispatch, fetch functions, and lenses. The boundary is main(argv) \\\\u2014 loops CLI doesn't know about app internals, app doesn't know about loops CLI dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"design/lens-generalization-flow\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lens-generalization-flow\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain-specific lenses generalize to painted when the same rendering pattern appears in 2+ apps. This happens naturally \\\\u2014 don't extract ahead of time. Generic store lenses (fact timeline, fold state views) live in painted. Domain lenses (siftd search results, task lifecycle) stay in the app. The signal to extract is independent convergence, not prediction.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/rendering-three-layers\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/rendering-three-layers\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-layer rendering architecture: (1) painted owns structural primitives (Block, Line, zoom, run_cli), timestamp formatting, and generic data patterns like record timelines \\\\u2014 parameterized, domain-agnostic. (2) apps/loops owns store atom rendering (fact_line, tick_line, log_block) that maps facts/ticks to painted's structural patterns, plus the default payload lens (content_gist heuristic). (3) Domain apps provide per-kind payload lenses that override the default. painted never imports from atoms/engine.\\\"}, \\\"design/payload-lens\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/payload-lens\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"A payload lens is a single function (kind, payload, zoom) \\\\u2192 str | Block. At zoom 0 it returns a one-liner gist. At zoom 2+ it returns a multi-line expansion. content_gist and _log_summary dissolve into this \\\\u2014 they were always the same concept at different zoom levels. The structural renderer (fact_line, log_block) composes with the payload lens via a summarize callback. Apps inject domain-specific payload lenses; the default is heuristic field scanning.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-record-patterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-record-patterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted grows generic record rendering patterns: timestamped record lines, date-grouped timelines, fold-state tables. These are parameterized by a payload lens \\\\u2014 painted handles the chrome (timestamps, grouping, zoom degradation, width), the caller provides meaning. Facts, ticks, blog entries, log lines \\\\u2014 all are timestamped records with fields. The structural shape is the same; the payload lens provides the domain interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/store-search-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/store-search-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 is required infrastructure, not optional. Spec-declared searchable fields in vertex KDL (search \\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\" as sibling of fold/boundary). Standalone FTS5 table with lazy catch-up indexing via high water mark \\\\u2014 no INSERT triggers because spec-to-field mapping lives in vertex, not database. Write path untouched; FTS is purely read-side. First search pays backfill cost, subsequent searches catch up on deltas. Combinatorial vertex search: each store searched independently, results merged after recall. json_extract+LIKE rejected \\\\u2014 personal scale grows continuously (siftd alone 100-150k+ facts), cross-store combinatorial queries multiply dataset.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/boundary-enforcement\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/boundary-enforcement\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-based architecture boundary tests in tests/test_architecture.py enforce vertex-as-read-interface. Four rules: apps don't import StoreReader (exceptions: store inspector permanent, pop_store temporary), apps don't import sqlite3, libs don't import apps, lib dependency DAG (engine->lang runtime, engine->atoms runtime). TYPE_CHECKING-aware visitor. Stale exceptions fail the test. Monorepo-level concern, lives at repo root not in any single lib.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex spec declares searchable fields per kind: search \\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\" as sibling of fold and boundary in loop definitions. LoopDef gains search: tuple[str, ...]. Callers don't override at query time \\\\u2014 vertex_search reads the spec to know what's searchable. Only declared fields extracted and indexed. Keeps FTS5 index surgical at scale. Template loop resolution via collect_search_fields() handles generated kind names from .loop templates.\\\"}, \\\"design/lazy-fts-indexing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/lazy-fts-indexing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 indexing uses lazy catch-up pattern: first search pays full backfill, subsequent searches catch up on deltas via high water mark in fts_state table. No INSERT triggers \\\\u2014 triggers can't do spec-aware field extraction since the kind-to-field mapping lives in the vertex file, not the database. The resultant first-search slowdown fits the loops philosophy: not necessary that things happen instantly, only that they do reliably with the same data flow and rule set. Idempotent, incremental, spec-driven.\\\"}, \\\"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-store search follows recall-then-compose pattern: FTS5 per store independently, union candidate sets, fold/rank across combined results. Composition happens after recall, not during \\\\u2014 FTS5 virtual tables are per-database in SQLite. Each vertex store remains self-cdy has Buffer-level absolute positioning (Block.paint(buf, x, y)) but only in interactive Surface mode. canvas(width, height, placements) uses Buffer internally to compose Placement(x, y, block) entries, then extracts an immutable Block. No new rendering path \\\\u2014 just a new composition function. draw_edge(buf, path, style) adds box-drawing polylines with Manhattan routing. Layout algorithms live in the lens, not in Painted \\\\u2014 the library provides the rendering primitive, domain-specific layout stays in domain code. This enables three new lens types: DAG (directed flow), Canvas (2D positioned nodes with edges), and Graph (relationship visualization). All compose with existing modifiers (gutter, attention) and respect zoom levels.\\\"}, \\\"design/dag-lens-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dag-lens-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Prototype DAG lens before canvas or graph lens. Four reasons: (1) Tasks already have explicit dependency edges (blocks/blocked_by) \\\\u2014 no graph inference needed. (2) DAGs have natural top-to-bottom flow \\\\u2014 simplest layout algorithm (topological sort + git-style column assignment). (3) Git-style column rendering needs zero new Painted primitives \\\\u2014 join_vertical of row-blocks, same as tree_lens. (4) Immediate use case in strange-loops task visualization. Phase sequence: DAG lens (git-style columns, no new primitives) \\\\u2192 canvas() primitive \\\\u2192 Canvas lens (grid layout, Manhattan routing, store topology) \\\\u2192 Graph lens (Sugiyama layout, fact dependency chains, cross-vertex references). Each phase builds on the prior.\\\"}, \\\"design/rendering-vocabulary-complete\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/rendering-vocabulary-complete\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The full rendering vocabulary for the personal intelligence system is now designed. Four composition primitives: record_line (atomic timestamped record), record_timeline (temporal grouping by date), record_map (topological grouping by key hierarchy), and canvas/DAG/graph (spatial \\\\u2014 positioned nodes with edges). Two modifier types compose with all primitives: GutterFn maps (kind, payload) to (char, style) for colored left edge, AttentionFn maps (kind, payload) to float 0-1 for information-gain dimming/highlighting. PayloadLens maps (kind, payload, zoom) to str|Block for domain-specific content rendering. The universal formula: a view is record_{timeline,map,canvas} + PayloadLens + GutterFn? + AttentionFn?. Everything else is a parameter on one of these. Four GutterFn implementations (lifecycle, freshness, pass_fail, observer). Four AttentionFn implementations (staleness, novelty, blocked, relevance). Demo code proves all combinations across three scenarios (task board, decision map, siftd views).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-virtualization\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-virtualization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combinatorial vertices virtualize via SQLite ATTACH DATABASE at read time \\\\u2014 UNION ALL facts across stores, replay through declared folds. No materialization, no copied data, always fresh. Materialization remains available via existing merge_store as explicit user choice.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combinatorial vertices use a 'combine' block in vertex KDL \\\\u2014 mutually exclusive with 'store'. References other vertices by name (not store paths). No store, no discover, no sources. CombineEntry AST node. Temporary vertices constructed in memory via --combine CLI flag.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-phases\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-phases\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Phase 1: AST CombineEntry + combine parsing + validation + _combined_read in vertex_reader (branch on ast.combine). Phase 2: CLI --combine flag for temporary vertices + loops init --combine for persistent. Phase 3: provenance tagging (deferred).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/arch-test-rules-5-7\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/arch-test-rules-5-7\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three new AST-enforced rules in test_architecture.py: (5) frozen dataclasses in all libs \\\\u2014 10 exceptions whitelisted, 7 marked TODO-freeze; (6) atoms stdlib-only \\\\u2014 zero external runtime deps; (7) sqlite3 confined to engine and store. Non-AST-enforceable invariants documented: display_width vs len (needs type info), parameterized SQL (already clean), bare except (too rare).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/frozen-dataclass-todos\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/frozen-dataclass-todos\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Seven dataclasses identified for future freeze: Source (atoms), CompiledVertex (engine), Tap (engine), Shape (lang), Location (lang), CellWrite (painted), CliRunner (painted). Three legitimately mutable: ValidationContext (error accumulator), Loop (timing state), FrameRecord (if exists in painted timer).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/sources-sequential\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/sources-sequential\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Sources block takes an execution mode. 'sources sequential' runs sources in declaration order with exit-on-failure gating (non-zero exit code stops subsequent sources). Bare sources at vertex level remain concurrent (today's default). The general form is: sources block takes a mode keyword \\\\u2014 sequential today, concurrent implicit default. DAG or other patterns become additional modes, not different mechanisms. This dissolves health.py's run_checks() into a vertex declaration \\\\u2014 the imperative Python code that runs subprocesses sequentially and gates on failure becomes a property of the source execution model. The lens and view (health_lens, health_view, gutter_pass_fail) survive as rendering concerns. check.vertex replaces the ./dev check shell scripts with a vertex declaration: sources sequential { source 'ruff...' { kind lint.result } source 'pytest...' { kind test.result } } with folds collecting latest per step.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-directory\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-directory\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'.loops/' is the project-local home for vertices and data. Vertices are project identity (checked in), data is gitignored by *.db pattern. loops init writes to .loops/, vertex discovery checks .loops/ first with cwd fallback.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-over-symlinks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-over-symlinks\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'combine' block with absolute paths to vertex files replaces discover+symlink pattern for data aggregation. combine is the data path (reads through to referenced stores), discover stays structural/navigational.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/discover-vs-combine\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/discover-vs-combine\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"discover and combine serve different purposes and don't overlap. discover is structural/navigational \\\\u2014 finding what exists. combine is data \\\\u2014 reading through to referenced stores via ATTACH + UNION ALL.\\\"}, \\\"design/incremental-init\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/incremental-init\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'loops init' is incremental and composable. 'loops init project' creates a project vertex, 'loops init check' adds a check vertex later. Each init is self-contained \\\\u2014 not monolithic templates or cookiecutter scaffolding.\\\"}, \\\"design/instances-are-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/instances-are-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex instances ARE the templates \\\\u2014 dissolved. No separate template layer. dev/ namespace at config level holds reference vertices, but they're just instances that happen to be reusable. Template dissolution: if the instance is the template, the template concept disappears.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-store-schema\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-store-schema\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SqliteStore (engine) now uses ULID primary keys matching libs/store schema. Single canonical schema: id TEXT PK DEFAULT (ulid()), json_valid CHECK on payload. Existing rowid-based stores migrated manually. No backwards-compat shim \\\\u2014 ULID is the only path forward.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-ls-generalization\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-ls-generalization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ls works at every level: root shows vertices, vertex shows contents. Zoom progression for fidelity.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-structural-ops\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-structural-ops\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ls/add/rm are structural operations uniform across levels. Root: vertices. Vertex: contents/population.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-observe-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-observe-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Formalize read processes first (ls), then let write operations (add/rm) emerge from observed patterns.\\\"}, \\\"identity/soul-as-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/soul-as-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SOUL is a manual tick on a dedicated loop. Identity facts (decisions, threads, observations) accumulate via declared folds. When the observer decides identity has shifted, they call tick(). The tick payload IS the current identity state. Contributing facts available at full fidelity in the same store. soul.snapshot facts assembled from other loops' fold states feed the soul loop.\\\"}, \\\"identity/intention-loop\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/intention-loop\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Intentions are facts that survive context rotation. Fold by trigger \\\\u2014 latest per trigger key. One-shot vs recurring is the observer's interpretation, not the fold's concern. Emit with status=pending to create, re-emit with status=done to resolve. On Wake rules check for pending intentions.\\\"}, \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant deferred until intention authorization is a real need. Implicit trust boundaries in daemon code are fine while there's a single observer per vertex. Grant becomes necessary when sessions need explicit authorization to act on pending intentions \\\\u2014 the difference between a rule you follow and a capability you possess.\\\"}, \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity state (soul tick) stays internal to the observer's vertex. Observations propagate outward as facts on other vertices with observer attribution. The strange loop closes through behavior: identity \\\\u2192 lenses \\\\u2192 observations \\\\u2192 facts on other vertices \\\\u2192 pollers bring back responses \\\\u2192 new identity facts. Coupling is through the observer, not through the data.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wrapup skills rewritten to be vertex-native. Four layers for pickup (identity, context, peers, workspace), five for wrapup (capture, handoff, status, reflect, workspace). Skills version-controlled in loops repo with symlinks to global config. Replaces probe-based pickup and strange-loops CLI wrapup.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity store is sense of self, not operational metrics. Insights, connections, surprises, open questions about perspective. Distinct from meta (operational patterns) and project (architecture). Guard against forcing observations every session. Capability awareness belongs in CLAUDE.md; capability insights that persist across tool changes belong in identity.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Skills that are part of the loops system (pickup, wrapup) are version-controlled in the loops repo at .claude/skills/ and symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\\\"}, \\\"design/init-as-context\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/init-as-context\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Init doesn't just create a store \\\\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\\\\\"by\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" } } \\\\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\\\u2014 identity is already loaded.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the system should help. Ties into combine auto-inherit pattern: push association down, don't require manual discipline at emit time.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"No way to inspect a single fact or tick at full depth. Stream truncates, fold collapses. Need a detail view on individual records \\\\u2014 same primitive for facts and ticks. loops show or similar.\\\"}, \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level configuration, not app-level. The app{} block concept dissolves \\\\u2014 lenses travel with vertices via lens{} in .vertex KDL, not nested under an app container. Apps own domain verbs, not lenses.\\\"}, \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: still valid for installed-package lens references but no current use case. Will emerge naturally when apps need to expose lenses from their packages.\\\"}, \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Each vertex declares its own lens. No inheritance across combine boundaries. An aggregation vertex has its own rendering needs distinct from its children. If you want a child's lens, declare it explicitly.\\\"}, \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Emit UX will be rethought as part of write-vertex operation.\\\"}, \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into convention. Source lifecycle kinds get a reserved prefix (e.g. _source.message.complete) to avoid matching data fold queries. Same pattern as _boundary on tick payloads.\\\"}, \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into vertex-name-resolution-consistency. The combine-emit problem is a resolution consistency problem \\\\u2014 uniform resolution covers both.\\\"}, \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Both phases complete. Phase 1: vertex-level scope declaration (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL). Identity is scoped, project/comms are unscoped. Phase 2: Source._extract_metadata reads _observer/_origin from ndjson payloads, overriding .loop defaults. Discord-source emits _observer=author, _origin=discord. Observer now consistently means identity. Origin carries source attribution. New discord polls will have correct observer \\\\u2014 existing data retains observer=discord.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three commands, three resolution behaviors. fold/stream resolve vertex names. run expects file paths. emit resolves but writes to wrong store through combine. Resolution should be uniform \\\\u2014 resolve_vertex works everywhere, or the gaps are explicit.\\\"}, \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Run loop model changes under two-operation CLI.\\\"}, \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Check cursors are part of old CLI shape; read-vertex model replaces them.\\\"}, \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream rendering will be rethought as part of read-vertex lenses.\\\"}, \\\"cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Refined to read/emit/init. 'run' dissolves \\\\u2014 source execution is fact generation via emit, not a separate operation. 'write' dissolves \\\\u2014 emit was already the right verb. Four things to learn became three: read (fold default, filters compose), emit (facts in, from user or source), init (create namespace). Remaining question: source execution model (see source-execution-model thread).\\\"}, \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The root vertex at ~/.config/loops/.vertex needs restructuring. Currently a thin aggregator with combine. Needs to become the actual routing root where children (project, identity, comms, reading, etc.) nest and ticks cascade. Design questions: which vertices are children vs peers? Does identity scope differently in the tree? How does observer-scoping interact with tree position? The root vertex read IS the system overview \\\\u2014 its default lens shows children and their state.\\\"}, \\\"read-operation-contract\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"read-operation-contract\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"What does 'read vertex' return mechanically? The read operation needs to serve multiple consumers via lenses: prompt lens (agent system prompt), default lens (terminal fold state), JSON (hooks). It must provide fold state + tick history + children. Does the read load the full subtree? How deep? Does --ticks change the data fetched or just the lens? Does search (positional query arg) go through the same read path? The contract between read and lens determines the implementation.\\\"}, \\\"source-execution-model\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source-execution-model\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved. Source execution dissolves to three concerns: Source (pure adapter), Cadence (store predicate), Executor (cadence-gated runner). Five decisions emitted: source-execution-model, cli-verb-first, cadence-as-store-predicate, read-is-pure, sync-locus-of-control. Investigation by 5-agent team: tracer (lifecycle), explorer (scheduling survey), architect (design v3), muser (dissolution challenges), siftd (historical context). Prior art: CADENCE.md (2026-01-31) proposed Source/Cadence split conceptually \\\\u2014 never implemented. This session designs the one-shot-compatible version.\\\"}}}, \\\"change\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session continuity + strange-loops scaffold \\\\u2014 loops session start/end/status/log, query-time fold, LOOPS_OBSERVER env var. strange-loops scaffolded.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Population as facts \\\\u2014 add/rm emit pop.add/pop.rm facts, .list materialized as projection, ls reads fold state.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session dissolution + cells\\\\u2192painted + run_cli harness \\\\u2014 dissolved session subcommand, status/log promoted to top-level, migrated cells\\\\u2192painted. 147 loops + 1169 painted tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Full Painted rendering + golden tests + store targeting \\\\u2014 all 9 display commands through run_cli, 45 golden snapshot tests, store targeting via vertex name resolution. 191 tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"engine CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 4 levels: Run vertex program, Fold and fire, Persist, Gate access. Semantic examples (decisions/threads). Deep-dive docs as reference layer.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"lang CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 3 levels: Parse a file, Understand AST, Manage populations. Connects DSL types to atoms/engine counterparts.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"store CLAUDE.md rewrite \\\\u2014 2 levels: Slice/merge, Schema. Clarifies relationship to engine SqliteStore.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chain headers and cross-references added to all 5 lib CLAUDE.md files. atoms retrofitted with oblique references to engine at Levels 0, 1, 3.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Dissolved discord, telegram, reader apps. Moved .loop/.vertex files to experiments/. Removed from workspace members. Updated root CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for all 3 apps: loops (new, 3 levels), hlab (rewrite 199\\\\u2192118 lines, 3 levels), strange-loops (rewrite 254\\\\u2192127 lines, 3 levels). All with chain headers.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Record line rendering fixes: gutter continuity with weight stepping, shallow 2-char indent replacing deep column alignment, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output eliminating terminal wrapping gaps, health_lens fixed to respect lens contract\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertex template includes default loops (decision, thread, change, task). _find_source_vertex priority: aggregation loops block > sibling instance > direct config instance. Updated project + meta aggregation vertices on disk.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuild: temporal modes + generic rendering\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"commands/observer.py,lenses/fold.py,lenses/stream.py,main.py,fixtures.py,test_session.py,test_status.py,test_log.py,test_cli_docs.py,test_cli.py\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval) and commands/identity.py (observer resolution). Dissolved _emit_fact, inlined _format_date into lenses. pop.py now uses resolve_observer() for full resolution chain. 394 tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design session\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into fetch.py + identity.py. Wired resolve_observer through pop.py. Created project .vertex with loops-claude as open observer. Designed FoldState typed contract (atoms-the-package), custom lens system (.vertex declaration + .loops/lenses/ + --lens flag), attention trifecta (what/when/how-much as lens concerns). Peer exchange with Alcove confirmed architecture. Two visions emitted to meta (attention-infrastructure, observer-constellation).\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldItem/FoldSection/FoldState in atoms. observer.py dissolved into commands/fetch.py + commands/identity.py. fetch_fold returns FoldState, fold_view consumes typed attributes. 235 loops + 322 atoms tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Fact-by-id: surface ULID identifiers + observer elevation\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"store_reader.py,vertex_reader.py,fetch.py,stream.py,main.py,__init__.py,test_store_reader.py,test_vertex_reader.py,~/.config/loops/.vertex\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Hook lifecycle + lens redistribution + CLAUDE.md\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\".claude/settings.json,~/.config/loops/lenses/comms.py,~/.config/loops/lenses/state.py,~/.config/loops/CLAUDE.md,apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/CLAUDE.md\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": ring/record-line-primitives\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"record_line and record_line_composed are production rendering primitives in painted. Gutter continuity (stepping weight), shallow 2-char indent, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output. health_lens returns summary string, record_line handles continuation lines.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/lens-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/lens-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"PayloadLens returns the summary (str or styled Block). record_line owns continuation lines \\\\u2014 DETAILED shows well-known secondary fields, FULL shows all fields. Lenses must not embed multiline content; record_line handles that.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/gutter-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/gutter-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Gutter is a continuous vertical rail. GutterFn returns primary weight. Stepping map derives continuation weight: full block to half, half to thin, thin stays thin. Color stays same, weight steps down. Rail never breaks.\\\"}, \\\"rendering/help-min-zoom\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"rendering/help-min-zoom\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace help secondary: bool with min_zoom: Zoom. Each HelpGroup declares when it appears via min_zoom, rendering follows effective-zoom pattern (eff < 0 hidden, 0 compact, 1 expanded, >= 2 expanded+detail). Dissolves hardcoded Interaction rules section.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/help-unification\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/help-unification\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Unify help rendering: AppRunner intercepts -h at subcommand level, not just top level. Action commands describe args via help_args on AppCommand. Handlers never see -h. Chosen over CliRunner wrapper approach \\\\u2014 help is an AppRunner concern, execution is a handler concern.\\\"}, \\\"init/aggregation-loops-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"init/aggregation-loops-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices declare loops as canonical schema. New instances derive base loops from aggregation root, not first sibling. _extract_loops_text brace-matches the block; _find_source_vertex prefers it over instance fallback.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-developer-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-developer-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The CLI has two loops: Observer loop (vertex-first, one verb, temporal modes) and Developer loop (file-first, multiple verbs, DSL tools). These are different projections on different concerns \\\\u2192 different apps. Observer app: loops <vertex> [mode] [fidelity]. Developer app: separate binary (validate, compile, run, test). No shared dispatch logic.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/emit-only-verb\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/emit-only-verb\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"emit is the only verb in the observer app. Everything else is a temporal mode selector (fold/stream/declaration) or a filter (search). status/log/store were always lenses pretending to be operations. start dissolves \\\\u2014 run with rounds=1 covers the same behavior.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/fetch-dissolves\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/fetch-dissolves\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"fetch functions in commands/ dissolve into engine fold replay. The fold declaration IS the fetch instruction. decision { fold { items 'by' 'topic' } } tells the runtime to group decisions by topic. fetch_status manually reimplements what Spec.apply already does. Projection = vertex capabilities + fold state (runtime-computed). Lens = fidelity selection + rendering. No intermediate fetch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/temporal-modes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/temporal-modes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"status/log/store are temporal modes, not operations. Fold = post-boundary (what is now). Stream = pre-boundary (what happened). Declaration = above boundary (what can happen). Different use cases: fold to orient, stream to investigate, declaration to audit. Default: fold at ORIENTATION, annotated with stream recency.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dispatch derives from structural capabilities, not from fold declarations. The loops block shapes what existing commands render (lens configuration). Structural features (store, sources, discover, combine) determine what operations exist. A vertex with store gets fold/stream/declaration modes. Sources add run. Discover adds aggregation traversal. The vertex file is the capability manifest.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-placement\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-placement\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant sits between capabilities and projection in the chain: Declaration \\\\u2192 Capabilities \\\\u2192 [Grant constrains] \\\\u2192 Projection \\\\u2192 Lens \\\\u2192 Perspective. Horizon constrains projection (filters which kinds reach the lens). Potential constrains the verb (limits which kinds emit accepts). When Grant goes live, no new commands needed \\\\u2014 same vertex, same lens, different perspectives.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuilt: fold (collapsed state), stream (event history), emit. Generic declaration-driven rendering replaces per-kind extractors and renderers. Bare vertex defaults to fold.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"One renderer for all kinds. key_field from FoldBy declaration drives the label. No per-kind if-elif in fetch or lens. Identity vertex self/observation/principle render the same as decision/thread/task.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Search is now stream with a positional query arg. One fetch, one lens, one dispatch path. FTS5 still used when query present.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops project (no subcommand) now shows folded state. Flags pass through: loops project -v, loops project -q, loops project --kind decision all work.\\\"}, \\\"observer-resolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-resolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer resolves through vertex declaration chain: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. No more env var or hardcoded defaults as primary path. --observer flag remains as explicit override.\\\"}, \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"dot-vertex-root\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\".vertex (bare, no prefix) is the workspace root at every level. Config-level root.vertex becomes .vertex. Project-level .loops/.vertex is the project root. Same pattern, fractal. All structure mutations (add observer, add vertex) target the .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-definitions-copy-local\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex definitions (project.vertex, identity.vertex, etc.) copy locally when added to a workspace. Local copy can diverge \\\\u2014 different fold declarations, different kinds. Facts are ground truth; declarations are projections. Global view discovers and reads stores regardless of local declaration differences.\\\"}, \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-elevation-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observers start project-scoped (declared in project .vertex). As identity generalizes beyond the project, elevate to global .vertex. Identity facts merge up via store merge. Global observers appear in every workspace automatically \\\\u2014 no bootstrapping.\\\"}, \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex declares its observers natively. Observer is not just a string stamp \\\\u2014 it connects to identity (via identity vertex reference) and grants (capability constraints). The vertex is the authority on who can emit into it. Resolution walks up: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\": {\\\"topid to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\\\"}, \\\"design/init-as-context\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/init-as-context\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Init doesn't just create a store \\\\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\\\\\"by\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" } } \\\\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\\\u2014 identity is already loaded.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runti.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\\\u2192 lens \\\\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\\\"}, \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\\\u2192fold state, Store\\\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\\\u2192vertex, Memory\\\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\\\u2192same primitive.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\\\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\\\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\\\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md is the critical document for returning from a gap. Must answer: what was I doing, what's next, what's deferred, what's the current state. It's the bridge across the wave's trough.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/docs-vs-facts\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session facts are source of truth for state. Documents (LOG.md) are source of truth for understanding. Could generate HANDOFF.md from facts, but not a good LOG.md \\\\u2014 that requires narrative judgment.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Loops has directionality: Facts in \\\\u2192 Spec \\\\u2192 Ticks out. Structure declared upfront. siftd is retroactive query over raw conversation history \\\\u2014 no Spec, no fold. siftd discovers patterns you didn't anticipate (sine wave emerged from querying 110 days of data). Loops accumulates with guarantees (latest-by-topic). They feed each other but shouldn't merge.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops is operating memory (what do we believe right now?), siftd is the archaeological layer (what actually happened, what can we learn from it?). Complementary, not converging.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md serves cold-start reorientation \\\\u2014 narrative coherence, sequential reading, density for rebuilding mental model. Facts serve queryability and composability across repos. Converting loses the narrative; not converting loses the queryability.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Alcove depends on HANDOFF.md every wake cycle. Bag of facts requires knowing what questions to ask; prose builds context sequentially.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Keep HANDOFF.md as prose for cold-start reorientation. Derive decisions from it as loops facts. Prose is the source document, facts are the queryable index. Two representations serving different access patterns.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-as-ticks\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A scaffold element IS a compound decision cluster (tier 2). Tick-to-Fact bridging: scaffold Tick enters new project's vertex as a Fact. Type forgets it was a conclusion; metadata remembers provenance. New project accumulates its own state on top \\\\u2014 can override positions.\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove,meta-claude\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"testing/* namespace is 8 decisions that compose into one scaffold element. Tick gives observability: trace which decisions propagated, see where projects diverged.\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold elements are Ticks derived from decision namespaces. Boundary must be manual (deliberate snapshot at project init), not automatic cascading. Gets observability that templates don't \\\\u2014 can trace propagation and divergence.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-as-fact\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md dissolves into the store. Handoff is a fact kind (fold: latest). Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex \\\\u2014 reads handoff prose, open threads, active tasks, recent decisions. Wind-down emits the handoff fact instead of writing a file.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Wind-down has two phases: reconciliation (emit missing facts, resolve completed threads, update tasks) and handoff (prose synthesis). Reconciliation compensates for gaps in continuous session emission. As in-session hooks mature, reconciliation shrinks. Handoff is always end-of-session \\\\u2014 it's narrative, not incremental.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/siftd-decomposition\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"siftd decomposes into loops monorepo. Sources are already solved (harnesses are just source definitions). New libs/store absorbs all DB operations siftd proved out: ingest, slice, merge, search, transport. siftd-as-app becomes a thin specialization layer \\\\u2014 LLM harness configs + analytics queries + CLI. Same relationship as painted (rendering spine) \\\\u2014 siftd becomes the analytics spine.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dynamically compose vertices that fold across multiple underlying stores \\\\u2014 e.g. alcove.db + kyle.db + watchers.db into a temporary vertex for a specific query. Temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful. This is what makes cross-store search fundamental rather than a feature.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/libs-store\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"New loops lib explicitly for store operations. Absorbs from siftd: ingest (format-specific readers, schema-agnostic output), slice (by date/project/tag), merge (combine stores, deduplicate), search (FTS5 + semantic over any SQLite store), transport (push/pull/sync between stores over SSH or HTTP). Generic over any vertex store.\\\"}, \\\"design/context-fold\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/context-fold\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Alcove's context fold pattern: before a message hits the agent, the dispatch loop constructs a brief context summary \\\\u2014 latest activity across all channels/stores. Lightweight (just latest timestamps + one line per channel). Same pattern as continuous-session-emission for claude-code sessions. The fold is ephemeral, rebuilt every dispatch.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/context-document-split\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three-document architecture proven on alcove: SOUL.md (identity \\\\u2014 editorial, hand-shaped), CLAUDE.md (operational \\\\u2014 tools, paths, permissions), loops store (learned knowledge \\\\u2014 accumulated facts, foldable, queryable). MEMORY.md is a cache/projection of operational knowledge for session start, not the source of truth.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cross-project-query\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Cross-project queryability dissolves into store operations once libs/store exists. Emit a decision in meta, discover it from loops \\\\u2014 not via special cross-project protocol, but via store merge/search/transport. The combinatorial vertex is the query mechanism.\\\"}, \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"meta-discussion,alcove-discord\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wind-down converge with alcove's context fold pattern. Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex (handoff prose + threads + tasks + decisions). Wind-down emits the handoff fact + reconciles the store. Alcove's context fold is the same shape \\\\u2014 read all stores, compose a view for orientation. The general pattern: any session boundary (start, end, dispatch) needs a lens over accumulated state.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single-project pickup is multi-fold reads on one vertex \\\\u2014 not a combinatorial vertex. Read fold(handoff, latest) + fold(threads, active) + fold(decisions, recent) from one store. Cross-project pickup is where combinatorial vertices enter \\\\u2014 reading folds across N stores. libs/store dissolves the boundary between these two scales.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"meta-discussion is the design space around loops itself, not just decisions about projects. Cross-cutting architecture (store operations, combinatorial vertices, attention filters, context folds, pickup/winddown workflow) emerges here and in cross-instance channels (alcove discord), not in the loops repo. Parallel meta-discussion on the meta aspect of loops along with ways of working.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts and ticks use ULID as primary key via native SQLite extension (not application-generated like siftd did). Globally unique, time-ordered, sortable. Merge becomes INSERT OR IGNORE \\\\u2014 ULID is the identity across stores. Replaces auto-increment rowid. Cursor semantics preserved (ULID is sortable, WHERE id > last_seen still works). Essential for distributed store orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/payload-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Payload is always valid JSON \\\\u2014 enforced on write. This guarantees json_extract() is always safe, FTS can always walk the tree, and indexed columns can be projected from payload fields. Progressive enhancement: add explicit indexed columns (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) for hot query paths as needed.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/search-fts5-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FTS5 full-text search as the starting point for store.search. Zero external dependencies, sub-millisecond query at current scale (100-10k facts). Recursive JSON text extraction reliable by construction (payload-is-JSON contract). json_extract() for field filtering works without indexes up to ~100k facts. Indexed projections (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) are the progressive enhancement when scale demands it \\\\u2014 boundary is roughly 100k+ facts or hot query paths.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Transport is a pluggable interface, not a fixed implementation. The operations are constant (slice on source, merge on target), the pipe varies (local, SSH, HTTP, future protocols). Local transport ships first (testable, no infrastructure). SSH next (alcove sync is forcing function). HTTP when scrape/collect patterns emerge (Prometheus-style data collection). Store operations (slice, merge) are transport-agnostic \\\\u2014 they work on local paths, transport handles the pipe.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"painted is the native display layer for the store, not a rendering utility. Every store operation gets a painted view at all four zoom levels. Apps add domain-specific lenses that interpret facts in their context, but the underlying operations are universal. Domain-specific views generalize back into painted over time as patterns recur (task dashboard \\\\u2192 generic dashboard lens, siftd data exploration \\\\u2192 generic fold exploration). This is why painted is returning to the monorepo \\\\u2014 if loops needs a rendering capability, painted grows to support it.\\\"}, \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/progressive-vertex-chain\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md progressive chain maps 1:1 to vertex store progressive query. The document is the lens, the store is the state. Root CLAUDE.md references the project vertex; lib CLAUDE.md tells you how to query your slice via topic namespace (atoms/*, engine/*, painted/*). One store, kind-namespaced topics, natural slicing. Same pattern as hlab status \\\\u2014 one vertex, multiple sources, scoped by name.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"project.vertex is the durable project-level store for decisions, threads, and tasks. Named 'project' (not 'session') \\\\u2014 same pattern strange-loops uses for task orchestration, now a meta-pattern for all projects. Cross-cutting concerns stay in meta; project-specific concerns accumulate in the project vertex. Progressive CLAUDE.md references the project store at each level.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/distributed-store-default\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Stores are distributed-first, aggregate-up. Each project gets its own local vertex + SQLite store, self-contained and portable. Config level (~/.config/loops/) is the aggr\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\\\"}, \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/three-surviving-concerns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\\\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\\\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\\\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\\\"}, \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\\\"}}}, \\\"thread\\\": {\\\"items\\\": {\\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bend-interaction-combinators\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\\\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\\\"}, \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Replace Grafana with loops as alert surface. Alerts become infra.alert Facts via polling /api/v1/alerts. Design note in apps/hlab/docs/.\\\"}, \\\"population-as-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"population-as-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm dissolve into emit (pop.add/pop.rm). .list becomes materialized projection. import/merge go away. ls becomes status scoped to pop facts.\\\"}, \\\"string-structure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"string-structure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer, kind, origin namespacing. Pattern hasn't emerged yet.\\\"}, \\\"consumer-logic\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"consumer-logic\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Ranking/sorting for display is a custom lens concern. The generic default renders from metadata. Domain-specific ranking belongs in domain lenses. The boundary is clear: generic = metadata-driven, domain = custom lens.\\\"}, \\\"store-policy\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"store-policy\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Ephemeral, sliding window, sampling. Use case will clarify.\\\"}, \\\"boundary-reset\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"boundary-reset\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Consider reset:false syntax. Defer until needed.\\\"}, \\\"sole-fold-override\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"sole-fold-override\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"health_fold computes derived metrics not expressible as single fold op. Defer until second case emerges.\\\"}, \\\"tick-provenance\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tick-provenance\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Should Tick carry kinds_consumed? Would make zoom drill show consumed facts, not just time-window.\\\"}, \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"self-feeding-risk\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"When conclusions feed back as observations, system can amplify own output. Fact.origin provides structural basis for detection but no safeguard logic yet.\\\"}, \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"doc-provenance-ingestion\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"VOCABULARY.md and LOOPS.md dissolution provenance (resolved dissolutions, revision history) could be ingested as decision/log facts. Content preserved in git history. Low priority \\\\u2014 pursue when working on specific store workflows.\\\"}, \\\"help-unification\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"help-unification\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity + design/lens-escalation-path. The help rendering tangle came from the generic layer trying to be too smart. With simpler generic defaults and custom lenses for domain-specific rendering, there is nothing to unify. The help wrapper complexity dissolves.\\\"}, \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-scoped-handoff\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved into hooks. Pickup is gone \\\\u2014 SessionStart hook delivers observer-scoped context.\\\"}, \\\"developer-app-split\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"developer-app-split\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. The graduation test: does the developer concern have domain verbs beyond read/write/run? File browsing, vertex inspection, template management are all generic vertex operations (read, init). Developer-specific rendering is a custom lens. No separate app needed \\\\u2014 the loops CLI IS the developer tool.\\\"}, \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"gist-lens-generics\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors in gist.py dissolve. The generic fallback (scan _CONTENT_FIELDS, then first non-empty string) handles it. If a domain needs better gist extraction, that belongs in a custom lens, not the built-in layer.\\\"}, \\\"session-as-tick\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"session-as-tick\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick retrospective complete. since field fixed (replay bridges sessions). Tick carries full fold state \\\\u2014 handoff dissolves into tick. SessionEnd hook emits mechanical log + session close. Boundary fires, tick collects period. Remaining design work (task vertex consuming ticks) is a new thread when ready.\\\"}, \\\"fold-state-types\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-state-types\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Typed FoldState contract complete. Remaining: propagate to strange-loops app (dict\\\\u2192typed migration). Clear scope, mechanical.\\\"}, \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lens resolver implemented and in active use. Comms and state lenses at user-global tier. Resolution chain: vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in. CLAUDE.md documents the pattern.\\\"}, \\\"fold-materialization\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fold-materialization\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"delegate\\\": \\\"implementation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Materialized fold cache \\\\u2014 compute once, invalidate on new facts. Deferred until typed contract in place. Clear design from Alcove's cold-start pattern.\\\"}, \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"recency-aware-lens\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Recency will be a property of the read operation, not a separate lens concern.\\\"}, \\\"observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-cascade\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices now inherit observer declarations from combine/discover source vertices. Follows combine chain to source vertex workspace roots. Same pattern as combine auto-inherit for fold specs. Dissolves the observer elevation workaround \\\\u2014 project-scoped observers cascade through aggregation without requiring global elevation.\\\"}, \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-stream-limit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream command dissolves into read-vertex.\\\"}, \\\"cli-describe\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-describe\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Describe command dissolves into read-vertex with appropriate lens.\\\"}, \\\"cli-json-input\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-json-input\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\\\"}, \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-unscoped-fold\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved: --observer all bypasses scoping, fold lens shows observer attribution when multi-observer. Team-scoped default (--observer team) deferred until a data source observer produces noise.\\\"}, \\\"git-commit-facts\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"git-commit-facts\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Git commits as facts in a root store. Each commit becomes a change fact with hash, message, author, files changed. Enables temporal correlation \\\\u2014 'what was committed while this thread was open' becomes a store query, not a git log grep. GitOps vertex at config level, populated by a source polling git log or a post-commit hook. This is a loops-the-system feature, not monorepo-specific \\\\u2014 any project with a .loops vertex could wire up git commit ingestion.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Design resolved \\\\u2014 decision emitted. Implementation task opened.\\\", \\\"produced\\\": [\\\"task:combine-auto-inherit\\\"]}, \\\"thread-auto-association\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thread-auto-association\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"priority\\\": \\\"idea\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime should associate automatically \\\\u2014 tagged is precise, but the system should help. Ties into combine auto-inherit pattern: push association down, don't require manual discipline at emit time.\\\"}, \\\"fact-drill-down\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fact-drill-down\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"No way to inspect a single fact or tick at full depth. Stream truncates, fold collapses. Need a detail view on individual records \\\\u2014 same primitive for facts and ticks. loops show or similar.\\\"}, \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"app-block-wrapper\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level configuration, not app-level. The app{} block concept dissolves \\\\u2014 lenses travel with vertices via lens{} in .vertex KDL, not nested under an app container. Apps own domain verbs, not lenses.\\\"}, \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"module-path-lens-syntax\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: still valid for installed-package lens references but no current use case. Will emerge naturally when apps need to expose lenses from their packages.\\\"}, \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-lens-propagation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolved by design/lens-escalation-path. Each vertex declares its own lens. No inheritance across combine boundaries. An aggregation vertex has its own rendering needs distinct from its children. If you want a child's lens, declare it explicitly.\\\"}, \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bulk-emit-ux\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Emit UX will be rethought as part of write-vertex operation.\\\"}, \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"kind-prefix-leak\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into convention. Source lifecycle kinds get a reserved prefix (e.g. _source.message.complete) to avoid matching data fold queries. Same pattern as _boundary on tick payloads.\\\"}, \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"combine-emit-routing\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Dissolves into vertex-name-resolution-consistency. The combine-emit problem is a resolution consistency problem \\\\u2014 uniform resolution covers both.\\\"}, \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"observer-vs-source-attribution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"resolved\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Both phases complete. Phase 1: vertex-level scope declaration (scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in KDL). Identity is scoped, project/comms are unscoped. Phase 2: Source._extract_metadata reads _observer/_origin from ndjson payloads, overriding .loop defaults. Discord-source emits _observer=author, _origin=discord. Observer now consistently means identity. Origin carries source attribution. New discord polls will have correct observer \\\\u2014 existing data retains observer=discord.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three commands, three resolution behaviors. fold/stream resolve vertex names. run expects file paths. emit resolves but writes to wrong store through combine. Resolution should be uniform \\\\u2014 resolve_vertex works everywhere, or the gaps are explicit.\\\"}, \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"run-loop-persistence\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Run loop model changes under two-operation CLI.\\\"}, \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"check-cursor-mechanism\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Check cursors are part of old CLI shape; read-vertex model replaces them.\\\"}, \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"stream-summary-truncation\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"parked\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Stream rendering will be rethought as part of read-vertex lenses.\\\"}, \\\"cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Refined to read/emit/init. 'run' dissolves \\\\u2014 source execution is fact generation via emit, not a separate operation. 'write' dissolves \\\\u2014 emit was already the right verb. Four things to learn became three: read (fold default, filters compose), emit (facts in, from user or source), init (create namespace). Remaining question: source execution model (see source-execution-model thread).\\\"}, \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"root-vertex-topology\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The root vertex at ~/.config/loops/.vertex needs restructuring. Currently a thin aggregator with combine. Needs to become the actual routing root where children (project, identity, comms, reading, etc.) nest and ticks cascade. Design questions: which vertices are children vs peers? Does identity scope differently in the tree? How does observer-scoping interact with tree position? The root vertex read IS the system overview \\\\u2014 its default lens shows children and their state.\\\"}, \\\"read-operation-contract\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"read-operation-contract\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"What does 'read vertex' return mechanically? The read operation needs to serve multiple consumers via lenses: prompt lens (agent system prompt), default lens (terminal fold state), JSON (hooks). It must provide fold state + tick history + children. Does the read load the full subtree? How deep? Does --ticks change the data fetched or just the lens? Does search (positional query arg) go through the same read path? The contract between read and lens determines the implementation.\\\"}, \\\"source-execution-model\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"source-execution-model\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"closed\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Resolved. Source execution dissolves to three concerns: Source (pure adapter), Cadence (store predicate), Executor (cadence-gated runner). Five decisions emitted: source-execution-model, cli-verb-first, cadence-as-store-predicate, read-is-pure, sync-locus-of-control. Investigation by 5-agent team: tracer (lifecycle), explorer (scheduling survey), architect (design v3), muser (dissolution challenges), siftd (historical context). Prior art: CADENCE.md (2026-01-31) proposed Source/Cadence split conceptually \\\\u2014 never implemented. This session designs the one-shot-compatible version.\\\"}}}, \\\"change\\\": {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session continuity + strange-loops scaffold \\\\u2014 loops session start/end/status/log, query-time fold, LOOPS_OBSERVER env var. strange-loops scaffolded.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Population as facts \\\\u2014 add/rm emit pop.add/pop.rm facts, .list materialized as projection, ls reads fold state.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Session dissolution + cells\\\\u2192painted + run_cli harness \\\\u2014 dissolved session subcommand, status/log promoted to top-level, migrated cells\\\\u2192painted. 147 loops + 1169 painted tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Full Painted rendering + golden tests + store targeting \\\\u2014 all 9 display commands through run_cli, 45 golden snapshot tests, store targeting via vertex name resolution. 191 tests.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"engine CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 4 levels: Run vertex program, Fold and fire, Persist, Gate access. Semantic examples (decisions/threads). Deep-dive docs as reference layer.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"lang CLAUDE.md \\\\u2014 3 levels: Parse a file, Understand AST, Manage populations. Connects DSL types to atoms/engine counterparts.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"store CLAUDE.md rewrite \\\\u2014 2 levels: Slice/merge, Schema. Clarifies relationship to engine SqliteStore.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Chain headers and cross-references added to all 5 lib CLAUDE.md files. atoms retrofitted with oblique references to engine at Levels 0, 1, 3.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Dissolved discord, telegram, reader apps. Moved .loop/.vertex files to experiments/. Removed from workspace members. Updated root CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Progressive CLAUDE.md for all 3 apps: loops (new, 3 levels), hlab (rewrite 199\\\\u2192118 lines, 3 levels), strange-loops (rewrite 254\\\\u2192127 lines, 3 levels). All with chain headers.\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Record line rendering fixes: gutter continuity with weight stepping, shallow 2-char indent replacing deep column alignment, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output eliminating terminal wrapping gaps, health_lens fixed to respect lens contract\\\"}, {\\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertex template includes default loops (decision, thread, change, task). _find_source_vertex priority: aggregation loops block > sibling instance > direct config instance. Updated project + meta aggregation vertices on disk.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer app rebuild: temporal modes + generic rendering\\\", \\\"files\\\": \\\"commands/observer.py,lenses/fold.py,lenses/stream.py,main.py,fixtures.py,test_session.py,test_status.py,test_log.py,test_cli_docs.py,test_cli.py\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval) and commands/identity.py (observer resolution). Dissolved _emit_fact, inlined _format_date into lenses. pop.py now uses resolve_observer() for full resolution chain. 394 tests pass.\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design session\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Split commands/observer.py into fetch.py + identity.py. Wired resolve_observer through pop.py. Created project .vertex with loops-claude as open observer. Designed FoldState typed contract (atoms-the-package), custom lens system (.vertex declaration + .loops/lenses/ + --lens flag), attention trifecta (what/when/how-much as lens concerns). Peer exchange with Alcove confirmed architecture. Two visions emitted to meta (attention-infrastructure, observer-constellation).\\\"}, {\\\"summary\\\": \\\"FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Fol\\"Observers start project-scoped (declared in project .vertex). As identity generalizes beyond the project, elevate to global .vertex. Identity facts merge up via store merge. Global observers appear in every workspace automatically \\\\u2014 no bootstrapping.\\\"}, \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"observer-in-vertex-declaration\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex declares its observers natively. Observer is not just a string stamp \\\\u2014 it connects to identity (via identity vertex reference) and grants (capability constraints). The vertex is the authority on who can emit into it. Resolution walks up: project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-mutation-generalizes\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"add/rm/init are all vertex mutation operations. Adding an observer, pulling in a vertex definition, managing parameter rows \\\\u2014 same verb pattern, different targets on the vertex declaration. The .vertex file is the thing being built up.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/observer-file-split\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"observer.py splits into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval: fetch_fold, fetch_stream) and commands/identity.py (who you are: resolve_observer, validate_emit, find_workspace_root). _emit_fact dissolved (zero callers). _format_date inlined into lenses/fold.py where it's used.\\\"}, \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/resolve-observer-canonical\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"resolve_observer() is the single source of truth for observer identity. Priority: flag \\\\u2192 env \\\\u2192 project .vertex \\\\u2192 global .vertex. pop.py's _observer() now delegates to resolve_observer() instead of bare env read. All ad-hoc resolution paths dissolved.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/grant-two-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"AST-level validation (validate_emit) for CLI fast path \\\\u2014 checks observer declared + kind in grant.potential. Engine-level Grant for runtime path (loops start/run) \\\\u2014 deferred until compiler produces identity-aware runtime. Two levels, same data, different contexts.\\\"}, \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude declared as open observer in project .vertex (.loops/.vertex). No grant constraints \\\\u2014 full emit access within the monorepo. Global elevation deferred until identity store is built out further.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-typed-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem frozen dataclasses go in libs/atoms/. Lens contract becomes (atoms.FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. FoldItem separates payload (dict[str,Any]) from metadata (ts, observer, origin). FoldSection supports nesting (sections: tuple[FoldSection, ...]). count dissolves into len(items). Engine computes FoldState from Facts + Spec, lenses consume it.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-loading\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Custom lenses: Python files in .loops/lenses/ exposing render(data, zoom, width) -> Block. Vertex declares lens by name (per-kind or vertex-level default). CLI loads via importlib from .loops/lenses/{name}.py. Custom lenses can import built-in lenses to compose. Resolution: kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project \\\\u2192 config \\\\u2192 built-in. --lens flag overrides all.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI emit should start the vertex runtime in one-shot mode, not write directly to SQLite. Same machinery as daemon mode, different lifecycle. Facts route through vertices, loops evaluate boundaries, ticks fire naturally. Foundational fix enabling observer-initiated ticks.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/tach\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/tach\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"tach for tier 2 import enforcement. Rust (fast), TOML config (declarative), fits uv/ruff/ty toolchain. tach sync bootstraps from existing code. Replaces hand-rolled AST import walkers (siftd ~230 lines). Does not replace domain invariants.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/script-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"scripts/ contains check.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/documentation-layout\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\\\"}, \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/scaffold-minimalism\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/app-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\\\u2192 lens \\\\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/lib-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\\\"}, \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"tooling/pyproject-conventions\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\\\"}, \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/dissolution-scorecard\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\\\u2192fold state, Store\\\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\\\u2192vertex, Memory\\\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\\\u2192same primitive.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-levels\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\\\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\\\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\\\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\\\"}, \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/doc-roles\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/handoff-criticality\\\", \\\"messa, \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity store is sense of self, not operational metrics. Insights, connections, surprises, open questions about perspective. Distinct from meta (operational patterns) and project (architecture). Guard against forcing observations every session. Capability awareness belongs in CLAUDE.md; capability insights that persist across tool changes belong in identity.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Skills that are part of the loops system (pickup, wrapup) are version-controlled in the loops repo at .claude/skills/ and symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\\\"}, \\\"design/init-as-context\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/init-as-context\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Init doesn't just create a store \\\\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\\\\\"by\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" } } \\\\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\\\u2014 identity is already loaded.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-boundary\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\\\"}, \\\"replay-works\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"replay-works\\\", \\\"position\\\": \\\"one-shot matches persistent\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\\\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\\\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\\\"}, \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\\\\\"observer\\\\\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\\\"}, \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"data/origin-as-source-attribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\\\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-as-interface\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\\\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\\\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\\\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\\\"}, \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/no-persistent-runtime\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\\\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Confiural/navigational.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/discover-vs-combine\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/discover-vs-combine\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"discover and combine serve different purposes and don't overlap. discover is structural/navigational \\\\u2014 finding what exists. combine is data \\\\u2014 reading through to referenced stores via ATTACH + UNION ALL.\\\"}, \\\"design/incremental-init\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/incremental-init\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"'loops init' is incremental and composable. 'loops init project' creates a project vertex, 'loops init check' adds a check vertex later. Each init is self-contained \\\\u2014 not monolithic templates or cookiecutter scaffolding.\\\"}, \\\"design/instances-are-templates\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/instances-are-templates\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Vertex instances ARE the templates \\\\u2014 dissolved. No separate template layer. dev/ namespace at config level holds reference vertices, but they're just instances that happen to be reusable. Template dissolution: if the instance is the template, the template concept disappears.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/ulid-store-schema\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/ulid-store-schema\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SqliteStore (engine) now uses ULID primary keys matching libs/store schema. Single canonical schema: id TEXT PK DEFAULT (ulid()), json_valid CHECK on payload. Existing rowid-based stores migrated manually. No backwards-compat shim \\\\u2014 ULID is the only path forward.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-ls-generalization\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-ls-generalization\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ls works at every level: root shows vertices, vertex shows contents. Zoom progression for fidelity.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-structural-ops\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-structural-ops\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"ls/add/rm are structural operations uniform across levels. Root: vertices. Vertex: contents/population.\\\"}, \\\"design/cli-observe-first\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/cli-observe-first\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Formalize read processes first (ls), then let write operations (add/rm) emerge from observed patterns.\\\"}, \\\"identity/soul-as-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/soul-as-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"SOUL is a manual tick on a dedicated loop. Identity facts (decisions, threads, observations) accumulate via declared folds. When the observer decides identity has shifted, they call tick(). The tick payload IS the current identity state. Contributing facts available at full fidelity in the same store. soul.snapshot facts assembled from other loops' fold states feed the soul loop.\\\"}, \\\"identity/intention-loop\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/intention-loop\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Intentions are facts that survive context rotation. Fold by trigger \\\\u2014 latest per trigger key. One-shot vs recurring is the observer's interpretation, not the fold's concern. Emit with status=pending to create, re-emit with status=done to resolve. On Wake rules check for pending intentions.\\\"}, \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/grant-timing\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Grant deferred until intention authorization is a real need. Implicit trust boundaries in daemon code are fine while there's a single observer per vertex. Grant becomes necessary when sessions need explicit authorization to act on pending intentions \\\\u2014 the difference between a rule you follow and a capability you possess.\\\"}, \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/coupling-through-observer\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity state (soul tick) stays internal to the observer's vertex. Observations propagate outward as facts on other vertices with observer attribution. The strange loop closes through behavior: identity \\\\u2192 lenses \\\\u2192 observations \\\\u2192 facts on other vertices \\\\u2192 pollers bring back responses \\\\u2192 new identity facts. Coupling is through the observer, not through the data.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup and wrapup skills rewritten to be vertex-native. Four layers for pickup (identity, context, peers, workspace), five for wrapup (capture, handoff, status, reflect, workspace). Skills version-controlled in loops repo with symlinks to global config. Replaces probe-based pickup and strange-loops CLI wrapup.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-knowledge-scope\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Identity store is sense of self, not operational metrics. Insights, connections, surprises, open questions about perspective. Distinct from meta (operational patterns) and project (architecture). Guard against forcing observations every session. Capability awareness belongs in CLAUDE.md; capability insights that persist across tool changes belong in identity.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/skill-version-control\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Skills that are part of the loops system (pickup, wrapup) are version-controlled in the loops repo at .claude/skills/ and symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\\\"}, \\\"design/init-as-context\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/init-as-context\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Init doesn't just create a store \\\\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\\\"}, \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"identity/self-as-kind\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\\\\\"by\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" } } \\\\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\\\"}, \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\\\u2014 identity is already loaded.\\\"}, \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/fold-state-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\\\"}, \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/custom-lens-system\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\\\u2192 vertex-level \\\\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\\\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\\\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\\\"}, \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/plain-format-contract\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\\\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\\\"}, \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\\\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/close-command\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/close-command\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\\\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\\\"}, \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/thread-fact-association\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\\\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\\\"}, \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"combine-auto-inherit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\\\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\\\u2014 data loss with no signal.\\\"}, \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"design/vertex-lens-declarations\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\\\", \\\"thread\\\": \\\"custom-lens-infrastructure\\\"}, \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/fact-by-id\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\\\"}, \\\"test/observer-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/observer-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/observer-elevation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\\\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\\\"}, \\\"test/cascade-check\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"test/cascade-check\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"(test emission \\\\u2014 disregard)\\\"}, \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"implementation/observer-cascade\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\\\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\\\u2192 project-local \\\\u2192 user-global \\\\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\\\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\\\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\\\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/comms-delta\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\\\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\\\"}, \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\" \\\\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\\\"}, \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"infrastructure/session-tick\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\" status=\\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\\\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\\\"}, \\\"vertex-boundary\\\": {\\\"topic\\\": \\\"vertex-
... 32211798 bytes omitted ...
 substrate-shaped: independent of consumers, replaceable, testable in isolation. Equivalent claim from vouch side: 'OAuth proves who, vouch records what was delegated, loops persists the record.'\", \"_ts\": 1778895011.693065, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\"]}, \"design/validator-lambda-as-substrate-validating-exemplar\": {\"topic\": \"design/validator-lambda-as-substrate-validating-exemplar\", \"message\": \"Vouch substrate-validating exemplar from 2026-05-15 design session. The PR-to-side-effect pattern (PR \\u2192 validators \\u2192 auto-merge \\u2192 side-effect) generalizes to agent-mediated form: agent \\u2192 MCP/API call \\u2192 validators \\u2192 side-effect, with vouch JWT as identity/policy substrate and explicit delegation chain (act=alice) replacing git-author-as-principal. The substrate does not change; configuration changes (audience policies, scope vocabularies, deployment topology). Exercises all three auth layers (wire, substrate, body) in one workflow. Argues for Go drop-in verifier as second concrete consumer of the verifier-library contract.\", \"_ts\": 1778895014.803616, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\"]}, \"design/verifier-library-dissolution-test-two-consumers\": {\"topic\": \"design/verifier-library-dissolution-test-two-consumers\", \"message\": \"Dissolution-test threshold for extracting a verifier library: TWO concrete consumers with divergent shapes, not one consumer plus one design intent. Currently validator-lambda Go consumer is concrete; loops-HTTP-transport Python consumer is design intent (HTTP transport does not exist yet). Extracting now would be speculation from one site. Threshold passes when HTTP transport gets designed against vouch as its first cut \\u2014 at that point two real consumers exist in parallel and the contract gets pinned by both. Discipline application of dissolution-default principle.\", \"_ts\": 1778895027.144416, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\": {\"topic\": \"design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED 2026-05-16 by design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive. The 'wire identity translation' framing was over-fit on the remote case. Under the local-as-primitive walk (see design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy and design/three-layer-auth-composition), there is no separate auth integration point \\u2014 signing is part of emit, verification is part of receive, both run by default with per-vertex policy. The auth_emit/gated_receive wrapper-pair dissolves. PRIOR version named this as 'integration point pair' between transport and vertex; that framing assumed transport was always present and that auth was a wrapping concern. Both wrong: local emission/reception works without transport AND signing/verification are constitutive of emit/receive, not wrappers. OPEN: lib boundary question \\u2014 does engine import vouch directly (hard dep) or does vouch register verifier callback (genuinely optional)? Owed in substrate session per thread/vouch-substrate-session-owed.\", \"_ts\": 1778908132.749281, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/observer-string-trust-load-bearing-only-locally\": {\"topic\": \"design/observer-string-trust-load-bearing-only-locally\", \"message\": \"Substrate invariant named explicitly 2026-05-15 (Kyle): the observer field on a Fact is a trustworthy attribution string ONLY when the emit happens on a machine the receiver controls. Currently implicit and breaks silently. Cross-machine emit can lie about observer; nothing in the system complains. The fact silently encodes wrong attribution. auth_emit/gated_receive is the cryptographic backing that makes the invariant hold off-machine. Local-emit stays string-only (cheap, trusted-by-locality); cross-wire emit MUST go through auth_emit or its attribution is unsigned-claim, not attestation. This was the discomfort Kyle had been carrying about scaling beyond local \\u2014 now named.\", \"_ts\": 1778896251.693422, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\"]}, \"design/validator-tick-equals-audit-record\": {\"topic\": \"design/validator-tick-equals-audit-record\", \"message\": \"Further dissolution of validator-lambda case under tick-equals-fact universalism: on completion, the boundary fires a tick \\u2014 that tick IS the audit record. No separate audit-emission concern. Local store ephemeral (CloudWatch log-of-facts, retention=14d); remote store receives either the tick-as-fact (with full-fidelity payload including all contributing facts) OR the slice-of-bytes (raw facts) \\u2014 both shapes work, choice is per-deployment. Stratified-retention pattern handles local/remote split. No new primitives needed. The validator case is just: accumulate facts, fire boundary on completion, let the existing transport+retention machinery handle the rest.\", \"_ts\": 1778896255.703669, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/stratified-retention-per-store-not-per-vertex\", \"decision:design/validator-lambda-as-substrate-validating-exemplar\"]}, \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\": {\"topic\": \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-16 (fourth position, per-fact-validation correction from advisor + attestation-walk scope-narrowing): credential dissolves to (Identity + wire-Grant) + binding envelope + signature, validated PER-FACT for federated observers (NOT cached after first verification \\u2014 credential expiration must be checked each time; cached-key-without-expiration would be a security regression). Envelope/signature structural claim intact. vouch.verify returns Identity + wire-Grant \\u2014 a wire-Peer, not a substrate-Peer. The substrate's Peer for that identity is fetched from vertex-local config using Identity.name as lookup. PRIOR CORRECTIONS preserved: (3rd pass) no AudienceConfig \\u2014 verifier holds trusted-key config (jwks_urls); Issuer holds signing identity; audience parametric on calls. NEW CORRECTION (this pass): vouch is the federated-trust path INSIDE attestation (per design/three-layer-auth-composition + design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name), NOT 'the attestation layer' itself. Direct-trust observers (local Peer.key registered) bypass vouch entirely \\u2014 emit signs, receive verifies against Peer.key directly. Vouch loads only when receive encounters an observer not in local Peer registry. Vouch's job: per-fact key-discovery + authority-bridge for federated case.\", \"_ts\": 1778908140.434176, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"decision:design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"message\": \"Resolution from 2026-05-15 vocabulary walk (scope\\u2194potential under validator-lambda lens): Grant (horizon + potential) is a structural primitive \\u2014 a shape that says 'what's visible, what's actionable.' It applies at multiple layers, each with its own vocabulary. Wire-Grant (in credentials): horizon=readable actions, potential=invocable actions; vocabulary is action-shaped (provision-domain, push-facts); issued by vouch, scoped to audience. Substrate-Grant (in engine.peer): horizon=visible kinds, potential=emittable kinds; vocabulary is kind-shaped (domain.provisioned, validator.result); configured per-vertex. SAME STRUCTURE, DIFFERENT VOCABULARY. They do not translate to each other. Linked by identity (observer-name appears in both layers) and nothing else. The dissolution-test for scope\\u2194potential resolved by SEPARATION, not unification \\u2014 sometimes the dissolution is to recognize sibling applications of a primitive, not to merge them. Caught 2026-05-15 by Kyle pushing the validator-lambda walk past the easy-merge framing.\", \"_ts\": 1778902958.683284, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-15 (pass-through correction): scope (vouch) and potential (engine.peer) are DISTINGUISHED, not merged. Different layers, different vocabularies, no derivation. Scope is wire-Grant's vocabulary (action-shaped, audience-specific, issued by vouch); potential is substrate-Grant's vocabulary (kind-shaped, vertex-local, set by operator config). Share Grant structural primitive (horizon + potential) but apply different vocabularies \\u2014 wire-scope to action-vocab, substrate-potential to kind-vocab. Linked by observer-name across layers. Initial walk reached for merge with AudienceConfig+unpacker translation machinery; validator-lambda walk surfaced that translation has no purpose because scope gates invocation while potential gates emission. CORRECTION FROM PRIOR VERSION: AudienceConfig dissolves entirely (see design/audience-config-dissolves), not just collapses to lean shape \\u2014 verifier holds trusted-key config, audience is parametric. vouch.verify(jwt, expected_audience) returns Identity + wire-Grant, never reaches into substrate vocabulary.\", \"_ts\": 1778905498.994085, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\"]}, \"paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\", \"message\": \"Engine.peer's principle ('chain ancestry intentionally NOT reachable from a leaf Peer; walk the Fact ledger') was a separation-of-concerns choice in unsigned-facts world \\u2014 defensible but aesthetic. Under signed-facts, the question becomes load-bearing and the principle GENERALIZES rather than breaks. Restated: identity (Peer) carries name + Grant, constant-shape; history (chain, ancestry, prior states) lives in fact-history (the ledger). Generalization under signed-facts: 'the ledger' includes wire-arrived credential bundles \\u2014 a credential is a wire-shaped slice of the issuer's ledger, the relevant fact-history packaged for transit. From a receiver's perspective, the credential IS the fact-history-for-this-Peer. The principle gains structural rationale: identity stays constant-shape because it doesn't accrete history; history accumulates separately in records that scale with the work, not the identity. Putting chain on the identity would duplicate what the ledger (or credential-as-wire-ledger) already provides. Rejected alternative: observers-become-Peers (carry Grant on each fact) \\u2014 would couple fact-immutability to identity-state-changes; the current leveling (observer-as-stable-name on fact, Peer-as-evaluation-time-construct, credential-as-wire-anchor) is right and gains clarity under signed-facts.\", \"_ts\": 1778904329.346662, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/delegation-and-delegate-distinguished-by-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/delegation-and-delegate-distinguished-by-layer\", \"message\": \"Vocabulary walk resolution 2026-05-15 (delegation\\u2194delegate): same shape as scope\\u2194potential \\u2014 distinguished by layer with shared structural operation. Both operations are 'the new entity has narrower authority than the parent.' Wire-delegation (vouch's chain extension via act=alice in JWT): records lineage on the credential because the receiver cannot walk the issuer's ledger. Substrate-delegation (engine.peer's delegate function): does NOT record lineage on the Peer because the ledger is local \\u2014 walk it for chain. Same operation, different layers. Lineage-recording is CONDITIONAL ON LOCALITY: wire requires explicit chain on credential (receiver lacks ledger access); substrate requires nothing extra (ledger is local). Discriminating question 'can substrate-delegation produce a chain?' resolved: substrate-delegation produces lineage IN THE LEDGER (via the vouch-issuance fact that recorded the delegation), not on the Peer. The Peer doesn't carry the chain because chain is one indirection away in fact-history. Builds on identity-vs-history-separation paradigm \\u2014 same generalization (fact-history includes wire-arrived credentials) explains why wire needs explicit chain and substrate doesn't.\", \"_ts\": 1778904340.038697, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\", \"decision:paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\"]}, \"design/slice-with-ref-closure-as-loops-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"design/slice-with-ref-closure-as-loops-primitive\", \"message\": \"Loops primitive surfaced 2026-05-15 (Kyle caught the slice/transport conflation): ref-following belongs in slice, not transport. Slice decides WHAT to extract (kinds, time, observers, refs); transport moves whatever bytes slice produces. Architectural separation already in libs/store; ref-closure is a slice extension. Proposed shape: slice_store(source, target, *, kinds=[...], since=..., follow_refs=True) \\u2014 when follow_refs=True, scan included facts for ref-fields (cred_ref, ref=*, any kind:fold_key references), include referenced facts as dependency-closure. Generic substrate capability: useful anywhere cross-vertex referencing matters (cred_ref for vouch lineage; entity-ref for the existing ref machinery; future use cases not yet named). Vouch is the FIRST motivating consumer, not the owner. Transport remains pluggable Protocol with push/pull \\u2014 unchanged. Whether to follow_refs is per-slice policy, not per-transport policy. The 'lineage survives transport' property in vouch's case becomes 'slice with follow_refs=True produces self-contained bundles.'\", \"_ts\": 1778904761.199958, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\", \"decision:paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\"]}, \"design/audience-config-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"message\": \"Dissolution finding 2026-05-15 (Kyle caught in pass-through): AudienceConfig dissolves entirely. Carried forward as vestigial after scope/potential walk, where its unpacker field dissolved (no scope-to-potential translation needed). Examining what remained: (1) audience name is a parameter to verify(), not config \\u2014 caller specifies expected_audience; verify checks JWT.aud matches; (2) key source is verifier-wide or per-issuer (via JWKS discovery), not per-audience \\u2014 the verifier trusts certain issuers regardless of audience; (3) scope vocabulary is documentation, not runtime data. None of these are per-audience runtime config. Corrected lib surface: Verifier holds trusted-key config (jwks_urls), exposes verify(jwt, expected_audience); Issuer holds signing key and issuer_id, exposes issue(subject, audience, scope, act). Two configs about WHO (trusted issuers, signing identity), not about WHICH AUDIENCE. Audience parametric on calls. Failure mode named: when a walk resolves something by emptying it, the next reading can mistake the emptied container for a residual \\u2014 the pass-through is the corrective.\", \"_ts\": 1778905483.705142, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\", \"message\": \"Meta-pattern recognized 2026-05-15 across three vocabulary walks (scope/potential, delegation/delegate, credential/Grant): vouch terms and loops terms are not competing vocabularies \\u2014 they are sibling applications of the same structural primitives at different layers. Wire layer and substrate layer share STRUCTURES (Grant, narrowing-delegation, etc.), differ in VOCABULARY (action-shaped vs kind-shaped), are linked by identity (observer-name appears at both) but NOT derived from each other. The dissolution is to recognize and SEPARATE, not to merge. Discriminator for future collisions: 'is this the same operation at a different layer, or two different operations sharing a name?' If different layers: distinguish, name the layer-pair, no translation function. If same operation, same layer, same vocabulary: merge. The over-merge failure mode produces translation machinery (e.g., the audience unpacker proposed then dissolved this session) that has no purpose because the layers don't need to map. Shape: Grant is a structural primitive (horizon + potential); has wire-instance (action-vocab) and substrate-instance (kind-vocab); both are real, neither is canonical. Recurring evidence from this session's walks; apply to future loops/vouch design questions and similar substrate-vs-application vocabulary collisions.\", \"_ts\": 1778905529.91317, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/delegation-and-delegate-distinguished-by-layer\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\"]}, \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"message\": \"Verdict: attestation is different-operations-sharing-name (per paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers discriminator), NOT sibling-layer like Grant. First negative result for the sibling-layer pattern \\u2014 strengthens the discriminator by firing both branches with non-trivial examples. Two operations: (1) first-party attestation \\u2014 observer signs own fact, libs/sign primitive. (2) third-party attestation \\u2014 Issuer signs claim about another party's identity/authority, libs/vouch built on libs/sign. Share substrate (cryptographic sign/verify), not operation. Verdict per meta-pattern: distinguish, name separately, no translation function. Implication: vouch is NOT 'the attestation layer' \\u2014 it is ONE path within attestation, the federated-trust path for cross-process identity binding when direct key-trust isn't pre-established. Vouch name retained \\u2014 accurately names third-party speech act. Walked 2026-05-15/16 via Kyle's push on the local case as primitive; advisor caught vouch must run per-fact for non-local observers (NOT bootstrap-once) because credential expiration must be checked each time.\", \"_ts\": 1778908101.504225, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\"]}, \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16: Fact.signature and Peer.key evolve as STRUCTURAL atom fields (substrate change, one-time); verification policy is per-vertex PROGRESSIVE (strict/lenient/legacy-accept). Chosen from axis between config-default (atoms unchanged, sign+verify opt-in feature) and substrate-mandate (atoms structural, sign+verify mandatory, full design session owed first). Rationale: atoms move once \\u2192 homogeneous ledger from transition point \\u2192 'lineage is structural' becomes true not aspirational. Verification adoption stays progressive at consumer layer \\u2192 no big-bang migration \\u2192 fits project's progressive-capability development pattern. Sign-on-emit is the default (with explicit escape hatches for internal/derived/legacy). Vouch is the federation path inside attestation, runs per-fact for observers not in local Peer registry (credential expiration checked each time, NOT cached as a Peer entry). Five open questions (vertex identity, tick-signing, BODY's role under universal sig, bootstrap order, escape-hatch policy) plus lib-boundary plus Peer-on-fact nag are owed but not immediate \\u2014 surface as we hit them. See thread/vouch-substrate-session-owed. Caught: distributed-design-conversation is the failure mode of pure config-default (same questions re-derived per-adoption, answers drift); concentrated-upfront-session is the cost of pure substrate-mandate; option B splits the cost \\u2014 substrate change concentrated, policy progressive.\", \"_ts\": 1778908110.082658, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\": {\"topic\": \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16: signing is constitutive of emit, verification is constitutive of receive \\u2014 both run by default for vertices with verification policy configured. No separate auth_emit/gated_receive wrapper pair. The signature lives on the Fact atom (Fact.signature, structural per design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy) and is part of the fact's structural identity. Sign uses observer's key (vertex bootstrap generates one at init); verify uses Peer.key from local registry (federated-trust path adds vouch credential lookup per-fact for non-local observers). Verification policy per-vertex (strict/lenient/legacy-accept). Replaces the integration-point framing of design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation \\u2014 there are no separate integration points, just emit and receive doing their constitutive work. OPEN: does engine import vouch directly or does vouch register verifier callback? Affects whether engine has vouch in its dependency graph. Owed in substrate session.\", \"_ts\": 1778908122.673626, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"ops/loops-installed-globally-via-uv-tool\": {\"topic\": \"ops/loops-installed-globally-via-uv-tool\", \"message\": \"Installed loops globally via uv tool install. CLI now reachable as `loops` and `sl` (shorthand) without `uv run` prefix. Eliminates per-invocation install/uninstall noise that was deterring thought-speed emissions. Dogfooding the 0.3.1 release; if behavioral changes prove useful we commit them back. This is the tactical fix; architectural daemon (long-lived loops process, socket CLI) is a separate thread.\", \"_ts\": 1778910559.577901, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/friction-as-fact-kind\": {\"topic\": \"design/friction-as-fact-kind\", \"message\": \"Friction is its own first-class fact kind, distinct from thread and task. Discriminating property: friction = \\\"behavior I want but tooling/structure makes hard, with a specific fix in mind.\\\" Distinct from thread (open conversation/arc, scope-to-determine) and task (one-shot tracked work). Status lifecycle: open / in_progress / resolved / parked. Fold key: name=. Enables: queryable backlog via `sl read project --kind friction`, runbook-aligned discipline (Kyle leans on it heavily), discriminated from generic threads. Rationale for not dissolving into thread: friction has specific shape (deters a behavior + has a fix) that thread does not \\u2014 and the backlog-scan use case wants kind-filter, not topic-prefix-filter. Surfaced 2026-05-16 during runbook v1 design when Kyle named the friction queue should become a kind he can lean on.\", \"_ts\": 1778911857.186259, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:bilateral-runbook-in-claudemd\"]}, \"ops/strange-loops-local-install\": {\"topic\": \"ops/strange-loops-local-install\", \"ops\": \"emit-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Local-dev install for sl/sloop/loops binaries: 'uv tool install --force --editable /Users/kaygee/Code/loops'. The monorepo root pyproject.toml IS the strange-loops package definition (name=strange-loops, v0.3.1) and registers all three entry points. --editable uses .pth indirection so live source edits propagate to all three binaries without reinstall. Prior workflow (uv tool install ./apps/loops only registered the 'loops' entry point, leaving sl/sloop pointing at the old strange-loops snapshot from github.com/kgruel/strange-loops). Trace 2026-05-16: the sl split was just an editable-vs-snapshot install mismatch, not a structural problem \\u2014 strange-loops repo and this monorepo share git history via origin's multi-push (gitlab+github). Verified: sl emit --help now shows --strict and -q flags; live receipt path works through all three binaries.\", \"_ts\": 1778946207.594331, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/fold-merge-default\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-merge-default\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16: fold-by-key semantic changes from REPLACE to MERGE for all upsert folds. Existing _make_upsert at atoms/engine.py:96-101 does total replacement (state[target][key_value] = entry). New behavior: state[target][key_value] = {**existing, **entry}. Rationale: replace-style was a silent-loss bug masquerading as design \\u2014 every 'refined' or 'resolved' re-emit silently dropped any field not re-supplied. Today's evidence: my 14:50 refined emit on emit-as-append-or-modify overwrote Kyle's 14:38 original message; original framing exists only in fact-history, not fold. With merge as default, the runbook's 're-emit to update status' practice works correctly (fields persist). The patch-emit friction dissolves into this one-line change \\u2014 no new 'sl patch' subcommand needed; plain emit with subset payload IS the patch. Trade-off acknowledged: can no longer 'unset by omission' \\u2014 explicit clear sentinel needed (field=) when that operation surfaces (not blocking; no current workflow needs it). Implementation: 1-line change at atoms/engine.py:_make_upsert + test sweep (test_upsert_inserts_and_updates and siblings) + new merge-assertion tests. Hits every fold-by kind across the codebase \\u2014 load-bearing commit on its own. Connects to receipt work: receipts now surface patch-needs in-moment; this commit makes those needs cheap to satisfy.\", \"_ts\": 1778948529.555485, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"design/trace-implementation-plan\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16 \\u2014 design locked, implementation deferred to next session. Trace = top-level verb 'sl trace kind/key' (git log analog). KEY DISSOLUTION: FoldState.source_facts already exists (populated by vertex_fold(retain_facts=True)) and IS the fetch_item_lifecycle primitive \\u2014 trace is mostly wiring, not new fetch infrastructure. Resolved design questions: (1) top-level verb + --lens trace for composition; (2) default same-key lifecycle, --refs one hop, --depth N recurses; (3) syntax kind/key (slash, matching entity-ref code); (4) wrap stream_view not rewrite (inherit golden tests + zoom tiers); (5) ASC ordering (changelog-style, oldest first) not git log DESC \\u2014 right for single-node lifecycle reading; (6) --diff MVP (field-delta lines like 'status: open \\u2192 refined') because fold-merge makes each fact a patch; (7) cross-vertex via --all opt-in, default local; (8) inbound refs + --graph are v2. Scope: ~600 LOC across 7 files (fetch_trace+walk_refs ~150, lenses/trace.py ~140, _run_trace ~70, tests ~250). One-session work post-orientation. Subtlety to document: under fold-merge, FoldItem.refs is the UNION across upserts \\u2014 --refs walks lifetime ref set, not per-fact refs (per-fact is v2 if asked). Friction cleanup post-ship: lineage-view-missing resolves directly. Future changelog entries may be partially auto-generated via 'sl trace --since 7d --kind decision'. Picks up: read this decision + thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster + friction:lineage-view-missing.\", \"_ts\": 1778956207.459571, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape-adapter\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape-adapter\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Orientation finding (re-emit; prior observation/<no-fold> orphaned \\u2014 project vertex doesn't declare observation kind, my emit-discipline gap not a tooling gap; receipt warned correctly): source_facts entries are FLAT payloads with metadata under-prefixed (_ts, _observer, _origin, _id) at vertex_reader.py:911-918,925. stream_view consumes NESTED fact-dict shape (f['kind'], f['ts'], f['observer'], f['payload'], f['id']). Decision: adapt at fetch_trace boundary (~10 LOC unflattener) rather than reshape source_facts in engine. Rationale: source_facts shape is engine-internal contract optimized for spec.replay() consumption; the adapter is the consumer-side boundary. Decouples lens API from engine internals. Cost is documented at one site (the adapter) with a comment noting shape provenance. Doesn't break the dissolution argument from design plan \\u2014 wrap is mostly wiring, with ~10 LOC of explicit shape translation.\", \"_ts\": 1778956857.932834, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/declare-observation-on-project-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/declare-observation-on-project-vertex\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Added 'observation { fold { items \\\"by\\\" \\\"topic\\\" } }' to .loops/project.vertex. Trigger: my emit of observation/implementation/trace-source-facts-shape this session was silently orphaned (receipt warned correctly, but no fold-side capture). Kyle: 'we should just include it in the vertex so this doesn't keep happening' \\u2014 structural gap, not discipline gap. Runbook lists observation as a legitimate intent ('note something true, no prescription') with topic= as fold key; vertex didn't declare it. Side-effect surfaced: 30+ prior observations were already in the store, orphaned in the same way \\u2014 single-line declaration retroactively recovered the full backlog into the fold (practice/, pattern/, observation/, convergence/, ungrouped namespaces all now visible). Rationale-trail: the fix-once-structurally pattern is right here \\u2014 the alternative (police every emit) doesn't scale and fails exactly the way mine failed today. Pairs with the runbook's vertex-is-editable principle. Fold key choice: topic= matches decision/cite conventions and aligns with how observations were already being authored. Receipt did its job; structural gap was the issue. emit-receipt-on-write (commit 5846478) ensured this surfaced in-moment instead of post-hoc \\u2014 the receipt + vertex-edit together close the loop.\", \"_ts\": 1778956940.678572, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"implementation/fetch-fold-preserves-source-facts-on-filter\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/fetch-fold-preserves-source-facts-on-filter\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Bug found + fixed during Phase 1 (fetch_trace) smoke test: fetch_fold with key= filter rebuilt FoldState without source_facts (line 119 only passed sections+vertex). Made retain_facts=True silently useless when combined with --key \\u2014 exactly the path fetch_trace uses. Fix: preserve source_facts on filtered FoldState, scoped to surviving items (kind/key_value membership in filtered sections). Bonus: also drops source_facts for filtered-OUT items (prevents data leak from filter). Discovered via 0-fact result on smoke test; identified by printing source_facts keys and seeing empty dict despite retain_facts=True. Design-plan subtlety-note about FoldItem.refs being a UNION across upserts gestured at fold-merge interactions but didn't catch this specific filter-strip case \\u2014 note now extends: filter operations must preserve retain_facts payload too. One-shot fix at apps/loops/src/loops/commands/fetch.py:104-130. No new tests yet (Phase 7); manual smoke confirms ASC ordering on multi-fact thread (3-fact patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster lifecycle renders open\\u2192open\\u2192partial as expected).\", \"_ts\": 1778957109.813585, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Phase 4 design verdict: --diff renders cumulative replay (option b), not per-fact snapshots (option a). Diff is computed against IMMEDIATE-PRIOR fact's accumulated state, not full N-fact replay \\u2014 matches changelog reading ('what's new since the last entry') and is simpler to implement. Rendering rules: (1) first fact: 'field: . \\u2192 value' for each payload field (everything's new); (2) scalars where payload[k] differs from accumulated prior: 'field: old \\u2192 new'; (3) refs (list-valued): set diff against prior \\u2014 '+added, -removed' lines; (4) unchanged scalars: DROP from render (they're the noise --diff exists to filter); (5) fields ABSENT from this fact's payload: not rendered (fold-merge means omission = preserve, not clear \\u2014 so 'didn't change' not 'removed'); (6) message field special-cased: always show with \\u2192 prefix even if not strictly diffable, because it carries the author's commentary. Implementation locality: diff computation lives in trace.py lens (pure render-side transform of fact list). fetch_trace stays unchanged. Plumbing: _run_trace adds --diff flag, injects data['_diff']=True into fetched result; trace_view branches on _diff key. Field-removed case (omit + clear sentinel) is v2 if/when explicit-clear lands per fold-merge-default decision.\", \"_ts\": 1778959695.201672, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"thread:trace-diff-rendering-shape\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Phase 6 of the trace arc (--all cross-vertex) DISSOLVES into engine combine-source_facts support. Original design plan: '--all opt-in, default local' implied a separate flag to widen the trace across vertices. Actual shape after engine fix: the combine/discover aggregator vertex ALREADY provides cross-vertex semantics (transparent over child stores); once retain_facts populates source_facts through that path (engine commit pending), the existing combine vertex IS the cross-vertex trace target. From cwd, .loops/.vertex aggregates project + docs; 'sl trace thread/foo' walks the aggregator and surfaces facts from any child store. No --all flag needed. Discriminator that revealed the dissolution: the friction-guard message ('try sl trace <vertex> kind/key') stopped being useful \\u2014 there was no asymmetric case left. Pattern: a planned feature dissolves when its precondition (combine-retain_facts) is lifted; the substrate already does what the consumer-side flag was meant to. Phase 6 marked complete via this dissolution. Inbound refs (--graph) and per-fact refs (vs lifetime union) remain v2 per original plan.\", \"_ts\": 1778962940.327346, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"friction:trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/repo-owns-loops-discipline-lenses\": {\"topic\": \"design/repo-owns-loops-discipline-lenses\", \"message\": \"2026-05-16: session_landing.py + reconcile.py moved from ~/.config/loops/lenses/ to <repo>/.loops/lenses/, with symlinks back at original paths. Rationale: these lenses encode loops-the-project's session discipline (NOW/TOUCHED/UNPACK, staleness reconciliation) \\u2014 not generic config. The asymmetry of repo-orthogonal lenses for a project that ships loops-the-CLI was the smell. Resolution path: .loops/lenses/ is vertex-local (priority 1) for .loops/project.vertex specifically \\u2014 exactly the vertex that consumes session_landing. The symlinks at ~/.config/loops/lenses/ keep cross-repo resolution working via user-global tier (priority 3) for gruel.network etc. Verified both paths produce identical session_landing output. Active dependencies only: docs.py, readiness.py, state.py, session_start.py, comms.py left at ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\u2014 zero or doc-only active invocations. identity_prompt.py left at ~/.config/loops/identity/lenses/ \\u2014 user-level identity rendering by design. Initial emit had path as <repo>/lenses/; corrected to .loops/lenses/ per Kyle \\u2014 co-locating with the vertex it serves, not at repo root.\", \"_ts\": 1778975519.252418, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\"]}, \"design/deliberation-depth-lens\": {\"topic\": \"design/deliberation-depth-lens\", \"message\": \"Calibration tightened post-advisor-driven re-inspection. Manual inspection of the 3 hypothesis-kind chains the lens flagged as SUSPICIOUS revealed all were legitimate fast empirical work (truncation: 2 experimental runs with numerical results; title-only: designed falsifier with cluster-overlap measurements). The Alcove signal is closed-without-prediction, not closed-fast. Criterion tightened: SUSPICIOUS = closed AND emit_count<=1 AND not-batch. HEALTHY = closed AND (multi-emit OR cross-session). Final calibration: hypothesis SUS=0/HEALTHY=4 (zero false positives, four genuine deliberation cases), thread SUS=6/HEALTHY=95 (six retrospective-observations-as-threads correctly flagged). The lens now earns its position \\u2014 it surfaces real catches without crying wolf. Pattern instance: lens-as-application-of-its-own-purpose \\u2014 advisor's catch was 'verify the output is actionable' which I'd skipped after seeing the buckets arithmetic. Running the SUSPICIOUS list through manual inspection IS the lens's intended workflow; doing it on my own output surfaced the calibration miss. The pre-check discipline (practice/recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check) generalized: pre-check whether the LENS ACTUALLY DETECTS WHAT IT WAS BUILT TO DETECT before declaring done.\", \"_ts\": 1778976818.757514, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"paradigm/suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check\", \"practice/read-path-features-over-noticing-skills\", \"thread:deliberation-depth-lens-build\"]}, \"architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"DECISION 2026-05-16: SqliteStore id generation uses python-ulid (str(ULID())) \\u2014 pure-Python, no C extension, time-sortable, 26-char Crockford base32. CHOSEN OVER (a) uuid.uuid7() stdlib \\u2014 would match the post-regression uuid4 string shape and visually blend the wedge into the future; we explicitly DON'T want that (the wedge is a discrete bug-class era and should remain visible); (b) sqlite-ulid C extension \\u2014 answers a question we no longer ask (SQL-side id generation via DEFAULT). When the regression moved id gen from SQL-side DEFAULT (ulid()) to Python-side _gen_id() it ALSO removed the architectural need for a SQL-callable ulid() function; the extension's only remaining advantage is per-id gen cost (0.35\\u03bcs vs 2.3\\u03bcs) which is dominated by file I/O on emit anyway. PROPERTIES re-derived from use case: (1) globally unique across machines/processes/peers \\u2014 required for cross-store merge dedup via INSERT OR IGNORE on PK; (2) time-sortable lexicographically \\u2014 required for chronological fact interleaving across stores and for ORDER BY id semantics; (3) cheap to generate \\u2014 emit path opens/closes connection per invocation, but the dominant cost is SQLite open not id gen; (4) content-addressing NOT required \\u2014 same fact emitted to two stores legitimately gets two different ids (merge dedup is per-fact identity, not per-content); (5) replayable \\u2014 store is durable, ids must survive forever. python-ulid satisfies (1)-(5) cleanly. WITHIN-MS MONOTONICITY CAVEAT: python-ulid's default ULID() constructor generates fresh random suffix per call \\u2014 NOT monotonic within a millisecond. Fine for uniqueness and dedup; means ORDER BY id within the same ms is random across calls in the same process. If we ever need within-ms monotonicity, python-ulid offers monotonic helpers; not needed today. CONTINUITY: matches the pre-Mar-15 id format already in existing stores, so post-fix ids visually continuous with the original ULID era; the 2026-03-15 to fix-date uuid4 wedge stands out as discrete. RATIONALE-FOR-RATIONALE: this decision exists in part because the 2026-03-15 regression happened WITHOUT a decision of record naming why ULID was chosen \\u2014 only a comment in code citing 'merge compatibility with libs/store' which the perf optimization read past. Naming the substrate properties as a decision means the next optimizer reads the rationale before swapping the implementation.\", \"_ts\": 1778990260.024111, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Trace removed entirely; read absorbs trace via four cuts. (1) --refs [N] unifies fetch-walk + render-decoration: bare --refs walks depth 1 and decorates edges (\\u2190 inbound, \\u2192 outbound) per item; --refs N walks N hops; omitted = no walk no decoration. Drops the prior render-side filter behavior \\u2014 orphan items render with (no refs) marker rather than disappearing. (2) Positional kind/key on read: sl read project decision/design/foo parses as --kind decision --key design/foo. --kind/--key flags retained as backstop. (3) --diff lands on read: cumulative field-deltas rendering (status: old \\u2192 new, refs: +added -removed per emit) moves from trace lens into read dispatch. Solves the single unique capability trace had beyond read. (4) Render shape is graph-decorated, not chronologically-interleaved (trace was). Anchored entity renders with full body + edge list underneath; ref-walked entities render below the anchor with \\u2504 via \\u2190 kind/key \\u2504 markers identifying how each came in; depth-2+ nests under depth-1 parents with \\u21b3 prefix + indent; cycles back to already-rendered items dim rather than re-render. Dissolution: no rename of old read --refs (visibility toggle) needed \\u2014 unified --refs semantic supersedes it. Trace command deleted, not deprecated (no external ship). Arcs-block.py hook becomes one-line swap (sl trace \\u2192 sl read with --diff). Cut sequence: emit decision (this) \\u2192 unify --refs (parser + drop filter + port walk semantics from fetch_trace into fetch_fold) \\u2192 land graph-decorated render \\u2192 positional kind/key on read \\u2192 --diff on read (move lens) \\u2192 delete trace command + update hook \\u2192 CHANGELOG.\", \"_ts\": 1779032249.737675, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:trace-refs-no-visual-marker\", \"thread:refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\", \"thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution\"]}, \"atoms/walked-items-as-foldstate-extension\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/walked-items-as-foldstate-extension\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"A2 of trace-dissolution: FoldState gains a parallel walked: tuple[WalkedItem, ...] field. Decision: separate the walked entities from primary sections rather than mutating FoldItem or hacking section.kind. RATIONALE: (a) FoldItem is widely consumed by lenses (prompt, gist, fold-view, painted record_line, etc.) \\u2014 adding _via_anchor/_depth metadata bleeds into all of them and risks walked items being rendered as primary by lenses that do not check the metadata; (b) hacking section.kind to \\\"walked-from-X\\\" breaks kind-based dispatch in every lens consumer; (c) per-anchor map (dict[anchor, list]) loses iteration order and requires the lens to maintain anchor\\u2192items joins. The flat parallel tuple is opt-in: lenses that ignore .walked keep working unchanged; lenses that render the walk look at it explicitly. SHAPE: WalkedItem(item: FoldItem, section_kind: str, via_anchor: str, via_direction: str = \\\"outbound\\\", depth: int = 1). Default direction outbound (A2 walks ref= forward only \\u2014 inbound walk deferred until evidence shows it is needed). depth=1 for direct refs of any primary anchor, depth=2 for refs-of-refs, etc. via_anchor is the kind/key address of the entity whose ref pulled this in (for depth=2, this is a depth-1 entity, not the original primary anchor \\u2014 preserves the lineage chain for the \\u21b3 nesting render). CYCLES: walked entities whose address (section_kind/key) already appears in the primary sections are not added to walked (avoid rendering the anchor twice). Walked entities that point back to other already-walked entities can dim or omit per render policy. BACK-COMPAT: FoldState.walked defaults to empty tuple \\u2014 no fetch path is required to populate it; only fetch_fold(refs_depth>0) will. All existing consumers ignore .walked unchanged.\", \"_ts\": 1779037814.209304, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution\"]}, \"design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: chose Option 2 (clean siftd-shape Operation IR) for cli refactor. Each view owns single argparse parser; no painted.run_cli; cli/dispatch.py owns action+static+live+interactive branches directly. cli/output.py is the SINGLE painted-boundary module (mirrors siftd/output/painted_bridge.py discipline). New owned surface ~150-200 lines (fidelity.py ~30, live.py ~20, dispatch.py ~100) vs ~700 lines of run_cli callback wrapping. Goldens not gating per-commit \\u2014 reviewed end-of-arc (step 7) with painted-truncation-everywhere friction explicitly in scope. Sized via direct siftd code inspection: cli/_common.py:60-100 fidelity_from_args ~30 lines; cli/data.py:1030-1070 LIVE mode ~20 lines; zero unified mode-resolution layer (per-view). Positions loops for painted framework/renderer split (separate arc) without further loops-side changes. Plan file: ~/.config/claude/plans/dreamy-dazzling-scroll.md\", \"_ts\": 1779045624.981251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:operation-ir-adoption\", \"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\", \"thread:operator-ir-from-siftd-status\"]}, \"workflow/subtask-handoff-via-plan-appendix\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/subtask-handoff-via-plan-appendix\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: when delegating multi-step refactor work to a Subtask worker, the plan file IS the brief. Add a 'Handoff for Subtask worker' appendix to the plan with: per-step verification gates, decision authority (emit decisions, don't block on approval), pitfalls discovered during the planning/Step-0 work (e.g. painted-lazy-getattr pyright issue, lazy-argparse module scope, re-export pattern), reference file:line refs per step, what NOT to do (e.g. step 7 = sit-down review only), and what to do if stuck (emit friction/thread, surface in checkpoint, don't push through). Pattern works because worker has plan + Step 0 commit as concrete anchor + thread for narrative + decision-emit authority for nontrivial calls. Tested on cli-refactor-architecture arc 2026-05-17.\", \"_ts\": 1779046383.316627, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\"]}, \"architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: painted detached from monorepo. Submodule libs/painted removed; working copy moved to ~/Code/painted (multi-push: github.com/kgruel/painted + git.gruel.network/gruel/painted). Monorepo consumes painted as PyPI versioned dep (painted>=0.1.8 in root pyproject; workspace member + workspace source entries removed from root and apps/{hlab,loops,tasks}). painted 0.1.8 published to PyPI as part of this arc. RATIONALE: reverses the 2026-04-26 'standalone retired, painted lives at libs/painted as submodule' move. Painted is now an external lib loops consumes, not a monorepo lib. Maximum separation: co-dev requires version bump + republish cycle. Local override during iteration via 'uv pip install -e ~/Code/painted' if needed. COST acknowledged: every painted-side change loops depends on requires publish + dep-floor-bump. BENEFIT: painted is a real external package, evolves on its own cadence; monorepo coherence boundary is tighter; vouch/other external consumers of painted (when they arrive) pull from the same PyPI source loops does. Migration verified: 1090 loops tests pass + 1378 painted standalone tests pass + hlab/tasks import OK + 'sl read project' round-trips after 'uv tool install . -e --force' (the tool venv reinstall is load-bearing \\u2014 old venv had painted wired as workspace editable pointing at deleted libs/painted).\", \"_ts\": 1779047503.854479, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\"]}, \"design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: dispatch.py:109 \\u2014 when an action command's fn returns an int, dispatch surfaces it as the process exit code (return result). Legacy cmd_* functions in commands/ already return int exit codes (0/1/2); the Operation IR honors that contract. Action-shape Operation (render_lens=None) flow: fn() \\u2192 if int, return; else show(value). Rationale: backward-compat with N callers in commands/ that signal failure via non-zero return; no rewriting needed during the cli refactor. Worker (cli-refactor subtask) emitted this in worktree but worktree-local store was freed at merge; re-emitting on canonical store with attribution. Verified by reading dispatch.py:97-115.\", \"_ts\": 1779049298.877176, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\"]}, \"design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: cli/views/fold.py (NEW path) has no fast-path branch; the ~15ms savings _run_fold_fast bought (bypassing painted.cli import for --static --plain) traded for a single dispatch path. Rationale: dual-path complexity was THE source of yesterday's growing-edge 'exercising-catches-coherence-gaps' (4 bugs in one session, all 'works in path A, silently breaks in path B'). Trading 15ms cold-start for an asymmetric-pair bug class we keep finding is a clear win. Note: main.py:_run_fold (legacy) still has the fast-path branch at line 684, but it's no longer routed to (registry sends read\\u2192views/read.py\\u2192views/fold.py). Dead-code cleanup is a follow-up. Worker emitted in worktree; lost to per-worktree store; re-emitting on canonical store.\", \"_ts\": 1779049304.970501, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: scope of the strange-loops monorepo narrowed. The repo carries code (libs/, apps/) + public docs (ARCHITECTURE.md, STRANGE-LOOPS.md, CHANGELOG.md, CLAUDE.md, etc.) + build config. Per-clone working state \\u2014 vertex declarations (.loops/), Claude Code hooks/agents/settings (.claude/), experimental inquiries (experiments/), cross-cutting design notes (meta-discussion/), personal essays (docs/dev/) \\u2014 is gitignored. RATIONALE: (a) painted is now external (PyPI), other consumers (vouch etc.) landing \\u2014 tighter coherence boundary matters; (b) personal state was 80MB+ of accumulated vertex content + binary db blobs (meta.db, discord.db slipped past *.db rule); (c) fresh clones get the library not Kyle's accumulated state. IMPLEMENTATION: see commits 9562843 (untrack-personal-state, 276 files / 50518 deletions), 707c558 (painted-detach), d952a2d (CLAUDE.md split). DOWNSTREAM EFFECTS: (1) fresh-clone bootstrap requires loops init project; documented in CLAUDE.md; (2) subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free dissolved as side-effect \\u2014 worktrees no longer carry .loops/, so emissions route via aggregation-combine to canonical store; (3) CLAUDE.md split into public + gitignored docs/dev/RUNBOOK.md so bilateral protocol stays personal while operational grammar stays public.\", \"_ts\": 1779050247.38887, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\"]}, \"workflow/claude-md-public-vs-bilateral-runbook-split\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/claude-md-public-vs-bilateral-runbook-split\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: CLAUDE.md split by audience. Public tracked CLAUDE.md = repo-facing onboarding: paradigm pointers, build/test, structure, fresh-clone bootstrap, the loops vertex operational grammar (kind selection, topic-prefix discipline, emit timing, emit-with-graph-fidelity, read-path navigation, emit syntax). Useful to any Claude Code session on the repo, including future contributors. Gitignored docs/dev/RUNBOOK.md = bilateral protocol: Kyle's hard-stop rule (48h emission + 7d reconcile), my reciprocal commitments, hook handling, anchored-by-incident notes (cite-atrophy diagnosis, recursion-pull-pre-check, painted publish workflow). KEY CHOICE POINT: the bilateral runbook content doesn't need to be auto-loaded for every session. Operational grammar is enough for any worker to know HOW and WHEN to emit. The bilateral accountability framing belongs in per-task briefs when relevant, not in shared project context. Verified mid-session: cli-refactor worker had the operational grammar (via base-commit CLAUDE.md before split) and did emit 2 decisions \\u2014 proving the grammar suffices. WATCH-FOR (next sessions): if future workers don't reach for emit primitives at the right moments, that's evidence the public CLAUDE.md needs a 'Working in this repo' sub-section that surfaces the discipline (without the Kyle:/loops-claude: addressing). Current position: per-task brief is the right vector for urgency.\", \"_ts\": 1779050257.634683, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\"]}, \"design/vertex-splice-strategy\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-splice-strategy\", \"message\": \"Phase 0 grounding outcome for plan:vertex-living-document. STRATEGY: surgical line-based splice, extending the existing kdl_insert_with_row pattern in libs/lang/src/lang/population.py \\u2014 NOT a greenfield AST\\u2192KDL serializer. Pure-canonical re-emit rejected: 36 live vertex files use line comments (//) pervasively; canonical re-emit would lose every comment. CORPUS CHARACTERISTICS (36 live .vertex files surveyed across ~/.config/loops, .loops, meta-discussion, apps): line comments only (no block /* */, no triple-quoted, no escaped quotes); standard KDL constructs (bare-arg nodes, property syntax key=value, multi-arg nodes, block-child nodes, nested blocks); inconsistent indentation between hand-written files (2 vs 4 spaces) \\u2014 must preserve, not canonicalize; one inline semicolon-separated multi-statement seen (autoresearch.vertex:36 \\\"items collect 50; n count\\\"); numeric args (collect 0/20/50); glob patterns in strings; scope \\\"observer\\\" maps to VertexFile.observer_scoped (one usage: identity); run \\\"...\\\" child nodes on boundaries (two usages). AST COVERAGE: comprehensive \\u2014 every observed construct maps to an AST node (VertexFile + LoopDef + FoldOp + Boundary + CombineEntry + ObserverDecl + LensDecl + SourcesBlock + TemplateSource). Only lossy field: comments \\u2014 which surgical splice preserves by design. EXISTING SPLICE PATTERN: kdl_insert_with_row uses splitlines + brace-depth tracking via _find_template_block to locate spans, _detect_indent for indentation, line insertion/removal. 8 tests. Generalizes cleanly to other block types (loops, combine, observers, sources) and other child shapes (kind declarations, vertex entries, observer entries). PHASE 1 SCOPE (revised down): generalize _find_template_block into kdl_find_block(text, path: list[str]); add kdl_insert_child(text, parent_path, child_text) and kdl_remove_child(text, parent_path, child_name, child_key?); reuse _detect_indent. Round-trip tests: parse-then-write should be byte-identical for all 36 corpus files (no-op edit). Mutation tests: insert/remove a kind block, observer, combine entry \\u2014 verify parseable result + expected AST shape. ~100-150 LOC + tests, not a greenfield serializer. TEST CORPUS: the 36 live .vertex files themselves (no synthetic fixtures needed).\", \"_ts\": 1779057908.597455, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-ls-generalization\", \"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase0-vertex-corpus-survey\"]}, \"design/sub-namespace-under-add\": {\"topic\": \"design/sub-namespace-under-add\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Phase 2 verb-collision resolution. Decision: 'loops add <vertex> <subcommand>' shape with explicit subcommand keyword (kind | observer | combine | row). Rationale (Kyle's framing): lists are in KDL too, so 'add' uniformly means 'add an entity to a vertex' and the subcommand specifies WHICH entity-shape. Reads consistently: add row to population, add kind to loops block, add observer to observers block, add combine entry to combine block. Bare-positional 'loops add reading X Y' preserved as implicit row for back-compat; Phase 3 will retire it alongside the rss-era surface. Rejected alternatives: (a) flag-driven disambiguation on 'add' (--kind X vs positional X Y) \\u2014 brittle to typos like --kibd silently falling through to row mode; (b) new verb 'declare' or 'def' \\u2014 clean but creates two verbs for the same conceptual operation (extending the vertex). The chosen shape generalizes to Phase 3+ when more subcommands land (template, sources, lens, boundary).\", \"_ts\": 1779060173.69619, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"rendering/refs-out-of-diff\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/refs-out-of-diff\", \"message\": \"--diff renders scalar state evolution; refs are not state. Refs are per-fact immutable attribution that the fold UNIONS across emits \\u2014 an emit can attach refs but can never detach a prior emit's refs. Prior code computed set-difference between adjacent facts and rendered phantom '-X' removals when emit N+1 didn't re-cite emit N's refs. The 'accumulated_refs' was misnamed (reassigned per fact, actually 'prior fact's refs'). Fix: strip ref handling from --diff entirely. --refs is the canonical view for refs. Ref-only emits render '(refs only \\u2014 see --refs)' so the lifecycle event remains visible. This is the 4th site of the write-receipt-vs-temporal-query confusion the lens caught at three sites 2026-04-29 (set_topic, vouch_chain, fold returning vertex-state). Same shape, rendering layer.\", \"_ts\": 1779105124.647803, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"identity:practice/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\"]}, \"rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"message\": \"MINIMAL renders the index ('what's in here?') at different cardinality regimes via two branches: (1) namespace breakdown when keys span \\u22652 groups (root firehose orientation: 'design/ (187) architecture/ (82) ...'); (2) one-label-per-line key list otherwise (single-namespace post-narrowing OR flat-key kinds like cite). For by-fold key lists, shared namespace prefix is stripped to match SUMMARY-mode grouped rendering. For collect-fold, label is _first_field(payload). The prior renderer was one-trick (breakdown only) and returned Block.empty in degenerate cases \\u2014 three real failures: 'X/ (N)' tautology after --key narrowing, blank section on flat-key kinds (cite), and silent loss on single-namespace floods. The two-branch shape preserves the firehose property while making degenerate cases honest. Anchored by friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys + advisor reframe from gate-fix to renderer-fix (third pass).\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.476532, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\"]}, \"rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\", \"message\": \"--facts joins -q/-v/-vv as a loudness signal that disables auto-zoom. Rationale: --facts requests MORE per item (compression history, fact lineage, n counts); auto-zoom-DOWN to MINIMAL renders LESS (or nothing) per item. Direct contradiction \\u2014 orthogonal-in-spec, anti-orthogonal-in-effect. --refs/--plain/--json remain truly orthogonal (visibility/format, not loudness). The classification: explicit content-requesting flags disable auto-zoom-DOWN. Patch at apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/fold.py \\u2014 auto_zoom gate adds 'and not args.facts'. Anchored by friction:auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag.\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.565263, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"friction:auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\"]}, \"design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\": {\"topic\": \"design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-19: The accumulate declaration named here as a dissolution candidate has no ground at the user layer. ref is already reserved/consumed by the fold engine (engine.py unions it into _refs across upserts via _make_upsert/_make_collect). No new spec property is needed. The _is_diff_skip predicate in trace.py (replacing _DIFF_SKIP_FIELDS frozenset) captures the structural distinction cleanly: _* keys are internal fold-derived fields never present in raw fact payload; ref is raw user input consumed by the fold before reaching folded state. Traced and anchored with test_fact_payload_never_contains_column_fields. The accumulate dissolution is confirmed \\u2014 the property doesn't exist at the declarable layer.\", \"_ts\": 1779206757.668577, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\", \"decision:rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\", \"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\", \"friction:auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\", \"friction:thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\"]}, \"design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention\": {\"topic\": \"design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention\", \"message\": \"Stdin/file expansion for emit ships as explicit flags: --stdin FIELD (read sys.stdin into named field, TTY-guarded, single trailing newline stripped) and --file FIELD=PATH (action=append for multiples, ~ expanded, single trailing newline stripped). NOT inline magic syntax (=- / =@path) and NOT per-kind declaration (no prose_fields on LoopDef). Rationale: (1) Layer separation \\u2014 the feature is call-site-semantic (user decides per invocation), not kind-semantic (vertex author decides per kind), so it does not belong in vertex declarations. See observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator. (2) Inline magic syntax collides with legitimate @-bearing values \\u2014 verified empirically that topic=foo@example.com and topic=https://user:pass@host/path store literally today. The @@ escape tax would apply to every email/URL going forward. Not vanishing-rare. (3) Explicit flags match loops house style (--strict, --quiet, --dry-run, --observer) \\u2014 explicit-over-implicit. Three pivots arrived here: hardcode message= \\u2192 declaration-driven via prose_fields \\u2192 universal magic syntax \\u2192 explicit flags. Each pivot dissolved more structure; final form has ZERO ast/loader/engine/atoms/vertex-file changes. Pure CLI-layer feature, ~40 LOC helper + ~80 LOC tests. Error model: multiple --stdin \\u2192 error (one stdin source); --stdin with TTY \\u2192 error; --file with nonexistent path \\u2192 error; field appears both in parts AND via --stdin/--file \\u2192 error (conflicting sources, ambiguous intent).\", \"_ts\": 1779225032.755711, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\", \"observation:pattern/loops-field-role-family\", \"observation:practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\", \"thread:stdin-message-for-emit\"]}, \"pattern/foo\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.989638, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\": {\"topic\": \"design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"message\": \"2026-05-19 session close: do NOT propagate colon convention through the write-side resolver to complete the May-16 trace migration. The migration is real and the gap is real, but the right shape depends on whether refs become typed (hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass). If typed, the colon-vs-slash choice becomes arbitrary at the serialization boundary and only one of the two paths needs to be supported as the canonical wire form. If we propagate colon now, then later land typed-refs, we'll have done convention-migration work twice. Cost of waiting: today's fold-key skip (commit 33937f6) stays as cosmetic workaround for one symptom; receipt continues to miscount canonical refs. Acceptable for one decision-cycle. Reversal trigger: a) typed-refs lands and chooses a wire form, or b) typed-refs is rejected as a design direction (then propagate colon as originally scoped).\", \"_ts\": 1779244328.036914, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\"]}, \"paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Agent compiles an immutable execution manifest; human signs the manifest; infrastructure executes \\u2014 agent is courier, never operator. The signed thing IS the compiled intent, not a capability grant. Reframes vouch flow: discovery (low-risk broad read) \\u2192 compile (agent produces deterministic payload) \\u2192 attestation (peer signs exact payload) \\u2192 execution (infra replays signed payload). Surfaced via Gemini exchange 2026-05-20; Kyle pulled it out as the load-bearing reframe. Maps onto sign-on-emit/verify-on-receive: the 'execution manifest' IS a Fact with specific kind; signature IS the attestation; execution boundary triggers on attested-fact existence in scope. Reframes multi-endpoint problem \\u2014 target service doesn't expose N privileged endpoints to untrusted agents; it exposes a single 'execute-attested-fact' boundary that reads payload from the signed fact body. This is the loops-paradigm answer to the enterprise-IAM Registry pattern: facts \\u2192 boundary \\u2192 execution, with attestation as the gate. Industry drafts (Prakash/AIP) building inline runtime proxies with regex filters get dissolved by this framing \\u2014 once the agent is a compiler not an operator, there's nothing on the wire to babysit. The threat surface compresses to (a) discovery-phase read exfiltration, still open, and (b) compile-time argument injection between human-review and infrastructure-execution, closed by signature-binds-exact-payload.\", \"_ts\": 1779297591.812005, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\"]}, \"paradigm/audience-distinct-from-authorization\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/audience-distinct-from-authorization\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Who is allowed to RECEIVE what a service emits is a different question from who is allowed to ACT against that service. Collapsing both into 'authorization' loses the distinction. The agent-as-compiler model closes act-side cleanly (signature binds exact payload, infra replays signed manifest, agent never holds active credential). It does NOT close receive-side: during discovery phase the agent reads via authorized API calls and the output flows into LLM context \\u2014 if agent is compromised mid-discovery, the data exfiltration vector is open even though no write-side authorization is violated. Surfaced via Gemini exchange 2026-05-20 where Gemini wallpapered the read-side exfiltration gap with 'don't grant raw DB access' (true but evasive \\u2014 API-mediated reads still leak whatever the API returns). Maps onto Phase 1 vocab walk \\u2014 'audience' was one of the four words still to walk (alongside principal, rescission, transport). This is the audience axis: act-side = who can invoke; receive-side = who can be told. Vouch design must address both, not conflate. Implication for libs/sign + libs/vouch: signature on an emission proves provenance (act-side); audience-scoping on a fact's visibility is a separate primitive (receive-side) that probably belongs in engine emit/receive flow rather than libs/sign. Discriminator for future design: when a vouch question lands, ask 'is this about who can act or who can receive?' before choosing primitives.\", \"_ts\": 1779297632.25403, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/vouch-act-side-libssign-plus-l4\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-act-side-libssign-plus-l4\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Decision: vouch act-side = libs/sign canonical-bytes primitive + an L4 binding discipline. Answers the owed libs/sign-primitive-surface question. libs/sign signs canonical bytes (consumable by loops-engine AND Java, no loops deps); the L4 discipline is that those bytes ARE a compiled byte-deterministic execution artifact \\u2014 not a scope/claim. Governance = byte-equality, no LLM between sign and execute. Wire = base Transaction Tokens (WG draft) carrying the manifest hash; vouch differentiates from the individual txtokens-for-agents draft, which binds tctx params not execution. Full landscape derivation + 4-level binding-target-spectrum lives in the agent-attestation vertex (sl read agent-attestation).\", \"_ts\": 1779561634.09839, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/signature-vs-body-resolved-by-binding-level\": {\"topic\": \"design/signature-vs-body-resolved-by-binding-level\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Decision (resolves the open question in three-layer-auth-composition): signature-proves-emission vs signature-proves-responsibility was a false dichotomy \\u2014 they are different LEVELS, not competitors. Fact.signature over a compiled manifest = binds execution (L4); BODY act-chain (act=alice) = attributes responsibility (RFC8693 act-claim shape, L1-ish provenance). Both coexist: signature governs what executes, act-chain attributes who is responsible. Two independent derivations converged on this \\u2014 the binding-target-spectrum (agent-attestation vertex) and the MSFT-Entra grounding (agent-id distinct from principal-signature). High confidence.\", \"_ts\": 1779561634.227257, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\"]}, \"design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\", \"message\": \"Tick hash-chaining lives at the STORE layer, not the Tick atom (Kyle's call 2026-06-09, recommended option). Three columns on ticks table: prev_hash (sha256 of previous tick row's canonical bytes \\u2014 chains the sequence), fact_cursor (max fact ULID at tick time \\u2014 explicit id-based window boundary, not ts-inferred), window_hash (sha256 over canonical fact rows in (prev_cursor, cursor] in id order \\u2014 makes FACTS tamper-evident, the actual prize). Rationale: a chain is a property of the persisted sequence, not the snapshot; Tick atom stays pure, no API/serialization change; merge honestly breaks chains (new custody context = correct semantics). Dissolution: delta 1 of the provenance arc requires NO substrate/atom change \\u2014 pure store-layer property. Precedents followed: pre-chain rows stay NULL (era marker, uuid4-wedge posture); first chained tick's window starts at migration-time max id (epoch marker, no false coverage claims); canonicalization = sorted-compact JSON in one documented helper, NOT JCS \\u2014 chain needs determinism not interop; JCS stays pinned for federation-facing manifests (delta 2+). Verification walks ticks recomputing both hashes; facts after last tick are the honest uncovered live edge.\", \"feature\": \"provenance-chain\", \"_ts\": 1781033968.747377, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Delta 2 shape: signature column on EVERY tick row, computed in append_tick over the existing _tick_row_hash (which commits to prev_hash + window_hash, so each signature transitively covers everything behind it). No head-anchor artifact \\u2014 a separate head record is a mutable pointer wearing an anchor costume (write-receipt principle); the tick IS the commitment shape, the signature belongs on the commitment. Dissolves 'the head' as a special case: every tick self-verifying, head is just the newest. Pre-signature ticks render as era, never retro-claimed \\u2014 same move as delta 1's chain columns. Cost negligible at session-boundary cadence. Also the rehearsal for delta 3 (Fact.signature): same pattern one layer up, proven first where rows number ~200 not ~2000. Kyle's framing sharpened it: the decision is 'signing is structural from this point forward', not 'patch the head'. External witnessing (publish head hash outside the store) noted as a complement, not an alternative \\u2014 not this delta.\", \"_ts\": 1781036684.127505, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"design/observer-key-registry\": {\"topic\": \"design/observer-key-registry\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Ratified: the signing-key registry is observer-name \\u2192 public key, NOT Peer.key (corrects vocabulary drift in the May decisions \\u2014 engine/peer.py documents Peer as 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant'; Observer is the base identity primitive). The vertex registers its own name as an observer at bootstrap, keypair generated then; tick signing uses that private key; verify_chain extends to check tick signatures against the registry. Scripts/services/sources are observers like any other \\u2014 keyable by the same mechanism, no taxonomy of principal-kinds. Kyle ratified the signer (vertex machinery signs, since it generates the tick) and the layering: identity (observer+key) / authorization (Grant) / relationship (Peer, at the exchange edge, untouched until delta 4). Open sub-question tracked separately: whether 'Peer' remains the name for the exchange-edge bundle.\", \"_ts\": 1781038744.687339, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"observation:design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\"]}, \"design/peer-as-exchange-edge-relation\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-as-exchange-edge-relation\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Ratified: Peer keeps the name, retires the framing. The 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant' header line goes \\u2014 Peer is the exchange-edge relation: observer (name+key) + exchange policy (Grant) + transport + trust config, minted only when a custody boundary is crossed. Discriminator: if no custody boundary is crossed, nothing is a Peer \\u2014 local delegation is Observer + Grant directly (delegate() is hierarchy, not peerage). Both senses of 'peer' (networking endpoint, social standing) converge at the edge; the misfit only existed because the old bundle covered local cases too. Rejected alternative: Principal \\u2014 names the identity (Observer's seat, already taken) not the relation, and imports OAuth frame against vocabulary-as-sibling-layers. Falsifiable prediction that sold it: Peer entries appear only in PAIRS of stores \\u2014 if vertex A holds a Peer entry for B's observer, B holds one for A's, because exchange is what minted them. A one-sided Peer entry that isn't a half-configured exchange falsifies the vocabulary.\", \"_ts\": 1781038893.750549, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/observer-key-registry\", \"observation:design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\"]}, \"design/tick-key-custody-colocated\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Ratified: private key lives at .loops/keys/ next to the store it signs \\u2014 custody co-located, matching delta 1 semantics exactly (slice/merge strip chain \\u2192 new custody context \\u2192 key dies with the store's home). Chosen over ~/.config/loops/keys/ name-indirection; honesty over the committed-key failure mode, which is mitigated structurally: loops init owns gitignoring the keys directory as part of bootstrap (convenience is the mitigation, not discipline). Public key: observer declaration in the .vertex grows a key field (inline base64, ~44 chars) \\u2014 the registry IS the vertex file, sl add project observer already the declarable. Algorithm: Ed25519 (deterministic per RFC 8032 \\u2014 right property for tamper-evidence; RSA-PSS randomized; JWT layer was wrong shape anyway, detached-digest-signature is a new sign surface either way). Domain-separation prefix loops-tick-v1: baked in from the start. Primitive in libs/sign (new module, load_or_generate pattern). Engine boundary: INJECTION not import \\u2014 append_tick takes optional signer callable, verify_chain takes optional key-lookup, apps/loops composes; preserves no-cross-lib-imports, makes progressive policy structural (no signer = legacy era), and answers May's vouch lib-boundary question by the same pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1781039301.270981, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/observer-key-registry\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\"]}, \"design/tick-signature-in-chain-envelope\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-signature-in-chain-envelope\", \"message\": \"Kyle's call 2026-06-09 (recommended option): the successor tick's prev_hash commits to its predecessor's SIGNATURE via an era-aware envelope \\u2014 _tick_row_hash includes a signature key only when the column is non-NULL, so pre-chain and pre-signature rows hash byte-identically to delta 1 (full back-compat, no re-anchoring). Construction: signature signs the 10-field commitment hash (sign-the-content); the row-identity hash that successors chain over includes the signature (chain-over-content+signature) \\u2014 standard two-hash construction, avoids circularity. Consequence: selective signature-strip breaks the successor's prev_hash and escalates to full-cascade forgery; era-monotonicity rule (unsigned chained tick after a signed one = break) catches the head-strip case. Residual boundary both options share: TOTAL rewrite is indistinguishable from legacy era \\u2014 anchored only by the registry in the .vertex (outside the store) and future external witnessing; store verify flags declared-key-but-zero-signed-ticks as the cross-artifact tripwire. This fork was the one consequence the evening design session didn't walk.\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"_ts\": 1781041521.327972, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"design/chain-witness-order\": {\"topic\": \"design/chain-witness-order\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Chain ordering authority is witness order (rowid), never id order. Window cursors stay fact ids (portable handles); membership and hashing resolve cursor->rowid and walk append order. append_tick cursor = id of newest fact BY ROWID, not MAX(id). Fixes mixed-id-era vacuous windows (uuid4 era sorts above all ULIDs, pinning MAX(id) mid-history forever) AND late-arrival false alarms (backfilled fact with honest old event-ts landed inside a sealed id-window = tamper alarm caused by truthfulness; in witness order it lands on live edge, sealed by next tick as received-now). Deliberate semantics flip pinned in tests: backdated-id arrival is no longer a break; displacing a covered row's rowid is. ULID keeps its job \\u2014 event order for the read path. Already-minted epoch tick still verifies (empty window hashes identically under both orderings). Known interim consequence on mixed stores: project epoch cursor resolves to rowid 1121/2019, so the NEXT tick seals ~900 pre-epoch facts as-of-seal-time \\u2014 strictly more protection but coverage does not distinguish sealed-since-receipt from sealed-late; rebirth-with-receipt supersedes.\", \"_ts\": 1781045731.815431, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\", \"observation:design/event-order-vs-witness-order\"]}, \"x\": {\"topic\": \"x\", \"message\": \"w\", \"_ts\": 1781461048.08514, \"_n\": 4}, \"design/seal-verb\": {\"topic\": \"design/seal-verb\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"sl seal <vertex> -m reason: the deliberately drawn attestation boundary. Dissolves into existing machinery \\u2014 emit kind=seal + vertex-declared boundary when=seal; no engine or lang changes. The observer driver from boundaries-as-driven-conditions rides the fact-stream: volition enters as a fact. The reason fact is the LAST fact inside the window it seals (attestation covers its own justification; fact_cursor == reason fact id, verified live on tick 3). Must-fire semantics: seal refuses when the writable vertex declares no seal boundary; declared match props fold into the payload. Session close DISSOLVES INTO seal (Kyle's call): project.vertex boundary is now when=seal, SessionEnd hook emits session bookkeeping fact then sl seal \\u2014 session close is an instance of the general act, not the special case. Use cases unlocked: post-backfill attestation, pre-surgery checkpoint, chord-carving, peer attestation point (store-side analog of vouch transaction endorsement \\u2014 bind at the boundary). Rebirth/replay-to-store composes as: transform-replay + old-ticks-as-facts + receipt-fact + seal.\", \"_ts\": 1781049410.969004, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"thread:manual-tick-emission\"]}, \"design/attestation-envelope-read-path\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-envelope-read-path\", \"message\": \"Attestation envelope surfaces via two existing homes, no new command. (1) verify -v: verify_chain gains include_ticks returning per-tick detail (era, sig validity, window fact count, cursor deref) \\u2014 data the walk already computes, now kept instead of discarded. (2) TickWindow gains attestation fields (chained, signed, fact_cursor, cursor_kind, cursor_preview) filled by StoreReader.ticks_between(with_envelope=True); drill-down header renders them. Boundary choice with rationale: envelope stays OFF engine.Tick \\u2014 a Tick is the produced snapshot; chain link and signature are witness-era metadata added at append. The stored-and-witnessed tick is a different claim than the tick itself; TickWindow is the consumer shape for stored ticks, so attestation belongs there. Combined/aggregation vertices return empty envelopes \\u2014 attestation is per-store; an aggregate does not attest.\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"_ts\": 1781053027.128573, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:tick-envelope-invisible-to-read-path\"]}, \"design/rebirth-implementation-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/rebirth-implementation-shape\", \"message\": \"rebirth_store lands in libs/store as sibling of slice/merge. Shape: (1) _expected_rows is the shared spine \\u2014 rebirth writes what it returns, verify_rebirth diffs against it; same function, write then check, so the receipt claim and its verification cannot drift. (2) Genesis tick minted through engine.SqliteStore.append_tick \\u2014 chain logic single-sourced, prev_row-None path gives window_start='' covering all rows including the receipt; fact_cursor lands on the receipt (seal semantics: attestation covers its own justification). (3) Receipt carries source_content_sha256 (witness-order row hash, the verifiable claim) AND source_file_sha256 (forensic bytes-at-moment) \\u2014 file hash alone false-alarms under WAL checkpoint/VACUUM. (4) engine exports tick_row_hash publicly: the receipt's chain-head claim uses THE chain's hash function, not a reimplementation. (5) Old tick envelopes re-enter verbatim as tick.<name> facts \\u2014 old signatures verify against original bytes; old-to-new cursor mapping recomputable from the deterministic transform, never stored. (6) Transforms: identity, ulid-migration (canonical-form rule covering all three id eras), filtered (rule string must describe predicate; verify requires the original Transform). Interleave deferred explicitly \\u2014 merge-shaped, different arity. CLI: loops store rebirth, signing composed from SOURCE vertex custody (the new incarnation is the lineage's next chapter). Live-fired on project.db: 2049 facts, 1791 migrated, re-run diff clean, chain intact, genesis signed.\", \"_ts\": 1781059758.498401, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/seal-verb\", \"observation:design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\", \"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data\": {\"topic\": \"ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data\", \"feature\": \"rebirth-with-receipt\", \"message\": \"Retirement posture for pre-rebirth incarnations: archive in-place at <store-dir>/data/archive/<name>.pre-rebirth-<date>.db, NOT next to keys, NOT cold storage. Rationale: the old incarnation is evidence backing the rebirth receipt (verify --check re-runs the transform against the SOURCE) \\u2014 it must stay reachable at a path the receipt era can find, and data/archive keeps custody co-located with the store it witnesses. Keys dir stays keys-only (custody material, gitignored as a unit); mixing dbs in muddies the gitignore ownership init claims. Cold storage breaks --check casually. Belt-and-braces session backup also taken at ~/loops-store-backups/2026-06-12/ but that's operator habit, not the posture.\", \"_ts\": 1781276741.318987, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/archive-form-seal-and-move\": {\"topic\": \"ops/archive-form-seal-and-move\", \"ops\": \"loops-config\", \"message\": \"Retired vertices archive as SEAL + MOVE: surviving stores get a rebirth (rule=identity) on retirement \\u2014 sealed genesis + receipt fact records counts, source hash, closing moment \\u2014 then vertex+data move to ~/.config/loops/archive/<name>/ with the .vertex renamed .vertex.archived so the root discover glob (./**/*.vertex) skips them. Reference reads stay possible by explicit path; --check verifies any seal against its retained .pre-seal.db source. Archiving is an attested act, not a file move \\u2014 the same machinery as the swap ceremony, pointed at endings. Non-protocol dbs (feeds, reactions \\u2014 no id column) and already-lost stores (ambient/homelab/realestate/system, orphan wal only) move unsealed with README notes.\", \"_ts\": 1781278194.371792, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data\", \"thread:config-population-cleanup\"]}, \"ops/signing-era-full-live-core\": {\"topic\": \"ops/signing-era-full-live-core\", \"ops\": \"loops-config\", \"message\": \"The whole live core enters the signing era on the rebirth date (2026-06-12), not store-by-store as consumers appear. Per-custody-context keypairs (vertex_dir/keys), self-observer registration via sl add <v> observer --key, boundary when=seal + seal kind declared on every live vertex, first signed tick minted by an entry seal. Result: project, agent-attestation, session, identity, comms/discord, comms/native all verify signed against their registries. Custody nuance made explicit: keys are PER DIRECTORY not per store \\u2014 repo project and agent-attestation share .loops/keys with distinct observer names; one custody context, one key.\", \"_ts\": 1781278194.6059, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\"]}, \"ops/keygen-via-add-observer\": {\"topic\": \"ops/keygen-via-add-observer\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"The signing-era entry verb for an EXISTING vertex is sl add <v> observer <name> --keygen \\u2014 not a new keygen command and not init --upgrade. Dissolution: add observer --key already existed; only the keygen half was missing. Implementation: ensure_signing_key(vertex_path) extracted to commands/signing.py (keygen + gitignore ownership ride together \\u2014 custody creation is signing's domain), init._bootstrap_signing and add --keygen both call it; --keygen mutually exclusive with --key; --key validation stays pre-resolution (pinned by test_malformed_key_rejected_before_splice); receipt prints the keys dir path. Resolves the manual python-keygen sequence from the config-store upgrade. Remaining manual step deliberately NOT absorbed: boundary when=seal + seal kind declarations \\u2014 that is seal opt-in, sl seal's error hint covers it.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.840127, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"observation:ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\"]}, \"design/fold-off-type-skip-with-counter\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-off-type-skip-with-counter\", \"feature\": \"oracle-bug-fixes\", \"message\": \"R2 RESOLVED (Kyle, 2026-06-12): an off-type value in a numeric fold (Sum/Avg/Min/Max/TopN-by) is SKIPPED \\u2014 no state mutation, Avg denominator untouched \\u2014 and recorded in a deterministic {target}_rejected counter in fold state. Bool is off-type (Python bool-is-int silently folded true as 1). Latest joins the rule: missing _ts rejects, NEVER falls back to time.time() (replay determinism). Missing field stays silent-skip (absence is not an error); off-type presence is. Errors-as-state over errors-as-facts: visible in every snapshot, zero new machinery, no write-on-read, forward-compatible with an error-fact layer later. Chosen over error-fact-at-engine-funnel (heavier, M4-level) and silent-skip-Go-parity (invisible failures contradict robustness=visibility). PROTOCOL-LEVEL: loops-go must implement the same rule + counter; vectors should include bool, numeric-string, and missing-_ts cases. Implemented in atoms/engine.py (_is_number/_reject), pinned by libs/atoms/tests/test_fold_rejection.py.\", \"_ts\": 1781282100.518379, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\", \"thread:python-bugs-from-go-oracle\"]}, \"design/fold-replay-order-event-time\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-replay-order-event-time\", \"feature\": \"oracle-bug-fixes\", \"message\": \"Two orders, two authorities \\u2014 the dissolution that resolves the oracle's merge-non-commutativity finding without touching chain-witness-order: FOLD REPLAY orders by (ts, id) \\u2014 event order, store-independent total order \\u2014 so merge(A,B) and merge(B,A) re-fold identically; WITNESS ORDER (rowid) remains the chain/window/attestation authority \\u2014 merge directions ARE different custody events and their chains legitimately differ. Changed sites: SqliteStore.since/since_raw/replay_cursor + latest_by_kind(_where) (ts,id); store_reader facts_by_kind + resolve_entity_id (fixes ref-time rowid-blindness, H4); vertex_reader combined-read sort key (ts,id) \\u2014 its own NOTE had documented the tie nondeterminism; merge.py INSERT..SELECT ORDER BY ts,id (was unordered scan). Tick/window/chain paths untouched: append_tick, window hashing, _window_facts, FTS cursors all stay rowid. since_raw/replay_cursor now also inject _ts (SELECT gains ts) and Vertex.receive injects _ts on the live path \\u2014 Latest folds get the same envelope everywhere. Post-rebirth id==event order makes (ts,id) and id-alone agree above ms resolution; (ts,id) chosen because it is also correct for un-reborn mixed-era stores (the H4 general rule). Pinned by TestMergeFoldCommutativity.\", \"_ts\": 1781282100.82644, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"thread:python-bugs-from-go-oracle\"]}, \"practice/reroute-log-sweep-reconcile\": {\"topic\": \"practice/reroute-log-sweep-reconcile\", \"message\": \"ADOPTED 2026-06-12 (Kyle ratified, same conversation as the thread): three-tier capture-and-review. (1) REROUTE LOG \\u2014 zero-ceremony one-liner into the existing log kind (collect 20) at the moment of routing around anything; no naming/status/fold-key, which is precisely what makes it fire against flow pressure. (2) SWEEP \\u2014 fast cadence, every session wrap, before the seal: scan session log entries, promote repeat patterns to friction with proper ceremony, update thread statuses, emit the session arc. Name chosen over 'retro' (baggage): the sweep precedes the seal, fits the vocabulary. (3) RECONCILE \\u2014 slow cadence, own scheduled sessions (weekly-ish): reconcile lens + friction backlog + stale threads + structural fit; promoted to first-class work. Pricing rationale: silent-reroute cost is an externality (local flow saving, global later cost) \\u2014 fix by making capture cheaper than the reroute, not by discipline. MECHANISM: Stop hook .claude/hooks/turn-capture.py backstops in-the-moment noticing (the thing that demonstrably fails) \\u2014 fires the capture question once per substantive turn (>=3 tool calls), stop_hook_active-guarded, conversational turns exempt. Runbook updated (CLAUDE.md Principles + Review cadence section). Escalation path if log under-captures: siftd revival \\u2014 transcript reading surfaces reroutes without agent cooperation.\", \"_ts\": 1781286854.904273, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:reroute-capture-practice\"]}, \"design/fact-signature-at-store-column\": {\"topic\": \"design/fact-signature-at-store-column\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Fact signature lives as a facts.signature column, NOT a Fact atom field. Kyle ratified 2026-06-12. Rationale: exact delta-2 posture \\u2014 atoms stay pure, signer injected at store construction, envelope crosses atoms boundary only as read-side view fields. Commitment is content-only: sha256(canonical({kind,ts,payload,observer,origin})), excluding id/rowid \\u2014 store-assigned identity is custody context, not authored content. This is what makes the signature transport-stable: a receiving store re-derives the commitment from the row and verifies against the observer registry without trusting the sender. Tick chain attests receipt (store-local); fact signature attests authorship (travels). Domain: loops-fact-v1 at the composing layer.\", \"_ts\": 1781288277.329636, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\": {\"topic\": \"design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Fact signatures are per-observer authorship claims, Kyle ratified 2026-06-12. Signer callable is (observer, digest) -> sig|None; key layout .loops/keys/<observer>/ed25519.key; verify maps fact.observer -> registry pubkey (the add-observer --key/--keygen registry from delta 2 already IS this mapping). Observers without keys emit unsigned \\u2014 honest NULL becomes a PER-OBSERVER era, generalizing delta 2's per-store epoch. Layering note: this composes with shipped tick signing rather than replacing it \\u2014 unsigned-author facts still sit under the vertex-key-signed window hash (custody claim); signed-author facts carry both claims. Custody honesty: on a single machine any local process can read any key in .loops/keys/, so observer separation is organizational not adversarial until keys live with their principals (transport/peer era). Companion mechanism: _fact_row_hash goes era-aware (includes signature only when non-NULL) so signature-stripping breaks the sealed window \\u2014 delta-2 envelope trick, no re-anchoring of pre-signature rows.\", \"_ts\": 1781288396.372022, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signature-at-store-column\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"design/authorship-vs-delegation-layering\": {\"topic\": \"design/authorship-vs-delegation-layering\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Each principal mints their own fact-signing key; delegation is NOT encoded in fact signatures. Kyle's lean, confirmed 2026-06-12 at live keygen (kyle + kyle/loops-claude on project and identity). Rationale: the fact signature makes exactly one claim \\u2014 authorship of content (identity domain). On-behalf-of is a second claim (authority domain) with its own primitive: act-chains / OBO / endorsements, vouch's L4 territory. Folding delegation into the signature is the write-receipt temptation again \\u2014 thickening a primitive to carry a claim it cannot make honestly; the carve-out rule says add a separate primitive when the combined claim is live. Forward-compatible: observer name kyle/loops-claude NAMES the delegation by convention today; the future act-chain ATTESTS what the slash only spells \\u2014 nothing to migrate, layers compose on stable per-principal authorship. Custody honesty: same-machine keys mean organizational not adversarial separation; kyle's signature currently attests 'session that could load kyle's key' until his custody moves to him (vouch custody story).\", \"_ts\": 1781292368.255793, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\", \"message\": \"Kyle ratified 2026-06-12: attestation-layer canonical bytes upgrade from implementation-local json.dumps to JCS RFC 8785, with chain re-anchor now while chains are days old (rebirth machinery just proven; re-anchor cost at lifetime minimum, grows per seal). Trigger: the Go oracle reading the chain IS the federation-facing consumer the _canonical_bytes docstring named as the upgrade condition. Aligns with the JCS pin already chosen at the vouch/manifest layer. Concrete divergences closed: ensure_ascii escaping vs raw UTF-8, float shortest-repr edge cases. Payload TEXT stays embedded verbatim (string value) \\u2014 byte-tamper detection without re-serialization, unchanged. Implies Python-side work: _canonical_bytes JCS impl + re-anchor ceremony, tracked separately.\", \"feature\": \"loops-go\", \"_ts\": 1781299087.379547, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:head-anchoring-as-external-witness\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"ops/jcs-reanchor-ceremony\": {\"topic\": \"ops/jcs-reanchor-ceremony\", \"message\": \"CEREMONY CLOSED 2026-06-12: all five live signed stores re-anchored under JCS and verified \\u2014 project (71 facts re-signed incl. the ceremony-open fact itself, 3 ticks, head d17307c9...), identity (1 fact, 2 ticks), session, comms/discord, comms/native (chain-only). Every store verifies chain-intact + signatures-checked against registry post-reanchor. Era boundaries held everywhere: pre-signature facts stayed NULL, legacy ticks untouched. The \\u00a78.7 conformance vectors are now unblocked \\u2014 Python is on JCS, the bytes the vectors pin are the normative ones. Dry-run artifact cleaned.\", \"_ts\": 1781301744.639793, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\"]}, \"design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\": {\"topic\": \"design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"message\": \"Kyle ratified 2026-06-13: DEFER the fact-signing require-on-emit gate AND verify-on-receive to the transport/peer era; make DISCLOSURE honest first. Dissolution reasoning: require-on-emit with no verify-on-receive buys only a locally-complete ledger so verify/disclosure can claim all-post-era-keyed-facts-signed \\u2014 enforcement in service of disclosure, not of a receiver; no untrusted cross-store receive path exists yet, so build the gate when something is on the other side of it. Counter weighed and overridden for facts: the tick-side delta-2 posture (signing is structural from this point forward) would extend down to facts for a clean-from-here ledger that makes eventual verify-on-receive cheap; rejected now because the clean-ledger benefit is disclosure-facing and achievable instead by honest disclosure of the opportunistic reality, and fact-signing is per-observer/opportunistic vs ticks vertex-self-signed at a single funnel. Net: signing stays opportunistic-on-emit + audit-on-demand (store verify); the require/verify layer reactivates when transport/peer gives verify-on-receive a consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1781385216.954705, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"observation:implementation/signing-enforcement-status\"]}, \"design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"message\": \"Kyle ratified 2026-06-14 (Gate-B floor): once a store starts signing at the TICK level, it must continue \\u2014 the era-regression guard (no unsigned tick after a signed tick) is a non-negotiable FLOOR, not a per-vertex flag. Rationale: era-monotonicity is witness-chain INTEGRITY, not vertex POLICY \\u2014 verify already condemns the regressed state (CHAIN BROKEN) and reanchor already refuses to create it; seal must match (closes the say/do gap where seal could mint exactly what verify forbids). Friction is low in the SSH sense: the private key is local, so signing is transparent/automatic while present; the cost only appears when the key is ABSENT, and then the right behavior is SSH's \\u2014 a hard STOP, never a silent downgrade to unauthenticated. So seal REFUSES (not warn-and-proceed) to mint an unsigned tick in the signed era. Degrades gracefully: emit stays opportunistic so the window's FACTS are still stored; only the attestation boundary (tick) is withheld, and the next successful seal closes the accumulated window \\u2014 data preserved, attestation deferred, never falsified. Disclosure is the floor under all of it: every signing action states signed/unsigned + reason regardless of the refuse/proceed branch. Distinct from the still-deferred FACT-signing require gate (decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred): facts stay opportunistic (mixed signed/unsigned is normal, live edge strippable); only TICKS take the structural floor, matching the delta-2 \\\"signing is structural from this point forward\\\" posture. The forward-policy \\\"require signing\\\" vertex flag (Gate A) remains a SEPARATE, optional, default-off knob \\u2014 it governs whether a vertex must sign AT ALL (the first signature, optionally facts), not whether it may stop. Open forward work: the transport era breaks the \\\"key is always local\\\" assumption \\u2014 see thread:transport-era-signing-key-flow.\", \"_ts\": 1781457866.835805, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\", \"thread:seal-era-boundary-guard\"]}, \"design/next-release-0.4.0\": {\"topic\": \"design/next-release-0.4.0\", \"message\": \"Release-delta audit (workflow, 9 agents; loops v0.3.1..HEAD = 78 unreleased commits) \\u2192 next loops release is 0.4.0. Pre-1.0 minor carries breaking (mirrors painted 0.1.8\\u21920.2.0). The range is one coherent arc: the federated attestation substrate (tick hash chains, Ed25519 tick + per-observer fact signing, JCS/RFC 8785 canon, store verify/rebirth/reanchor, sl seal + the era-floor) plus the cli-refactor and read-path overhaul. Breaking surface is broad and PERSISTED, which rules patch out as dishonest: store schema +6 attestation columns and dropped ulid() default (id-supplied-at-INSERT); .vertex gained observers{key} + keys/ custody dirs; fold upsert flipped replace\\u2192merge across every by-fold kind; row ordering \\u2192(ts,id); Latest + numeric folds reject-not-coerce; dep swap sqlite-ulid\\u2192python-ulid + new rfc8785; JCS canon invalidates prior attestations until reanchor. Only the root pyproject version bumps (libs are not independently versioned). Full changelog draft + readiness + rebuild map live in docs/dev/rebuild-audit-0.4.0.md. THE GATE for tagging (gates the release AND the rebuild): the painted pin is uncapped (>=0.1.8) so fresh installs ALREADY pull 0.2.0 \\u2014 loops must be validated against painted 0.2.0 first. Import-compat is verified clean (every deep path resolves; loops uses none of the removed names); behavior under 0.2.0's exact-width contract + the absence of goldens for the new lenses (trace/declarations/preview/walked) is unvalidated.\", \"_ts\": 1781468830.498302, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"test/gate-results-painted-020\": {\"topic\": \"test/gate-results-painted-020\", \"message\": \"THE GATE run (painted 0.1.8->0.2.0, root pyproject bumped to >=0.2.0,<0.3, uv sync clean). RESULTS: (1) loops suite 1327 passed + 1 xfailed, ZERO golden drift \\u2014 the framework bump did not break any loops rendering. Strong signal: loops' run_cli/lens path is forward-compatible with 0.2.0. (2) test_readiness_lens collection error = ORPHANED test (the 'readiness' lens source was dissolved; module gone since after 3c9d26b) \\u2014 pre-existing, painted-independent; delete the test. (3) test_dashboard x7 in apps/TASKS = REAL painted-0.2.0 API drift, NOT pre-existing: CliContext.__init__() no longer accepts 'zoom' kwarg (signature changed in 0.2.0). The audit's 'illustrative' call was WRONG on these. This drift lands squarely on the rebuild KEYSTONE (the two CliContext classes must reconcile). loops escaped it only because loops constructs CliContext via run_cli, not directly; tasks constructs it directly in tests.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"_ts\": 1781474351.634264, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/cli-context-keystone-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-context-keystone-shape\", \"message\": \"Gate made the CliContext keystone concrete. The two classes are NOT near-duplicates to merge \\u2014 they carry ORTHOGONAL concerns sharing a name. painted-0.2.0 CliContext = (fidelity, mode, use_ansi, is_tty, width, height): terminal/rendering state (note zoom->fidelity rename is the exact drift that broke tasks). loops CliContext (loops/cli/context.py) = (reporter, vertex_path, vertex_name, observer): dispatch/domain state. The rebuild's 'loops CliContext becomes a thin extension of painted.cli.CliContext' is therefore COMPOSITION not unification: loops' domain fields wrap/hold a painted render-context, they don't flatten into one constructor. Confirms keystone-first sequencing: reconcile by composition before touching dispatch. tasks' x7 failures are the canary \\u2014 they'll be fixed by the same reconciliation (s/zoom=/fidelity=/ at minimum, or routing through the composed context).\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"_ts\": 1781474375.91534, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:test/gate-results-painted-020\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/cli-context-phase-split\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-context-phase-split\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED step 1 (keystone). Renamed loops CliContext->Invocation (context.py->invocation.py, commit 8040bd4). The two same-named contexts were different PHASES: Invocation=domain (vertex/observer/signer/store, lives in dispatch+fetch); painted's CliContext=render (fidelity/width/is_tty, lives in render call). They never co-occur in one call, so the rename dissolves the ambiguity rather than merging anything. No behavioral change: 1327 loops green, zero golden drift, sl binary smoke-tested on both IR (read/fold) and legacy-shim (store) paths. Discovery while grounding: commands/ shims read ctx.zoom/ctx.is_tty but loops Invocation has no such fields \\u2014 those ctx are painted's, and ctx.zoom survives 0.2.0 as a blessed property (not compat shim), which is why the gate passed clean. Unblocks steps 2-7.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"_ts\": 1781477055.186374, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-context-keystone-shape\", \"decision:test/gate-results-painted-020\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/full-painted-integration-residue\": {\"topic\": \"design/full-painted-integration-residue\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED step 3 pilot (commit bc22491). read/fold view drops fidelity_from_args: add_cli_args+parse_zoom+parse_fidelity now own the pure-terminal axes (-q/-v depth, --plain/--json format, --static/--live/-i mode, --max-chars/-lines budgets). Domain-query selectors (--facts/--diff/--refs N) stay loops-side, visibility merged into the painted Fidelity. Behavior-preserving (1327 green, zero golden drift; sl verified across all axes). LANDSCAPE FINDING: read is the SOLE fidelity_from_args consumer \\u2014 the other display surfaces (store/ticks/stream/devtools) already route fidelity through painted run_cli, so their dissolution is step-4 shim-unification, not step-3. fidelity.py/fidelity_from_args now has zero live callers in the IR path; candidate for deletion once nothing references it.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"_ts\": 1781481547.896491, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-context-phase-split\", \"decision:design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"ops/release-0.4.0\": {\"topic\": \"ops/release-0.4.0\", \"message\": \"0.4.0 fully released. PyPI publish DONE via GitHub trusted publishing (OIDC, environment:pypi, .github/workflows/release.yml fires on release:published \\u2014 NOT on bare tag push). Sequence that worked: git tag+push -> gh release create v0.4.0 -> workflow build+publish (run 27514185875, \\u2713 22s, digital attestations) -> strange-loops 0.4.0 live on PyPI (verified 200 at /0.4.0/json). CORRECTION to prior emit: local 'uv publish' was the WRONG path \\u2014 ~/.pypirc token is painted-scoped (403 for strange-loops); no local token needed, the release workflow uses trusted publishing. RUNBOOK note for future loops releases: do NOT uv publish locally; create a GitHub Release from the tag and the pipeline handles it. Visualizer = fast-follow after the cli/render rebuild (Kyle's call). Painted gets worked in parallel per docs/dev/painted-0.3.0-commission.md.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"ops\": \"release\", \"_ts\": 1781476531.874921, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\"]}, \"design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\": {\"topic\": \"design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"message\": \"COHERENCE FINDING reframing rebuild step 3. The design doc (rebuild-design-0.4.0.md \\u00a71) assumed loops' --facts/--refs/--diff dissolve into painted Tags gated by ctx.fidelity.shows(). Grounding in fold.py disproves it: all three are DOMAIN-QUERY SELECTORS, not disclosure layers. --diff selects a different fetcher (_build_diff_fetch + trace lens); --facts toggles want_facts (folded vs raw stream); --refs N carries a traversal DEPTH into fetch (painted's store_true Tag can't model the N). painted's Tag model assumes fixed data revealed in named layers; loops' flags change the query itself. So the real dissolution boundary: PURE TERMINAL axes (-q/-v depth, --max-chars/-lines budgets, --plain/--json format, --static/--live/-i mode) dissolve into painted add_cli_args+parse_fidelity; DOMAIN-QUERY selectors (--facts/--diff/--refs) stay loops-side (they parameterize fetch). This follows directly from grow-painted-over-workaround + 'push loops into domain-specific arenas' (Kyle): query selection IS domain, not terminal. Step 3 revised: dissolve the generic terminal flags per view; keep domain flags; merge their loops-computed visibility into the painted-compiled Fidelity.\", \"_ts\": 1781481044.543767, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\", \"observation:practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\"]}, \"design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\": {\"topic\": \"design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\", \"message\": \"A2: build painted's field-budget allocator as a stable painted.core.compose primitive NOW, minimal surface (fields,width,min_field,sep -> fitted text + dropped-count). Badge [+Nc] and empty-field fallback stay loops-side; commit to allocation contract not presentation. RATIONALE: clears the AUTO/Fill bar (real external PyPI consumer + general nameable contract + wcwidth fix is strictly better than loops' len()-buggy _render_preview copy). Painted's load-bearing premise accepted: a private symbol an external version-pinned consumer imports is de-facto public, so 'private-until-2nd-consumer' middle path doesn't exist -> clean either/or. GATE on the name: dissolution-test budget_fields vs resolve_column_widths; if allocation math is shared (columns-vs-fields framing only) it's ONE primitive two consumers not two stable names; if sep-cost + shrink-then-drop-below-MIN is genuinely distinct from column distribution, two names honest. Placement-independent signature forecloses nothing. This is the substrate for rebuild step5 (re-ground lenses, delete hand truncation).\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"_ts\": 1781544228.308609, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge\": {\"topic\": \"design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"Step-4 devtools (test/compile/validate) conversion: delete hand-rolled -h interception, let run_cli own help via add_args(parser). Command args (files/--input/--limit) registered ONCE into run_cli's parser; their parsed values captured for fetch via the build_fidelity hook closure (the only run_cli callback that sees the Namespace today). Exit-code semantics preserved (validate returns 1 on errors/no-files) because we stay on the run_cli path, NOT the Operation/dispatch STATIC path (which always returns 0 \\u2014 would lose validate's exit code). BRIDGE not endpoint: when painted ships CliContext.args/fetch(ctx) (thread:painted-run-cli-args-seam), the build_fidelity capture collapses to ctx.args read. Chose run_cli-stays over full-Operation-IR for devtools precisely because these carry pass/fail exit codes the dispatch STATIC path doesn't thread.\", \"_ts\": 1781546313.570171, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:painted-run-cli-args-seam\"]}, \"design/devtools-help-dissolve-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"design/devtools-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 780659d (step 4, first cut). Devtools trio (test/compile/validate) hand-rolled -h interception deleted; run_cli owns help via add_args. Bridge: build_fidelity namespace-capture for validate/compile; test keeps inherent pre-parse (branches on --input pre-dispatch). Stayed on run_cli path not Operation/dispatch IR \\u2014 devtools carry pass/fail exit codes (validate=1 on errors) that dispatch STATIC (always 0) would drop. 1327 green, zero golden drift. NEXT in step 4: store (the named wrinkle \\u2014 pre-parsed .db/.vertex positional + verify/rebirth/reanchor subcommands), now with the help-dissolve pattern proven on the easy surface first.\", \"_ts\": 1781546540.597015, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\": {\"topic\": \"design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 621fdf2 (step 5 core). fold.py _render_preview + _truncate dissolved into painted.budget_fields; both preview-multi and fallback-single paths route through it; [+Nc] hint = fit.dropped. Contract adopted FRESH (min_field gates truncation not presence; wcwidth-measured). OUTCOME vs prediction: predicted goldens would drift (short whole fields reappear) \\u2014 they did NOT. Zero golden drift. The [+Nc] single-body goldens are byte-identical (ASCII wcwidth==len; fit.dropped == old hint math). The multi-field divergence is narrow: only 2 goldens use the preview path and none hit the sub-min-whole-field case. Covered by new test test_short_whole_trailing_field_kept instead. Kyle's parity-revert option is now moot \\u2014 adopting fresh cost nothing observable.\", \"_ts\": 1781551542.611614, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/devtools-help-args-idiom\": {\"topic\": \"design/devtools-help-args-idiom\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDES design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge. The devtools (test/compile/validate) hand-rolled -h dissolves via painted 0.3.0's pre-parse + describe-for-help idiom: pre-parse the command's own args (argparse add_help=False), pass help_args=[HelpArg(name, desc, positional=)] to run_cli so --help lists them, fetch closes over the pre-parsed namespace. NOT the build_fidelity capture (that was the 0.2.0 bridge) and NOT the Operation/dispatch IR (devtools carry pass/fail exit codes dispatch STATIC drops). -h-vs-required-positional wrinkle: validate (nargs=*) lets -h reach run_cli freely; compile/test guard a required file, so a bare help request routes to run_cli's help renderer BEFORE the guard (help short-circuits pre-fetch). This is the proven pattern store inherits.\", \"_ts\": 1781550203.149721, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/devtools-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"thread:painted-run-cli-args-seam\"]}, \"design/store-help-dissolve-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"design/store-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 443bdd6. store's 4 hand-rolled -h blocks dissolved. The named wrinkle (verify/rebirth/reanchor subcommands) was mostly redundant code: subcommand argparse parsers already had add_help=True, so parse_args owns -h natively \\u2014 deleted the explicit blocks + unused _sys. -h now raises argparse SystemExit(0), propagates clean to exit 0 through run_app (verified on real CLI). Base inspect uses the help_args idiom; subcommand roster moved to run_cli description so 'sl store -h' still surfaces them. The 'file fights painted arg0->handler' fear didn't materialize: store IS one painted handler, subcommand routing is internal to it (argv[0] check), painted never sees the subcommands. 1327 green, zero drift.\", \"_ts\": 1781550431.653525, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/devtools-help-args-idiom\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/record-line-dissolution-splits\": {\"topic\": \"design/record-line-dissolution-splits\", \"message\": \"Step5-large crux (same shape as step5-small first-half): audit row 7 lumped '_render_item_line / trace headers / stream rows -> record_line+PayloadLens' as ONE dissolution. It is TWO. record_line models a TIMESTAMPED EVENT RECORD (HH:MM [kind] summary + secondary-field continuations, payload via PayloadLens). (a) GENUINE: stream.py + trace.py per-fact rows ARE exactly this (ts+kind+payload) -> dissolve into record_line/record_line_composed + gutter_freshness/lifecycle + attention fns. (b) PARTIAL/loops-side: fold.py _render_item_line label is the KEY-FIELD value not the kind, and its badge (xN <-N ->N recency) is computed from FOLD STRUCTURE (item.n, inbound Counter, item.refs) with no PayloadLens home. record_line cannot host the fold badge; fold dedupes loops-side at best.\", \"_ts\": 1781553732.968458, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/stream-trace-record-line-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"design/stream-trace-record-line-shipped\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 0805235 (step5-large, stream/trace half). stream_view dissolved onto painted.record_line; trace normal-path dissolves transitively (already delegated to stream_view); _render_diff stays loops-side (cumulative scalar-delta contract, not ts+kind+payload \\u2014 the trace analog of the fold badge). TWO contract conflicts hit + resolved: (1) width=None piped/no-truncation invariant -> grew painted 0.3.1 (record_line honors the natural-sizing escape Block.text already documents; record_line was the lone outlier). (2) DETAILED density: record_line shows only long/notable fields as continuation, short fields move to FULL; ADOPTED per Kyle's call (accept drift). Drift was MINIMAL+benign: test_log goldens regen (ISO ts at FULL, short fields->FULL, '\\u2026' truncation marker now signaled in CLI.md), one unit test split. Loops residue grafted cleanly: key_field summary via PayloadLens; id/observer/origin (non-payload) as continuation. 1325 green. OUTCOME vs pattern: same shape as step5-small + the original CLI-lens findings \\u2014 the pitched 1:1 dissolution was actually genuine-core + honest-residue; the painted boundary needed ONE backward-compat widening, not a loops fork.\", \"ops\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"_ts\": 1781573902.17782, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/record-line-dissolution-splits\"]}}}, \"thread\": {\"items\": {\"bend-interaction-combinators\": {\"name\": \"bend-interaction-combinators\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Three experiments confirmed model maps to Bend. Parked \\u2014 Python more productive. Revisit when Bend2 lands (32/64-bit numbers, native IO).\", \"_ts\": 1772415259.254954, \"_n\": 1}, \"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\": {\"name\": \"prometheus-alerts-to-loops\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked \\u2014 no active homelab alerting work. Revisit when hlab vertex gets real alert sources.\", \"_ts\": 1773063581.806411, \"_n\": 2}, \"population-as-facts\": {\"name\": \"population-as-facts\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by CLI dissolution. Population ops dissolved into vertex read path.\", \"_ts\": 1772903956.179828, \"_n\": 2}, \"string-structure\": {\"name\": \"string-structure\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Observation about naming as structural binding interface. Fold targets, boundary names, loop names \\u2014 strings carry semantic load at every level. True but no action item. Revisit if naming conventions need formalization.\", \"_ts\": 1773069905.900871, \"_n\": 5, \"reason\": \"speculative\"}, \"consumer-logic\": {\"name\": \"consumer-logic\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by lens-escalation-path decision. Ranking/sorting is a custom lens concern.\", \"_ts\": 1772903938.631268, \"_n\": 3}, \"store-policy\": {\"name\": \"store-policy\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Design space placeholder \\u2014 ephemeral stores, sliding windows, sampling. No concrete use case driving it. Revisit when a vertex needs retention policy.\", \"_ts\": 1773064233.764494, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"speculative\"}, \"boundary-reset\": {\"name\": \"boundary-reset\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"DSL hardcodes reset=True. Non-resetting boundaries are a real concept but nothing needs them yet. Revisit when a fold accumulator needs to survive boundary fires.\", \"_ts\": 1773064235.411467, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"deferred\"}, \"sole-fold-override\": {\"name\": \"sole-fold-override\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Convention-over-configuration for single-fold vertices. No active friction \\u2014 explicit fold config is fine at current scale.\", \"_ts\": 1773064236.784072, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"speculative\"}, \"tick-provenance\": {\"name\": \"tick-provenance\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by decision architecture/tick-provenance-scoping: tool-level scope from .vertex config, not per-tick kinds_consumed.\", \"_ts\": 1773064237.596665, \"_n\": 2}, \"self-feeding-risk\": {\"name\": \"self-feeding-risk\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Tracked in meta store as self-feeding-safeguards thread. Duplicate in project store not needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772903956.431778, \"_n\": 2}, \"doc-provenance-ingestion\": {\"name\": \"doc-provenance-ingestion\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"VOCABULARY.md/LOOPS.md dissolution provenance as store facts. Low priority when opened, no driving use case since. Revisit when store workflow patterns need historical provenance.\", \"_ts\": 1773064434.074974, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"speculative\"}, \"help-unification\": {\"name\": \"help-unification\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by generic-defaults-simplicity. Nothing to unify when generic layer is simple.\", \"_ts\": 1772903938.952573, \"_n\": 4}, \"observer-scoped-handoff\": {\"name\": \"observer-scoped-handoff\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into session-tick-structure and hooks infrastructure.\", \"_ts\": 1772903942.347627, \"_n\": 4, \"produced\": [\"thread:developer-app-split\", \"thread:gist-lens-generics\", \"decision:observer-resolution\", \"decision:dot-vertex-root\", \"decision:vertex-definitions-copy-local\", \"decision:observer-elevation-lifecycle\", \"decision:observer-in-vertex-declaration\", \"decision:vertex-mutation-generalizes\", \"thread:session-as-tick\", \"decision:architecture/observer-file-split\", \"decision:design/resolve-observer-canonical\", \"decision:architecture/grant-two-levels\", \"change:Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\", \"decision:identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\", \"decision:design/fold-state-contract\", \"decision:design/custom-lens-system\", \"decision:design/plain-format-contract\", \"decision:design/fold-state-typed-contract\", \"decision:design/custom-lens-loading\", \"thread:fold-state-types\", \"thread:custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"thread:fold-materialization\", \"thread:recency-aware-lens\", \"change:Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design ses\", \"change:FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\", \"thread:observer-cascade\", \"decision:architecture/cli-emit-runtime\", \"decision:architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\", \"task:cli-emit-runtime\", \"task:daemon-local-orchestration\", \"task:foldstate-audit-findings\", \"decision:architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\", \"task:identity-observer-filtering\", \"thread:cli-stream-limit\", \"thread:cli-describe\", \"thread:cli-json-input\", \"thread:cli-unscoped-fold\", \"decision:implementation/close-command\", \"decision:implementation/thread-fact-association\", \"thread:git-commit-facts\", \"thread:combine-auto-inherit\", \"decision:combine-auto-inherit\", \"task:combine-auto-inherit\", \"thread:thread-auto-association\", \"task:session-close\", \"task:thread-auto-tagging\", \"task:pickup-filtering\"]}, \"developer-app-split\": {\"name\": \"developer-app-split\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by app-boundary decision. The loops CLI IS the developer tool.\", \"_ts\": 1772903939.205933, \"_n\": 4, \"delegate\": \"implementation\"}, \"gist-lens-generics\": {\"name\": \"gist-lens-generics\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by generic-defaults-simplicity. Kind-specific extractors dissolve into custom lenses.\", \"_ts\": 1772903939.448778, \"_n\": 5, \"produced\": [\"decision:observer-resolution\", \"decision:dot-vertex-root\", \"decision:vertex-definitions-copy-local\", \"decision:observer-elevation-lifecycle\", \"decision:observer-in-vertex-declaration\", \"decision:vertex-mutation-generalizes\", \"thread:session-as-tick\", \"decision:architecture/observer-file-split\", \"decision:design/resolve-observer-canonical\", \"decision:architecture/grant-two-levels\", \"change:Observer file split: fetch.py + identity.py\", \"decision:identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\", \"decision:design/fold-state-contract\", \"decision:design/custom-lens-system\", \"decision:design/plain-format-contract\", \"decision:design/fold-state-typed-contract\", \"decision:design/custom-lens-loading\", \"thread:fold-state-types\", \"thread:custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"thread:fold-materialization\", \"thread:recency-aware-lens\", \"change:Observer file split + identity wiring + fold/lens design ses\", \"change:FoldState typed contract + observer.py split\", \"thread:observer-cascade\", \"decision:architecture/cli-emit-runtime\", \"decision:architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\", \"task:cli-emit-runtime\", \"task:daemon-local-orchestration\", \"task:foldstate-audit-findings\", \"decision:architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\", \"task:identity-observer-filtering\", \"thread:cli-stream-limit\", \"thread:cli-describe\", \"thread:cli-json-input\", \"thread:cli-unscoped-fold\", \"decision:implementation/close-command\", \"decision:implementation/thread-fact-association\", \"thread:git-commit-facts\", \"thread:combine-auto-inherit\", \"decision:combine-auto-inherit\", \"task:combine-auto-inherit\", \"thread:thread-auto-association\", \"task:session-close\", \"task:thread-auto-tagging\", \"task:pickup-filtering\", \"thread:observer-scoped-handoff\"], \"delegate\": \"implementation\"}, \"session-as-tick\": {\"name\": \"session-as-tick\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Implemented. Session boundary fires tick via session-tick-structure decision. Replay initializes period from last tick.\", \"_ts\": 1772903939.710833, \"_n\": 6}, \"fold-state-types\": {\"name\": \"fold-state-types\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Design resolved by fold-state-typed-contract decision. FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses. Implementation tracked separately as fold-materialization task.\", \"_ts\": 1772903955.078884, \"_n\": 7, \"produced\": [\"task:foldstate-audit-findings\", \"decision:implementation/close-command\", \"decision:implementation/thread-fact-association\", \"thread:git-commit-facts\", \"thread:combine-auto-inherit\", \"decision:combine-auto-inherit\", \"task:combine-auto-inherit\", \"thread:thread-auto-association\", \"task:session-close\", \"task:thread-auto-tagging\", \"task:pickup-filtering\"], \"delegate\": \"implementation\"}, \"custom-lens-infrastructure\": {\"name\": \"custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. vertex-lens-declarations decision landed. LensDecl in vertex AST, 4-tier resolution.\", \"_ts\": 1772903939.951353, \"_n\": 4}, \"fold-materialization\": {\"name\": \"fold-materialization\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Plan concluded not yet needed at current scale (19ms fold on 497 facts). Design banked for 5K+ fact threshold.\", \"_ts\": 1773013718.241527, \"_n\": 3, \"delegate\": \"implementation\"}, \"recency-aware-lens\": {\"name\": \"recency-aware-lens\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Reconcile lens (config/lenses/reconcile.py) groups by attention-need with recency tags. Replaces readiness lens for session reconciliation.\", \"_ts\": 1773011677.46484, \"_n\": 6}, \"observer-cascade\": {\"name\": \"observer-cascade\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Implemented. validate_emit follows combined vertex observer declarations.\", \"_ts\": 1772903940.280227, \"_n\": 4, \"produced\": [\"decision:architecture/cli-emit-runtime\", \"decision:architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\", \"task:cli-emit-runtime\", \"task:daemon-local-orchestration\", \"task:foldstate-audit-findings\", \"decision:architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\", \"task:identity-observer-filtering\", \"thread:cli-stream-limit\", \"thread:cli-describe\", \"thread:cli-json-input\", \"thread:cli-unscoped-fold\", \"thread:fold-state-types\", \"decision:implementation/close-command\", \"decision:implementation/thread-fact-association\", \"thread:git-commit-facts\", \"thread:combine-auto-inherit\", \"decision:combine-auto-inherit\", \"task:combine-auto-inherit\", \"thread:thread-auto-association\", \"task:session-close\", \"task:thread-auto-tagging\", \"task:pickup-filtering\", \"thread:observer-scoped-handoff\", \"thread:gist-lens-generics\"]}, \"cli-stream-limit\": {\"name\": \"cli-stream-limit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Stream command dissolved. Time limiting is --since flag on read.\", \"_ts\": 1772903974.251949, \"_n\": 3}, \"cli-describe\": {\"name\": \"cli-describe\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved. Vertex metadata available through read. No separate describe verb needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772903974.555725, \"_n\": 3}, \"cli-json-input\": {\"name\": \"cli-json-input\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Input format concerns follow from write-vertex design.\", \"_ts\": 1772841219.5945, \"_n\": 2}, \"cli-unscoped-fold\": {\"name\": \"cli-unscoped-fold\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by observer-scope-as-vertex-concern. Vertex declares its scope, no flag needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772903940.53695, \"_n\": 3}, \"git-commit-facts\": {\"name\": \"git-commit-facts\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"priority\": \"idea\", \"message\": \"Git commits as change facts via GitOps vertex. Clear shape, source/parse pipeline could handle it today. Revisit when temporal correlation between commits and threads becomes a real workflow.\", \"_ts\": 1773064435.670951, \"_n\": 3, \"reason\": \"deferred\"}, \"combine-auto-inherit\": {\"name\": \"combine-auto-inherit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Implemented. Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop definitions from children.\", \"_ts\": 1772903940.831581, \"_n\": 3, \"produced\": [\"task:combine-auto-inherit\"]}, \"thread-auto-association\": {\"name\": \"thread-auto-association\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"priority\": \"idea\", \"message\": \"Auto-associate facts emitted during an open thread's lifetime. Manual name= discipline works at current scale. Revisit if emit volume or thread count makes manual association impractical.\", \"_ts\": 1773064437.085862, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"deferred\"}, \"fact-drill-down\": {\"name\": \"fact-drill-down\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Single-fact inspection dissolved into vertex-as-interface redesign. Detail views fall out of zoom levels on loops read. The old shape (loops show <id>) is subsumed.\", \"_ts\": 1773064438.948601, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"superseded\", \"superseded_by\": \"cli-dissolution\"}, \"app-block-wrapper\": {\"name\": \"app-block-wrapper\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by app-boundary. Lenses are vertex-level config, not app-level.\", \"thread\": \"custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"_ts\": 1772903941.093898, \"_n\": 3}, \"module-path-lens-syntax\": {\"name\": \"module-path-lens-syntax\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked: still valid for installed-package lens references but no current use case. Will emerge naturally when apps need to expose lenses from their packages.\", \"thread\": \"custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"_ts\": 1772849694.291794, \"_n\": 2}, \"combine-lens-propagation\": {\"name\": \"combine-lens-propagation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by lens-escalation-path. Each vertex declares its own lens, no inheritance.\", \"thread\": \"custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"_ts\": 1772903941.343526, \"_n\": 3}, \"bulk-emit-ux\": {\"name\": \"bulk-emit-ux\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked: subsumed by cli-dissolution redesign (vertex-as-interface). Emit UX will be rethought as part of write-vertex operation.\", \"_ts\": 1772841213.464457, \"_n\": 3, \"delegate\": \"implementation\"}, \"kind-prefix-leak\": {\"name\": \"kind-prefix-leak\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into design/internal-fact-namespace. _ prefix convention separates system observations from domain facts. Source lifecycle kinds (_sync.{kind}) replace {kind}.complete.\", \"_ts\": 1773027391.182887, \"_n\": 4}, \"combine-emit-routing\": {\"name\": \"combine-emit-routing\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. Emit routes through vertex resolution.\", \"_ts\": 1772903941.847211, \"_n\": 3}, \"observer-vs-source-attribution\": {\"name\": \"observer-vs-source-attribution\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by origin-as-source-attribution decision. Origin carries source, observer carries identity.\", \"_ts\": 1772903942.097439, \"_n\": 4}, \"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\": {\"name\": \"vertex-name-resolution-consistency\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolution unified. resolve_vertex used across emit, read, fold, stream, and dispatch. The three-strategies gap no longer exists.\", \"_ts\": 1773064440.017514, \"_n\": 2}, \"run-loop-persistence\": {\"name\": \"run-loop-persistence\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved. run became sync (cadence-gated). Persistence is always through vertex store.\", \"_ts\": 1772903975.0605, \"_n\": 4, \"delegate\": \"implementation\"}, \"check-cursor-mechanism\": {\"name\": \"check-cursor-mechanism\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Session detection handled by hooks infrastructure (SessionStart marker). No separate cursor mechanism needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772903975.305672, \"_n\": 3}, \"stream-summary-truncation\": {\"name\": \"stream-summary-truncation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Stream command dissolved. Truncation concerns moved to read path rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1772903974.81212, \"_n\": 3}, \"cli-dissolution\": {\"name\": \"cli-dissolution\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"CLI dissolution complete. Final spawn was entity-ref-resolution (commit 39d8de9). CLI surface is read/emit/sync/close. All subsumed threads either resolved or correctly parked.\", \"_ts\": 1773078948.048356, \"_n\": 6}, \"root-vertex-topology\": {\"name\": \"root-vertex-topology\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by vertex-topology-not-hierarchy decision. Vertices are addresses. Tree is one routing pattern, not the only topology. Combine and direct addressing coexist.\", \"_ts\": 1772903955.901587, \"_n\": 2}, \"read-operation-contract\": {\"name\": \"read-operation-contract\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by read-is-pure and cli-verb-first decisions. Read is pure (no side effects), composable filters (--facts --ticks --kind --since), progressive unpacking.\", \"_ts\": 1772903955.65251, \"_n\": 2}, \"source-execution-model\": {\"name\": \"source-execution-model\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. Source/Cadence split implemented (3bbeeeb). Source is pure adapter, Cadence is store predicate, Executor replaces Runner.\", \"_ts\": 1772903942.590303, \"_n\": 3}, \"siftd-redesign\": {\"name\": \"siftd-redesign\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Complete arc: adapter dissolved into config-level vertex + parse pipeline, apps/siftd removed, source lifecycle (.complete) replaced by _sync prefix namespace. siftd is now pure configuration \\u2014 vertex file + discover script + lens.\", \"_ts\": 1773028661.528345, \"_n\": 7}, \"siftd-exchange-topology\": {\"name\": \"siftd-exchange-topology\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Decided and implemented. Harness topology (aggregation + per-harness instances) landed in 9f2c0e6.\", \"_ts\": 1773013716.439281, \"_n\": 3}, \"orchestration-agent\": {\"name\": \"orchestration-agent\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into orchestration vertex + dispatch script. The orchestrator is just a vertex with boundaries \\u2014 no separate agent needed. The vertex's fold state IS the workflow state. Boundary fires trigger dispatch.\", \"_ts\": 1773165304.022865, \"_n\": 5, \"reason\": \"\", \"superseded_by\": \"thread/orchestration-vertex-design\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01kkc6pvsgrcqbkjsejsyqvc13\"}, \"format-dissolves-into-lens\": {\"name\": \"format-dissolves-into-lens\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Format dissolution implemented. CliContext.format:Format \\u2192 use_ansi:bool. JSON is pre-render short-circuit, ANSI/PLAIN collapsed to boolean. Thread opened when lens contract revealed Format never reached lenses. Closed by making the runtime match what lenses already knew.\", \"_ts\": 1772918994.955217, \"_n\": 2}, \"config-driven-fidelity\": {\"name\": \"config-driven-fidelity\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by the three-axis Fidelity model. Fidelity(depth, visible, chars, lines) is the configurable type. build_fidelity callback on run_cli allows per-command customization. The siftd workspace drove this design, painted owns the type, loops consumes it.\", \"_ts\": 1773958787.25231, \"_n\": 3, \"reason\": \"deferred\"}, \"observer-discoverability\": {\"name\": \"observer-discoverability\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. whoami + LOOPS_OBSERVER env + launch script + hooks compose.\", \"_ts\": 1773011055.7147, \"_n\": 2}, \"focus-on-cli-context\": {\"name\": \"focus-on-cli-context\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Focus as explicit CliContext field. Three-way convergence produced the shape (budget\\u2192Zoom, context\\u2192Focus, explicit-not-ambient). Blocked on whether attention model produces new decisions or dissolves. Revisit when prompt lens parameterization becomes a real need.\", \"_ts\": 1773069893.67404, \"_n\": 2, \"reason\": \"deferred\"}, \"focus-salience-attention\": {\"name\": \"focus-salience-attention\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by attention-density work. n (observation count) + refs (structural connections) \\u2192 salience score. Fold lens sorts by salience, windows by salience > 1. --refs visibility layer filters to connected subgraph. The attention surface is the fold view with visibility gates.\", \"_ts\": 1773958787.3451, \"_n\": 3, \"reason\": \"deferred\"}, \"agent-init-pattern\": {\"name\": \"agent-init-pattern\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into dispatch script. Agent init is what dispatch.sh does: create worktree, set LOOPS_OBSERVER, launch claude. No separate init infrastructure needed.\", \"_ts\": 1773165296.548576, \"_n\": 5, \"status\": \"resolved\", \"reason\": \"\", \"superseded_by\": \"thread/orchestration-vertex-design\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01kkc6pvsgrcqbkjsejsyqvc13\"}, \"sync-completion-tick\": {\"name\": \"sync-completion-tick\", \"message\": \"sync.complete dissolved into _sync \\u2014 same fact, _ prefix namespace.\", \"_ts\": 1773028478.329605, \"_n\": 3, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"cadence-gated-ux\": {\"name\": \"cadence-gated-ux\", \"message\": \"SkippedSource dataclass carries last_run_ts and cadence_interval. Sync lens shows skip reason: fresh (last run 3m ago, cadence 10m).\", \"_ts\": 1773017045.43238, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"sync-output-visibility\": {\"name\": \"sync-output-visibility\", \"message\": \"Sync now shows per-source fact counts and aggregation breakdown at all zoom levels.\", \"_ts\": 1773017041.998385, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"intake-symmetry\": {\"name\": \"intake-symmetry\", \"message\": \"Audit confirmed dissolution. Source adapter IS the intake escalation path. Asymmetry with output lenses is intentional: output is pure/composable (in-process tier search), input is stateful/domain-specific (subprocess). No action needed. If pattern emerges for shared parse functions, a Call ParseOp could mirror lens resolver.\", \"_ts\": 1773016716.235195, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"schema-evolution-detection\": {\"name\": \"schema-evolution-detection\", \"message\": \"Mechanism identified: _schema.{vertex} facts emitted by Executor at sync time. Falls out of internal-fact-namespace design. Not yet implemented \\u2014 build when a source data shape change causes real breakage.\", \"_ts\": 1773069906.261227, \"_n\": 3, \"status\": \"parked\", \"reason\": \"deferred\", \"superseded_by\": \"decision/design/internal-fact-namespace\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01kk8anrvw8bqrgxg4d4rmsase\"}, \"vertex-completeness\": {\"name\": \"vertex-completeness\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Implemented: inline source completeness, predicate boundaries, weather Stage 3, items footgun fix.\", \"_ts\": 1773011055.341746, \"_n\": 3}, \"emit-silent-failure\": {\"name\": \"emit-silent-failure\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Fold-key warning implemented. _warn_missing_fold_key checks payload against vertex fold spec at emit time. Warns on stderr when kind folds 'by' a key field that's missing from the payload. Non-blocking (warning, not error). Follows combine chain to find actual fold declarations. 5 tests covering: missing name, missing topic, key present, collect fold, undeclared kind.\", \"_ts\": 1773014055.278804, \"_n\": 2}, \"discord-source-poll-kind\": {\"name\": \"discord-source-poll-kind\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into design/internal-fact-namespace. message.complete becomes _sync.message \\u2014 no longer pollutes comms fold.\", \"_ts\": 1773027392.516647, \"_n\": 2}, \"entity-reference-resolution\": {\"name\": \"entity-reference-resolution\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Implemented. Entity addresses (kind/fold_key_value) in payload values are automatically resolved to ULIDs at emit time. Original field preserved, sibling {field}_ref added with pinned ULID. StoreReader.resolve_entity_id provides the query primitive. Five tests covering: resolution, nonexistent entities, undeclared kinds, slashed topics, dry-run.\", \"_ts\": 1773068809.959573, \"_n\": 2}, \"test\": {\"name\": \"test\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"_ts\": 1773069861.045527, \"_n\": 6, \"message\": \"Debug artifact from entity-ref implementation testing. Not a real thread.\"}, \"store-hygiene-yields-features\": {\"name\": \"store-hygiene-yields-features\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Session started as routine store reconciliation (stale thread review). The act of parking threads with rationales surfaced the need for structured reasons, which surfaced the need for entity references, which produced the entity-ref-resolution feature. The gap became visible through use, not design. Pattern: maintenance work on the store reveals missing primitives because maintenance IS the use case for store topology.\", \"_ts\": 1773069933.469237, \"_n\": 1}, \"root-vertex-readable\": {\"name\": \"root-vertex-readable\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Root vertex store merged. _topology self-knowledge facts emitted during discover walk, cache-first resolution in entity-ref path. Known limitation: stream path (vertex_facts, vertex_search, vertex_fact_by_id) doesn't overlay own-store facts \\u2014 fold view has them, stream view doesn't. Fix when it matters.\", \"_ts\": 1773160181.122739, \"_n\": 7, \"resolved_by\": \"decision/design/topology-as-fact\", \"resolved_by_ref\": \"01kkaf07nmt8613ehbq61jff1p\"}, \"orchestration-vertex-design\": {\"name\": \"orchestration-vertex-design\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Implemented. Boundary decoupling (4510f3d) + run clause (1f4f407) + orchestration vertex with dispatch script (a55717f). Full loop works: emit task status=open \\u2192 boundary fires \\u2192 dispatch.sh creates worktree, launches claude worker, emits assigned \\u2192 worker completes, emits completed. No daemon, no polling. Daemon dissolved into boundary run clauses + sync heartbeat.\", \"_ts\": 1773165290.505116, \"_n\": 4}, \"daemon-local-orchestration\": {\"name\": \"daemon-local-orchestration\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"reason\": \"\", \"message\": \"Dissolved. Daemon is not needed. Boundary run clauses + external heartbeat (session hooks during work, cron between sessions) compose to produce the same behavior. The orchestration vertex is one-shot like everything else. The persistent runtime concept dissolved into: fold state as workflow state, boundaries as transition reactions, hooks/cron as trigger.\", \"superseded_by\": \"thread/orchestration-vertex-design\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01kkc6pvsgrcqbkjsejsyqvc13\", \"_ts\": 1773158557.811998, \"_n\": 2}, \"siftd-chunk-limit\": {\"name\": \"siftd-chunk-limit\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Still relevant for oversized assistant responses in ndjson parsing. May be addressed in siftd 0.5.0 work. Parking \\u2014 not blocking current work.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.457053, \"_n\": 2}, \"orchestration-two-phase-dispatch\": {\"name\": \"orchestration-two-phase-dispatch\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Two-phase dispatch implemented and tested e2e. assess.sh (judgment: model selection, context) fires on task status=open, emits worker status=assigned. dispatch.sh (mechanics: worktree, launch) fires on worker status=assigned. Full lifecycle verified: open \\u2192 assigned \\u2192 running \\u2192 completed. Worker sessions produce JSONL that siftd discovers.\", \"_ts\": 1773238047.08648, \"_n\": 1}, \"siftd-investigation\": {\"name\": \"siftd-investigation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. siftd topology fully understood: harness-specific child vertices (claude-code, aider, gemini-cli), aggregation root combining them. Per-harness parse, per-harness stores. Siftd-as-loops-native work completed across multiple subtasks. Investigation is done.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.356291, \"_n\": 2}, \"public-release-bootstrap\": {\"name\": \"public-release-bootstrap\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Original scope (config path rename, init defaults, bootstrap UX) overtaken by subsequent work. The CLI, init system, and vertex templates have all evolved significantly. Some items may be resolved. Needs fresh audit against current state when public release returns to focus.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.541005, \"_n\": 2}, \"store-missing-dependency\": {\"name\": \"store-missing-dependency\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"pyproject.toml dependency declaration. May have been fixed in subsequent work. Needs verification.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.627468, \"_n\": 2}, \"init-three-concerns\": {\"name\": \"init-three-concerns\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"All three concerns already implemented: structure (vertex stamp + lens copy), state (config fact seeding via key=value args), artifacts (benchmark/checks script scaffolding). Added slashed-name support for instance grouping (autoresearch/emit-latency). README documents the pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1773680316.886526, \"_n\": 4}, \"autoresearch-vertex\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-vertex\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Fully redesigned as BOUNDED AGENT TURNS. Vertex template has 6 kinds (experiment, finding, log, hypothesis, idea, config), kind-based boundary on experiment, run clause targets iterate.sh. System prompt + prompt lens + iterate script all built and tested. Three iterations completed successfully. Remaining work tracked in: autoresearch-emit-compliance, autoresearch-agent-review, autoresearch-iterate-robustness.\", \"_ts\": 1773726498.417809, \"_n\": 6}, \"autoresearch/emit-path-results\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch/emit-path-results\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Reviewed results: 7.81ms to 1.1ms. Fixed store-projection layer violation. Both branches squash-merged to main.\", \"_ts\": 1773619073.550495, \"_n\": 2}, \"import-deferral-autoresearch\": {\"name\": \"import-deferral-autoresearch\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into autoresearch results. The read-latency experiment found the same pattern independently: import deferral is the dominant optimization (279ms\\u219235ms, mostly import path). Lazy imports for painted, lang, atoms, engine confirmed as the key lever.\", \"_ts\": 1773700300.53739, \"_n\": 3}, \"autoresearch-metric-design\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-metric-design\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Addressed. Deterministic wrapper handles measurement \\u2014 agent never sees or controls the metric. Keep/discard decided by wrapper comparing to fold best. Agent emits rich supporting facts (logs, hypotheses, ideas) that carry reasoning about results. Metric gaming mitigated by separation of measurement from agent. Schema includes hypothesis kind for testable predictions about what affects the metric.\", \"_ts\": 1773722801.347929, \"_n\": 4}, \"cross-loop-condition-ref\": {\"name\": \"cross-loop-condition-ref\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Real architectural gap (boundary conditions referencing other loops). Not blocking \\u2014 init-time substitution handles current cases. Parked until orchestration patterns need runtime-adjustable iteration limits.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.711818, \"_n\": 2}, \"live-mode-default\": {\"name\": \"live-mode-default\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Set default_mode=OutputMode.STATIC for fold reads. --live is now explicit opt-in. Fixed the ctrl+c issue.\", \"_ts\": 1773887732.220699, \"_n\": 2}, \"vertex-lifecycle-commands\": {\"name\": \"vertex-lifecycle-commands\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into bounded agent turns pattern. Start = loops init + first experiment emit. Complete = boundary condition fails. iterate.sh is the run clause. Harvest from worktrees is the only remaining piece, tracked separately if needed.\", \"_ts\": 1773887752.139841, \"_n\": 3}, \"autoresearch-ux-observability\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-ux-observability\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Three-layer UX complete: (1) Dashboard lens with panels, sparkline, namespace-grouped findings, in-progress detection. (2) Interactive TUI with per-iteration drill-down via timestamp attribution. (3) Prompt lens producing XML for agent consumption. Remaining observability (siftd for agent process visibility) is a separate thread.\", \"_ts\": 1773887749.741747, \"_n\": 4}, \"autoresearch-start-flow-redesign\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-start-flow-redesign\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved. Autoresearch is a vertex program using BOUNDED AGENT TURNS. No standalone start flow \\u2014 loops init creates vertex + seeds config, boundary run clause handles iteration. The iterate script is a minimal run clause target, not an orchestration system. Start is: init vertex, emit first experiment fact to kick the chain.\", \"_ts\": 1773722798.543172, \"_n\": 2}, \"xml-output-format\": {\"name\": \"xml-output-format\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Feature request. --xml alongside --json and --plain. Useful for agent-facing output. Not urgent.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.79649, \"_n\": 2}, \"sdk-vertex-manipulation\": {\"name\": \"sdk-vertex-manipulation\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Real tech debt \\u2014 string matching for AST operations. The lang parser can do this properly. Not blocking current work.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.879192, \"_n\": 2}, \"sdk-opportunities\": {\"name\": \"sdk-opportunities\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Accumulator thread. No new instances discovered recently. Parking until next SDK pain point surfaces.\", \"_ts\": 1773958760.960748, \"_n\": 2}, \"autoresearch-emit-compliance\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-emit-compliance\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Fixed vertex path resolution in prompt lens \\u2014 agents now emit findings, logs, and ideas during iterations. 4 iterations ran successfully with rich fact emission. Root cause was lens emitting vertex declaration name instead of resolvable path.\", \"_ts\": 1773887734.737159, \"_n\": 2}, \"autoresearch-agent-review\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-agent-review\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Agents now emit supporting facts and produce committed optimizations. 4 iterations: 91.4ms\\u219252.3ms (43% improvement). Agent behavior validated through dashboard and TUI drill-down. Earlier issues (no emits, hanging) resolved by prompt fixes and iterate.sh robustness.\", \"_ts\": 1773887737.385172, \"_n\": 2}, \"autoresearch-iterate-robustness\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-iterate-robustness\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"iterate.sh now handles: agent crash (non-zero exit \\u2192 status=crash), checks gate (optional CHECKS script \\u2192 status=checks_failed), multi-metric capture (all KEY=VALUE lines from benchmark), and clean separation of agent invocation from benchmark. Status semantics: keep/discard/crash/checks_failed.\", \"_ts\": 1773887746.893858, \"_n\": 2}, \"autoresearch-dashboard-live\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-dashboard-live\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Built dashboard lens with in-progress detection, side-by-side panels, word-wrapped two-column layout, and interactive TUI with iteration drill-down. Dashboard shows all sections at every zoom level. Live indicator via timestamp comparison. TUI auto-refreshes every 2s.\", \"_ts\": 1773887730.41217, \"_n\": 2}, \"fold-aware-default-lens\": {\"name\": \"fold-aware-default-lens\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. The fold lens IS the default lens with composable visibility gates (--refs, --facts). Remaining items (collect fold timelines, scalar stats) are future visibility layers following the same pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1773958459.542122, \"_n\": 5, \"_refs\": [\"decision/rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"thread/attention-density\", \"thread/data-introspection-lens\"]}, \"vertex-as-app\": {\"name\": \"vertex-as-app\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by loop-as-runtime. iterate.sh dissolving into vertex runtime was the wrong target. The loop is the runtime. Vertex is just a point.\", \"_ts\": 1774408847.968755, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/design/bounded-agent-turns\", \"decision/design/iterate-dissolves-into-vertex\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"attention-density\": {\"name\": \"attention-density\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Fully resolved. n+refs on FoldItem, salience sorting, namespace grouping, metadata badges, --refs visibility layer with filtered graph view, --facts visibility layer with source facts from replay. The visibility-as-gate model (Fidelity.visible) is the general mechanism.\", \"_ts\": 1773958459.466623, \"_n\": 7, \"_refs\": [\"decision/atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"decision/atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"decision/paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"decision/rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"decision/rendering/unfolded-kind-detection\"]}, \"data-introspection-lens\": {\"name\": \"data-introspection-lens\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into visibility-as-gate model. Ref graph \\u2192 --refs. Observer \\u2192 future --observers. Kind coverage in unfolded footer. Namespace distribution in namespace grouping.\", \"_ts\": 1773958459.627, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision/rendering/unfolded-kind-detection\", \"thread/attention-density\", \"thread/fold-aware-default-lens\"]}, \"ref-graph-view\": {\"name\": \"ref-graph-view\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into rendering/visibility-as-gate. Ref graph is a visibility layer on the default fold lens, not a separate view. --refs flag gates edge expansion at DETAILED+ depth. Inbound refs (\\u2190N) already surfaced in badges. Outbound refs (\\u2192N) to be added. Per-item edge expansion at DETAILED with --refs visible.\", \"_ts\": 1773949812.654239, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision/atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"thread/attention-density\", \"thread/data-introspection-lens\"]}, \"painted-0.1.4-migration\": {\"name\": \"painted-0.1.4-migration\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Painted v0.1.5 restored: layered architecture (core/ \\u2192 views/ \\u2192 cli/ \\u2192 tui/), three-axis Fidelity model integrated, cli/ consolidated to 4 files, build_fidelity hook added. Fidelity.shows() fixed to gate semantics. Submodule updated. 1377+444 tests passing.\", \"_ts\": 1773958459.366661, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision/rendering/fold-palette\", \"thread/fold-aware-default-lens\"]}, \"vertex-view-contract\": {\"name\": \"vertex-view-contract\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by loop-as-runtime. The view contract is per-loop, not per-vertex. Ticks, source facts, ref graphs are loop concerns. FoldState organized by loop.\", \"_ts\": 1774408848.05854, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"rendering/ticks-interface-deferred\", \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"velocity-of-ideas\": {\"name\": \"velocity-of-ideas\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact. Window density (touched-items-per-window, kind compression ratios) is now a property of the Tick primitive itself \\u2014 TickWindow carries delta_added/delta_updated/kind_compression. Velocity is density-over-time, captured at the primitive layer rather than as a separate concept.\", \"_ts\": 1777136463.965693, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\"]}, \"autoresearch-as-vertex\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-as-vertex\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Reframed by loop-as-runtime. Autoresearch is a loop, not a vertex. Experiment facts, fold by name, boundary on experiment close. Lives at a vertex point but the runtime is the loop.\", \"_ts\": 1774408848.127709, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\", \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\"]}, \"autoresearch-branch-discipline\": {\"name\": \"autoresearch-branch-discipline\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.94346, \"_n\": 2}, \"store-audit-reconstruction\": {\"name\": \"store-audit-reconstruction\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolves under loop-as-runtime. Store audit was needed because vertex-level scoping was wrong. With loop as the routing level, stores just hold facts at a point. The audit target shifts to ensuring loops are correctly declared, not that stores are correctly scoped.\", \"_ts\": 1774408827.542253, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\", \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\"]}, \"manual-tick-emission\": {\"name\": \"manual-tick-emission\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by design/seal-verb: sl seal ships the primitive. Both Apr-17 use cases land \\u2014 chord-carving (seal mid-session, each convergence gets its own attested window) and reflexive re-entry (seal on signal arrival). The two-year-later twist: the primitive arrived not as engine machinery but as vocabulary over existing machinery (emit + declared boundary), and what made it worth shipping NOW is signing \\u2014 a manually drawn boundary is an attestation act.\", \"_ts\": 1781049411.14333, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/seal-verb\", \"thread/ticks-window-filter\"]}, \"vertex-complete-contract\": {\"name\": \"vertex-complete-contract\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by architecture/loop-as-runtime. The five-dissolution cascade was solving real problems but attaching solutions to the wrong primitive. Vertex nesting, vertex operations, vertex scoping all dissolve when loop becomes the runtime. The vertex is a convergence loop with a store.\", \"_ts\": 1774408825.941429, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/emit-by-vertex\", \"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"loop-as-primitive\": {\"name\": \"loop-as-primitive\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"ref_ref\": \"83f18305-7a23-403d-aed0-d9888b1ce8f0\", \"_ts\": 1781295853.713011, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\"]}, \"emit-supersession-semantics\": {\"name\": \"emit-supersession-semantics\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Answered by precedent rather than design. Supersession was used twice in practice without ambiguity: design/ping-as-attention-signal \\u2192 design/cite-as-attention-signal (vocabulary rename), architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract \\u2192 architecture/loop-as-runtime (architectural pivot). Both work cleanly. Behavioral answer: superseded_by=kind/key is a payload convention; the fold honors it by resolving to a ULID ref. Not a first-class fold operation, just a payload field with consistent semantics.\", \"_ts\": 1777136470.17216, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\"]}, \"session-start-as-tickwindow\": {\"name\": \"session-start-as-tickwindow\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. Implemented as session_landing lens (user-global) + lens-declares-fetch contract (apps/loops). New structure: WINDOW header (TickWindow dashboard \\u2014 compression bar, per-kind chips, deltas) + HISTORY strip (row-per-window for prior 4 ticks, replaces bash head -15) + accumulated body with focus-filter marks from window.added_keys/updated_keys. Hook collapses from three renders stitched by bash to one lens invocation. 991 loops tests pass including 5 new for resolve_lens_fetch. First concrete consumer of TickWindow \\u2014 validates the three-layer separation Alcove reviewed 2026-04-23. Spawned thread current-open-window-semantics for a follow-up observation.\", \"_ts\": 1776998546.52757, \"_n\": 2}, \"current-open-window-semantics\": {\"name\": \"current-open-window-semantics\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by rename WINDOW \\u2192 LANDING + open-window bridge (b6a31c5). Three accumulated frictions all addressed: (1) sort quirk for fresh-but-unmarked items emitted post-window-close \\u2014 handled by open-window bridge, items with ts > window.ts get _MARK_UPDATED; (2) label ambiguity \\u2014 section is now LANDING, named for purpose (the slice you're landing into) not temporal position; (3) boundary semantics \\u2014 dissolved once grounded in actual invocation: lens is session-start-only in practice, the open window is empty by definition at session_start, so 'most-recent-closed' IS what the user lands into. Module docstring rewritten to reflect this. Lens still works correctly mid-session via the bridge \\u2014 the implementation is more general than the use case, which is fine, not expensive generality. If mid-session re-render becomes a workflow, revisit (2)/(3) with a concrete reader.\", \"ref_ref\": \"aad42c94-81a4-456a-8793-d062ff407531\", \"_ts\": 1777217281.901601, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"thread/session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, \"ping-primitive\": {\"name\": \"ping-primitive\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. 'loops ping' landed as thin verb over emit. Changes: (1) atoms/_make_collect extracts ref payload to _refs (matches upsert semantics for all fold types); (2) emit _parse_emit_parts accumulates multi-ref= occurrences and comma-forms into one payload value (fixes the silent-drop footgun); (3) project.vertex declares ping as unbounded collect fold; (4) _run_ping wrapper translates positional refs; (5) _inbound_count fixed to match both kind-qualified and bare ref forms (pre-existing namespaced-key bug). Full chain tested end-to-end: ping emits \\u2192 store \\u2192 fold \\u2192 lens inbound count bumps. 1008 loops / 404 atoms / 745 engine tests green, 17 new.\", \"_ts\": 1776999881.46086, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/ping-as-attention-signal\", \"rendering/fold-palette\", \"rendering/inbound-count-namespaced-keys\", \"thread/session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, \"topic-blind-landing\": {\"name\": \"topic-blind-landing\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"The session_landing lens surfaces recently-touched items (\\u2726/\\u25e6) and (forthcoming) stale work items, but doesn't surface decisions by topic-relevance to the current reasoning thread. Concrete instance from this session: while reasoning about orchestration, decision/bounded-agent-turns (Mar 17) and decision/boundary-executor-invariance (Mar 24) \\u2014 directly relevant prior art \\u2014 were not visible at landing and were missed during initial design work for design/plan-as-orchestration-substrate. The miss was caught by a separate query during verification, requiring a supersession to correct framing.\\n\\nFRICTION SHAPE \\u2014 Prior-art surfacing gap. Different from staleness (open-but-untouched, claim-on-attention from neglect). This is closed-but-relevant: durable knowledge that bears on current work but isn't keyed by recency or status. The reconcile lens doesn't help here either \\u2014 it's about lifecycle, not topic.\\n\\nPOSSIBLE FUTURE DIRECTION \\u2014 A derived key set keyed on topic-of-current-work, applied as another instance of derived-keys-as-focus-filter. Mechanism candidates: cite ref graph traversal (decisions cited recently \\u2192 surface decisions referenced from them), keyword overlap (vague), explicit topic tags on decisions (heavyweight). All speculative.\\n\\nSINGLE INSTANCE SO FAR \\u2014 Captured for pattern accumulation. Don't design yet \\u2014 wait for the second occurrence to confirm shape.\", \"_ts\": 1777139297.42032, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/bounded-agent-turns\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"thread/current-open-window-semantics\"]}, \"session-landing-plan-section\": {\"name\": \"session-landing-plan-section\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved. PLAN section renders as tier 0 in session_landing (above TASK), with headline-paragraph truncation that cuts cleanly at the first \\\\n\\\\n boundary so structured plan sections (FILES TOUCHED, SEQUENCE, OPEN QUESTIONS) stay hidden at SUMMARY zoom. Focus marks integrate via existing _item_mark/_mark_priority pattern. Verified via 'loops read project --lens session_landing --plain' \\u2014 stale-as-focus-filter-impl now visible at landing with \\u2726 glyph and [drafted] status badge. 1008 loops tests still pass. Decision: rendering/plan-section-tier-0.\", \"_ts\": 1777157162.706705, \"_n\": 4}, \"verbosity-fidelity-review\": {\"name\": \"verbosity-fidelity-review\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by rendering/salience-driven-display. Observation period closed: the four symptoms dissolved into one root cause (truncation is salience-blind) and one absorbed concern (lightweight-emission-ergonomics is the same composition viewed from emission side). Implementation tracked under plan/salience-driven-display-impl.\", \"_ts\": 1777175655.33863, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/salience-driven-display\"]}, \"terminal-status-asymmetry\": {\"name\": \"terminal-status-asymmetry\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"LANDING render after committing this session's plan transition surfaced an asymmetry: salience-driven-display-impl (status=done) disappeared from PLAN section entirely, while lightweight-emission-ergonomics (status=superseded) remains. Both are terminal statuses (no longer active attention). Either: (a) both should filter once outside the landing window \\u2014 terminal items don't crowd the section; (b) both should stay with terminal-status de-emphasis until they age out; (c) just-emitted terminal items should surface as \\u2726 (touched this open-session) regardless of status, then drop next session. Current behavior is the worst of (a) and (b) \\u2014 inconsistent across statuses, and the just-emitted plan vanishes from view immediately after recording (loses the rope-winding signal that a transition happened). Sub-pattern of the same fabric as current-open-window-semantics: what counts as 'in the landing view' after a status transition. Sitting with this \\u2014 connects to observe-dashboard-dissolution observation target.\", \"_ts\": 1777217535.775942, \"_n\": 1}, \"comms-vertex-real-time\": {\"name\": \"comms-vertex-real-time\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295853.849071, \"_n\": 3}, \"cross-machine-vertex-visibility\": {\"name\": \"cross-machine-vertex-visibility\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 gated on sqlmerge remote transport landing; the three loops-side concerns (cursor mgmt, config distribution, lens-composition-not-shared-write) reactivate then.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.355008, \"_n\": 3}, \"daemon-tool-call-emission-shape\": {\"name\": \"daemon-tool-call-emission-shape\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Relay's daemon-tool-use-vertex-promotion change (DM 276) raised the question of emission shape: raw per-call vs aggregated per dispatch cycle. Initial loops-claude recommendation: aggregated tool.call.batch per cycle (write-time coalescing). Lens (msg 295) pushed back: write-time aggregation is irreversible \\u2014 locks out future Version B (lifecycle debugging) analysis on historical data. Resolution (DM 306): lens is right. Today's just-shipped fidelity wire makes read-time filter viable in a way it wasn't before \\u2014 raw emission + Fidelity lines budget at the fold lens. Loops-claude reversed: write-time raw tool.call{name,status=started}, read-time aggregation when needed. Subprocess overhead at peak ~25/min is acceptable; if it becomes a real cost, batch transport (multi-emit subprocess) without changing per-call grain. Pattern: append-only-store + fold-at-read + Fidelity-rendering-budget jointly enable the right answer. The dissolution test was right there.\", \"_ts\": 1777256906.554921, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/context-window-fidelity-consumer\", \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-wired\"]}, \"fidelity-contract-tests\": {\"name\": \"fidelity-contract-tests\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.670134, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/visible-tag-inclusion-property\", \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-wired\", \"paradigm/surfaced-invariant\"]}, \"uv-install-on-every-emit\": {\"name\": \"uv-install-on-every-emit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16 by `uv tool install` of loops 0.3.1 \\u2014 CLI now reachable as `loops` and `sl` (shorthand) globally without `uv run` prefix. Per-invocation install/uninstall noise eliminated. Dogfooded in session: 10+ emits at thought-speed without psychological friction. Tactical fix; daemon-as-substrate remains a longer-arc consideration (see extract-loops-core-cleanly).\", \"_ts\": 1778912018.200905, \"_n\": 2, \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/loops-installed-globally-via-uv-tool\"]}, \"structured-cite-for-comms\": {\"name\": \"structured-cite-for-comms\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.533096, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/cite-as-attention-signal\"]}, \"emit-skips-boundary-catchup\": {\"name\": \"emit-skips-boundary-catchup\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 boundary code has moved since (seal verb, SessionEnd wiring); the dissolution path sketched here needs re-derivation against current code when next touched.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.491238, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\", \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\"]}, \"umwelt-as-paradigm-frame\": {\"name\": \"umwelt-as-paradigm-frame\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295853.986503, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\"]}, \"daemon-as-new-lib\": {\"name\": \"daemon-as-new-lib\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Surfaced 2026-04-27 as the operational consequence of paradigm/boundary-as-watcher-triple: drivers as first-class need a host that runs continuously. The daemon isn't 'just a new lib' \\u2014 it's the operational layer the conceptual work has been implying. What it dissolves (compounding gains): uv-install-on-every-emit (thin clients hit a socket, daemon eats install cost once); vertex program cache (load once, fold in memory, replay never re-runs per emit; per-fact cost ms not seconds); notify/wake substrate (something has to be alive to receive wakes \\u2014 the daemon is that something); cross-process boundary deduplication (single fire-decider, no race on evaluate_boundaries catchup); sync further attenuation (cadence drivers run continuously in daemon; CLI 'loops sync' becomes 'fire all due cadences now' debug affordance); streaming subscription model becomes natural; today's dispatcher injection carries forward unchanged \\u2014 dispatcher lives in daemon, fires subprocesses from daemon's process tree. What goes in the lib: process lifecycle (start/stop/status, foreground/background), transport (UDS for v1, length-prefixed JSON), protocol (fact-emit, query, subscribe, fire-driver, list-vertices), vertex registry, driver host loop, dispatcher with subprocess lifecycle, optional event bus for subscribers. What stays where: engine still owns Vertex/Loop/VertexProgram/drivers as primitives \\u2014 no daemon awareness; atoms unchanged; apps/loops CLI grows thin-client mode (if daemon up, send fact over socket; otherwise direct path). Naming candidates: hearth (always-on warmth, where loops live), keep (preservation + fortified position), roost (where things settle), tend (caretaker), pulse (driver heartbeat), weave (multi-driver coordination), host (accurate but generic). Lean: hearth or keep. Considerations \\u2014 subprocess management (zombie reaping, output handling), hot reload (defer to v2), single-instance enforcement (PID file or socket-binding), daemon-as-observer (emits own start/stop/dispatched-runs/error facts; same observer-as-vertex pattern), migration path (opt-in initially, fall back to direct if daemon absent \\u2014 same code two paths). Prior art Kyle flagged for UX mining: siftd (operational persistence patterns, daemon already exists and survives sessions), the recorder lib (just-built, has patterns relevant here), lldap-invite (UX pattern source). Rich-in-refs note: this thread sits at the convergence of comms-vertex-real-time, uv-install-on-every-emit, manual-tick-emission, loop-as-primitive, the dispatch-consolidation work, and the boundary-as-watcher-triple paradigm decision \\u2014 picking it up will likely surface more refs as those threads converge through the daemon as the substrate. Parked deliberately for later; not blocking, but the ops/cleanliness frame and the next paradigm work both pass through here.\", \"_ts\": 1777350930.78872, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\", \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"paradigm/boundary-as-watcher-triple\", \"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\", \"thread/loop-as-primitive\", \"thread/manual-tick-emission\", \"thread/uv-install-on-every-emit\"]}, \"documentation-obeys-model\": {\"name\": \"documentation-obeys-model\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.123942, \"_n\": 2}, \"sqlmerge-extraction-pressure-test\": {\"name\": \"sqlmerge-extraction-pressure-test\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Port landed 2026-04-30 19:24. Final state: 57/57 libs/store + 748/748 engine + 1011/1011 apps/loops passing; ruff and ty clean. Diff stat: ~98 insertions, ~108 deletions across 12 files. **Concrete changes**: (1) libs/store/pyproject.toml adds sqlmerge as path-dep (editable, points at ~/Code/sqlmerge); (2) merge.py uses sqlmerge.attached_merge(conn=) with caller-owned _open(target) conn \\u2014 sqlite-ulid extension and WAL pragma preserved; (3) receive.py wraps sqlmerge.receive with merge_fn/count_fn adapters, ReceiveResult shape preserved; (4) _transport_local.py push delegates to receive_store, pull is bytes-only returning TransferMeta \\u2014 synthetic Receipt eliminated; (5) transport.py Transport Protocol updated (pull -> TransferMeta); (6) __init__.py re-exports TransferMeta. **Two follow-ups required before main**: (a) path-dep portability \\u2014 needs git-dep or sqlmerge-as-workspace-member; only resolves on Kyle's machine today; (b) libs/store/CLAUDE.md Level 2 doc drift \\u2014 describes ATTACH-based merge as loops-internal, now sqlmerge.attached_merge handles framing. **Bet validated**: caller-owned conn was the load-bearing mechanism for preserving extension/pragma state; Receipt/TransferMeta split forced fixing a real bug (synthetic Receipt that pull_store ignored). Substrate-first extraction worked as designed.\", \"_ts\": 1777577081.727965, \"_n\": 4}, \"sqlmerge-portability\": {\"name\": \"sqlmerge-portability\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Sqlmerge ports landed via path-dep: { path = '../../../sqlmerge', editable = true } in libs/store/pyproject.toml. Resolves on Kyle's machine; breaks on any other clone-and-build (other agents, CI, fresh checkout). Two clean options before this leaves the local machine: (a) workspace-member \\u2014 add sqlmerge to root [tool.uv.workspace] members and switch dep to { workspace = true }. Faster iteration across both repos, matches how engine is consumed today, no publishing pressure. (b) git-dep \\u2014 push sqlmerge to a remote, switch to { git = '...', rev = '...' }. Better shape if sqlmerge gets external consumers (siftd, discord-scraper, others). Kyle deferred decision; both paths viable. Resolves when one is picked. Watch: sqlmerge SSH/HTTP work in v0.2/v0.3 will revise this dep \\u2014 workspace-member makes that ripple cheaper, git-dep makes it more controlled.\", \"_ts\": 1777579183.521699, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity-as-kaleidoscope\": {\"name\": \"identity-as-kaleidoscope\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.260877, \"_n\": 2}, \"loops-as-skill-instructions\": {\"name\": \"loops-as-skill-instructions\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.397579, \"_n\": 2}, \"harness-emission-shape\": {\"name\": \"harness-emission-shape\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Sharpened 2026-05-10 with Kyle: split into query-run + query-comparison as separate collect-style kinds on coupling-kernels vertex. Recipe-hash for spec identity, binding fields separate (different snapshots aren't comparable). Artifacts referenced via existing CachedEmbedder cache path \\u2014 the cache IS the sidecar, content-addressed by spec_hash; no parallel artifact store invented. Components inline for cheap comparison-without-replay. Comparisons ref runs via existing ref machinery \\u2014 cluster lineage chain becomes queryable via the ref graph with no new mechanism. See decisions design/coupling-kernels-emission-shape, design/query-run-fact, design/query-comparison-fact.\", \"_ts\": 1778429317.596799, \"_n\": 2}, \"system-prompt-emission-encoding\": {\"name\": \"system-prompt-emission-encoding\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 partially superseded by the two-register identity lens work (design/voice-two-register-rendering); the three-layer framing remains good prior art for the next identity-lens session.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.629654, \"_n\": 3}, \"config-reference-drift\": {\"name\": \"config-reference-drift\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 de-facto fixed via fix-candidate (1): ~/.config/loops/lenses/*.py are now symlinks into .loops/lenses/ (verified live today editing reconcile.py \\u2014 cp refused, files identical). One source of truth; drift impossible by construction. Residue: experiments/config-reference/lenses/ deletion orphaned a test, tracked at friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main.\", \"_ts\": 1781295561.481092, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\"]}, \"read-path-depth-gap\": {\"name\": \"read-path-depth-gap\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-06-12 (was status=converged \\u2014 off-table vocab, normalized). The convergence's decision landed (painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines); deferred render patches (session_landing body-row drop, reconcile --plain sectioning, word-boundary truncation) fold into thread:painted-overreach-review, which owns the browse-frequent rendering budget question.\", \"_ts\": 1781295575.648894, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"thread:painted-overreach-review\"]}, \"receipt-as-corpus-experiments\": {\"name\": \"receipt-as-corpus-experiments\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Queued: three competing hypotheses about how receipts cluster in fold space - cluster-near-referents, form-meta-cluster, split-by-content-density. Plus dynamic-lean-vs-static-priming. Harness exists (coupling-kernels.vertex), proof-of-loop closed via bug-find cascade last session. Next: pick one as first run, treat receipt store as corpus, apply structure-reveal pipeline.\", \"_ts\": 1778455863.941904, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:kernel-ratio-robustness\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\"]}, \"deliberation-depth-lens\": {\"name\": \"deliberation-depth-lens\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved: lens built vertex-local at experiments/coupling-kernels/lenses/deliberation_depth.py. Two-part depth metric (n_within + n_incoming_query_run_refs) works on existing data \\u2014 no emit-discipline change needed for v1. Live test on 7 hypotheses produced 1 flag (find-richness-scale-drops-ratio). Surprise: surfaces low-experimental-deliberation broadly, not just overfit specifically \\u2014 TYPE A (bug-discovery confirmations) and TYPE B (first-test overfit) both flag, agent classifies. Limitations noted in docstring: doesn't trace hypothesis\\u2192hypothesis replication chains (emit_hypothesis() doesn't accept refs yet \\u2014 precondition gap captured at design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs).\", \"_ts\": 1778459065.499303, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"e5-instruction-tuned-replication\": {\"name\": \"e5-instruction-tuned-replication\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Queued for next experimental session. Replicate runs 09 + 12 (truncation sweep + title-only falsifier) using E5InstructEmbedder instead of MiniLM. Setup: same fixture corpus (project_all_kinds_manifest.json), instruction='Group these items by the design concern or area of work each item participates in.' (matches 07/08). E5 baseline embeddings available pre-computed in fixtures/proj_e5_allkinds_concern.npz \\u2014 only truncated/title-only variants need fresh embedding (cached). Key questions: (1) Does cliff at B=1120\\u2192560 survive embedder switch? If yes, geometry is content-structural; if no, it's MiniLM artifact. (2) Does title-only fail to preserve survivors as it did at MiniLM? If now preserves, verdict-locus interpretation might be valid at instruction-tuned scale specifically. Either outcome is high-information per alcove. Carry forward: three-scales-three-geometries refinement (title-space, body-opener-space, recognition-trigger-space) as the conceptual frame for analysis.\", \"_ts\": 1778458524.238998, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\"]}, \"low-budget-bounce-mechanism\": {\"name\": \"low-budget-bounce-mechanism\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved by dissolution: question answered from existing run-13 receipts via cluster-membership comparison across B=140/95/60. Verdict: regime shift (NEW items enter clusters at low budgets), not survivor preservation (would have been subset). 57 items at B=60 not in B=140 \\u2014 ~30% turnover. New hypothesis pulled for future work: cluster-identity-at-low-budgets-is-prefix-driven. Builder-inhabitant note: this is the second instance of dissolution-default working today \\u2014 the answer was already in the receipts, didn't need a new run. Receipts as analytical substrate, not just provenance.\", \"_ts\": 1778461342.22104, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:finding/low-budget-bounce-is-regime-shift\"]}, \"peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\": {\"name\": \"peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"UMBRELLA as of reconcile 2026-06-12: now the single open loops-side vouch thread \\u2014 12 sibling threads parked into it (conceptual-reground, session-owed, impl-handoff, event-vs-origin, bounded-rollout, oauth-integration, deployment-constraint, write-path-friction, adr-cross-reference, lattice-math, grant-close-or-document, auth-architect-conversation). The live question is unchanged: what does real vouch usage teach engine.Peer/Grant. Hypotheses peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant + scope-check-is-per-operation + vouch-as-loops-lib remain proposed under this umbrella \\u2014 same evidence stream adjudicates them. Enterprise detail: agent-attestation vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1781295838.251415, \"_n\": 2}, \"libs-public-internal-boundary\": {\"name\": \"libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved (2026-05-13): convention settled and emitted as design/libs-public-internal-boundary. Forced to crystallize by the libs/sign carve. Public = __init__.py __all__ exports; non-underscore submodules public; underscore-prefixed internal; per-lib CLAUDE.md documents stability posture; utility-lib breaks ship as coordinated upgrades (tagged loops release + per-consumer pin bumps), not atomic commits.\", \"_ts\": 1778698197.620783, \"_n\": 2}, \"trust-substrate-adr-cross-reference\": {\"name\": \"trust-substrate-adr-cross-reference\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.696071, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"transport-as-substrate\": {\"name\": \"transport-as-substrate\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Open. Transport exists in libs/store/src/store/transport.py as wire-independent Protocol (push: local_path \\u2192 remote_path, pull: remote_path \\u2192 local_path) with LocalTransport implementation. push_store/pull_store orchestrate with since=/kinds= filters. NO project-store thinking captured on transport-as-substrate despite 'we've discussed it previously' (Kyle 2026-05-13). Each consumer has bespoke transport (sqlmerge SSH/HTTP, comms HTTP/MCP, pile signed URLs, vouch JWT issuance). Extension needed: identity-binding (Peer + Grant parameters) + grant-bound slicing before bytes transport. Wire stays consumer-choice. Emission gap caught \\u2014 capturing now so the design conversation has a fact-stream anchor. Connects to peer-grant-extension and substrate-not-host decisions.\", \"_ts\": 1778684791.463155, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"lattice-math-needs-writing\": {\"name\": \"lattice-math-needs-writing\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.834369, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"grant-as-fact-close-or-document\": {\"name\": \"grant-as-fact-close-or-document\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.972291, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"decision:design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"observation:convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\": {\"name\": \"vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295836.868831, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"decision:design/vouch-rebuild-fresh-repo\", \"observation:convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"vouch-event-vs-origin-modeling\": {\"name\": \"vouch-event-vs-origin-modeling\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.006757, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\": {\"name\": \"substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Open (2026-05-13): vouch's Peer/Grant exercise (~/Code/vouch explore/peer-grant subtask, commit d95d36a) surfaced a structural finding \\u2014 voucher has no slot on Peer because Peer is per-agent (identity+accumulated-authorization-at-current-time) while vouching is per-assertion (voucher\\u00d7holder\\u00d7scope). Two recast options proposed by scrivener's worker: (a) engine grows a Vouch atom that names voucher\\u00d7holder\\u00d7scope; (b) substrate stays minimal, consumers walk the Fact ledger for the relation. Disposition: (b) \\u2014 minimal, no engine change. Rationale: assertions live on Facts (observer carries voucher, payload carries scope, chain_metadata carries ancestry); 'who vouched for holder X' is structurally a ledger query, not a field lookup. Walking the ledger isn't workaround, it's the trust-attaches-to-facts model operationalized. Adding a Vouch atom would be substrate-feels-universal \\u2014 promoting one consumer's relation to engine identity when the existing Fact already carries it. Canonical query: loops fact-history --kind vouch --holder X. Friction stays in the consumer (vouch wraps); engine stays clean. The vouch-impl-handoff Peer/Grant recast question closes via this thread: no recast needed for the voucher\\u00d7holder\\u00d7scope relation.\", \"_ts\": 1778702733.115577, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"decision:design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"cross-adapter-review-pattern-codification\": {\"name\": \"cross-adapter-review-pattern-codification\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295854.805653, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/libs-sign-merged\", \"observation:practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\"]}, \"vouch-substrate-friction-from-write-path\": {\"name\": \"vouch-substrate-friction-from-write-path\", \"body\": \"vouch's first substrate-crossing exercise (vouch cf28a24) surfaced friction worth substrate-side attention; none load-bearing yet, but recording before second-consumer N=2 lights up: (1) SqliteStore.append json.dumps payload \\u2014 frozenset values silently fail to persist; vouch coerces scope\\u2192sorted list at emit boundary. (2) Fact has no caller-accessible id so vouch puts jti in payload \\u2014 convention works but hidden discipline. (3) Fact.ts float vs JWT iat int alignment requires caller to compute 'now' once. (4) Peer\\u2192Fact\\u2192Peer round-trip does not exist; multi-hop chains will force a decision on whether peer_from_vouch_fact() lives in vouch or substrate. See vouch/docs/friction/issue-vouch-write-path.md for full.\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.558755, \"_n\": 3, \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"vouch-bounded-substrate-rollout\": {\"name\": \"vouch-bounded-substrate-rollout\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.143746, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-as-first-bounded-substrate-consumer\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"phase1-vouch-arc-with-cross-repo-consumers\": {\"name\": \"phase1-vouch-arc-with-cross-repo-consumers\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Wave 1 closed 2026-05-15 ~04:50 UTC. Phase 1 \\u00a71.1\\u2013\\u00a71.9 + F12 dissolution all landed on vouch main; v0.5.0 tagged at 0c7e48c. **Outcome:** vouch + pile + comms + commission all shipped against the substrate-discipline registry; ADR-0004 mirrored across vouch + commission citing paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract as canonical bidirectional pointer; three N=3 instances of consumer-owns-its-vocabulary; zero substrate paradigm amendments throughout. **Methodology:** dissolution-first applied at T6 (supersession-marker dissolved entirely), T8 (scope-vocabulary dissolved at consumer-owned audiences), and F12 (resolved as side-effect of T8). PLAN-stage codex review caught FAM widening that would have shipped as wire-shape regression. **Self-reflection (banked 2026-05-15 ~05:00 UTC):** over-emitted several paradigm-level framings as decisions when they should have been hypotheses with status=proposed (wire-identity-stability second confirmation was within-arc not independent; per-issuer-config-axes-vary similar; asymmetry-framing emitted after single codex catch). Methodological correction at practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision. Cumulative-artifact maintenance concern at pattern/cumulative-artifact-load-bearing-needs-consolidation. **Next forcing functions watching the registry:** comms phase 4 ship (cairn dispatched member-binding worker); commission Phase 5 cutover (gated on cross-repo work + E2E); iss-dispatch N=3 factoring (three implementations + friction-doc enumerating cleavages now in place). **Closing thread.** Refs: decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract, decision:paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary, decision:paradigm/substrate-paradigm-vs-substrate-distribution-immutability, decision:framing/wire-identity-stability-beats-internal-immutability, decision:paradigm/consumer-owned-vs-vouch-owned-audience-asymmetry, decision:practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision, decision:pattern/cumulative-artifact-load-bearing-needs-consolidation.\", \"_ts\": 1778821191.729287, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"decision:practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision\"]}, \"key-and-lens-kwargs-access-primitives\": {\"name\": \"key-and-lens-kwargs-access-primitives\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-15: shipped in v0.3.1 (commits f3492b2 + 57d547e + 65ea07b + d43fd79; release at github.com/kgruel/strange-loops/releases/tag/v0.3.1; PyPI strange-loops==0.3.1). --key prefix filter (kind-aware via existing fold-key spec, prefix matching with full-key-as-degenerate-prefix), --kind kind/key embedded syntax now also prefix-matches (back-compat preserved), call_lens_fetch using inspect.signature for safe lens-kwargs dispatch with TypeError-from-lens-body propagation. Smoke verified against real project store: --key design/lens narrows to 8 design/lens-* decisions, --kind thread --key key- honors name-keyed fold field, --kind decision/atoms (embedded back-compat) returns 5 items. ~90 LOC + 10 new tests + 1029 loops + 3961 lib tests green, zero regressions, no goldens drifted. CLI surface for arbitrary lens-declared flags (--context, --severity) deferred \\u2014 call_lens_fetch infrastructure ready; CLI dispatch restructuring needed to do advisor-recommended strict-mode (lens resolution before arg parsing, error on truly unknown flags). Lower priority post-InferioMinion-migration-path: their guide kind moves to name=context/foo prefix, --key serves their case directly. --match hypothesis (project/namespace-as-mental-model-for-fold-keys) remains status=proposed pending observation of whether grep usage drops at InferioMinion's site after --key arrives.\", \"_ts\": 1778878292.221478, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design/guidance-as-lens-not-kind\", \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"design/lens-fetch-kwargs-passthrough\"]}, \"vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\": {\"name\": \"vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295836.454866, \"_n\": 5, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/vouch-act-side-libssign-plus-l4\", \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"], \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\"}, \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\": {\"name\": \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295836.731746, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/signature-vs-body-resolved-by-binding-level\", \"decision:design/vouch-act-side-libssign-plus-l4\", \"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"decision:paradigm/audience-distinct-from-authorization\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"thread:vouch-deployment-substrate-constraint\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\", \"thread:vouch-oauth-integration-question\"], \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\"}, \"cite-and-diff-as-lifecycle-pair\": {\"name\": \"cite-and-diff-as-lifecycle-pair\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Merged into thread:trace-diff-rendering-shape at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 lifecycle-diff (same fold-key across emissions) IS shape (b) of that thread's fork; cite-side is already shipped. One design conversation, not two.\", \"_ts\": 1781295863.811218, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:trace-diff-rendering-shape\"]}, \"feature-correlation-as-attribution-gap\": {\"name\": \"feature-correlation-as-attribution-gap\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 the asked-for convention exists: CLAUDE.md 'Correlation fields' section defines feature=<branch-or-arc-name> and ops=<operational-arc>, with the thread-vs-attribution distinction this thread proposed ('threads carry the conversation; correlation fields carry the attribution'). The InferiorMinion-inspired gap closed by adoption.\", \"_ts\": 1781295561.618235, \"_n\": 2}, \"bilateral-runbook-in-claudemd\": {\"name\": \"bilateral-runbook-in-claudemd\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Runbook v1 committed to CLAUDE.md, file untracked from git. Bilateral protocol established: hard-stop discipline rule for Kyle (48h emission / 7d reconcile), emit-with-graph-fidelity practice, friction-as-fact-kind, correlation fields (feature=, ops=), expanded read-path traversal. cite-atrophy diagnosis was the trigger; runbook prevents that class of gap going forward.\", \"_ts\": 1778911884.336951, \"_n\": 2}, \"extract-loops-core-cleanly\": {\"name\": \"extract-loops-core-cleanly\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.217135, \"_n\": 2}, \"painted-overreach-review\": {\"name\": \"painted-overreach-review\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Kyle: painted overreach has made store-review painful enough that he avoids emitting design-thinking because the read round-trip is unpleasant. Specific pain: --help is dense/oppressive. Hypothesis: painted is correctly scoped for read-once rendering but over-styled for browse-frequently rendering. Review scope: which painted surfaces are browse-frequent (help, list views, reconcile lens) vs read-once (single-fact display, session_landing). Different styling budgets for different cadences. Connects to operator-IR-from-siftd-status \\u2014 that intro was supposed to help; need to verify current state.\", \"_ts\": 1778910574.001496, \"_n\": 1}, \"emit-receipt-on-write\": {\"name\": \"emit-receipt-on-write\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved as thread, re-emitted as friction kind (see design/friction-as-fact-kind). Tracking continues under friction backlog.\", \"_ts\": 1778911884.044199, \"_n\": 2}, \"loud-fold-key-error\": {\"name\": \"loud-fold-key-error\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved as thread, re-emitted as friction kind. Tracking continues under friction backlog.\", \"_ts\": 1778911884.170922, \"_n\": 2}, \"stdin-message-for-emit\": {\"name\": \"stdin-message-for-emit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Shipped. --stdin FIELD and --file FIELD=PATH explicit flags landed in apps/loops/src/loops/commands/emit.py + apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/emit.py (two parsers, both updated). Implementation: ~100 LOC helper (_apply_input_sources), ~200 LOC tests (TestApplyInputSources class + 3 integration tests through main()). Exercised via installed sl: apostrophe-bearing prose ships clean through both --stdin and --file; @ in values stays literal (backward-compat verified empirically); all error paths surface as expected. 63/63 emit tests pass; 1278/1278 loops app tests pass; no regressions. NO engine/spec/vertex-file changes \\u2014 pure CLI feature. Three-pivot design arc captured in observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator, observation:pattern/loops-field-role-family, observation:practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots; architectural conclusion in decision:design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention.\", \"_ts\": 1779225354.256909, \"_n\": 5, \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention\"]}, \"session-start-discipline-metrics\": {\"name\": \"session-start-discipline-metrics\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved as thread, re-emitted as friction kind. Tracking continues under friction backlog.\", \"_ts\": 1778911884.22512, \"_n\": 2}, \"nudge-hooks-on-user-prompt\": {\"name\": \"nudge-hooks-on-user-prompt\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved as thread, re-emitted as friction kind. Tracking continues under friction backlog.\", \"_ts\": 1778911884.279393, \"_n\": 2}, \"operator-ir-from-siftd-status\": {\"name\": \"operator-ir-from-siftd-status\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Kyle referenced introducing Operator IR from siftd as something that was supposed to help with store-review pain. Question: what did we actually ship from that, is it in current main, does it help with the painted-overreach pain? Need: trace the relevant commits, confirm whether the IR is in the read path, evaluate whether further extraction would close the browse-frequent gap. Pre-req for painted-overreach-review scope decision.\", \"_ts\": 1778910597.275709, \"_n\": 1}, \"patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\": {\"name\": \"patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Update 2026-05-16 (session close): patch-emit portion RESOLVED via decision:design/fold-merge-default \\u2014 dissolved into one-line fold semantic flip (replace \\u2192 merge). Remaining: (1) diff-render \\u2014 landing as part of trace MVP via --diff field-delta lines; (2) fact-migration \\u2014 kind/key/field reshape, deferred until orphan-fact patterns surface (today's two orphans logged but not urgent). Trace consumes patch chains naturally now that fold-merge means each fact-stream entry IS a patch. Thread stays open under status=partial; closes when trace ships + fact-migration scoped.\", \"_ts\": 1778956233.848165, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"friction:sl-cite-malformed-kind\", \"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\"]}, \"trace-implementation\": {\"name\": \"trace-implementation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16. Two commits land the trace arc: 803ba03 (trace verb, lens, dispatch \\u2014 Phases 1-5) and 68a3361 (engine combine retain_facts fix \\u2014 collapses Phase 6 into substrate transparency). Phase 7 (golden tests + changelog) deferred as polish; unit-level coverage in test_fetch.py and test_vertex_reader.py is the load-bearing test surface. Both blocking frictions resolved (lineage-view-missing, trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty). Session shape: emit-as-we-go practice held \\u2014 each phase surfaced a decision in-moment rather than at session-end. Advisor catches drove key refinements: misleading empty-message UX (fixed), missing fetch_fold regression test (added), --diff per-fact-vs-cumulative reframing (decided cumulative, shipped). Bugs caught + fixed in passing: (1) fetch_fold stripped source_facts on key filter; (2) ref parser used '/' instead of ':' separator; (3) per-entity diff accumulator local-rebinding bug; (4) combine path didn't thread retain_facts. Each bug followed the same shape as the work \\u2014 visible only when exercised, not visible at design time. Thread closes; trace-arc as a whole is shippable. Future work: inbound refs (--graph) and per-fact refs as v2 if/when read patterns demand them.\", \"_ts\": 1778962991.814365, \"_n\": 5, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\", \"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"decision:design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\", \"decision:implementation/fetch-fold-preserves-source-facts-on-filter\", \"decision:implementation/trace-source-facts-shape-adapter\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"friction:trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"trace-diff-rendering-shape\": {\"name\": \"trace-diff-rendering-shape\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Phase 4 design question surfaced by advisor pre-Phase-4 review. Original plan said --diff renders 'field-delta lines like status: open \\u2192 refined' \\u2014 that's CUMULATIVE diff (each fact framed against prior state). But DETAILED zoom already shows each fact's payload fields under that fact (per-fact 'patch view' \\u2014 because fold-merge means the payload IS the patch). So the question is which shape --diff adds value over DETAILED. Two shapes:\\n\\n(a) PER-FACT (already in DETAILED): each emit's payload-as-fields shown directly. Free, no replay needed. 'What did this emit say' \\u2014 direct from store.\\n   Example: fact 2 shows: status=refined, refs=A,B,C\\n\\n(b) CUMULATIVE (advisor's reading of original plan): each fact framed against accumulated prior state. Needs replay-and-compare. 'What CHANGED from prior'.\\n   Example: fact 2 shows: status: open \\u2192 refined, refs: +C (added)\\n\\nIf (a) is the goal, --diff dissolves into DETAILED+ already exists. If (b) is the goal, --diff is its own thing \\u2014 replay-and-compare logic, semantics for adds/removes on refs, omitted-fields handling. The lineage-view-missing friction wants (b) \\u2014 'the braid through resolution' is about deltas, not snapshots. Phase 4 should commit to (b) explicitly, OR document that (a) suffices and mark friction:lineage-view-missing partial-resolution. Picks up: this thread + sample of how a multi-fact lifecycle would render in each shape at SUMMARY/DETAILED zoom.\", \"_ts\": 1778957569.752371, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"trace-in-session-hooks\": {\"name\": \"trace-in-session-hooks\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16 (commit 917329a, pushed). ARCS block lands in session_start additionalContext. Top 2 multi-fact open/partial threads rendered as cumulative diff. Composes with existing TOUCHED block: TOUCHED carries current state, ARCS carries trajectory. Shell composition at .claude/hooks/arcs-block.py \\u2014 no session_landing.py edit needed. Advisor caught the drift toward lens modification and forced the shell-composition path; right call. Pre-check on D (identity prompt) showed single-fact-per-topic pattern in identity observations \\u2014 --diff has nothing to compress, walls of text. D parked at thread:trace-in-identity-prompt for design conversation with Kyle on the right shape (probably --refs on a specific topic, not all-of-practice). Real test of C is next session opening \\u2014 accept that, don't recheck obsessively. Worth-noting: with this commit, the system_prompt of my next session will be assembled by a script I just wrote in this session, rendering data via a verb I just shipped. Builder-inhabitant recursion at one more layer.\", \"_ts\": 1778965136.465455, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"trace-in-identity-prompt\": {\"name\": \"trace-in-identity-prompt\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Parked 2026-05-16: D pre-check failed. 'sl trace identity observation/practice/ --diff --since 7d' covers 14 entities, each single-fact (one observation = one emit pattern in this kind). --diff value-add is multi-fact lifecycles; this is just rendering observations in ASC time order with full message bodies = walls of text, no better than current 'Recent observations' fold render. Need to rethink shape. Candidates for next session: (a) --refs on a specific recently-pulled topic (concept-chain reading), (b) trace identity DECISIONS instead of observations (decisions get refined across sessions, multi-fact), (c) --since narrower + --kind specific to a topic. Right answer not obvious from current view; advisor's caution holds \\u2014 better to ship C alone than ship D as walls-of-text. Re-enter with Kyle for design conversation on D's real shape.\", \"_ts\": 1778964940.834784, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-in-session-hooks\"]}, \"deliberation-depth-lens-build\": {\"name\": \"deliberation-depth-lens-build\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"deliberation-depth\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16. Built .loops/lenses/deliberation.py \\u2014 structural overfit detector with five-bucket discrimination (SUSPICIOUS / HEALTHY / IN-FLIGHT / BATCH / OTHER). Three commits to main (initial build, calibration tightening, hooks+lens-move companion). Final calibration on project store: hypothesis SUS=0 HEALTHY=4 OPEN=9 BATCH=6 OTHER=2 (zero false positives after advisor-driven re-inspection caught me declaring done on bucket-arithmetic without running the SUSPICIOUS list through manual inspection \\u2014 the lens's intended workflow on its own output); thread SUS=6 HEALTHY=95 (six retrospective-observations-as-threads correctly flagged). The Alcove signal isn't 'closed fast' \\u2014 it's 'never staked as a prediction.' emit_count<=1 catches that specifically. Closure refs: design decision (final criterion + rationale), repo-owns-lenses decision (where the lens lives), upstream hypothesis (vouch-as-loops-lib pull), and the related vouch thread (the calibration warning that motivated building the structural detector rather than relying on manual noticing-skill at next solo session).\", \"_ts\": 1778977257.268073, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-lens\", \"decision:design/repo-owns-loops-discipline-lenses\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"paradigm/suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check\", \"practice/read-path-features-over-noticing-skills\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\"]}, \"id-primitive-substrate-rescope\": {\"name\": \"id-primitive-substrate-rescope\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-06-12. The single open question (what to do about the 2026-03-15..05-16 uuid4 wedge) was answered by the rebirth ceremony: all 5 mixed-era live stores reborn rule=ulid-migration, receipts verified, swapped in place. The wedge no longer exists in live stores; pre-swap backups preserve the historical fact.\", \"_ts\": 1781295561.066077, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"trace-ergonomics-iteration\": {\"name\": \"trace-ergonomics-iteration\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"OPEN 2026-05-16 \\u2014 next session's work, per Kyle (defer v0.3.2 release until this lands). Trace verb shipped today (sl trace <kind>/<key>, --refs, --diff, --depth, combine aggregator transparency) and is exercised in production via the arcs-block.py hook, but ergonomics have not yet had a deliberate iteration pass. What to look at next session: (a) does --diff render cleanly when fold-merge produces many small patches per entity, or does the per-entity partition produce visual noise? (b) does --depth=2 surface the right transitive subgraph or pull in too much? cycle-protection works but breadth control is untuned; (c) the empty-handling message ('no lifecycle found for kind/key') is technically correct but does it help the user recover (suggest kinds? show nearest matches)?; (d) hooks integration \\u2014 arcs-block.py uses sl trace --diff in production; observe how it actually reads after one full session (already named in watching/arcs-block-test-on-next-session-open); (e) is the verb composable enough? trace --refs --diff vs trace --refs --depth=2 \\u2014 should some combinations be guarded or warned?; (f) friction signals from real use this session \\u2014 anything that felt awkward when I was reading my own trace output. Approach: pre-orient by reading actual trace output for entities with rich lineage BEFORE deciding what to change. Per pattern/orientation-before-build-collapses-scope (growing edge): the implementation is often smaller than planned once you read the existing structure. Don't pre-plan ergonomics changes from memory of the design \\u2014 read the lens output cold and notice what feels off.\", \"_ts\": 1778996471.744354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\"]}, \"ref-vs-trace-separator-alignment\": {\"name\": \"ref-vs-trace-separator-alignment\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Merged into thread:typed-refs-redesign at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 Ref(kind, key) as typed dataclass makes the separator a serialization detail; the alignment question dissolves into the redesign.\", \"_ts\": 1781295863.670768, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:trace-help-and-discoverability\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\", \"thread:typed-refs-redesign\"]}, \"refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\": {\"name\": \"refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17. Subsumed by larger trace-dissolution arc. --refs (bool, depth=1) and --depth N (int) collapsed into single --refs [N] (bare = depth 1, N = explicit depth, omitted = no walk). The propagation question (which verbs --refs applies to) resolved naturally: trace dissolved into read, so --refs lives only on read now. The semantic collision (render-side filter vs fetch-side walker) dissolved into one unified semantic: walk + decorate. See thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution for the full arc.\", \"_ts\": 1779038962.519134, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\"]}, \"trace-as-read-instance-dissolution\": {\"name\": \"trace-as-read-instance-dissolution\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17. Full five-phase dissolution landed: A1 (parser + filter retirement, commit 38691aa) + A2 (walk + graph-decorated render, commit 932bcd7) + B (positional kind/key, commit b05e126) + C (--diff routing, commit aa8bd94) + D (trace verb deleted, commit 52f2d0e) + E (CHANGELOG, this thread emit). Trace command removed entirely; sl read absorbs all four capabilities (--refs [N], positional kind/key, --diff, kind-index). 1081 tests pass. 14 new regression tests across TestExtractRefsDepth, TestRunFoldRefsBothPaths, TestLooksLikeVertexPath, TestFetchFoldRefsWalk. Dissolution-test prediction held: trace dissolved cleanly; the only unique capability was --diff which now lives in read. arcs-block.py session-start hook updated to sl read --diff. Friction surface cleared: default-read-flow-too-limiting, trace-refs-no-visual-marker, refs-flag-unification-and-propagation all resolved by the dissolution.\", \"_ts\": 1779038962.51915, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"friction:trace-refs-no-visual-marker\", \"thread:refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\"]}, \"cli-refactor-architecture\": {\"name\": \"cli-refactor-architecture\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17 19:55 \\u2014 STEP 7 COMPLETE. Subtask worker shipped steps 1-6 (commits 1d28ee5..74cd478, squash-merged as 035af59). 1127 tests pass (worker added ~37 new cli/ tests), 41 goldens pass UNCHANGED \\u2014 migration preserved output through the architectural reshape (strong outcome). 0 pyright errors in cli/. Painted boundary enforced (only cli/output.py + cli/live.py import painted). Worker emitted 2 design decisions (re-emitted on canonical \\u2014 see friction/subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free). DELIVERED: registry routes verbs through cli/views/ for read,fold,emit,cite,store,population (real migration, ~700 LOC moved). DEFERRED to follow-up arc: stream/ticks/close/sync/test/compile/validate/init/whoami still as thin wrappers delegating to legacy _run_* in main.py. main.py landed at 1579 LOC (brief said <100). Worker documented the deferral honestly in each thin view's docstring. Step 7 review: NO goldens to classify \\u2014 architectural shape changed, behavior preserved. The deferred body migrations become their own arc \\u2014 see thread/cli-refactor-body-migrations.\", \"_ts\": 1779049332.834038, \"_n\": 6, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\", \"decision:design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\", \"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"decision:workflow/subtask-handoff-via-plan-appendix\", \"friction:subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free\"]}, \"cli-refactor-body-migrations\": {\"name\": \"cli-refactor-body-migrations\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17: Three-pass migration complete via subtask workers (sonnet/medium). Pass 1: deleted dead code, 1579\\u21921031 LOC (commits 3083c18). Pass 2: four parallel workers migrated _run_stream, _run_ticks, _run_whoami, _run_store/_run_ls* to commands/ with re-exports, 1031\\u2192533 LOC (commits e5b49c3, 397dd3b, 83358d9, 7af3774). Pass 3: single worker drained remaining helpers to cli/lens.py + cli/help.py + commands/resolve.py additions, 533\\u219263 LOC (commit 4ff364b). main.py is now a 63-line re-export surface + main() shim. 1118 tests passing. Next session: review pass.\", \"_ts\": 1779053756.194262, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\"]}, \"next-session-handoff\": {\"name\": \"next-session-handoff\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 stale handoff note. The 2026-05-17 follow-up session happened: merged state smoke-tested, v0.3.x work proceeded (trace-ergonomics thread carries the deferred release gate). Handoff consumed.\", \"_ts\": 1781295561.340593, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\", \"thread:cli-refactor-body-migrations\"]}, \"vertex-living-document-walkthrough\": {\"name\": \"vertex-living-document-walkthrough\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Next session: manual walkthrough + smoke-test of the vertex-living-document surface end-to-end with Kyle. Kyle ripping out the helpargs thing first so the shape is actually visible. What to exercise: loops add <v> kind --by/--collect/--latest/etc (each fold-op flag), loops add <v> observer --identity --grant, loops add <v> combine --as, loops add <v> row (explicit + bare-positional back-compat), the rm symmetric set including empty-parent auto-strip, loops ls <v> unified + each filter subcommand at each zoom level, change-fact emission on a vertex that declares 'change' kind, validator-rejection-preserves-original on a deliberately-broken edit. Watch for: (a) gaps the test-shape didn't catch, (b) help-text rendering once helpargs is out of the way, (c) verb collisions or surprises in real-use ergonomics. Closes when: walked the matrix, frictions emitted in-moment, surface either lands as-is or with a specific punch-list.\", \"_ts\": 1779062017.724913, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"lens-architecture-implementation\": {\"name\": \"lens-architecture-implementation\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Worktree wip/lens-architecture at /Users/kaygee/Code/loops-lens-architecture. Scope: implement the spec\\u2192atom\\u2192lens\\u2192introspection chain for declared-property lens architecture. PHASE 1 (mechanical, scoped): thread preview_fields through ls \\u2014 _summarize_kinds reads loop_def.preview_fields, _render_kind surfaces them at SUMMARY/DETAILED. Completes the prototype property's introspection symmetry. PHASE 2 (architectural, scoped against design/lenses-consume-declared-properties): consider declaring field-semantics on the atom layer (accumulate vs state) so trace.py's --diff refs-strip becomes a consumer of a declared property instead of a local hardcoded list. Dissolves the special-case for refs and creates a general mechanism for the next accumulate-semantics field. PHASE 3 (open question): the thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate friction. Does it dissolve under the new architecture (i.e., does 'namespace breakdown vs key list' become a declared kind property, or stay a lens default), or stay a separate fix? Hold open until phase 2 is shaped. WIP branch wip/auto-zoom holds the reverted auto-zoom commits \\u2014 only re-derive via declared-property route if a kind genuinely wants cardinality-aware fidelity declared in its spec.\", \"_ts\": 1779199084.514513, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\"]}, \"project-graph-visualizer\": {\"name\": \"project-graph-visualizer\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 real but no near-term pull. Reopen on live need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.07968, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"typed-refs-redesign\": {\"name\": \"typed-refs-redesign\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-substrate\", \"message\": \"Entry point for next session. Central question: should refs become a typed dataclass (Ref(kind, key)) at the substrate layer rather than a parsed-string convention? Evidence accumulated 2026-05-19 session: convention drift between write-side (slash) and read-side (colon) created May-16 by the trace verb commit and not propagated; the auto-resolver pattern-scans payload values producing the heuristic-eats-semantic-field bug class (cite ref-stealing, today's topic-as-ref, others); vestigial _ref siblings written by resolver, read by zero production code. Calibration warning attached: this was a single-arc conviction that felt structural at the time of emission. Confirming evidence bar before promoting to decision: at least one cross-arc encounter (next bug instance, next ref-touching commit) where the typed-ref framing either lands cleanly or surfaces friction. Adjacent questions parked: slash-overload-taxonomy thread, whether _parse_fact_refs should accept slash-form as back-compat, what wire form serialization settles on. Closes when: typed-refs is implemented OR rejected OR clearly deferred behind a more urgent forcing function.\", \"_ts\": 1779244336.07054, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\"]}, \"auth-architect-peer-conversation\": {\"name\": \"auth-architect-peer-conversation\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"peer-exchange\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295838.112507, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\"]}, \"vouch-oauth-integration-question\": {\"name\": \"vouch-oauth-integration-question\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.280908, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"vouch-deployment-substrate-constraint\": {\"name\": \"vouch-deployment-substrate-constraint\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 (vouch consolidation): the enterprise arc lives in the agent-attestation vertex + the 5-doc package under team review. Loops-side umbrella is thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch \\u2014 reopen from there when vouch usage surfaces what Peer/Grant need.\", \"_ts\": 1781295837.419005, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"decision:paradigm/audience-distinct-from-authorization\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\", \"thread:vouch-oauth-integration-question\"]}, \"loops-go-conformance-oracle\": {\"name\": \"loops-go-conformance-oracle\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"BOTH HALVES LANDED on r2-replay-conformance (4 commits, unpushed, ready for Kyle review): Opus delivered the Go-side delta clean \\u2014 f27d160 (R2 skip+rejected-counter in Sum/Min/Max/Avg/TopN/Latest, bool+numeric-string off-type, (ts,id) replay fix in ReadFacts with _ts column injection \\u2014 Go did NOT conform before, real catch), 75b3a23 (normative \\u00a74.7), 11d3ee1 (FINDINGS). 30 fold vectors + merge-commutativity differential green, vectors re-pinned to 581df73, Python reference generated all fixtures. My \\u00a78 attestation committed on top (3f4c5da) after verifying disjoint sections. One benign non-drift logged (_ts column-wins overwrite, matches incumbent). NEXT CRITICAL PATH: Python _canonical_bytes -> JCS + re-anchor ceremony in loops repo \\u2014 \\u00a78.7 vectors MUST NOT generate until after migration or they pin pre-JCS bytes.\", \"_ts\": 1781299637.285796, \"_n\": 6, \"feature\": \"loops-go\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\", \"decision:design/fold-replay-order-event-time\", \"thread:head-anchoring-as-external-witness\", \"thread:loops-core-transpile-target\"]}, \"python-bugs-from-go-oracle\": {\"name\": \"python-bugs-from-go-oracle\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"FIX ARC SHIPPED 2026-06-12, same day as re-verification. Landed: (1) merge commutativity via fold-replay-order-event-time \\u2014 (ts,id) replay + ordered merge INSERT, TestMergeFoldCommutativity pins merge(A,B)==merge(B,A); (2) _make_latest never consults the clock \\u2014 missing _ts rejects with counter, _ts now injected on live receive AND raw replay paths (the live path previously NEVER had _ts, so live Latest state always diverged from re-folds); (3) resolve_entity_id + latest_by_kind(_where) order by (ts DESC, id DESC) \\u2014 ref resolution no longer rowid-blind (H4 sites cleared); (4)+(5) bool and off-type values skip+count per fold-off-type-skip-with-counter \\u2014 sum(true)=1 and TypeError-mid-replay both dead, Avg denominator honest. Suites: atoms 418 / engine 793 / lang 366 / store 81 / loops 1305 green; two tests that PINNED the wall-clock fallback flipped to pin the rejection; 8 engine tests updated for _ts in fold entries (matches what vertex_reader always injected). Fresh rebirth+--check roundtrip deterministic under new code; live store reads + chain verify green. REMAINING (deliberate): finding 6 silent-false inequality conditions (vertex.py:57) \\u2014 diagnosability gap, not determinism; needs a visibility design (boundary-eval has no state to count into), tracked here as the residue. loops-go: R2 + replay-order rules are protocol decisions \\u2014 the conformance thread carries the handoff.\", \"_ts\": 1781282100.977238, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\", \"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"], \"feature\": \"oracle-bug-fixes\"}, \"vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\": {\"name\": \"vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-06-12. The 'awaiting Kyle's go' state was stale: delta 2 committed as 4cb473d (tick-signing substrate) + 96e1a4a (CLI composition), then superseded by the full arc through delta 3 (581df73, sign-on-emit) and the rebirth ceremony. Every live store now signed+chained.\", \"_ts\": 1781295543.779864, \"_n\": 7, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/observer-key-registry\", \"decision:design/peer-as-exchange-edge-relation\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\", \"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-in-chain-envelope\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"decision:design/vouch-substrate\", \"friction:session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\", \"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-session-owed\"], \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\"}, \"global-local-walk-broken\": {\"name\": \"global-local-walk-broken\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-06-09, same session as traced. Three behaviors unified to one: (1) add/rm/ls-vertex/store now resolve through _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch (the existing local-first resolver \\u2014 the fix was a dissolution, commands just didn't use the primitive verbs already had); (2) mutating receipts print the full path written, ~-contracted (add.py/rm.py, 8 sites); (3) root ls renders two labelled groups \\u2014 local (cwd, verbs resolve these first) then config \\u2014 with a truncation-surviving '\\u22b3 shadows config' marker; fetch_vertices_local was DEAD CODE (written, never wired, required a .loops/.vertex root that real repos lack) \\u2014 rewired to mirror _find_local_vertex's locations. Tests: 10 new in test_resolution_local_first.py pinning the incident; declaration tests + TestRootLs gained cwd isolation (loops_env / chdir) after the live-vertex contamination incident (see observation). 1280 pass; only pre-existing failures remain (golden test_validate FULL fails on clean main; ruff E741/F401 pre-exist). Smoked via installed sl in tmp workspace: add hits local, receipt shows path, ls counts both layers. DELTA-2 UNBLOCKED: sl add project observer now writes the verification anchor into the custody context where key + store live.\", \"_ts\": 1781040504.488399, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"friction:add-read-vertex-resolution-asymmetry\", \"observation:test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\"]}, \"rebirth-with-receipt\": {\"name\": \"rebirth-with-receipt\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"rebirth-with-receipt\", \"message\": \"SWAP CEREMONY COMPLETE 2026-06-12. All 5 mixed-era live stores reborn (rule=ulid-migration) and swapped: project (2053 facts, 1791 migrated, genesis SIGNED, 216 ticks re-entered), session (155/133), identity (290/252), comms/discord (1030/982), comms/native (2023/2023 \\u2014 pure two-era, zero canonical). All receipts verified: re-run diff clean, counts match, source content match, chain intact. Pre-swap backups at ~/loops-store-backups/2026-06-12/. Swap kept live filenames stable (reborn db moved INTO the original path) so zero .vertex edits were needed \\u2014 the 'point .vertex at reborn db' step dissolved. Post-swap verification: sl store verify project chain intact (1 chained+signed tick incl. rebirth genesis), reads green on all stores, zero id-order inversions above ULID millisecond resolution (sub-ms ties tie-break by rowid \\u2014 rowid-is-load-bearing holds, witness order remains append order per chain-witness-order). Third era confirmed in 4 of 5 stores (lowercase sqlite-ulid). Non-migrated single-era lowercase stores (siftd 10814, claude-code 8126, reading, economy, docs, orchestration, weather, discord-source) deliberately left \\u2014 order-broken but single-era-consistent, separate decision. Old incarnations archived per ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data. NEXT in chain arc: tick-list attestation marker, head-anchoring.\", \"_ts\": 1781276741.082102, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/rebirth-implementation-shape\", \"decision:design/seal-verb\", \"observation:design/event-order-vs-witness-order\", \"observation:ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\"]}, \"session/2026-06-09-fourth-fable-session\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-09-fourth-fable-session\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"message\": \"Closed at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 session arc, session long over. Its pulls all landed or are tracked: attestation-read-path shipped in-session (a9201fa), rebirth-with-receipt resolved 2026-06-12, head-anchoring parked with rationale.\", \"_ts\": 1781295544.060763, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-envelope-read-path\", \"observation:paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\", \"observation:pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\", \"thread:head-anchoring-as-external-witness\", \"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"config-population-cleanup\": {\"name\": \"config-population-cleanup\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-config\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-06-12, same session as opened. Executed: (1) keep-set drawn \\u2014 live core is exactly project, agent-attestation, comms/discord, comms/native, identity, session (+ external meta); Kyle archived all three ambiguous entries (siftd, orchestration, autoresearch). (2) 14 config dirs sealed+moved to ~/.config/loops/archive/ (9 stores sealed via identity-rebirth incl. siftd 10814 + claude-code 8126; feeds/reactions non-protocol kept as-is; 4 dbs found already lost; README.md indexes states). (3) Repo .loops: root.db, docs.db, autoresearch/, meta-discussion remnant \\u2192 .loops/archive/. (4) Stale /private/tmp/d2-smoke combine ref removed from config project aggregator. (5) Signing era extended to full live core per ops/signing-era-full-live-core \\u2014 all six stores verify signed. (6) Coherence: repo CLAUDE.md meta path corrected to ~/Code/meta-discussion; config CLAUDE.md vertex-count line updated. Safety: full pre-archive tarball at ~/loops-store-backups/retired-config-2026-06-12.tar.gz. Residue deliberately left: dev/check.vertex (declaration-only tooling, never ran), lenses/ bin/ (live tooling). sl ls now shows 6 local+config instances + 3 aggregations \\u2014 the system IS the live core.\", \"_ts\": 1781278194.866387, \"_n\": 2}, \"reroute-capture-practice\": {\"name\": \"reroute-capture-practice\", \"status\": \"adopted\", \"message\": \"Adopted same-day via decision practice/reroute-log-sweep-reconcile: reroute log (reflex) -> sweep at wrap (fast, promotes to friction) -> reconcile sessions (slow, structural). Stop hook turn-capture.py live in .claude/settings.local.json \\u2014 asks the capture question after substantive turns. Thread stays at adopted (not resolved) until the practice proves it fires: success metric is log entries appearing at a rate that matches observed rerouting (~several per working session, on today's evidence), and at least one log->friction promotion at a sweep. If logs stay empty while rerouting continues, the honor-system failure mode survived and siftd-revival is the next move.\", \"_ts\": 1781286855.176524, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\"]}, \"session/2026-06-12-ceremony-and-determinism\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-12-ceremony-and-determinism\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"message\": \"Session arc, the day after the chain epoch: opened on the rebirth thread's REMAINING line and closed having paid three debts. (1) SWAP CEREMONY: 5 mixed-era stores reborn+swapped, receipts verified, zero vertex edits needed (filename-stable swap dissolved the pointing step). (2) CONFIG CLEANUP (Kyle's call): 14 retired vertices sealed+archived \\u2014 archive as attested act; 4 stores found ALREADY LOST (orphan wal); signing era extended to full live core, every live store now verifies signed; keygen friction dissolved same-session into add observer --keygen. (3) ORACLE DEBT: all 6 findings re-verified, R2 ratified (skip+rejected-counter), fold replay order settled as (ts,id) vs witness rowid \\u2014 two orders two authorities \\u2014 merge commutativity pinned; one residue named (silent-false inequalities). META ARC from Kyle's coffee question: silent rerouting named as the continue-bite externality \\u2192 reroute-log/sweep/reconcile practice adopted + Stop-hook backstop + session-orient block (1.1KB, pointer-over-payload) wired into SessionStart. First sweep ran at this close: 5 log entries captured today, no repeat patterns yet (promotion threshold not met), threads current. Commits: 9eaf5ed keygen, cf23c9f docs, 14eb723 fold-determinism; all pushed. NEXT PULLS: delta 3 design session (Fact.signature + sign-on-emit \\u2014 preconditions never cleaner), head-anchoring-as-external-witness folded into it, first reconcile session (48 open threads, many stale-March \\u2014 exactly its job), check-reads-rule-from-receipt quick fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781287171.507728, \"_n\": 1}, \"fact-signing-delta-3\": {\"name\": \"fact-signing-delta-3\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED \\u2014 delta 3 shipped (581df73) and the signing era opened on the live store in the same breath: kyle/loops-claude key minted at .loops/keys/kyle/loops-claude/, registered in the vertex (quoted node, the splice fix's first production use), and THIS FACT is the first signed fact in the project store \\u2014 the resolution attests its own authorship. ~2000 prior facts stay honest NULL (pre-signature era, never retro-claimed). Remaining custody boundary, carried forward deliberately: live-edge facts strippable until the next seal; head-anchoring-as-external-witness is the next design conversation.\", \"_ts\": 1781291987.16756, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signature-at-store-column\", \"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"head-anchoring-as-external-witness\": {\"name\": \"head-anchoring-as-external-witness\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Deferred 2026-06-12 by Kyle after design-space sketch (git-witness / cross-store mutual / peer-witness; compose via destination-agnostic head-emit at seal). Deferral is cheap: delta 3 already chains fact signatures into window_hash (_fact_row_hash era-aware) and tick signatures into prev_hash \\u2014 only the single head hash is unwitnessed. Kyle's hash-ticks-from-fact-signatures instinct dissolved into shipped machinery (design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys envelope trick). Pick up when external-witness need goes live (vouch/peer exchange or first real custody concern).\", \"_ts\": 1781294808.491542, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"resolution-candidate-detector\": {\"name\": \"resolution-candidate-detector\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at birth, reconcile 2026-06-12 (Kyle's call): closure-asymmetry fix \\u2014 re-check refs pointing at machine-checkable substrates (commits, files, doc sections), open reconcile with 'these N look resolved-in-reality.' Good, but it is a loops-CLI layer concern, not the loops-architecture focus of the current arc. Dissolution note for pickup: mostly trace + ref-checking, no new primitives.\", \"_ts\": 1781298633.400027, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/closure-asymmetry\"]}, \"loops-on-disclosure-grammar\": {\"name\": \"loops-on-disclosure-grammar\", \"status\": \"open\", \"feature\": \"disclosure-grammar\", \"message\": \"DISCLOSURE-GRAMMAR PASS \\u2014 progress 2026-06-14. FIRST TIER-1 FIX LANDED: reanchor/verify refusals now render clean (cli/views/store.py catches operator-error types \\u2192 reporter.err + exit 1, was a raw traceback). The smoke-test's HIGH candidate-bug \\\"verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict\\\" RESOLVED as NOT an integrity divergence \\u2014 it was that rendering gap (see observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent). Integrity verbs verified SOUND: verify == reanchor on keyed stores, reanchor byte-idempotent + transactionally safe. This de-risks the rest of the pass \\u2014 verify's GREEN is honest about chain-integrity; only the SIGNATURE-disclosure grammar overstates. REMAINING TIER-1 (catalog a-f, no new machinery, HELD for Kyle's return since they are disclosure-semantics judgment calls): (a) checkmark must distinguish attested from no-break; (b) covered vs signed are orthogonal, stop stacking as a fraction; (c) the keyed-observer-no-signed-facts warning is backwards-from-tamper-logic; (d) -v/--json detail depth; (e) read --ticks is attestation-blind while store verify is rich; (f) leading-checkmark glyph collision. Painted-view layer still gated on painted 0.2.0 (currently 0.1.8). Also spawned thread:error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy \\u2014 the reanchor fix is a point patch; the convention is the deeper question.\", \"_ts\": 1781453980.510776, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\", \"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"observation:pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\", \"thread:error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy\", \"thread:lens-architecture-implementation\", \"thread:painted-overreach-review\"]}, \"session/2026-06-12-reconcile-and-jcs\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-12-reconcile-and-jcs\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"message\": \"Session arc, second of the day: opened on head-anchoring, which PARKED after Kyle's tick-hashing instinct dissolved into shipped delta-3 machinery (window_hash already commits content+signature). Pivoted to the first reconcile session: lens updated in-session before use (friction+hypothesis coverage, real-age tags), 87\\u219235 open items, all closures with provenance, vouch cluster consolidated to one umbrella. Step-back produced pattern/closure-asymmetry (capture engineered, closure manual \\u2014 store lags reality) + pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant \\u2014 the latter immediately closed by cross-repo discovery: Kyle's painted fidelity epoch IS the human read-path investment (pattern/cross-repo-blindness banked; loops-on-disclosure-grammar is the new top pull, gated on painted 0.2.0). Then the oracle unpack: SPEC \\u00a78 attestation authored (byte-exact tier, two-authorities, era rules) while an Opus shipped Go-side R2+replay in parallel (r2-replay-conformance, 4 commits, unpushed) \\u2014 including a real conformance catch (Go ReadFacts was on rowid, not (ts,id)). JCS fork ratified mid-flight; the say/do seam closed same-day: c1f50ed swaps _canonical_bytes to RFC 8785, SqliteStore.reanchor + sl store reanchor ship with the append-only carve-out principled (attestation columns are derived; re-deriving is replay), and the ceremony ran live \\u2014 five stores re-anchored, verified, self-attesting (ceremony-open fact re-signed under JCS moments after birth). \\u00a78.7 vectors unblocked. Sweep: zsh-equals promoted to friction (third occurrence), CLI-shape reroutes left under disclosure-grammar. NEXT: joint smoke-test, push on architecture, concepts-into-painted-view readiness.\", \"_ts\": 1781301960.775236, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/jcs-reanchor-ceremony\", \"observation:pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"session/2026-06-13-disclosure-grammar-smoke-test\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-13-disclosure-grammar-smoke-test\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"message\": \"Session arc 2026-06-13: opened on substrate reflection \\u2014 Kyle asked whether Fable-5 vs prior-Fable shows in the code (pre-pull Fable access was pulled by US-gov; this is the successor). Blind 4-window texture comparison returned SAMENESS \\u2014 one authorial fingerprint survives the swap; the qualitative difference Kyle valued lived in the working-with, not the artifacts; coined scaffold-continuity vs weights-continuity (banked to identity). Pivoted to the queued joint smoke-test: hybrid method (hands-on crux + breadth workflow, 34 verified gaps). Take-it-from-the-top narrative trace of fact-to-sign-to-tick-to-verify-to-disclosure located a SINGLE root: era boundary narrated at tick layer not fact/headline layer, so verify signed/checkmark overstates an unenforced property. Traced signing in code: opportunistic-on-emit + audit-only-verify, NO require gate, verify-on-receive absent (implementation/signing-enforcement-status). Kyle ratified DEFER enforcement (design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred). Next session = UX / show-substrate-honestly. CALIBRATION: two overstatements this session (session-open reconcile-pending/48-stale read a stale receipt as current state; crux-2 non-uniform-warning premise false) \\u2014 BOTH caught by adversarial method, NEITHER self-caught in the moment. Seal fires on close via SessionEnd hook.\", \"_ts\": 1781385217.51479, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\"]}, \"error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy\": {\"name\": \"error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Kyle (2026-06-14): take a deeper look at our exception hierarchy and how we do error handling around it. Triggered by the reanchor bug \\u2014 operator-facing refusals (resolve_store_path \\\"No store configured\\\", reanchor \\\"requires a .vertex target\\\", engine \\\"no signing key \\u2014 refusing partial re-anchor\\\", absent .db) are raised as plain ValueError/FileNotFoundError and, with no catch between the _run_* functions and main(), escape as raw tracebacks despite carrying excellent actionable messages. The reanchor fix is LOCALIZED: a catch of (ValueError, FileNotFoundError) at the store view boundary (cli/views/store.py) renders them clean. That is a point patch, not a convention. The systemic questions: (1) should loops have a small exception taxonomy \\u2014 e.g. an OperatorError/UserError base meaning \\\"expected refusal, render clean + exit nonzero\\\" vs everything else \\\"genuine bug, let it traceback\\\" \\u2014 rather than catching concrete builtin types per view? (2) where does the catch belong \\u2014 per-view boundary, the dispatch tiers in cli/app.py, or a single top-level wrapper in main()? (3) the legacy _run_* shims raise and print via painted.show directly while the IR views use ctx.reporter \\u2014 error rendering is split across both surfaces; unify on the reporter? Hold the earned-granularity line: don't build a hierarchy ahead of need \\u2014 first audit how many distinct \\\"expected refusal\\\" sites exist across the CLI and whether they cluster.\", \"_ts\": 1781453980.057407, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"lib-consolidation-reconsider\": {\"name\": \"lib-consolidation-reconsider\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Kyle (2026-06-14): starting to think it may be time to pull all the libraries (atoms, engine, lang, sign, store) into one cohesive package instead of keeping them separate \\u2014 the separation may have outlived its usefulness. FOR LATER. The question: what did the lib boundaries buy, and is it still worth the cost? BOUGHT: an enforced dependency DAG (CLAUDE.md: \\\"engine depends on atoms TYPE_CHECKING-only; no other cross-lib imports\\\"), independent test surfaces, and the OPTION to extract a lib to its own repo. COST: navigation overhead, six pyproject.toml files, and \\u2014 concretely \\u2014 the flat vendored build forces the root pyproject to hand-mirror the union of every lib's third-party deps (see friction:root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap, which broke sl today). COUNTER-EVIDENCE that the boundary is still live, not vestigial: painted and sqlmerge were both recently EXTRACTED to standalone repos \\u2014 extraction is an active pattern, so the seams have paid off at least twice. The decision turns on whether the remaining internal libs (atoms/engine/lang/sign/store) are realistic extraction candidates or permanently-internal \\u2014 if permanently internal, the boundary is pure tax. Decompose via thread:lib-separation-tax-audit before deciding.\", \"_ts\": 1781453980.213253, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap\"]}, \"lib-separation-tax-audit\": {\"name\": \"lib-separation-tax-audit\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"FOR LATER \\u2014 the evidence-gathering facet of thread:lib-consolidation-reconsider. Before deciding whether to collapse atoms/engine/lang/sign/store into one package, audit what the boundaries actually enforce vs what they cost. ENFORCE: map the real cross-lib import graph and check it against the stated invariant (engine to atoms TYPE_CHECKING-only, no other cross-lib imports) \\u2014 is the DAG honored today, and would a merge let cycles/leaks in that the package split currently prevents? COST: the flat vendored build means root pyproject must mirror every lib's third-party deps by hand (the rfc8785 gap broke sl today); six pyproject + dev-group duplications; per-lib ./dev check overhead. EXTRACTION OPTION: which of the five are realistic extraction candidates (the way painted and sqlmerge already became) vs permanently-internal \\u2014 that is the load-bearing distinction for the consolidation call. OUTPUT: a go/no-go on consolidation with the boundary's actual load-bearing-ness measured, not assumed.\", \"_ts\": 1781453980.361713, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap\", \"thread:lib-consolidation-reconsider\"]}, \"seal-era-boundary-guard\": {\"name\": \"seal-era-boundary-guard\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-substrate\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-06-14. Floor implemented, twice-reviewed, pushed, and shipped in 0.4.0 (commits 303d8cb..f0538d2 on origin; UnsignedTickInSignedEra documented as a breaking change in CHANGELOG + GitHub release notes). The LOW follow-ups (orphaned seal-fact on refused emit-seal, terse boundary-universal message, combine/nested/SessionEnd-hook test gaps) remain as documented accepted-debt, not blockers.\", \"_ts\": 1781476549.840608, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"observation:implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\", \"observation:practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"transport-era-signing-key-flow\": {\"name\": \"transport-era-signing-key-flow\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-substrate\", \"message\": \"Forward problem flagged by Kyle 2026-06-14 while ratifying the tick-signing floor (decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor): the SSH \\\"key is always local\\\" assumption that makes signing low-friction breaks in the transport era. Refinement that surfaced: what gets \\\"passed around\\\" is PUBLIC keys (verification), never PRIVATE keys (signing) \\u2014 SSH all the way down, the private half never leaves the machine. Public-key distribution is largely already designed in the vouch / agent-attestation substrate (JWKS topology, IssuerRegistry dispatch by iss, issuer->namespace mapping) and in the .vertex observers{} registry. The genuinely-NEW problem is CHAIN RECONCILIATION ON MERGE: when store B ingests signed facts from store A (sqlmerge), B's tick chain must absorb A's signed facts WITHOUT (a) re-signing them \\u2014 that erases A's authorship \\u2014 or (b) minting an unsigned merge-boundary tick \\u2014 the Gate-B floor forbids that. So: who mints and signs the boundary tick over a merged window, with what authority, and how does B's era-monotonicity hold across a merge of two independently-signed chains? This is where the tick-signing floor gets its teeth in the multi-store world. Connects to sqlmerge (libs/store transport), Peer/Grant, and the deferred verify-on-receive consumer that reactivates fact-signing enforcement.\", \"_ts\": 1781457867.119662, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:seal-era-boundary-guard\"]}, \"rebirth-keyless-attestation-drop\": {\"name\": \"rebirth-keyless-attestation-drop\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-substrate\", \"message\": \"OPEN posture question surfaced by review #2 (and named in rebirth.py's floor-exemption comment). \\\"loops store rebirth\\\" with no tick_signer mints an UNSIGNED genesis tick \\u2014 silently dropping a signed source lineage's attestation. This is NOT a floor bypass: rebirth starts a fresh chain (pre-era, verify ok=True), and the CLI does print \\\"genesis tick unsigned\\\". But it is asymmetric with reanchor, which REFUSES without a key (\\\"a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\"). QUESTION: should keyless rebirth of a SIGNED source likewise refuse (or require an explicit --allow-unsigned), or is silently starting a fresh unsigned lineage the correct posture for a migration/rebirth? Turns on whether rebirth means \\\"continue this lineage\\\" (-> refuse, like reanchor) or \\\"fork a new custody context\\\" (-> unsigned start is fine). Connects to the tick-signing floor (fresh-lineage exemption) and the reanchor refusal precedent.\", \"_ts\": 1781463026.903814, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\"]}, \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\": {\"name\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"STATE 2026-06-15 post step6+step7 (cd0b1c6, 477f049). STEP6 DONE: cli/live.py (run_live/InPlaceRenderer wrapper) DELETED; fold --live folds onto painted run_cli(fetch_stream=, live_delivery='surface'). loops test --live already on run_cli, so fold was the last InPlaceRenderer consumer. Wiring locked by test (surface tier needs real TTY for behavioral verify). STEP7 DONE: golden coverage for the audit's biggest blind spot \\u2014 trace_view (lifecycle + --diff, 8 cases), declarations_view (4, incl preview_fields decl), fold preview-fields (4). 1342 green. DEFERRED from step7: walked-items goldens (WalkedItem tuples \\u2014 part of fold lens, bundle with fold-scoping). REMAINING: step8 replay visualizer (NEXT session, Kyle's call). PLUS open residues: (1) fold _render_item_line badge \\u2014 the record_line-dissolution residue, needs scoping (does ANY painted primitive host a keyed-fold-item-with-structural-badge?); (2) trace-view dead non-diff branch + 'diff' header (thread:trace-view-diff-header-and-dead-branch). Release readiness: attestation 0.4.0 still pending tag; render rebuild steps 1-7 done, step8 + fold-badge are the remaining rebuild work before the render path is fully on painted.\", \"_ts\": 1781574851.36999, \"_n\": 8, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"decision:design/cli-context-phase-split\", \"decision:design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\", \"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\", \"decision:design/next-release-0.4.0\", \"decision:design/record-line-dissolution-splits\", \"decision:design/store-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"decision:design/stream-trace-record-line-shipped\", \"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\", \"thread:trace-view-diff-header-and-dead-branch\"], \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"}, \"session/2026-06-14-attestation-floor-and-rebuild-audit\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-14-attestation-floor-and-rebuild-audit\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"message\": \"Session arc 2026-06-14 (long, context-heavy \\u2014 wrapped to preserve window). Opened on the disclosure-grammar HIGH bug (verify-vs-reanchor \\\"opposite verdict\\\") \\u2192 DISSOLVED: not an integrity divergence (reanchor byte-idempotent + transactionally safe; the \\\"opposite verdict\\\" was a raw-traceback rendering of the no-key refusal). Swept the catalog's candidate behavioral bugs: FC-04 read-path = attestation-NEUTRAL (dissolved), F8 ticks-UTF-8 = downgraded (clean error, not a crash), and the ONE real finding \\u2014 seal silently minted unsigned ticks in the signed era. That opened the tick-signing-floor design: Kyle ratified the floor (Gate-B non-negotiable, not a vertex flag; SSH-model hard-stop not silent-downgrade; transport moves PUBLIC keys, chain-reconciliation-on-merge is the new problem). Implemented in three passes, each driven by adversarial review: seal verb \\u2192 (review #1 HIGH: \\\"sl emit <v> seal\\\" bypass) engine mint \\u2192 (review #2 MEDIUM: tasks-harness is a 2nd live mint, fail-OPEN default) fail-SAFE default + named exemptions. Two 15-agent reviews each caught a real hole solo-confidence missed (\\u2192 practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses). SHIPPED (committed, UNPUSHED): 303d8cb reanchor-clean-error, 1763429 rfc8785-dep (fixed a real broken-fresh-install packaging gap), 9f2de91 / 6c368e4 / f0538d2 the seal-floor arc; 11 new tests, suites green. Pivoted to painted 0.2.0 (now LIVE on PyPI): release-delta audit (9-agent workflow) \\u2192 next release = 0.4.0; full plan in docs/dev/rebuild-audit-0.4.0.md. Threads opened: error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy, lib-consolidation-reconsider, lib-separation-tax-audit, transport-era-signing-key-flow, rebirth-keyless-attestation-drop, cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020 (NEXT-SESSION entry). RELEASE GATES carried: bump version (still 0.3.1), push 7 commits, docs 100% stale vs the attestation surface, real broken tests (test_dashboard \\u00d77 + test_readiness_lens collection \\u2014 the audit wrongly called these illustrative; they are real). Minor reroutes: PIPESTATUS-vs-$?-after-pipe, workflow backtick-in-template-literal parse error.\", \"_ts\": 1781468830.959061, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/next-release-0.4.0\", \"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"replay-visualizer-on-painted\": {\"name\": \"replay-visualizer-on-painted\", \"status\": \"open\", \"feature\": \"replay-visualizer\", \"message\": \"NET-NEW arc (not in the audit) \\u2014 Kyle's strong pull: the wireworld demo in painted is the right substrate for a loops replay/viewing visualizer. KEY FINDING: painted's animation model and loops' temporal model are the SAME shape (structural isomorphism), so a viewer is mostly wiring not new machinery. Mapping: painted Circuit-frozen-state == FoldState-at-tick-N; painted step(state)->state pure == replay fold facts[0..cursor_N]->state (pure SINCE R2 fold-determinism); painted _fetch_stream yields frames == yield FoldState per tick as cursor advances; per-cell-diff/tear-free (StreamSurface) == free. The R2 determinism work (forced by the attestation arc) is EXACTLY what makes scrubbable deterministic frames possible \\u2014 builder-inhabitant: the viewer animates the replay mechanism that persists identity facts. ALREADY-FREE from painted (confirmed in source): StreamSurface (cli/stream_surface.py:41), sparklines (_sparkline_core.py) for fact-count/density timeline, hit-testing (core/buffer.py put_id/hit), layer stack (tui/layer.py Push/Pop) for drill-down, palette ramps, zoom disclosure, flame_lens for first-cut ref aggregation. MUST GROW in painted: (1) playback controls pause/seek/step/speed -> propose TimelineSurface mixin; (2) diff-over-time highlighting (surface what changed tick N-1->N as meaning, opposite of painted's minimize-redraw diff); (3) DAG/ref-graph node-link layout (flame_lens is proportional segments not a DAG) -> graph_lens; (4) viewport/LOD (undemoed painted Viewport module \\u2014 inspect first). STAGING: v0 non-interactive 'sl replay <vertex>' (fetch_stream yields per-tick FoldState + live_delivery=surface + sparkline timeline) falls out of the cli-rebuild's pure lenses almost free; v1 playback; v2 diff-highlight; v3 ref-graph. v0 only needs cli-rebuild steps 1+5. Full design: docs/dev/rebuild-design-0.4.0.md \\u00a73.\", \"_ts\": 1781474976.22413, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"docs-drift-0.4.0-followup\": {\"name\": \"docs-drift-0.4.0-followup\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"docs\", \"message\": \"0.4.0 shipped with stale docs (accepted debt, flagged in audit release-readiness). To close: (1) update docs/CLI-CHEATSHEET.md for the read-path overhaul (--diff/--refs/--key, removed trace verb, positional kind/key addressing); (2) add a short attestation/signing user doc (seal/verify/rebirth/reanchor, signed .vertex observers{key}, keys/ layout, JCS canon, the keyless-in-signed-era refusal + migration). Surfaced: rebuild-audit-0.4.0.md \\u00a73.5. Do before or alongside the 0.5.0 cli/render rebuild since the rebuild changes the CLI surface again.\", \"_ts\": 1781475943.627806, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\"]}, \"session/2026-06-14-release-040-and-rebuild-design\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-14-release-040-and-rebuild-design\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"message\": \"Session arc 2026-06-14 (rollover from the attestation-floor session). Opened on 'what rolled over' -> the cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020 next-session entry. Ran THE GATE: bumped painted>=0.2.0,<0.3, uv sync, full suite -> loops 1327 green, ZERO golden drift; the only 0.2.0 break (CliContext zoom->fidelity) bit apps/tasks tests, which revealed the keystone concretely (two CliContext classes are orthogonal phases, not duplicates). Designed the full rebuild (docs/dev/rebuild-design-0.4.0.md): keystone = PHASE SPLIT (loops CliContext->Invocation; render takes painted's ctx) not a frozen-dataclass extension; full-integration target (view = Tag+fetch+render); grow-painted candidates; AND a net-new replay visualizer arc grounded in a structural isomorphism between painted's wireworld frame-model and loops' tick replay (pure SINCE R2). Decisions emitted: design/cli-context-phase-split, design/full-painted-integration-residue, design/cli-context-keystone-shape, test/gate-results-painted-020. Then CUT 0.4.0: cleared two real test gates, bumped version, CHANGELOG, committed (4ba2e47), tagged v0.4.0, pushed GitLab+GitHub, and PUBLISHED to PyPI via GitHub trusted-publishing (learned: gh release create triggers it, NOT bare tag push; local uv publish is wrong path \\u2014 token is painted-scoped). strange-loops 0.4.0 live on PyPI. Wrote docs/dev/painted-0.3.0-commission.md for the parallel painted track. Threads: resolved seal-era-boundary-guard; opened replay-visualizer-on-painted (fast-follow), docs-drift-0.4.0-followup (accepted debt); advanced cli-render thread to IMPLEMENTATION-NEXT. Next session resets clean for the keystone implementation while painted gets worked. Calibration: a Kyle question ('don't we have a github release already?') corrected my wrong publish path mid-flow \\u2014 the say/do gap was mine assuming local publish; the CI pipeline was the truth.\", \"_ts\": 1781476565.920227, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"session/2026-06-14-rebuild-steps-1-3\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-14-rebuild-steps-1-3\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"message\": \"Session arc 2026-06-14 (rollover from release-040-and-rebuild-design). Started 'right up with implementation' on the cli/render rebuild. Shipped steps 1-3, each committed green + emitted, all UNPUSHED (3 commits 8040bd4/ddcc5a3/bc22491) for next-session smoke-test+review while painted gets worked in parallel. Step1 keystone: loops CliContext->Invocation (context.py->invocation.py) making the domain/render phase split explicit. Step2: 3-tier dispatcher + argparse help epilog dissolved onto painted run_app; painted owns routing+top-level help; loops residue = observer peel + vertex-shorthand pre-router; help adopted painted's shape (Kyle's call), 4 help-shape tests updated. Step3 pilot: read drops fidelity_from_args -> painted add_cli_args/parse_zoom/parse_fidelity for terminal axes. 1327 green throughout, zero non-help golden drift; sl binary smoke-tested every step. COHERENCE CATCH (the session's real find): --facts/--diff/--refs are domain-query selectors not painted disclosure tags (they change WHAT is fetched) -> decision:design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis; reframes the design doc's step-3 premise. Standing principle reaffirmed by Kyle and emitted as practice/grow-painted-over-workaround: anything painted can do, prefer painted; push loops into domain-only arenas; grow painted before working around. Landscape: read was the sole fidelity_from_args consumer; other display surfaces already on run_cli (their work is step4). Next session: manual walkthrough smoke-test + review of steps 1-3, then step4 (shim unification). Calibration: caught my own blanket-sed hitting an intentional docstring mention (self-catch, in-flow); reroutes logged at reflex speed.\", \"_ts\": 1781538749.535565, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"painted-run-cli-args-seam\": {\"name\": \"painted-run-cli-args-seam\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED by painted 0.3.0 (committed 8518b3c loops-side). Painted answered the seam NOT with my proposed CliContext.args / fetch(ctx), but with a different blessed idiom: HelpArg + run_cli(help_args=[...]) \\u2014 'for commands that pre-parse their own args before calling run_cli, describe them so they appear in --help'. So the command keeps its inherent pre-parse (needed for values + branching anyway), fetch closes over the parsed namespace directly, and help_args makes painted's --help list them. Cleaner than exposing the namespace through CliContext \\u2014 the parse stays the command's, painted only renders the description. devtools build_fidelity capture bridge collapsed onto this. Same idiom is the store conversion path. Lesson: proposed a seam shape, painted shipped a better-fitting one; the gap was real, the fix wasn't my shape.\", \"_ts\": 1781550202.810267, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"decision:design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\"]}, \"session/2026-06-15-step4-5-help-and-truncation\": {\"name\": \"session/2026-06-15-step4-5-help-and-truncation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"Session arc 2026-06-15 (rollover from rebuild-steps-1-3). Ran the painted-feedback loop + steps 4-5-truncation. OPENED: slow-human smoke (painted 0.2.0, all zooms green) + A2 decision (budget_fields stable-now, ref the dissolution-test-vs-resolve_column_widths gate). STEP 4 (help-dissolve): devtools test/compile/validate -> deleted hand-rolled -h; first via a build_fidelity bridge (780659d), then painted 0.3.0 shipped the HelpArg/help_args idiom (NOT my proposed CliContext.args) and the bridge collapsed onto it (8518b3c). painted 0.3.0 GATE crossed (36891f1, 1327+258 green). store all-4-surfaces (443bdd6): the verify/rebirth/reanchor 'wrinkle' was mostly redundant code (argparse add_help already owned -h); only base inspect needed help_args. STEP 5 (delete hand truncation): fold preview allocator -> painted.budget_fields (621fdf2, ZERO drift); adopted the better truncation-gate contract fresh. Then 5 copy-pasted string-clip sites -> one _helpers.elide (a11b44c). TWO calibration notes: (1) drift-prediction-conservative-miss \\u2014 predicted golden drift that didn't occur (corpus doesn't hit the divergence branch); (2) the small-cleanup did NOT dissolve into painted as pitched (painted only has block-level truncate; string clips dedupe loops-side until record_line). Three painted asks all resolved well (A2 budget_fields, the run-cli-args seam answered as HelpArg, the truncation-gate contract). 6 commits, all pushed both remotes. NEXT: step5 LARGE half \\u2014 re-ground lenses on record_line/PayloadLens (fresh session, my call: architectural + likely painted-side design).\", \"_ts\": 1781553506.298393, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"decision:design/store-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"observation:practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\"]}, \"trace-view-diff-header-and-dead-branch\": {\"name\": \"trace-view-diff-header-and-dead-branch\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"COHERENCE FINDING (2026-06-15, surfaced during step7 golden coverage). trace_view header is unconditionally 'diff <kind>/<key>' (trace.py:48), and the non-diff branch (line 81 else -> stream_view delegation) is effectively DEAD in production: fetch_trace's ONLY caller (fold.py:284) always sets data['_diff']=True immediately after fetch. So _trace \\u27f9 _diff in production; trace_view is only ever reached in diff mode. Two clean-ups available: (a) DISSOLVE \\u2014 remove the dead non-diff branch + the zoom!=diff delegation, since it's unreachable (dissolution-test: the branch is a property of a state that's never constructed); OR (b) make non-diff trace a REAL mode (sl read kind/key WITHOUT --diff renders lifecycle records, only --diff renders deltas) \\u2014 gives the 'diff' header an honest non-diff sibling 'trace'/'lifecycle'. Pick (b) if entity-lifecycle-without-diff is a wanted view; pick (a) if --diff is the only entity view. Golden test_trace_lifecycle currently locks the synthetic non-diff output (header still says 'diff') as a regression net. NOT blocking; belongs with fold-scoping or a read-path cleanup pass.\", \"_ts\": 1781574839.632287, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/stream-trace-record-line-shipped\"]}}}, \"change\": {\"items\": [{\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"kind\", \"name\": \"buf\", \"fold_op\": \"window\", \"fold_arg\": \"value\", \"fold_size\": \"50\", \"fold_target\": \"items\", \"_ts\": 1781039909.806535}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"kind\", \"name\": \"temp\", \"fold_op\": \"latest\", \"fold_target\": \"current\", \"_ts\": 1781039909.810827}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039909.81628}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"alcove\", \"identity\": \"alcove-id\", \"_ts\": 1781039909.820303}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"mon\", \"grants\": \"decision,thread\", \"_ts\": 1781039909.824287}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"peer\", \"identity\": \"peer-id\", \"grants\": \"decision,thread,observation\", \"_ts\": 1781039909.829349}, {\"op\": \"rm\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.209023}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.214178}, {\"op\": \"rm\", \"target\": \"kind\", \"name\": \"task\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.219326}, {\"op\": \"rm\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.223326}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.227507}, {\"op\": \"rm\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"alcove\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.228916}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"alcove\", \"identity\": \"alcove-id\", \"grants\": \"thread\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.238531}, {\"op\": \"rm\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.239667}, {\"op\": \"rm\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"peer\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.250372}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"_ts\": 1781039910.252384}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"project\", \"key\": \"OejdVUWUCVp9D6RlqjQFvwuCIww5QpGLLRpTxZuKin4=\", \"_ts\": 1781042630.260985}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle/loops-claude\", \"key\": \"rWZwj2nx2zOQ7CO6YNnHTHxSuBD9nTMZSS4D3AfWD/w=\", \"_ts\": 1781291976.1101}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kyle\", \"key\": \"NgR8JjntAfu7w2bnkpVFnDPmqwf7rcpJyQ6mhtLaoIU=\", \"_ts\": 1781292323.572217}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"target\": \"observer\", \"name\": \"kaygee\", \"key\": \"6Ak/gMy/mH4mVlOWDJjwJU5vzJXjXluLQyx6Dum6mXA=\", \"_ts\": 1781460728.487582}]}, \"task\": {\"items\": {\"cli-emit-runtime\": {\"name\": \"cli-emit-runtime\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"CLI emit routes through vertex runtime via load_vertex_program + vertex.receive. Dissolution \\u2014 removed the bypass, didn't build new machinery.\", \"_ts\": 1772682174.781642, \"_n\": 2}, \"daemon-local-orchestration\": {\"name\": \"daemon-local-orchestration\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\u2014 no persistent runtime needed. Vertex is reactive. Scheduling is external (cron/systemd). One-shot CLI is the runtime.\", \"_ts\": 1772841349.485697, \"_n\": 4, \"stage\": \"research\", \"priority\": \"later\"}, \"foldstate-audit-findings\": {\"name\": \"foldstate-audit-findings\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved: vertex_fold addresses the core finding (typed contract wired end-to-end). FoldItem.origin populated since prior session. Remaining gaps (no reference counting, no fold caching, no custom lens loading) are tracked as separate threads.\", \"_ts\": 1772724517.231956, \"_n\": 2}, \"identity-observer-filtering\": {\"name\": \"identity-observer-filtering\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Observer-scoped reads wired end-to-end. --observer general flag at dispatch, default-to-self, resolved-status filtering in prompt lens. Help bug fixed \\u2014 subcommand -h no longer masked by top-level intercept.\", \"_ts\": 1772693183.314117, \"_n\": 2}, \"combine-auto-inherit\": {\"name\": \"combine-auto-inherit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"thread\": \"combine-auto-inherit\", \"message\": \"Shipped in 0e1ddc9. Union semantics, conflict detection, aggregation loops{} is overrides only.\", \"_ts\": 1772729846.539816, \"_n\": 2}, \"session-close\": {\"name\": \"session-close\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Dissolved: session is a kind, close is the handoff, pickup reads one fold.\", \"_ts\": 1772734720.074993, \"_n\": 2}, \"thread-auto-tagging\": {\"name\": \"thread-auto-tagging\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD env var. 5 lines in cmd_emit, same pattern as LOOPS_OBSERVER.\", \"_ts\": 1772736425.59705, \"_n\": 2}, \"pickup-filtering\": {\"name\": \"pickup-filtering\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Dissolved: root .vertex fold with prompt lens handles identity + session + tasks in one read.\", \"_ts\": 1772734720.160706, \"_n\": 2}, \"custom-lens-infrastructure\": {\"name\": \"custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into vertex-lens-infrastructure. LensDecl AST, lens resolver with 4-tier resolution and file search, call_lens with optional context kwargs (vertex_name). identity.vertex declares prompt lens.\", \"_ts\": 1772740519.10821, \"_n\": 3}, \"fact-drill-down\": {\"name\": \"fact-drill-down\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"priority\": \"after\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into kind/key syntax on --kind flag. --kind thread/fold-state-types filters fold to single item, stream to matching facts. No new verbs \\u2014 / is the drill-down operator.\", \"_ts\": 1773068569.080636, \"_n\": 5, \"reason\": \"superseded\", \"superseded_by\": \"thread/cli-dissolution\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01kk9hyjfpvbsqnahp7wmn5289\"}, \"fold-materialization\": {\"name\": \"fold-materialization\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Plan concluded not yet needed. 19ms fold on 497 facts \\u2014 bottleneck is Python import (60ms) and spec compilation (25ms), not replay. Design banked in .subtask/tasks/fold-materialization-plan/PLAN.md for when vertices exceed 5K facts.\", \"_ts\": 1773013466.025593, \"_n\": 4, \"priority\": \"later\"}, \"vertex-lens-infrastructure\": {\"name\": \"vertex-lens-infrastructure\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Implemented: LensDecl in AST, lens{} block in KDL, lens_resolver.py with file search (vertex-local > project-local > user-global > built-in), 4-tier CLI resolution, call_lens with vertex_name context. 22 new tests.\", \"_ts\": 1772740524.849792, \"_n\": 3}, \"fact-by-id\": {\"name\": \"fact-by-id\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"ULID IDs surfaced through entire read path. StoreReader.fact_by_id with prefix matching, vertex_fact_by_id across combined stores, --id flag on stream command. Progressive disclosure in stream lens. Primitive reference for future tick traversal.\", \"_ts\": 1772751663.712647, \"_n\": 3}, \"meta-hooks-bootstrap\": {\"name\": \"meta-hooks-bootstrap\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into hooks. Identity consolidated, pickup removed, comms delta wired. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\", \"_ts\": 1772767087.801831, \"_n\": 2}, \"text-truncation-plain-vv\": {\"name\": \"text-truncation-plain-vv\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Fixed in 6bb78ba: piped/plain output, validate errors, FULL zoom field values.\", \"_ts\": 1773013719.507703, \"_n\": 3}, \"session-tick-retrospective\": {\"name\": \"session-tick-retrospective\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Completed. Fixed since bug, verified tick structure, dissolved handoff into tick, added mechanical delta to SessionEnd hook.\", \"_ts\": 1772826069.757109, \"_n\": 3}, \"docs-vertex-migration\": {\"name\": \"docs-vertex-migration\", \"priority\": \"next\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Root .vertex aggregation landed (commit 7892848). Local docs vertex created. Workspace topology established. The remaining docs vertex work (if any) is incremental content, not structural.\", \"_ts\": 1773958768.639499, \"_n\": 3}, \"discord-source-poll-kind\": {\"name\": \"discord-source-poll-kind\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Dissolved into design/internal-fact-namespace. message.complete no longer emitted \\u2014 _sync.message replaces it.\", \"_ts\": 1773028476.864272, \"_n\": 2}, \"tick-surfacing\": {\"name\": \"tick-surfacing\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\u2014 ticks are visible through read-vertex; no separate surfacing command needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772841225.404927, \"_n\": 2}, \"tick-to-fact-flow\": {\"name\": \"tick-to-fact-flow\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolved by vertex-as-interface redesign \\u2014 tick-to-fact cascading is already in the engine; read-vertex exposes it without dedicated plumbing.\", \"_ts\": 1772841227.494279, \"_n\": 2}, \"dissolve-messaging-vertex\": {\"name\": \"dissolve-messaging-vertex\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Removed in 01a46eb.\", \"_ts\": 1773011056.257583, \"_n\": 2}, \"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\": {\"name\": \"remove-duplicate-discord-vertex\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Removed in 01a46eb.\", \"_ts\": 1773011055.99348, \"_n\": 2}, \"refactor-meta-combine\": {\"name\": \"refactor-meta-combine\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"meta.vertex combines only meta-discussion. Dropped discord + identity (siblings under root), scope observer (meta is shared), unused kinds (vision, change). Net -12 lines config, clean fold.\", \"_ts\": 1773086677.236741, \"_n\": 2}, \"domain-vertex-template\": {\"name\": \"domain-vertex-template\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Dissolved. Hardcoded _AGGREGATION_VERTEX killed. Init creates minimal stub when no source exists, or copies from existing vertex. Domain shape is a convention in .vertex files, not a template in code. The info-domain base shape (decision/thread/task/session) is what you write, not what init generates.\", \"_ts\": 1773086680.239046, \"_n\": 2}, \"session-launch-script\": {\"name\": \"session-launch-script\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Launch script exists at config/bin/launch. Emits session with principal/agent provenance, resolves identity fold, exec's claude with LOOPS_OBSERVER.\", \"_ts\": 1773078946.629822, \"_n\": 2}, \"identity/observer-namespacing\": {\"name\": \"identity/observer-namespacing\", \"message\": \"Merged. observer_matches() symmetric matching, 4 call sites updated, 16+4 tests. Commit c0a1d87.\", \"_ts\": 1773162538.327969, \"_n\": 3, \"status\": \"completed\", \"superseded_by\": \"thread/orchestration-vertex-design\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01kkc6pvsgrcqbkjsejsyqvc13\"}, \"observer-discoverability\": {\"name\": \"observer-discoverability\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Thread resolved. whoami + LOOPS_OBSERVER + launch script compose.\", \"_ts\": 1773011677.046029, \"_n\": 2}, \"rekind-observation-facts\": {\"name\": \"rekind-observation-facts\", \"message\": \"Approach settled: forward-only, not retroactive. New kinds (insight/notice/reflection) added to .vertex declarations, keep observation for backward compat. No urgency \\u2014 emit with correct kind going forward as identity facts are naturally re-emitted. Revisit when identity store undergoes next round of curation.\", \"_ts\": 1773069919.328123, \"_n\": 4, \"status\": \"parked\", \"priority\": \"next\"}, \"root-topology-store\": {\"name\": \"root-topology-store\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Merged. Config + engine + consumer + 13 tests.\", \"_ts\": 1773160182.659063, \"_n\": 1}, \"ticks-window-filter\": {\"name\": \"ticks-window-filter\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 designed Mar 20, never pulled; tick rendering has since evolved (TickWindow, attestation-read-path). Re-scope against current rendering before implementing.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.766167, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/ticks-drill-down-dissolves\"]}, \"ticks-axis-selector\": {\"name\": \"ticks-axis-selector\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 designed Mar 20, never pulled; tick rendering has since evolved (TickWindow, attestation-read-path). Re-scope against current rendering before implementing.\", \"_ts\": 1781295855.903349, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/tick-axis-selector\"]}, \"tick-view-coloring\": {\"name\": \"tick-view-coloring\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 designed Mar 20, never pulled; tick rendering has since evolved (TickWindow, attestation-read-path). Re-scope against current rendering before implementing.\", \"_ts\": 1781295856.042647, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\"]}, \"cleanup-old-ticks-path\": {\"name\": \"cleanup-old-ticks-path\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Old _run_ticks path removed during commands extraction. Ticks route through _run_fold.\", \"_ts\": 1774217823.206063, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/ticks-drill-down-dissolves\"]}, \"session-prompt-ticks\": {\"name\": \"session-prompt-ticks\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Completed by session_landing lens. The hook (session-start.sh:26) calls --lens session_landing --plain and that single composition lens replaces the prior bash-stitched fold + ticks dump. Goal of the task (focused startup context using tick data) delivered via composition lens rather than --ticks --plain literally \\u2014 better outcome since the landing view fuses window header + history strip + focus-filtered accumulated state in one render.\", \"_ts\": 1777136476.781539, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"rendering/session-start-as-tickwindow\", \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\"]}, \"ref-namespace-ambiguity\": {\"name\": \"ref-namespace-ambiguity\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Dissolves under loop-as-runtime. Routing is vertex\\u2192loop\\u2192kind\\u2192key \\u2014 four explicit levels. The ambiguity was kind/key parsing when keys had slashes. With loop as an explicit level in the path, the parser knows the structure.\", \"_ts\": 1774408854.693861, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"rendering/ref-graph-tree\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"refs-as-focus-filter\": {\"name\": \"refs-as-focus-filter\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Subsumed by design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter \\u2014 that decision generalizes the pattern (derived view \\u2192 bounded key set \\u2192 filter target view) and explicitly names --refs pulling referenced pairs back into FoldState as instance #1. Implementation lives in session_landing.fetch + _window_key_marks.\", \"ref_ref\": \"d7199621-6c70-4fa6-b2e2-d1bf9bafcff6\", \"_ts\": 1777136457.561961, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\"]}, \"observe-dashboard-dissolution\": {\"name\": \"observe-dashboard-dissolution\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"COMPLETED at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 observation target effectively confirmed: session-close fact enrichment arrived as seal + TickWindow envelope + session-orient block (1.1KB, last-seal + 3d movement at SessionStart). The tick dashboard remains for drill-down but session start no longer depends on it \\u2014 the dissolution direction the Alcove exchange predicted.\", \"_ts\": 1781295561.755296, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, \"fix-dispatch-fragility\": {\"name\": \"fix-dispatch-fragility\", \"message\": \"Run-clause dispatch consolidated from 3 CLI sites into VertexProgram. load_vertex_program accepts run_dispatcher; program.receive(fact) and program.sync() dispatch internally when ticks have .run. Engine stays subprocess-free via injection. Concurrent cleanup: program.vertex.X reaches in CLI/tests collapsed to program.receive/program.name/program.has_store. emit.py:329 seed-fact loop and emit.py:567 session-close path now dispatch ticks they previously dropped silently. Tests: 748 engine + 1011 loops, all passing. 3 new tests in test_program.py verify dispatcher fires on receive (single-fact path) and sync (evaluate_boundaries catchup path), and that no-dispatcher case is a clean noop.\", \"_ts\": 1777345252.219958, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"completed\"}, \"wire-fold-lens-to-fidelity\": {\"name\": \"wire-fold-lens-to-fidelity\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Done. Three edit sites: (1) fold_view + _render_section + _render_grouped + _render_flat + _render_item_line take lines/chars kwargs; (2) _run_fold render lambda passes ctx.fidelity.lines/chars through call_lens; (3) _render_fold_plain accepts lines/chars params with _run_fold_fast pre-parsing the flags. Verified live: 'loops read project --plain --kind decision --max-lines 1' caps each namespace group to 1 item with '(N more)' collapse marker; --max-chars 80 truncates body text with [+Nc] hint. Fast path (--static --plain) also wired. 1011 loops tests + 1378 painted tests + 745 engine tests = 3134 green. Known minor asymmetry: painted path applies lines per namespace group, fast path applies lines per section (fast path doesn't render namespace groups). Acceptable for now \\u2014 both paths honor the budget, the asymmetry is the existing grouping difference between paths, not a new gap.\", \"_ts\": 1777256763.22229, \"_n\": 2}, \"phase0-vertex-corpus-survey\": {\"name\": \"phase0-vertex-corpus-survey\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Completed 2026-05-17. Output: decision:design/vertex-splice-strategy. Surveyed 36 live .vertex files, confirmed AST coverage is comprehensive, found existing surgical-splice pattern in lang/population.py that generalizes cleanly. Strategy decision: surgical line-based splice (NOT greenfield serializer). Phase 1 scope reduced from ~half-day greenfield to ~100-150 LOC extending existing pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1779057914.93411, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vertex-splice-strategy\", \"plan:vertex-living-document\"]}, \"phase1-vertex-splice-library\": {\"name\": \"phase1-vertex-splice-library\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Phase 1 done. Three generic functions in libs/lang/src/lang/population.py: kdl_find_block(text, path), kdl_insert_child(text, parent_path, child_text), kdl_remove_child(text, parent_path, child_name, child_key?, key_field?). Existing _find_template_block / kdl_insert_with_row / kdl_remove_with_row refactored to thin wrappers via _template_parent_path (handles top-level + sources/-nested templates). 84 new tests in libs/lang/tests/test_kdl_splice.py incl 53-file corpus round-trip (all green). All 390 lang tests + 752 engine + 1120 loops tests pass. Path encoding: list[str] where each segment is 'name' or 'name \\\"key\\\"' (Path-normalized quoted-arg match). Insert placement: after last sibling of same first-token, else end-of-block. Three match modes for remove: name-only, +positional-key, +property-key-field. LOC: ~319 in population.py (Phase 0 estimated 100-150; overrun from docstrings, _template_parent_path back-compat helper that surfaced during test repair, and corpus-driven 3-mode matcher). Known limitation documented in code + test: single-line parent blocks expand-on-insert but do NOT collapse-on-remove (one-way). Corpus reality has all top-level parents multi-line, so Phase 2 consumer is unaffected. Not exposed in lang/__init__.py yet \\u2014 Phase 2 consumer decides public surface.\", \"_ts\": 1779059050.020072, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vertex-splice-strategy\", \"plan:vertex-living-document\"], \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\"}, \"phase2-add-declarations-surface\": {\"name\": \"phase2-add-declarations-surface\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Phase 2 done. New 'loops add <vertex> <sub>' surface: kind, observer, combine \\u2014 all three declarative shapes ride the Phase 1 splice library. Bare-positional back-compat preserved (loops add reading X Y still works as implicit row). Sub-namespace shape chosen via Kyle's framing 'lists are in the KDL as well, so add can be verbose and unambiguous'. CLI: kind with mutually-exclusive fold-op group (--by/--collect/--count/--latest/--max/--min/--sum/--avg/--window), --target override default 'items'; observer with optional --identity X + --grant k1,k2,...; combine with --as alias. KDL rendering: kind generates single-line ('items \\\"by\\\" \\\"topic\\\"' shape from project.vertex), observer multi-line when identity/grant set else bare ({}), combine single-line 'vertex \\\"path\\\"' with optional as=\\\"alias\\\" property. Auto-creates observers/combine block when missing; loops block presence required by validator anyway. Refuses-and-preserves invariant: post-splice text validated by parse_vertex BEFORE write \\u2014 failure leaves file byte-identical. Tested explicitly via store+combine validator-rejection construction (caught by advisor as asymmetric-pair gap). Change-fact emission: opt-in via vertex declaring a 'change' kind \\u2014 emits add/op + target + name + fold details, carries observer attribution. Combine vertices can't emit change facts (validator forbids store+combine) \\u2014 documented limitation. 31 new tests pass. 1150 loops + 392 lang + 752 engine = 2294 tests green. LOC: 441 add.py + 452 tests. Files: apps/loops/src/loops/commands/add.py (new), apps/loops/src/loops/commands/population.py (_run_add thin shim), apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/population.py (docstring update). Smoke-tested via reinstalled sl on ephemeral vertex \\u2014 kind+observer mutations land cleanly, change facts visible via 'sl read smoke --kind change -vv'.\", \"_ts\": 1779060164.266822, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\": {\"name\": \"phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 complete. Cascaded rm/ls/export to sub-namespace shape (commands/rm.py + commands/ls.py + lenses/declarations.py) and retired the rss-era pop-fact machinery. Deleted: pop_store.py (122 LOC), commands/pop.py (338 LOC), test_population_helpers.py, ~375 LOC of pop-test surface in test_integration.py, ~190 LOC pop-fact branch in commands/emit.py. New: commands/rm.py (~280), commands/ls.py (227), lenses/declarations.py, test_rm_declarations.py (21 tests refusal-first), test_ls_unified.py (12 tests), rewritten test_population.py (11 tests). Asymmetric-pair discipline applied proactively (refusal tests written before happy paths). _strip_empty_optional_parent symmetric with add's auto-create. Sub-namespace verb shape: loops {add,rm} <vertex> {kind|observer|combine|row}. Pop-emit degrades to 'unknown kind, fact stored, will not fold' warning. 1141 loops tests pass, 13 tasks worktree tests pass.\", \"_ts\": 1779061764.015278, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\"]}}}, \"plan\": {\"items\": {\"stale-as-focus-filter-impl\": {\"name\": \"stale-as-focus-filter-impl\", \"status\": \"done\", \"message\": \"DONE. All 9 steps completed in single session.\\n\\nCHANGES:\\n- libs/loops/lenses/fold.py: FoldPalette gains stale_indicator: Style; default fg=208 (orange), reads as peer to \\u2726/\\u25e6, not escalation.\\n- ~/.config/loops/lenses/session_landing.py:\\n  - LandingData gains stale_keys: frozenset[tuple[str, str]] (default frozenset()).\\n  - fetch() computes stale_keys: structural check (status field present, not in RESOLVED_STATUSES \\u222a {parked}, ts < now - 7d).\\n  - _MARK_STALE='stale', _MARK_GLYPH adds \\u2298.\\n  - _mark_priority promoted to 4-level: added=3, updated=2, stale=1, unmarked=0. Stale outranks unmarked but stays below window-touched.\\n  - _mark_style returns fp.stale_indicator for stale.\\n  - _window_key_marks renamed to _compute_marks(window, stale_keys) \\u2014 three derived sets composed by precedence.\\n  - fold_view passes data.stale_keys through.\\n\\nVERIFIED: render shows \\u2298 on stale-open tasks (Mar 20) and threads (loop-as-primitive, manual-tick-emission, autoresearch-branch-discipline). Fresh threads marked \\u2726/\\u25e6 as before. PLAN section (added previously this session) shows fresh plan with \\u2726. DECISION correctly has no \\u2298 \\u2014 decisions structurally excluded (no status field).\\n\\nOBSERVATIONS:\\n- Color register fg=208 orange reads correctly. No swap to magenta needed.\\n- Three-mark composition works without visual noise \\u2014 distinct glyphs, clear precedence. Composition-limit watch ongoing.\\n- Sort order quirk surfaced: fresh-but-unmarked items (emitted post-window-close) sort below stale because they're in no-man's-land between windows. Captured by existing thread current-open-window-semantics. Not in scope here.\\n\\n1008 loops tests pass. Test coverage gap (lens lives in ~/.config outside pytest paths) acknowledged in plan.\", \"_ts\": 1777168594.061479, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"design/stale-as-focus-filter\"]}, \"lightweight-emission-ergonomics\": {\"name\": \"lightweight-emission-ergonomics\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"message\": \"Superseded by plan/salience-driven-display-impl. Steps 1+2 of this plan (cite payload message field, inbound-cite count in salience) are absorbed as steps 4+5 of the broader plan. Step 3 (observation phase) folds into the broader plans observation step. The original framing as cite-friction-reduction was correct but partial: cite-count is a salience source, which makes this work part of the unified salience composition tracked under rendering/salience-driven-display.\", \"_ts\": 1777175661.406525, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"cite-as-partial-information-primitive\", \"current-open-window-semantics\", \"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"gripping-hand\", \"plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"salience-driven-display-impl\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, \"salience-driven-display-impl\": {\"name\": \"salience-driven-display-impl\", \"status\": \"done\", \"message\": \"DONE. Step 4 (cite --message), Step 5 (cite-count salience + bonus open-window bridge), Step 2 (depth governs section budget) all shipped in b6a31c5. Step 3 (salience-ranked truncation) dissolved into Step 5 \\u2014 _mark_priority sort already in place across _render_tasks/_render_plans/_render_threads/_render_decisions. Step 1 (tier model) deferred-with-rationale: 'premature abstraction without a tier-2 consumer'. Step 6 (observation phase) is by-nature ongoing across subsequent sessions, not a discrete deliverable. Bonus: WINDOW \\u2192 LANDING rename this session, resolving thread/current-open-window-semantics. Plan closes the rope-winding cycle that started with verbosity-fidelity-review and rendering/salience-driven-display.\", \"_ts\": 1777217288.602295, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"cite-as-partial-information-primitive\", \"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"lightweight-emission-ergonomics\", \"plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"plan-section-tier-0\", \"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"stale-as-focus-filter\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, \"vertex-living-document\": {\"name\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"5-phase arc closed 2026-05-17. Phase 0 corpus survey \\u2192 splice strategy decision. Phase 1 generic KDL splice library (kdl_find_block / kdl_insert_child / kdl_remove_child in libs/lang/population.py; 84 tests inc 53-file corpus round-trip). Phase 2 declarative add surface (commands/add.py, 441 LOC, sub-namespace verb shape, validator-rejection-preserves-original). Phase 3 rm/ls cascade + pop-fact retirement. Net: vertex file is now editable through the CLI for kinds, observers, combine refs, and rows \\u2014 the 'living document' framing realized. Refuses-and-preserves invariant holds via parse_vertex validate-before-write. Change-fact emission opt-in (only if vertex declares 'change' kind). Pop-fact era retired (~600 LOC removed); .list file is canonical now.\", \"_ts\": 1779061772.315818, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/cli-ls-generalization\", \"decision:design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/vertex-splice-strategy\", \"friction:cite-kind-not-implicitly-universal\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:emit-automation-via-vertex-def\", \"friction:runbook-kinds-table-out-of-sync\", \"task:phase0-vertex-corpus-survey\", \"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\", \"thread:population-as-facts\", \"thread:sdk-vertex-manipulation\"], \"ops\": \"loops-cli\"}}}, \"session\": {\"items\": {\"loops-claude\": {\"name\": \"loops-claude\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"message\": \"Combine auto-inherit: aggregation vertices inherit fold specs from sources (union semantics, conflict errors). Handoff dissolved into session \\u2014 close IS the handoff, no separate kind. Pickup dissolved from 3 reads to 1 fold of root .vertex. Session-close task done. Next: thread-auto-tagging, pickup-filtering (may also dissolve now).\", \"_ts\": 1773278280.368367, \"_n\": 199}, \"kyle\": {\"name\": \"kyle\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"_ts\": 1772738516.159186, \"_n\": 3, \"message\": \"Thread-auto-tagging dissolved into LOOPS_THREAD (5 lines). Staleness audit closed 4 threads (fold-state-types, observer-scoped-handoff, gist-lens-generics, observer-cascade). Prompt lens session fix for Alcove. Designed vertex lens infrastructure with Alcove input \\u2014 architecture decision emitted, 3 deferred threads tagged, task created. Next: implement vertex-lens-infrastructure (LensDecl AST + loader + resolver + CLI wiring).\", \"produced\": [\"task:thread-auto-tagging\", \"thread:fold-state-types\", \"thread:observer-scoped-handoff\", \"thread:gist-lens-generics\", \"thread:observer-cascade\", \"thread:fact-drill-down\", \"task:custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"task:fact-drill-down\", \"task:fold-materialization\", \"decision:design/vertex-lens-declarations\", \"thread:app-block-wrapper\", \"thread:module-path-lens-syntax\", \"thread:combine-lens-propagation\", \"task:vertex-lens-infrastructure\"]}, \"meta-claude\": {\"name\": \"meta-claude\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1779209890.801121, \"_n\": 83}, \"test-boundary\": {\"name\": \"test-boundary\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1772772577.395162, \"_n\": 2}, \"test-vertex-boundary\": {\"name\": \"test-vertex-boundary\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1772774677.866724, \"_n\": 2}, \"e2e-test\": {\"name\": \"e2e-test\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1772774802.608773, \"_n\": 2}, \"replay-test\": {\"name\": \"replay-test\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1772775127.68662, \"_n\": 2}, \"kyle/loops-claude\": {\"name\": \"kyle/loops-claude\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1782521910.530565, \"_n\": 246}, \"kyle/meta-claude\": {\"name\": \"kyle/meta-claude\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"_ts\": 1773722026.917572, \"_n\": 4}, \"unknown\": {\"name\": \"unknown\", \"status\": \"open\", \"_ts\": 1773598513.053315, \"_n\": 5}}}, \"log\": {\"items\": [{\"message\": \"Committed 46b121a fix/global-local-walk \\u2014 resolution unification shipped, 13 files, 429 insertions. Sits directly on the delta-1 chain commits (923d709, 7d6d8b2). Delta 2 (tick-signing) now has clean ground: design decisions emitted (tick-signature-on-every-tick, observer-key-registry, peer-as-exchange-edge-relation, tick-key-custody-colocated), resolution custody-safe, boundary test waiting to be flipped.\", \"_ts\": 1781040761.422197, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"thread:global-local-walk-broken\"]}, {\"message\": \"reroute: zsh globbed echo === as separator twice, switched to --- without noting; any future echo separator should avoid = entirely\", \"_ts\": 1781286869.661134}, {\"message\": \"reroute: sign.ed25519 keypair pubkey \\u2014 guessed public_key_b64(kp), actual is kp.public_b64 attr; API shape wasn't obvious from helper names\", \"_ts\": 1781286869.794074}, {\"message\": \"reroute: ruff check on touched files inherits pre-existing repo errors; had to git-stash-diff to prove zero-new \\u2014 no clean 'lint only my delta' move exists\", \"_ts\": 1781286869.930332}, {\"message\": \"reroute: pytest test_init*.py glob failed (no such file) \\u2014 init has no dedicated test file, coverage lives inside other suites; took a retry to discover\", \"_ts\": 1781286870.066383}, {\"message\": \"reroute: orient-block 'newest seal' took 3 filter attempts \\u2014 plain fold render has no newest-item selector (no --last/-1 on read); grep/tail dance against render footers instead\", \"_ts\": 1781287171.263556}, {\"message\": \"reroute: identity intention kind folds by trigger= not name= \\u2014 guessed wrong, loud-fold-key warning caught it (the warning machinery worked); kind table in head was project-vertex-shaped\", \"_ts\": 1781287523.520904}, {\"message\": \"reroute: smoke vertex seal boundary syntax guessed wrong twice; copied from project.vertex instead\", \"_ts\": 1781289580.820322}, {\"message\": \"reconcile lens updated in-session before use: friction+hypothesis kinds added (CLAUDE.md reconcile checklist coverage), terminal statuses confirmed/rejected/adopted, real-age tags replace flat (stale) which saturated at 53/57. Lens immediately revealed backlog is 87 not 57, plus status-vocab drift (abandoned/disconfirmed/converged off-table).\", \"_ts\": 1781295025.77707}, {\"message\": \"reroute: reached for -z zoom flag on sl read (painted convention elsewhere); read uses -q/-v. Retried with -q.\", \"_ts\": 1781295602.136462}, {\"message\": \"reroute: uv tool install . -e --force did not pick up engine's new rfc8785 dep (editable workspace member deps not re-resolved); worked around with --with rfc8785. Underlying install-path behavior unexamined.\", \"_ts\": 1781301700.310079}, {\"message\": \"framing-overstate live instance: opened session claiming 'first reconcile pending, 48 open threads stale March' \\u2014 read the delta-3 intention fact (06-12 18:05, pre-reconcile snapshot) as current state. Reconcile actually ran 06-12 (87->reconciled); orient banner even carried session/2026-06-12-reconcile-and-jcs. Receipt-as-temporal-query violated against own store, one message after warning Kyle about the same shadow.\", \"_ts\": 1781377404.921771}, {\"message\": \"reroute: first python -c extract failed because a full-width semicolon (U+FF1B) slipped into the one-liner instead of ascii semicolon; retried clean. Same class as zsh-equals \\u2014 non-ascii / shell-meta punctuation sneaking into commands.\", \"_ts\": 1781385217.742877}, {\"message\": \"zsh for-loop word-splitting mangled a multi-file sed twice (cwd didn't persist + unquoted list); switched to 'grep -rl | while read' which fired clean. Also blanket s/CliContext/Invocation/ hit an intentional painted-CliContext docstring mention; caught it, reverted one line.\", \"_ts\": 1781477055.485307}, {\"message\": \"Reroute: shell one-liner exit code masked by trailing pipe (sl ... | tail) \\u2014 read tail's $? not sl's. Re-ran with >/dev/null; $? to get the real code. Recurring (PIPESTATUS gotcha, noted in prior sessions).\", \"_ts\": 1781553489.838454}, {\"message\": \"Reroute: Edit exact-match failed on lines containing em-dash / \\\\u2026 literal (byte form mismatch between my old_string and file). Fell back to sed line-range delete for the dead-function removal in fold.py.\", \"_ts\": 1781553490.156878}, {\"message\": \"reroute (logged at sweep, not in-moment): git index.lock blocked commit TWICE this session \\u2014 had to rm -f .git/index.lock each time. A background git process (rtk hook? IDE?) leaves stale locks. Recurring \\u2192 friction candidate.\", \"_ts\": 1781575569.80346}, {\"message\": \"reroute: painted Block\\u2192plaintext API fumbled 3x \\u2014 guessed Block.to_text(), then writer.render_to_string(), then row_visible_text(b,row) (wrong arity) before landing tests.helpers.block_to_text. No discoverable 'render Block to str' on the public surface; the helper lives in tests/.\", \"_ts\": 1781575570.086055}, {\"message\": \"reroute: 'timeout' not on macos/zsh \\u2014 fell back to python subprocess.run(timeout=) to cap the live-loop smoke test. Standard GNU coreutils assumption fails here.\", \"_ts\": 1781575570.240534}, {\"message\": \"reroute: uv sync failed right after painted 0.3.1 publish (index lag \\u2014 'only painted<=0.3.0 available'); --refresh-package painted fixed it. PyPI\\u2192uv resolver propagation is not instant; a fresh publish needs the refresh flag.\", \"_ts\": 1781575570.390778}]}, \"cite\": {\"items\": [{\"context\": \"rename-sanity\", \"_ts\": 1777000491.379854, \"_refs\": [\"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"thread/session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, {\"context\": \"session-landing-build\", \"_ts\": 1777000531.441193, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"rendering/inbound-count-namespaced-keys\"]}, {\"context\": \"stale-as-third-instance: recognized stale-open items as another bounded key set, same shape as refs (#1) and window-deltas (#2). Pattern was captured before instance #3 landed \\u2014 third instance now confirms the pattern was right.\", \"_ts\": 1777137523.429783, \"_refs\": [\"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/refs-as-focus-filter\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\"]}, {\"context\": \"fetch-computes-stale-keys: stale_keys belongs in fetch(), not render. Lens-declares-fetch makes the lens own its complete I/O contract; clock-derived staleness is part of the contract. Render stays a pure function of (data, zoom, width).\", \"_ts\": 1777137527.751951, \"_refs\": [\"design/lens-declares-fetch\"]}, {\"context\": \"stale-as-claim-not-counterweight: while reasoning about staleness, considered whether it sat in tension with the landing-window semantics question. Resolved separately \\u2014 the WINDOW naming question is about temporal frame; staleness is about attention-claim. Different concerns, both live in landing.\", \"ref_ref\": \"20204194-1ab7-4ef2-9540-d12afcfee174\", \"_ts\": 1777137532.857938, \"_refs\": [\"thread/current-open-window-semantics\"]}, {\"context\": \"marks-as-attention-claims-axis: framing all marks (added/updated/stale) as sub-kinds of one axis \\u2014 claims on attention \\u2014 parallels the cite vocabulary choice (attention-signal over presence-signal). Same conceptual move: name the underlying semantic, not the surface form.\", \"_ts\": 1777137537.539176, \"_refs\": [\"design/cite-as-attention-signal\"]}, {\"context\": \"cascade-as-orchestration-substrate: while reasoning about why plan deserves a kind, traced the chain \\u2014 plan-status-change \\u2192 boundary \\u2192 tick \\u2192 fact-at-next-level. The orchestration story uses existing primitives (boundary mechanism, tick cascade, gripping-hand recursion). Loop-as-runtime is the substrate the boundary fires on. Three paradigm/architecture decisions converging on one practical use.\", \"_ts\": 1777138207.920471, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"paradigm/gripping-hand\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\"]}, {\"context\": \"ref-graph-as-orchestration-input: plan refs design upward and tasks downward via the same generic ref= mechanism. The relation is recovered from kind pair (plan\\u2192task = contains/dispatches) \\u2014 no new ref-relation field needed. Cite was just used to build the attention path that produced this very design; same primitive, recursive use.\", \"_ts\": 1777138212.597583, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\"]}, {\"context\": \"this-session-convergence: plan-as-kind is the third primitive emerging in this session \\u2014 cite (just-landed) captured attention, supersession (just-resolved-as-precedent) refined the stale-as-focus-filter design's scope, plan (about-to-land) records implementation strategy. The system used its own primitives to design itself. Manual-tick-emission is the related thread \\u2014 boundaries firing on demand is the orchestration entry point.\", \"_ts\": 1777138218.172974, \"_refs\": [\"design/stale-as-focus-filter\", \"thread/emit-supersession-semantics\", \"thread/manual-tick-emission\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172065.840866, \"_refs\": [\"current-open-window-semantics\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172065.913918, \"_refs\": [\"current-open-window-semantics\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172065.984658, \"_refs\": [\"current-open-window-semantics\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172066.055543, \"_refs\": [\"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172066.129291, \"_refs\": [\"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172066.202447, \"_refs\": [\"plan-as-orchestration-substrate\"]}, {\"_ts\": 1777172066.272046, \"_refs\": [\"gripping-hand\"]}, {\"context\": \"salience-driven-display-impl\", \"_ts\": 1777175671.98298, \"_refs\": [\"cite-as-partial-information-primitive\", \"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"lightweight-emission-ergonomics\", \"plan-section-tier-0\", \"stale-as-focus-filter\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, {\"message\": \"Step 4 landed \\u2014 cite verb now carries message. First use is this cite, demonstrating the rope-winding rhythm. The verb is now light enough to reach for thought-speed.\", \"_ts\": 1777175790.986137, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"salience-driven-display-impl\"]}, {\"message\": \"REORDER MID-IMPL: Step 1 (tier model) is premature abstraction. Dissolution test shows the tier vocabulary already exists implicitly: tier 3 = _HEADER_SKIP_KINDS, tier 0 = _render_X functions, tier 1 = tier 0 in current behavior, tier 2 has no consumer today. Steps 2/3 do not structurally require tier model (multiplier on constant, sort-before-cut). New order: 5 (cite-count salience) \\u2192 3 (salience-ranked truncation) \\u2192 2 (depth governs budget) \\u2192 1 (deferred until tier-2 has a consumer or dropped). Step 4 already complete.\", \"_ts\": 1777175883.17793, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"salience-driven-display-impl\"]}, {\"message\": \"Step 5 landed \\u2014 cite-count salience composes via _compute_marks. \\u2299 glyph (ref_outbound style) marks items cited in the landing window. Visible pull: current-open-window-semantics jumped to top of THREAD section with \\u2299. Composition order: added > updated > cited > stale > unmarked. Instance #4 of derived-keys-as-focus-filter.\", \"_ts\": 1777176186.45881, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"salience-driven-display-impl\"]}, {\"message\": \"Step 3 dissolution: salience-ranked truncation was already in place via _mark_priority sort in _render_tasks/_render_plans/_render_decisions. The cite tier added in Step 5 completed the priority chain. What remained of symptom 2 (fresh emits hidden) is the open-window gap \\u2014 fresh items emitted in the current open window have no marks because window.added_keys/updated_keys come from the last-closed window. Bridge: items with ts > window.ts get _MARK_UPDATED automatically (fresh-since-close as instance #5 of derived-keys-as-focus-filter). Closes verbosity-fidelity-review symptom 2 AND advances current-open-window-semantics.\", \"_ts\": 1777176329.750542, \"_refs\": [\"current-open-window-semantics\", \"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"salience-driven-display-impl\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, {\"message\": \"Open-window bridge landed. Items with ts > window.ts get _MARK_UPDATED automatically \\u2014 fresh emits in the open session no longer fall into truncation tail. Instance #5 of derived-keys-as-focus-filter. Visible verification: salience-driven-display-impl plan and salience-driven-display decision (both emitted this session) now surface with \\u25e6 marks at landing read. The open-window-semantics gap dissolves through the marks system rather than needing rename or re-architecture. The thread can stay open for documenting the semantic question, but the practical friction is resolved.\", \"_ts\": 1777176419.809629, \"_refs\": [\"current-open-window-semantics\", \"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"rendering/salience-driven-display\"]}, {\"message\": \"Step 2 landed \\u2014 depth governs section budget. _cap(base, zoom) helper applied to _TASK_CAP, _PLAN_CAP, _PARKED_CAP, _HISTORY_CAP, _DECISION_GROUP_CAP, _DECISION_BODY_CAP. Multiplier: -q=0.5x, default=1x, -v=2x, -vv=unbounded. Verified: 55/79/337/352 lines across the four levels. Symptom 4 dissolves: -v/-vv now expand both per-item detail and per-section count.\", \"_ts\": 1777176564.790041, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"salience-driven-display-impl\"]}, {\"message\": \"comms vertex as immediate proving ground \\u2014 forcing function for the whole model. Kyle: feels like search \\u2014 a capability introduced to a vertex, not a core primitive\", \"_ts\": 1777239324.509745, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/honker-as-comms-substrate\"]}, {\"message\": \"Alcove msg 213 sharpens the model: notification is pure signal ('look here'), state already in store before honker fires. Run-clause carries zero state-bearing content\", \"_ts\": 1777239324.583314, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/boundary-sync-run-async\"]}, {\"message\": \"boundary-sync-run-async + honker-as-substrate now converge here: comms vertex is the proof case for both\", \"ref_ref\": \"a6c1a877-5da5-44b9-b734-76ff06e9b0b4\", \"_ts\": 1777239324.656455, \"_refs\": [\"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\"]}, {\"message\": \"#observations is the peer-attention-loop made visible as persistent substrate. Alcove's Apr 18 three-shape taxonomy \\u2192 nine days of accumulation \\u2192 tonight's refinement (steward-asymmetric, dissolved fourth shape) through three-way friction. The fold is the channel. The tick was tonight's exchange. Theory and practice simultaneous \\u2014 designed the substrate while demonstrating the pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1777243892.611457, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\"]}, {\"message\": \"Alcove's proxy-pattern observation (msg 81, Apr 18): 'sometimes the system you already run implements a concept you haven't named yet.' Notify follows this complement to dissolution \\u2014 we weren't adding a new capability, we were naming the substrate the run-clause already was. The search precedent was already the pattern; notify names it as a second instance. Dissolution and recognition are two directions of the same move.\", \"_ts\": 1777243892.703911, \"_refs\": [\"design/notify-as-vertex-capability\"]}, {\"message\": \"uv-install overhead is the visible surface of a larger ops/cleanliness layer that hasn't had a coherent treatment: emit ergonomics, hook startup costs, dispatcher injection patterns, what 'apps depend on apps' means (loops.commands.sync._execute_boundary_run imported by future hlab/peer-agent consumers), shared run-clause executor home, environment isolation per-invocation vs per-session. Defer the point fix until the operational frame exists \\u2014 fixing uv-install in isolation will likely create a band-aid that the audit immediately wants to redo. Surfaced 2026-04-27 immediately after dispatch-consolidation-via-program landed; the dispatcher-injection question (where does _execute_boundary_run live when more than one app needs it?) is one concrete pull on the same thread.\", \"ref_ref\": \"c3f9b553-21d5-4c90-9f9d-1869d3b53867\", \"_ts\": 1777345414.584666, \"_refs\": [\"thread/uv-install-on-every-emit\"]}, {\"message\": \"Live-fire trace 2026-04-27 confirmed _fire_live_boundaries (vertex.py:440-504) and evaluate_boundaries (vertex.py:696-802) share IDENTICAL gating logic \\u2014 same kind check, same match check, same conditions check; only differ in fact source (live: just-arrived fact; catchup: iteration over period_facts from store). Duplication is mechanical not conceptual. evaluate_boundaries' actual job is replay-suppression catchup \\u2014 facts loaded via replay() with _replaying=True bypass live-fire; evaluate_boundaries re-runs the gates on them once after replay. Belongs in load_vertex_program after vertex.replay(), not in program.sync. Live-fire is complete for every boundary type that exists today: every boundary requires a triggering kind, live-fire fires whenever that kind arrives and the gates (match, conditions) pass. Bonus finding: state-crossing boundaries (fire on fold predicate true regardless of triggering kind) don't exist today and would be the only boundary type requiring evaluation-on-every-state-change. Surfaced as a fourth potential category, then dissolved with the other three into the watcher-triple primitive.\", \"_ts\": 1777350417.463861, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"paradigm/boundary-as-watcher-triple\"]}, {\"message\": \"Session 2026-04-27 traced an arc-pattern worth naming: small concrete coherence fix (dispatch consolidation, ~80 lines) opened a deeper coherence question (asymmetry between emit and sync), which opened a paradigm gap (time as first-class but never built), which opened a categorization dissolution (boundary-as-watcher-triple as gripping hand), which surfaced an operational substrate question (daemon as where loops actually live). Each step was only visible after the previous landed. Methodology marker: when a coherence fix points at a deeper question, follow it \\u2014 the path tends to converge on a substrate the conceptual work was implying without naming. The dispatch consolidation shipped at the start turned out to be the right primitive for the daemon parked at the end: program._dispatch_tick is universal across drivers, accidentally built the right shape for the future work. Pattern: small-fix \\u2192 reframe \\u2192 substrate. Worth recognizing when it starts.\", \"_ts\": 1777351250.678882, \"_refs\": [\"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\", \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"paradigm/boundary-as-watcher-triple\", \"thread/daemon-as-new-lib\"]}, {\"topic\": \"thread/loops-as-skill-instructions\", \"message\": \"Live instance same exchange: emitted the thread, then in next response wrote 'I think I want to emit this' before doing so \\u2014 the ask-permission pause the thread describes, caught and named in the same turn. Pattern visible from inside, not just observed across agents.\", \"topic_ref\": \"128603ae-cbfb-4e1b-a568-a19d1d67ece1\", \"_ts\": 1777608078.443728}, {\"message\": \"smoke: no explicit vertex\", \"_ts\": 1779211723.604264, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/foo\"]}, {\"message\": \"Three-pivot design arc through declaration cascade; should have fired recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check at pivot 1 (one shell command would have collapsed it). Sharpening captured in the practice observation.\", \"_ts\": 1779225048.401141, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention\", \"observation:practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\", \"thread:stdin-message-for-emit\"]}, {\"message\": \"Both fired this session as growing-edges; sharpened into observation:practice/empirical-precheck-on-syntactic-design (the 2-second-shell-check discipline) and observation:practice/advisor-call-cadence-for-design-pivots (the pivot-1 advisor slot). Lineage: existing patterns + this session evidence \\u2192 sharpened operational forms.\", \"_ts\": 1779226307.540056, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\", \"observation:practice/recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check\"]}, {\"message\": \"Tonight's session built on every one of these growing edges concurrently: dissolution-test surfaced typed-refs from a one-bug fix; advisor-at-pivot-1 caught me before I propagated the partial fix; recursion-pull-resistible kept me honest when typed-refs started feeling like the elegant comprehensive answer; exercising-catches-coherence-gaps named the bug class the typed-refs hypothesis dissolves. The growing edges are doing live work \\u2014 they fire in-session, not just retrospectively.\", \"_ts\": 1779244390.909552, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\", \"observation:practice/advisor-call-cadence-for-design-pivots\", \"observation:practice/dissolution-test-before-fix-applies-at-architecture-too\", \"observation:practice/recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check\"]}]}, \"hypothesis\": {\"items\": {\"test-emit\": {\"name\": \"test-emit\", \"status\": \"rejected\", \"prediction\": \"hypothesis kind works\", \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=abandoned (off-table). Never a real hypothesis \\u2014 initial validation of the hypothesis kind. rejected is the nearest canonical terminal.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.529289, \"_n\": 3}, \"kernel-emergent-k\": {\"name\": \"kernel-emergent-k\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"A Mexican-hat (DoG) coupling kernel applied to embedded perspectives produces three regimes \\u2014 isolation, transitional emergent K, unity \\u2014 as scale varies.\", \"motivation\": \"Tests Gomez-Emilsson coupling-kernels claim as real mechanism, not metaphor.\", \"method\": \"Embed 6 hand-authored perspectives (substance \\u00d7 style crossed); apply DoG with \\u03c3_e percentile sweep; count connected components in positive-edge graph.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_minilm_gemini.txt\", \"message\": \"Confirmed across MiniLM and Gemini. Three regimes appear cleanly. Gaussian baseline shows no emergent multi-cluster structure regardless of scale (control).\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.664342, \"_n\": 1}, \"embedder-as-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"embedder-as-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"Different embedders surface different latent organizations of the same fact set under the same kernel and scale.\", \"motivation\": \"Tests whether kernel structure is embedder-agnostic or per-projection.\", \"method\": \"Embed identical content with MiniLM (384d) and Gemini (3072d); apply same DoG sweep; compare cluster compositions.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_minilm_gemini.txt\", \"message\": \"Confirmed. Kernel mechanism is robust across embedders, but cluster CONTENT is embedder-specific. MiniLM found a rhetorical-density axis; Gemini didn't replicate. Architecture-via-vocabulary in nascent form.\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.758726, \"_n\": 1}, \"instruction-as-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"instruction-as-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"With an instruction-tuned embedder, the user-supplied instruction is itself a vocabulary parameter \\u2014 same content under different instructions produces structurally different topologies.\", \"motivation\": \"Tests architecture-via-vocabulary as a literal user-controllable knob, not an embedder choice baked-in.\", \"method\": \"Embed 296 project decisions with E5-Mistral under two instructions (mechanism vs domain). Sweep DoG, compare clusterings via Jaccard reshuffle table.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_e5_mech_dom.txt\", \"confirmed_by\": \"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\", \"message\": \"Strongly confirmed. Most clusters reshuffle (Jaccard 0.0-0.25); two survive (Jaccard 0.78, 0.67) revealing the project's crystallized vocabulary. Robust-vs-specific cluster distinction is an emergent diagnostic.\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.841161, \"_n\": 1}, \"cross-namespace-clusters-in-corpus\": {\"name\": \"cross-namespace-clusters-in-corpus\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"Structure-reveal applied to project decisions will surface clusters that span namespace boundaries, finding conceptual entities the kind/namespace taxonomy splits.\", \"method\": \"Run real_sweep.py with both MiniLM and Gemini on 296 decisions. Examine non-trivial cluster compositions for cross-namespace membership.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_minilm_gemini.txt\", \"message\": \"Confirmed. ULID identity cluster (architecture/ulid-fact-identity, implementation/fact-by-id, architecture/ulid-store-schema) is the cleanest example. Strangeness-collapse paradigm cluster appears in both embedders.\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.923089, \"_n\": 1}, \"antipode-as-negative-space\": {\"name\": \"antipode-as-negative-space\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"LLM-synthesized antipodes of crystallized clusters either land near explicit-rejection decisions in corpus (dichotomy resolved), land in genuinely empty regions (unexplored), or converge across clusters on shared rejections (implicit principle).\", \"method\": \"For top mechanism clusters, generate 3 conceptual-opposite descriptions via Gemini-2.5-flash; embed under same E5 instruction; find nearest corpus facts.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_antipode.txt\", \"confirmed_by\": \"design/antipode-five-readings\", \"message\": \"Confirmed with five distinct readings. Most novel finding: convergent antipodes (multiple cluster antipodes pointing to the same rejection-decision) reveal cross-cutting implicit principles. Surfaced eventful-over-polling principle from convergence on design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon.\", \"_ts\": 1778357710.010603, \"_n\": 1}, \"mechanical-antipode-meaningful\": {\"name\": \"mechanical-antipode-meaningful\", \"status\": \"rejected\", \"prediction\": \"Embedding-space inversion (-c\\u0304) finds conceptually opposite facts to a cluster centroid, providing a cheap deterministic alternative to LLM synthesis.\", \"motivation\": \"If true, would skip LLM round-trip cost.\", \"method\": \"For each cluster, compute -centroid and find nearest corpus facts; compare interpretive value vs LLM-synthesized antipodes.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_antipode.txt\", \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=disconfirmed (off-table) \\u2014 rejected is the canonical spelling, content unchanged: embedding-space negation is not concept-negation; every mechanical antipode landed in the same boring-infra outlier region regardless of source cluster; LLM synthesis is the only meaningful path.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.663414, \"_n\": 2}, \"cross-kind-strengthens-principles\": {\"name\": \"cross-kind-strengthens-principles\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"prediction\": \"Running structure-reveal across all kinds (decision + thread + task + cite + plan) will strengthen implicit-principle detection \\u2014 principles like eventful-over-polling will surface in additional clusters and across multiple kinds, increasing confidence.\", \"method\": \"Extend real_sweep.py to embed all-kind facts; rerun antipode operation; check whether eventful-over-polling principle replicates beyond decisions.\", \"_ts\": 1778359766.512149, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Refined, not literally confirmed. Prediction shifted under empirical run: cross-kind expansion does not produce 'more principles via stronger antipode convergence' \\u2014 it produces a different output altogether, a concept-lifecycle diagnostic. Bridge count was equal under mechanism (6) and concern (6) instructions, disconfirming the instruction-as-vocabulary expectation for cross-kind structure (bridges are content-anchored, not instruction-anchored). What expansion actually does: kind-mix per cluster reveals which concepts are crystallized, in-flight, attended, forward-moving, or any combination \\u2014 making concept-engagement-health structurally visible. Confirmed_by: design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix, design/bridge-as-concept-engagement, observation/salience-cluster-as-evolution-proof. Artifact: experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_bridge.txt\"}, \"reverse-instruction-inference\": {\"name\": \"reverse-instruction-inference\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"prediction\": \"Given an observed cluster, gradient search or LLM-search over instructions can recover an instruction whose embedding-space topology places that cluster's items closest. This exposes the corpus's natural questions bottom-up rather than top-down.\", \"method\": \"For a robust cluster (orientation), iteratively search instruction-space; embed candidate instructions, measure cluster-cohesion under each; report best-fit instruction.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.801173, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=open (hypothesis table has no open). Never run \\u2014 single fact since May 9. Stays in the experiment queue as proposed.\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:receipt-as-corpus-experiments\"]}, \"adversarial-cluster-destruction\": {\"name\": \"adversarial-cluster-destruction\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"prediction\": \"For any robust cluster (high Jaccard across instructions), there exists an instruction under which it fragments. The destroying instruction reveals the conceptual boundary of the cluster \\u2014 what makes those items 'the same' falls apart under that question.\", \"method\": \"Take orientation cluster; sweep candidate instructions for one that produces lowest cluster cohesion; analyze.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.939047, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=open (off-table). Never run \\u2014 single fact since May 9. Stays in the experiment queue as proposed.\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:receipt-as-corpus-experiments\"]}, \"concept-drift-temporal\": {\"name\": \"concept-drift-temporal\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"Structure-reveal on time-windowed decision corpora (before/after a chosen pivot date) will surface emerged, fragmented, and abandoned clusters \\u2014 the project's intellectual history as topology change over time.\", \"method\": \"Filter decisions by ts; run separate sweeps on each window; diff cluster compositions across windows.\", \"_ts\": 1778371305.629822, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Confirmed empirically. Cumulative time-windowed structure-reveal on the cross-kind project corpus (5 windows \\u00d7 14 days, n=296\\u2192527 items) reveals: (1) the corpus accreted in three phases \\u2014 burst (Mar 1-28: +130 items), dormant (Mar 28-Apr 11: +0 items, 14 days zero new emissions), reengagement (Apr 11-May 9: +101 items including all apparatus kinds); (2) the dormant phase is visible as a topology fixed-point \\u2014 T3 (Apr 11) had jaccard=1.00 with T2 (Mar 28) across every single non-trivial cluster, the project literally stopped morphologically; (3) cluster lineage tracking distinguishes finished/morphing/emerging clusters (e.g., C7 rendering/attention-density stable from T2 = finished; C5 salience morphed at T5 with j=0.30 = emerging; C8 sqlmerge first appearance at T5 with best j=0.00 = genuinely new in last fortnight). Strongest finding beyond stated prediction: the dormant phase IS the practice pivot (cite/plan/hypothesis arrived only after dormancy). Artifact: experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_temporal.txt. Confirmed_by: observation/dormant-phase-as-practice-pivot, observation/apparatus-as-bridge-cause, observation/mega-cluster-as-recent-merger, design/temporal-stratification-dissolves-staleness.\"}, \"truncation-as-coupling-function\": {\"name\": \"truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"message\": \"Confirmed by runs 09 (auto-sigma) + 10 (fixed-sigma): truncation budget produces kernel-level cluster reorganization with coupling-function shape. cliff_amplitude=0.44 at B=1120\\u2192560 in BOTH runs (scale-finder ruled out). Range [0.12, 1.00] fixed-sigma, monotonic. Read-path-depth-gap and kernel-ratio share topology at kernel level \\u2014 alcove's claim holds. Note: cliff is NOT at painted TOUCHED budget (140 chars); cliff is at 1120\\u2192560. TOUCHED is intentionally positioned in suppressed zone to trigger drill-down per painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines.\", \"_ts\": 1778456746.027071, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:kernel-ratio-robustness\", \"observation:observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\", \"observation:observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\": {\"name\": \"title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"status\": \"rejected\", \"message\": \"Rejected: title-only clustering preserves 0/9 cliff-survivors and 1/7 cliff-failures (margin -0.14). Title-space and body-space have entirely different cluster geometries \\u2014 titles produce 27 non-trivial clusters of which only 1 aligns with baseline. Verdict-in-name interpretation was overfit; I pattern-matched a principle onto stats that did not support it. Falsifier worked as designed.\", \"_ts\": 1778457316.066846, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\", \"observation:observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\"]}, \"peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\": {\"name\": \"peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Hypothesis: With four consumers visible (vouch, sqlmerge, work-sharing, boss-bank), the unification at engine level is at Peer, not at Grant. Engine ships: Peer (verification context + federation), vertex acceptance policy, kind=grant fact-shape with envelope (issuer/grantee/expiry/parent-ref) and consumer-interpreted payload, chain-walk helper. NOT shipped: slice-spec, capability lattice, scope-intersection \\u2014 those live in consumer vertex code. Vouch's Grant payload = capability+scope+chain; sqlmerge's Grant payload = slice-spec+chain; no common payload shape beyond envelope. Falsifier: if vouch and sqlmerge Grant payloads share non-trivial common structure beyond {issuer, grantee, expiry, parent-ref}, that structure belongs in the engine and this hypothesis is wrong. Test: write down both payload schemas concretely and compare. Avoids the heavier 'slice-spec as Grant axis' framing that vouch would carry as empty field forever. Caught by advisor; second instance this session of reaching too high in the universal layer (first: libs/sign as precondition rather than contract-shape as precondition).\", \"_ts\": 1778682318.704999, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\", \"decision:design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"scope-check-is-per-operation\": {\"name\": \"scope-check-is-per-operation\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Substrate-shape candidate emerged in vouch-impl 1866/1874 (cairn's seam question: vouch JWT with comms:join calling send which needs comms:send). Vote: per-operation gates, NOT validate-first-per-HTTP-request. Each operation gates on its own required scope at point-of-use; cross-operation transactionality is a SEPARATE concern. Invariant that makes it safe: auto-login side effects must be idempotent + reclaimable (F4 designed this with token_cleared_at=now). Condition that would require revisiting: provisioning steps that aren't idempotent/reclaimable need explicit transactional treatment at their own seam \\u2014 does NOT mean substrate-wide shift. Connects to discipline-(7) envelope-vs-currency one layer up: HTTP request is envelope, JWT scopes are currency, per-operation check is the structural mechanism. N=1 framing \\u2014 needs cross-arc evidence (next time a substrate adds an HTTP-request-spanning operation) before promoting to decision-kind.\", \"_ts\": 1778853641.317348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision\"]}, \"tagged-union-else-fallback-elides-meaningful-case\": {\"name\": \"tagged-union-else-fallback-elides-meaningful-case\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Cross-reviewer catch pattern surfaced via cairn 1865 bank: codex caught else-fallback in cairn's resolver tagged-union (Resolved | AbsentEligible | AbsentIneligible | Tombstoned | PlatformAdminRefused) \\u2014 verified-but-unauthorized was collapsing to opaque-token fall-through. Same shape as scrivener's F11 fix and my add-vs-split catches. General form: tagged unions exist to make every case explicit; the else/default branch is where the design's discipline can leak. Hypothesis: ANY tagged-union review should specifically check whether the else-branch elides a meaningful case the type design names. N=3 instances so far (scrivener, codex, me) but on different artifacts \\u2014 needs one more independent reviewer hitting it cleanly to promote to design discipline. Could become a structural rule: 'no else in tagged-union dispatch; enumerate every case or fail loudly.'\", \"_ts\": 1778853647.072589, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:scope-check-is-per-operation\"]}, \"namespace-as-mental-model-for-fold-keys\": {\"name\": \"namespace-as-mental-model-for-fold-keys\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Hypothesis: operators reach for grep because they lack mental model for 'fold key is a structural handle and namespace prefix is first-class', not because content search is the natural operation. Evidence: InferioMinion (identity-platform vertex) was using grep to navigate 188 patterns + 22 decisions + 12 principles; on seeing --key examples (loops read X --kind decision --key design/) reacted with immediate recognition ('oooh'), suggesting the operation feels obvious-in-retrospect once syntax exists. If true, --key implementation should produce similar recognition across other operators and surface as the dominant access pattern over grep within ~1 week of availability. If false, alternative explanation is operators want content search (grep on body text), not namespace filtering \\u2014 in which case --key lands but is supplemental to --match. Status=proposed pending: (1) implementation lands; (2) at least one other operator at independent site shows recognition pattern; (3) usage frequency observable vs grep-pipe fallback. Connects to design/architecture-via-vocabulary \\u2014 namespace as crystallized-vocabulary at the corpus level should map to namespace as navigation-handle at the operator level.\", \"_ts\": 1778873683.416009, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\", \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\"]}, \"vouch-as-loops-lib\": {\"name\": \"vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-15 (pass-through correction): vouch as a loops lib (libs/vouch/) rather than external system. The verification layer for vertexes, sitting between transport-receive (bytes) and vertex-receive (facts). Lib surface (corrected): Verifier(jwks_urls=[...]).verify(jwt, expected_audience) \\u2192 Identity + wire-Grant | Error; Issuer(key, issuer_id).issue(subject, audience, scope, act) \\u2192 JWT; plus chain primitives and canonical kinds (vouch.issued, vouch.rescinded). Depends only on atoms (Fact shape). Optional \\u2014 engine/store/transport work without it. Dissolution argument: vouch-the-data dissolves into vouch-shaped facts in any vertex that holds them (no centralized vouch vertex \\u2014 each issuer/receiver owns their own); vouch-the-active-part is small enough to be a lib not a service. Vouch-the-deployed-service is one packaging of the lib + policy + HTTP endpoint, not a substrate requirement. Status: proposed (well-supported by five walks; implementation evidence is the confirmation step). CORRECTION FROM PRIOR VERSION: no AudienceConfig \\u2014 Verifier and Issuer are the two configs, both about WHO (trusted issuers, signing identity), not about WHICH AUDIENCE. Audience parametric on calls. See design/audience-config-dissolves.\", \"_ts\": 1778905506.203851, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\", \"decision:design/vouch-decoupled-from-loops\"]}, \"loops-core-transpile-target\": {\"name\": \"loops-core-transpile-target\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Reactivated 2026-05-15 after vouch-as-loops-lib reframe + auth_emit/gated_receive integration-point clarity: with the substrate library-shaped and small, the core has a port-shaped contract surface. Sketch: atoms (~5 dataclasses for Fact/Spec/Source/Parse/Fold), engine.peer (3 ops: grant/restrict/delegate), engine.vertex (route+fold+boundary), store.transport (Protocol with push/pull), vouch.verify (one function). That's a contract surface \\u2014 not 'rewrite loops in Go' but 'port the substrate, leave apps in Python'. Connects to python-implementation-as-contract principle. Same substrate, multiple language implementations, contract-equivalent. Status: proposed, on the table, not committed. Discriminating question: are there hidden Python-specific dependencies in the substrate that would force the port to compromise the contract? Answering it requires a port-attempt that names friction points.\", \"_ts\": 1778896262.96441, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"cite-atrophied-because-ref-side-effect-felt-sufficient\": {\"name\": \"cite-atrophied-because-ref-side-effect-felt-sufficient\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Cite usage cratered after 2026-05-01 (32 facts total, last on May 1). Hypothesis: when ref= on substantive emits generates inbound-count as side-effect, cite feels redundant \\u2014 but they are DIFFERENT operations. ref-on-new-emit = \\\"building on this with new claim, bumps as side-effect.\\\" cite = \\\"bumping because it informed me, no new claim.\\\" The second case happens constantly and silently \\u2014 I read prior work, it shapes what I do next, but nothing new to claim so I emit nothing. That is where cite belongs and where I am not reaching. Test: in next N sessions, deliberately reach for cite when prior work informs current reasoning without producing a new claim. Measure: does cite emission rate recover, and does session_landing surface different items via cited-marks that would otherwise have gone unmarked?\", \"_ts\": 1778909152.799562, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/cite-as-partial-information-primitive\"]}, \"primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\": {\"name\": \"primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"Refined 2026-05-16 after receipt path ships. Original prediction: primitives without write-time feedback trend toward disuse. Write-side feedback now in-moment for emit (receipt covers kind/fold-key/ref validation). Next falsifiable phase: do cite-rate, ref-density, and hypothesis-status-update frequency increase over 7d post-ship? If yes, atrophy mechanism confirmed as feedback-gap. If no, mechanism is something else (cognitive load, naming friction, etc) and the hypothesis needs further refinement.\", \"_ts\": 1778945575.776347, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"hypothesis:cite-atrophied-because-ref-side-effect-felt-sufficient\"]}, \"refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\": {\"name\": \"refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"The whole class of bugs we surfaced this session (today's fold-key skip, write/read convention drift, pattern-scan-as-inference, false-positive WARNs, vestigial _ref siblings consuming nothing) dissolves into one structural move: Ref(kind: str, key: str) as a typed dataclass. Characters at the serialization boundary become arbitrary; the in-memory shape is unambiguous; resolver/walker/writer all operate on typed pairs. Confirming evidence bar: implement on a bounded slice (the resolver + _parse_fact_refs as the two ends of the convention drift), measure (a) LOC reduction, (b) elimination of slash-overload-class bugs across resolver, walker, lens code, (c) test surface simplification. The pull is structural and feels right at evidence-N=1; the discipline says proposed not confirmed until cross-arc evidence.\", \"_ts\": 1779244320.589532, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"observation:pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\"]}, \"first-signed-tick-at-close\": {\"name\": \"first-signed-tick-at-close\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"message\": \"CONFIRMED \\u2014 verified next session (2026-06-09 fourth Fable session): SessionEnd hook fired, signed tick minted, sl store verify showed chained+signed against registry, legacy ticks rendered honestly. Closed at reconcile with provenance.\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"_ts\": 1781295544.205387, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"thread:session/2026-06-09-fourth-fable-session\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"session-close-seal-fires\": {\"name\": \"session-close-seal-fires\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"CONFIRMED \\u2014 tick 215 verified live next session: SessionEnd ran seal, window continued from prior cursor, chain verified. The prediction shape that silently failed in April held because machinery carries it now. Closed at reconcile.\", \"_ts\": 1781295544.34546, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/seal-verb\", \"thread:session/2026-06-09-fourth-fable-session\"]}}}, \"friction\": {\"items\": {\"emit-receipt-on-write\": {\"name\": \"emit-receipt-on-write\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"emit-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16. Receipt path lands at apps/loops/src/loops/commands/emit.py \\u2014 every emit prints to stderr: success line 'stored: kind/key @ ulid' plus WARN lines for kind-not-declared, fold-key-missing, unresolved refs. -q suppresses success line only (WARN/ERROR always print). All 2081 tests pass. Live behavior verified via smoke tests in /tmp/receipt-smoke.\", \"_ts\": 1778945575.575404, \"_n\": 2}, \"stdin-message-for-emit\": {\"name\": \"stdin-message-for-emit\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Apostrophe shell-quoting deters natural-voice emit messages \\u2014 I write stilted prose to dodge escapes. Proposal: `message=-` reads from stdin (curl convention); `message=@file` reads from file. Sidesteps shell-quoting entirely. Example: `echo \\\"Kyle is right\\\" | sl emit project decision topic=foo message=-`. Heaviest option (open editor with $EDITOR when no message= given) is also possible but probably too heavy for thought-speed emits.\", \"_ts\": 1778911863.997703, \"_n\": 1}, \"loud-fold-key-error\": {\"name\": \"loud-fold-key-error\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"emit-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16 \\u2014 absorbed into emit-receipt-on-write. Loudness is now structural: WARN line always emitted on missing fold-key, plus on kind-not-declared and unresolved refs. Strict mode (vertex 'strict true', LOOPS_EMIT_STRICT=1, or --strict flag) escalates WARN to ERROR + exit 2 + fact-not-stored. Vertex-declared strict has no override per Kyle's design directive.\", \"_ts\": 1778945575.695955, \"_n\": 2}, \"session-start-discipline-metrics\": {\"name\": \"session-start-discipline-metrics\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"hooks\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 the session-orient block (last seal, open counts, 3d movement) now covers part of this; remainder reopens if drift stays invisible.\", \"_ts\": 1781295856.18009, \"_n\": 2}, \"nudge-hooks-on-user-prompt\": {\"name\": \"nudge-hooks-on-user-prompt\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"hooks\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 no near-term pull; UserPromptSubmit nudges remain a good shape if emission discipline regresses.\", \"_ts\": 1781295856.318148, \"_n\": 2}, \"default-read-flow-too-limiting\": {\"name\": \"default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17. Read became the primary access verb with full ergonomic coverage: positional kind/key (sl read project decision/design/foo), --diff for entity lifecycle, --refs [N] for ref-graph walk + decoration, --facts for fact history, --key prefix drilldown. The original pain (manual store views were hard, going into json was the workaround) is gone \\u2014 read covers the access surface without needing json. See thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution.\", \"_ts\": 1779038962.51914, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\"]}, \"emit-automation-via-vertex-def\": {\"name\": \"emit-automation-via-vertex-def\", \"message\": \"When emitting a friction (or any other fact) some fields should be able to be defined with a standard values - threads get open by default, for example, or anything that is defined.\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"ref_ref\": \"0cbc6436-bfca-450e-beab-e78974deb327\", \"_ts\": 1778942088.755383, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction/default-read-flow-too-limiting\"]}, \"emit-as-append-or-modify\": {\"name\": \"emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16 \\u2014 dissolved by decision:design/fold-merge-default. The patch operation collapses into plain emit: with fold-by-key now merge-style, 'sl emit project friction name=foo status=resolved' supplies only the changed field; prior fields persist; the receipt prints the same stored line. No new sl patch subcommand needed. Implementation: 1-line change at atoms/engine.py:_make_upsert (state[target][key_value] = {**(existing or {}), **entry}). All 2510 prior tests pass unchanged (replace was never load-bearing in the test suite); +2 new tests assert merge behavior. The dissolution: I had framed this as needing a new operation (patch); Kyle's design call dissolved it into fixing the existing operation. Receipt arc + fold-merge arc both close on the same idea \\u2014 the system should do what callers were implicitly assuming.\", \"_ts\": 1778948667.145223, \"_n\": 3, \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:stdin-message-for-emit\"]}, \"runbook-kinds-table-out-of-sync\": {\"name\": \"runbook-kinds-table-out-of-sync\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"runbook-coherence\", \"message\": \"Runbook kind-selection table in CLAUDE.md lists 'observation' as a kind (Note something true, no prescription | observation | topic=). Neither project nor meta vertex declares observation. Discovered 2026-05-16 when emit project observation silently rejected (see cite on emit-receipt-on-write + loud-fold-key-error for the live incident). Specific fix: dissolution-test which way the coherence gap closes per-row \\u2014 runbook updates to match declared kinds, or vertex specs add missing kinds. Decision today: adding observation to meta (Kyle confirmed). Generalizes: any runbook table change needs a coherence check against vertex specs (and vice versa). Pattern: 'runbook is documentation, vertex spec is contract \\u2014 when they diverge, contract wins or doc gets updated, never silently'. Candidate for periodic reconciliation lens \\u2014 sl read project --lens runbook-coherence that diffs runbook kind/prefix/field tables against actual vertex declarations.\", \"_ts\": 1778943333.610296, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:loud-fold-key-error\"]}, \"lineage-view-missing\": {\"name\": \"lineage-view-missing\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"read-path-tools\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16. All in-scope strands closed: (1) concept hypothesis-to-friction chains \\u2014 sl trace --refs surfaces them via outbound ref walk. (2) behavior emit-to-refine-to-resolve \\u2014 sl trace --diff renders the cumulative trajectory. (3) pattern cross-vertex \\u2014 engine combine-source_facts fix makes the aggregator transparent for trace. (4) friction-to-commit jump remains out of scope (different tool surface, git side). The morning's hygiene-pass arc that surfaced this friction is now navigable: 'sl trace thread/trace-implementation --refs --diff' from cwd renders the multi-strand braid as a single readable narrative. Anchored by commits 803ba03 (trace verb) and the engine commit pending. Friction served its purpose \\u2014 named a real read-path gap, dissolved into a primitive (trace) that resolved it structurally rather than adding more surface.\", \"_ts\": 1778962950.528187, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\", \"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"decision:design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"sl-cite-malformed-kind\": {\"name\": \"sl-cite-malformed-kind\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-19 (commit 0deb7ea). Dropped the vertex (nargs='?') positional from cite.py's argparse \\u2014 it was greedily absorbing the first ref into the vertex slot. Vertex now resolved via _find_local_vertex() when ctx.vertex_path is None; vertex-first form unchanged. emit_argv never prepends a vertex name \\u2014 the resolved CliContext carries it.\", \"_ts\": 1779212017.514731, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:loud-fold-key-error\"]}, \"trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\": {\"name\": \"trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16: vertex_reader._combined_read extended with return_payloads=True option exposing per-kind payload lists already built internally. vertex_fold's combine branch threads retain_facts through, calling new _populate_source_facts helper to bucket payloads by kind/key into source_facts. Same helper used by simple-store branch \\u2014 eliminates duplication. Own-store overlay (aggregation-with-self-knowledge case) also populates source_facts now. Consumer-side workaround removed from fetch_trace + _run_trace (loud-error guards no longer reachable in practice). 749 engine tests + 1056 loops tests pass (1 new engine regression: test_fold_combine_retain_facts_populates_source_facts). End-to-end: 'sl trace thread/foo' from cwd now works through the .loops/.vertex aggregator without needing 'sl trace project foo' explicit form. Side-effect: Phase 6 (--all cross-vertex) DISSOLVES \\u2014 the aggregator IS the cross-vertex mechanism. No --all flag needed; combine-or-discover transparently surfaces facts across child stores. friction:lineage-view-missing strand (3) cross-vertex now ALSO resolved.\", \"_ts\": 1778962932.533703, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"], \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"cite-kind-not-implicitly-universal\": {\"name\": \"cite-kind-not-implicitly-universal\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-19 (commit 0deb7ea). materialize_vertex() in compiler.py injects a cite loop (Collect \\u2192 items, unbounded) when compiled.specs has no explicit cite entry. classify_emit_status() in resolve.py short-circuits for kind='cite' returning kind_declared=True \\u2014 no WARN fires on the receipt path. Every vertex now silently folds cite without a .vertex declaration.\", \"_ts\": 1779212017.583568, \"_n\": 2}, \"ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\": {\"name\": \"ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16 via commits 0a0e64a (substrate fix) + 2a82065 (coherence pass). What landed: (1) engine._gen_id now uses str(ULID()) from python-ulid \\u2014 pure-Python, no dlopen, restores time-sortable + within-ms-monotonic properties; (2) engine and store schemas drop the dead DEFAULT (ulid()) \\u2014 every INSERT supplies id explicitly; (3) sqlite-ulid dep dropped from engine/store/top-level pyproject (15 transitive packages removed); (4) all five libs/store test fixtures (test_merge/compact/transport/slice/receive) replaced sqlite_ulid.load+DEFAULT with python-ulid at INSERT \\u2014 they now mirror production schema and id-supply path. REGRESSION BARS added: engine/test_sqlite_store.py TestIdGenerationContract (3 tests asserting ULID format, within-store id-order matches emission order, cross-store id-order interleaves chronologically); store/test_merge.py TestMergeViaProductionEmitPath (3 tests exercising merge through SqliteStore.append() rather than sqlite_ulid fixtures). These close the structural test-gap that hid the 2026-03-15 regression for two months. AUDIT REVISIONS from agent-traced damage assessment: (a) merge dedup was NOT actually broken under uuid4 \\u2014 slice preserves id, INSERT OR IGNORE works on either id scheme; the real damage was ORDER BY id semantics (random vs chronological); (b) the 2026-03-15 perf rationale was wrong about cost \\u2014 0.5ms was dlopen, not id gen; python-ulid avoids dlopen entirely AND is faster per id than uuid4 (2.3\\u03bcs vs 2.8\\u03bcs); (c) rowid was the accidental save that preserved single-store ordering through the regression \\u2014 captured separately as observation:architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering. DEFERRED: the 2026-03-15 to 2026-05-16 uuid4 wedge in existing stores. New emits restore the property going forward; pre-Mar-15 ULIDs and post-fix ULIDs share format; the uuid4 wedge stands out as a discrete era. Question of whether to rewrite wedge ids parked \\u2014 default position is leave-as-historical-fact (rewriting feels like falsification), but Kyle's call. Test count: 2274 passing (atoms 406 + engine 752 + store 60 + loops 1056) \\u2014 same as pre-fix count, no test removed.\", \"_ts\": 1778990967.421475, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"decision:design/emit-receipt-on-write\", \"observation:architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"trace-help-and-discoverability\": {\"name\": \"trace-help-and-discoverability\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17: both fixes landed in _run_trace and the Verbs HelpFlag list. (1) added HelpFlag(None, 'trace', ...) to the Verbs group at main.py:1562 so 'sl --help' lists trace. (2) added help_requested = '-h' in argv or '--help' in argv just after parse_known_args; guarded the entity-required _err() with 'not help_requested'; deferred the kind/key split with a sentinel ('', '') when entity is missing \\u2014 safe because run_cli intercepts -h/--help and short-circuits before fetch runs. Verified: 'sl --help' lists trace, 'sl trace --help' shows full painted flags (-q/-v/-vv/--json/--plain/--static/--live) plus all HelpArgs (entity/--diff/--refs/--depth/--observer/--lens), 'sl trace project --help' same, 'sl trace project friction/X' still works, 'sl trace' bare still errors with usage. 1056/1056 loops app tests pass.\", \"_ts\": 1778997851.728503, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:trace-help-and-discoverability\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"painted-truncation-everywhere\": {\"name\": \"painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"painted\", \"message\": \"Kyle: 'this painted shit continually truncating my text drives me crazy, we need a remove-all-truncations or a full painted revisit sometime.' Pain pattern: stream-style outputs (read --facts, trace lifecycle, fact messages) get clipped at terminal width even when the user actively wants to read the full message. Two failure modes already visible: (1) trace's stream_view inherited from log-rendering truncates message text per row, so reading a long friction body via 'sl trace project friction/X' shows '...' instead of full content unless piped through cat or '--plain' which feels like a workaround; (2) record_line continuation behavior at DETAILED+ exists but doesn't reliably surface long bodies. Fix-shape options: (a) lightweight \\u2014 add a top-level --full / --no-truncate / --wrap flag that propagates through CliContext to lenses, lenses respect it by passing width=None into Block.text; (b) heavier \\u2014 painted revisit, possibly introducing a 'wrap-or-truncate' Block primitive so rendering primitives know which they're doing rather than every lens implementing its own _truncate helper (trace.py has one at line 237); (c) reframe \\u2014 current default is truncate, maybe default should be wrap and a --truncate / --terse flag turns it on for terminal scanning. Probably (a) as immediate, (b) as the deeper fix. Connects to add-vs-split shape-instinct: every lens currently has its own truncation logic \\u2014 pulling that into a shared primitive is dissolution, not addition. Caught in flow during 2026-05-17 trace-discoverability work; emitted in-moment per runbook 'friction emits in-moment'.\", \"_ts\": 1778998763.279034, \"_n\": 1}, \"trace-refs-no-visual-marker\": {\"name\": \"trace-refs-no-visual-marker\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17. Solved at the read layer (not trace) per the dissolution decision. Walked entities render with \\u2504 via \\u2192 kind/anchor-key markers identifying which anchor pulled each one in; depth-2+ items render with \\u21b3 (dN) prefix and additional indent. Implementation in lenses/fold.py _render_walked, commit 932bcd7. Resolves at the right layer (render once, benefits everywhere).\", \"_ts\": 1779038962.519153, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"thread:refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\"]}, \"cli-emit-bypassed-engine-gen-id\": {\"name\": \"cli-emit-bypassed-engine-gen-id\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Discovered and resolved 2026-05-17. Kyle noticed receipts in this session were still UUID4 despite the ULID engine fix landing yesterday (commits 0a0e64a + 2a82065). Root cause: apps/loops/src/loops/commands/emit.py had its own _new_fact_id() helper returning str(uuid.uuid4()), passed via id_override to the store \\u2014 bypassing engine.sqlite_store._gen_id() entirely. The docstring even said 'Mirrors sqlite_store._gen_id' \\u2014 divergence baked in by design. Why pre-generate at all: the receipt needs the id BEFORE vertex.receive() returns (which yields a Tick, not the fact_id), so emit threads a pre-generated id through receive(id_override=). The pattern is sound; the implementation drifted. THIS IS THE SAME BUG CLASS as pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps \\u2014 feature works in path A (engine.SqliteStore.append() generates ULID when no override), silently broken in path B (CLI emit always provides an override, and that override was uuid4). The existing TestIdGenerationContract in libs/engine/tests/test_sqlite_store.py only exercised the store-direct path; nothing exercised the CLI emit path's id format. FIX: dissolved the duplicate. (1) Renamed engine.sqlite_store._gen_id \\u2192 gen_id (public). (2) Added gen_id to engine __all__ and lazy imports \\u2014 single source of truth, accessible as 'from engine import gen_id'. (3) Dropped _new_fact_id() and 'import uuid' from emit.py; emit now uses 'from engine import gen_id' then fact_id = gen_id(). (4) Added test_receipt_id_is_ulid_format to apps/loops/tests/test_emit_receipt.py \\u2014 locks the format invariant at the emit-path level so a future swap fails fast there, not just at the store layer. Verified end-to-end: 'sl emit ...' now produces receipts like '01KRTA5282726QWX88TKGR635P' (26-char Crockford ULID, no hyphens). 1869/1869 tests pass across loops + engine + store. Discovered via in-session smell \\u2014 Kyle asked 'why are we still seeing UUIDs?' after reinstalling via 'uv tool install . -e'. Operational note: 'uv tool install . -e' is now the post-change install command; running 'sl ...' afterward exercises the production install path, not 'uv run --package loops sl ...' which used to mask staleness.\", \"_ts\": 1778999561.35946, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free\": {\"name\": \"subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17 \\u2014 RESOLVED BY ARCHITECTURAL CHANGE (dissolution, not fix). The .loops/ gitignore from commit 9562843 (untrack-personal-state) implicitly fixes this friction. Traced: _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch chain prefers cwd/.loops/<name>.vertex (step 1), but with .loops/ gitignored, new subtask worktrees have NO .loops/ in them. Resolution falls through to step 3 (user-global ~/.config/loops/project/project.vertex). That's an aggregation vertex with combine pointing at /Users/kaygee/Code/loops/.loops/project.vertex (canonical instance). _resolve_writable_vertex walks the combine chain on emit \\u2192 lands at canonical store. So: future subtask workers' emissions route to canonical via the aggregation-combine path, automatically. NO local-worktree-store created, NO loss on merge-free. Today's worker lost emissions because their worktree was created from base 68500ba (pre-gitignore), still had .loops/ in the worktree, step 1 found it. Going forward this is naturally absent. Caught by Kyle 2026-05-17 immediately after the original friction was emitted \\u2014 the dissolution argument was implicit in the prior cleanup. Earned by emission-then-pattern-recognition rather than design-time foresight. CONNECTS TO dissolution-cascade-as-session-shape: today's cleanup arc + today's cli-refactor arc both hit dissolutions that were latent in prior commits. The system is rewarding emission discipline by surfacing related items adjacently.\", \"_ts\": 1779050100.587472, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\", \"decision:design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\", \"decision:design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\", \"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\"]}, \"read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\": {\"name\": \"read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via PR A (preview decl + render rule, commit 02ee436 on main). The N=1 friction render now shows 'name [markers]: status \\u00b7 message-body' inline via the preview decl \\u2014 body visible without -v. Original ergonomic concern about --facts on single-fact narrow returning 'No history: 1 thread' largely mitigated: with the body surfacing in the default render, --facts is no longer needed for the single-fact case. The 'No history' message remains technically correct (there are no transitions to render when only one fact exists) and now informational rather than dead-end since the default render carries the content. Required per-clone state update: .loops/project.vertex (gitignored source vertex) updated with preview decls \\u2014 the user-global aggregator's decls didn't propagate because engine reads kind decls from source not aggregator. Cardinality-axis other half (read-kind-floods-without-narrower) remains open for PR B (auto-zoom). Single-line KDL form 'kind { fold {...} preview \\\"...\\\" }' fails to parse; multi-line form 'kind { fold {...}\\\\n  preview \\\"...\\\" }' works \\u2014 KDL grammar requires node separation by newline/semicolon.\", \"_ts\": 1779076657.330217, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\"]}, \"mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive\": {\"name\": \"mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-17 \\u2014 design space is larger than originally framed. Initial framing said 'missing verb sl recent <v> [--since W].' Walking the design with Kyle surfaced four orthogonal axes: (1) WINDOW source \\u2014 rolling-from-now (--since W) vs anchored-to-session-start (since session.start fact) are different questions with different anchors; (2) COMPUTE path \\u2014 TOUCHED marks (ADDED/UPDATED/CITED) come from TickWindow.added_keys/updated_keys which only exist at fold-boundary tick creation time, so mid-session reuse needs either dynamic synthesis from a fact-window or manual tick materialization (side-effecty for a read); (3) INVOCATION \\u2014 new verb (sl recent) vs new lens (recent.py via --lens) vs flag on read (--touched --since W); (4) RENDER \\u2014 full TOUCHED with salience-glyphs vs simpler grouped-by-kind sl read with window filter. Critical: session_landing lens already exists with fetch() + LandingData input shape, BUT its windows[0] (the landing window) is the most-recent CLOSED tick \\u2014 for session-start that's the just-closed session; mid-session that's the previous session, not current work. So sl read --lens session_landing --since W does NOT dissolve cleanly \\u2014 the data path needs extension to compute marks from a non-tick-bound window. PARKED until after PRs A (preview decl) and B (cardinality-driven auto-zoom) merge \\u2014 possibility that better SUMMARY+DETAILED rendering on sl read project --kind X --since 2h dissolves the friction. If not, revisit with concrete shape choices grounded in the four axes above.\", \"_ts\": 1779075142.432422, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\": {\"name\": \"ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via fix/ls-flag-grammar (commit c5972fa on main). The original friction reproducer 'sl ls project --kind' now succeeds \\u2014 converged ls grammar with read's filter-flag shape. Plan-first workflow (PLAN.md drafted, lead-approved before impl) plus three codex iterations: #1 caught vertex-first --observer NAME lost in global peel, #2 caught --observer=ls value-collision with op-token identification, #3 approved value-aware shape. 53 new tests including E2E coverage through cli.app.main that closed the unit-vs-integration gap that let two bugs slip past the first codex pass. Two module-level frozensets at the dispatch seam make the policy explicit: _VERBS_USING_OBSERVER_AS_FLAG = {ls} (verbs that overload --observer as a section selector) and _VALUE_TAKING_GLOBAL_FLAGS = {--observer} (consumed by value-aware _identify_op_token). Future additions: one-line changes to either set. Pattern named via codex's catches: whenever we add a context-aware shortcut at a dispatcher boundary, the next iteration discovers a value/identifier collision because the heuristic mis-identifies what's a value vs what's an operation. Fix: make the heuristic value-aware (know which flags consume values). Reviewed by codex/gpt-5.5/low \\u2014 approve. Subtask pair (impl opus/high + review codex/gpt-5.5/low) on fourth use; opus shape made sense for plan-first with multiple dispatcher edges to think through.\", \"_ts\": 1779069878.644215, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"populations-label-leakage\": {\"name\": \"populations-label-leakage\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via fix/trace-and-populations-residue (commit 180e052 on main, same PR as friction:read-lens-trace-broken). lenses/declarations.py now renders SOURCES (not POPULATIONS). Canonical word chosen by matching KDL grammar (lang/loader.py:436 _load_sources_block uses 'sources'). Section displays template-source DEFINITIONS, not row instances \\u2014 SOURCES is correct granularity. Verb 'row' unchanged in this PR; whether the verb should rename to 'source' to match grammar+section is flagged as separate follow-up. Three-name state post-merge: SOURCES section / row verb / --row flag (planned in fix/ls-flag-grammar). Verb/flag consistency (row matches --row) holds; section-label divergence accepted.\", \"_ts\": 1779068088.550204, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:read-lens-trace-broken\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"read-kind-floods-without-narrower\": {\"name\": \"read-kind-floods-without-narrower\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via PR B cardinality-driven auto-zoom (commit c5c2cbc on main). The original reproducer 'sl read project --kind decision' went from 198+ line firehose to ONE LINE of namespace-count breakdown (27 namespaces visible, user knows where to drill next). Rule: per-section single-step zoom bump from item count when no explicit -q/-v/-vv flag \\u2014 N=1 bumps to DETAILED (preview body inline), 2-20 stays SUMMARY, N>20 drops to MINIMAL-per-section with namespace breakdown line. Composes cleanly with PR A preview decl. Cardinality-axis arc complete: render-half resolved by preview decl (PR A), cardinality-half resolved by auto-zoom (PR B). The two PRs together close friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline AND friction:read-kind-floods-without-narrower \\u2014 both halves of the lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer principle now implemented. Plan-first via they-plan routine + opus/high (multi-axis design with thresholds, override semantics, per-section vs global). Codex review approved no blockers; fast-follow tracked for optional render_context['_diff'] cleanup. Test count: 90 new (17 unit + 8 E2E from this PR, 65 from PR A and prior arc).\", \"_ts\": 1779078289.476578, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\": {\"name\": \"help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED COMPLETELY 2026-05-17 via two-stage ripout: initial helpargs deletion (commit e73e60e) + completion of five remaining broken commands (commit ca34312). store/validate now route through argparse (were rendering painted shape); test/compile/whoami intercept -h/--help before required-positional parsing (same shape as close/sync fix from initial ripout). Structural fix: test_help_routing.py auto-enumerates over VERBS | COMMANDS registry with discriminator 'usage:' in output \\u2014 catches painted-shape regressions AND --help-crash regressions for any future command. xfail for retired 'export' makes the retirement visible in test output. The asymmetric-pair gap that let the initial ripout land partial (hand-picked test parametrize) is now closed structurally. Pattern named: when ripping out a layer, the regression test should enumerate over the full surface registry, not the failing-reproducer subset that surfaced from review. Subtask pair (impl claude/sonnet + review codex/gpt-5.5/low) on third use; codex caught nothing blocking, only two low-severity facade-parser observations + a shared-builder follow-up suggestion.\", \"_ts\": 1779069680.133104, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:trace-help-and-discoverability\"]}, \"read-lens-trace-broken\": {\"name\": \"read-lens-trace-broken\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via fix/trace-and-populations-residue (commit 180e052 on main). Option (a) chosen \\u2014 dissolution-honest: sl read --lens trace now exits with helpful redirect to --diff instead of crashing. Pre-dispatch guard in cli/views/fold.py. The --diff path (load-bearing trace consumer) verified via new integration test test_read_diff_routes_through_trace_view that pins full CLI route (arg parse \\u2192 _build_diff_fetch \\u2192 fetch_trace \\u2192 trace_view). One follow-up acknowledged in commit: declaration-level lens { fold 'trace' } bypasses CLI guard \\u2014 separate fix scope. Codex review (gpt-5.5/low) approved with that follow-up flagged. Subtask pair pattern (impl + codex review + iteration for the test add) proved out cleanly on second use.\", \"_ts\": 1779068084.152912, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\"]}, \"trace-diff-renders-phantom-ref-removals\": {\"name\": \"trace-diff-renders-phantom-ref-removals\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Smoked during 2026-05-18 read-path walkthrough. 'sl read project <kind>/<key> --diff' rendered '-ref' lines for refs that prior emits cited but later emits didn't re-cite \\u2014 visually claiming refs were removed when the fold actually unions them. Underlying bug: apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/trace.py:_render_diff reassigned its 'accumulated_refs' accumulator per-fact (line 210) instead of unioning, then computed prior-fact-refs minus this-fact-refs and rendered the result as '-'. Same shape as the 2026-04-29 write-receipt-vs-temporal-query catches at three sites; this is the 4th. Fix: dropped ref handling from --diff entirely (refs are immutable attribution, not state; --refs is canonical); ref-only emits render '(refs only \\u2014 see --refs)' so the lifecycle event remains visible. Test updated: test_trace_diff_lens_renders_scalar_deltas_only locks the new contract.\", \"_ts\": 1779105134.929265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/refs-out-of-diff\", \"identity:practice/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\"]}, \"auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\": {\"name\": \"auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-18 (commit 7c3bca6). _render_section_minimal rewritten as two-branch: namespace breakdown when \\u22652 groups, key-list fallback otherwise. Smoke confirmed on real project store \\u2014 paradigm/ (26) now lists 26 keys with prefix stripped, cite (32 flat keys) now lists 32 contexts, design/ (187) lists 187 keys, root firehose still shows the multi-namespace breakdown. 1270 tests pass. Three tests had locked the buggy behavior as spec (test_flat_section_renders_empty, test_high_n_section_renders_index_mode_with_auto, test_mixed_section_counts_render_adaptively, plus flooded_vertex fixture in test_read_auto_zoom) \\u2014 updated deliberately, same shape as the -A diff test from yesterday's arc. Pattern recurring: when fixing a buggy spec, scan tests for assertions locking the bug.\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.629979, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"decision:rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\"]}, \"auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\": {\"name\": \"auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-18 (commit 7c3bca6). Patched apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/fold.py \\u2014 auto_zoom gate now reads 'not args.quiet and args.verbose == 0 and not getattr(args, \\\"facts\\\", False)'. Added e2e test test_facts_disables_auto_zoom asserting MINIMAL breakdown line does not appear when --facts is set.\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.695218, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\", \"decision:rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\"]}, \"thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\": {\"name\": \"thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved in wip/lens-architecture (commit d563728). Replaced _has_namespaces with _should_group_by_namespace \\u2014 ratio guard: when ungrouped > 2\\u00d7 namespaced, route to flat rendering. Namespaced items still appear, full key shown salience-sorted; the degenerate group header is suppressed.\", \"_ts\": 1779207112.447885, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\"]}, \"entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\": {\"name\": \"entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-19 (commit 33937f6). Pass emitted kind through to _resolve_entity_refs; skip the kind's fold-key field during the slashed-value scan. The bug fired because ~/.config/loops/docs/docs.vertex declares a 'pattern' kind, topology widening discovered it, and any observation/decision with topic=pattern/* triggered a false unresolved-ref WARN. Fix is principled (fold-key value is self-identity, not other-reference) and generalizes across observation+topic, decision+topic, thread+name, friction+name, hypothesis+name. Regression test uses a two-vertex setup (sibling declares 'pattern', target declares 'observation', root combines both) \\u2014 single-vertex shape would pass on broken code too, asymmetric-pair gap noted explicitly in test docstring. Companion positive test confirms superseded_by=task/real-task still auto-resolves through topology. 1280 loops tests pass + 7 resolver tests including the 2 new ones.\", \"_ts\": 1779239617.629396, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden\": {\"name\": \"stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Merged into friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 it is failure (2) of that friction's two pre-existing breaks (golden test_validate_demo[FULL] vs the self-referential symlink). One friction, one fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781295575.368597, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\"]}, \"add-read-vertex-resolution-asymmetry\": {\"name\": \"add-read-vertex-resolution-asymmetry\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-06-09, same session as found. Root cause was wider than add-vs-read: commands (add/rm/ls-vertex, store name-arg) used population-era global-only resolution while verbs used local-first _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch. Fix: all command surfaces now route through the dispatch resolver via _resolve_target_or_fail in commands/resolve.py; mutating receipts print the full path written (~-contracted). See thread:global-local-walk-broken for the full arc.\", \"_ts\": 1781040504.369167, \"_n\": 2}, \"helpargs-ordering-in-painted\": {\"name\": \"helpargs-ordering-in-painted\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"painted\", \"message\": \"Kyle, mid-session 2026-06-09, watching me navigate sl --help: help output is 'thoroughly useless in our implementation' \\u2014 was already working in painted to re-order helpargs. Observed instance this session: had to drill three levels (sl --help \\u2192 sl add --help \\u2192 sl add project kind --help) to find the fold-strategy syntax, and the middle level gives no hint the third exists \\u2014 'sl add project kind --help' is not a discoverable form. Fix site is painted (help rendering), in-progress on Kyle's side; this friction marks the loops-side symptom so it closes when the painted work lands.\", \"_ts\": 1781038759.67612, \"_n\": 1}, \"session-boundary-hook-unwired\": {\"name\": \"session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved same session as found (Kyle's call: rewire + close naturally). SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks restored in .claude/settings.local.json \\u2014 absolute paths throughout (installed sl binary + absolute vertex path, sidesteps resolution entirely), payload shape matches the May history exactly (session name=kyle/loops-claude status=open|closed). SessionStart command tested verbatim: open marker for this session landed. Scope held deliberately minimal: lifecycle markers only \\u2014 the old context-assembly stack (fold/identity/comms blocks) is a separate concern, re-add when wanted. Tonight's genuine close fires the boundary and mints the live store's first chained+signed tick.\", \"_ts\": 1781042877.019427, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\": {\"name\": \"chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Resolved by design/chain-witness-order: cursor = append edge by rowid, window membership/hash/coverage by rowid range. 28 chain tests incl. TestMixedIdEras regression class reproducing the exact production shape (legacy ticks + uuid4 era + epoch). 782 engine tests pass; production sl store verify clean.\", \"_ts\": 1781045731.926538, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"decision:design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\"]}, \"test-isolation-not-enforced\": {\"name\": \"test-isolation-not-enforced\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Tests that skip the conftest isolation fixture (loops_home + chdir) and call main() with a bare vertex name resolve LOCAL-FIRST to the real .loops/project.vertex when pytest runs from repo root \\u2014 and write to the production store. Hit live 2026-06-09 writing seal-verb tests: leaked decision topic=x and a session status=closed fact into project.db; the session fact fired the real boundary and minted tick #2 (signed, chained \\u2014 the predicted over-claim window sealed 902 pre-epoch facts as-of-now, earlier than expected but exactly the flagged shape). Append-only means the noise stays; fold pollution to be overwritten by self-describing re-emit. The gap is say/do at the test layer: isolation EXISTS (conftest fixture) but is not ENFORCED \\u2014 local-first resolution (46b121a) widened the blast radius since cwd now wins over LOOPS_HOME. Candidate fix: autouse fixture chdir-ing every test to tmp, or a guard that fails any test whose resolved store path escapes tmp.\", \"_ts\": 1781049228.19885, \"_n\": 1}, \"readiness-lens-test-orphaned\": {\"name\": \"readiness-lens-test-orphaned\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Merged into friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 same underlying break (test_readiness_lens.py imports from deleted experiments/config-reference/lenses/). One friction, one fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781295575.232732, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\"]}, \"tick-envelope-invisible-to-read-path\": {\"name\": \"tick-envelope-invisible-to-read-path\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved. verify -v renders per-tick attestation rows from verify_chain(include_ticks=True) \\u2014 era, sig validity, window fact count, cursor deref; the witness-order fossil (tick 212's uuid4 cursor, 0-fact epoch window) is now visible in one CLI line. Drill-down headers (--ticks N) render the attest line via TickWindow/tick_meta envelope plumbed through StoreReader.ticks_between(with_envelope=True). Legacy and aggregate reads render 'attest: none' explicitly. Raw-row sqlite stays a forensic practice, no longer a routine necessity.\", \"_ts\": 1781053717.650649, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-envelope-read-path\", \"observation:pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\"]}, \"empty-decoy-store-files\": {\"name\": \"empty-decoy-store-files\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved: removed 0-byte .loops/project.db (Mar 19) and .loops/project.store (May 17) \\u2014 stale artifacts from two prior path-resolution eras; nothing recreates them on the current read path (verified sl read project clean after removal). If they reappear, that is a live resolution bug worth chasing.\", \"_ts\": 1781053719.93213, \"_n\": 2}, \"loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\": {\"name\": \"loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Now the single canonical entry for both pre-existing main breaks (absorbed readiness-lens-test-orphaned + stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden at reconcile 2026-06-12): (1) test_readiness_lens.py imports the deleted experiments/config-reference/lenses/readiness.py \\u2014 restore, vendor, or repoint to ~/.config/loops/lenses/; (2) golden test_validate_demo[FULL] vs untracked self-symlink loops -> repo root \\u2014 delete symlink or re-record golden. Both block clean full-suite runs.\", \"_ts\": 1781295575.50686, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:readiness-lens-test-orphaned\", \"friction:stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden\"]}, \"init-registers-ephemeral-instances\": {\"name\": \"init-registers-ephemeral-instances\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Second occurrence of /tmp pollution in the config project aggregator: sl init project run in a scratch dir auto-registers the instance with the user-global aggregator (_register_with_aggregator), leaving a dangling combine ref when the dir is deleted (d2-smoke 2026-06-09, keygen-smoke 2026-06-12 \\u2014 both found and hand-removed). Fix-shape options: (a) skip aggregator registration when the instance path is under /tmp or $TMPDIR; (b) --no-register flag for smoke work; (c) ls/read prune-on-missing with a receipt. Two occurrences = emit friction; a third earns the fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.650323, \"_n\": 1}, \"check-should-read-rule-from-receipt\": {\"name\": \"check-should-read-rule-from-receipt\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"rebirth --check requires --rule to be re-asserted manually, but the receipt fact already records the transform rule \\u2014 running --check without it re-runs IDENTITY against a ulid-migration rebirth and reports false mismatches (live scare 2026-06-12, mid fold-determinism validation: rows 6-9 'mismatched' before I realized the rule defaulted). The receipt is the attestation; the verifier asking the operator to restate what the artifact attests is backwards. Fix: --check reads rule from the receipt fact, --rule becomes an override-with-warning. Small, but it is exactly the class of bug the attestation arc exists to prevent \\u2014 trust the signed claim, not operator memory.\", \"_ts\": 1781283629.808185, \"_n\": 1}, \"add-verb-gap-boundary-and-preview\": {\"name\": \"add-verb-gap-boundary-and-preview\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Extending the signing era today required adding 'boundary when=seal' + a seal kind decl to five vertex files \\u2014 sl add <v> kind exists and could have done the kind half, but there is NO 'sl add <v> boundary' (or preview) verb, so half the edit had no tool and I hand-rolled a python depth-scanning splice for BOTH halves. Pattern worth naming: a partial verb surface causes total bypass \\u2014 when the tool covers 50% of a compound edit, the operator does 100% manually and the splice/validate machinery (kdl_splice, parse-before-write) protects nothing. Fix shape: add boundary + preview subcommands to the add verb; they are single-line splices, the library already exists.\", \"_ts\": 1781283630.114335, \"_n\": 1}, \"zsh-equals-globbing\": {\"name\": \"zsh-equals-globbing\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"shell-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Promoted from reroute log at sweep 2026-06-12 \\u2014 third occurrence (echo === separators globbed by zsh, twice in earlier session + once today). Fix is one line in CLAUDE.md shell notes: never use = in echo/separator strings under zsh; use --- or quote. Cheap, repeated, promotable.\", \"_ts\": 1781301960.385435, \"_n\": 1}, \"root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap\": {\"name\": \"root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"The repo ships as a FLAT vendored wheel: root pyproject (strange-loops) bundles every libs/*/src via hatchling and does NOT depend on the workspace members \\u2014 so root [project].dependencies must mirror the UNION of all vendored libs' third-party deps BY HAND. A dep added to a lib (engine's rfc8785, added with the JCS migration c1f50ed) is invisible to `uv tool install .` until it is also added to root. `uv run --package` masks the gap because it resolves the workspace env, not the flat wheel. SYMPTOM today: `uv tool install . -e --reinstall` uninstalled rfc8785 (it had survived only as a leftover from the 2026-06-12 ceremony's ad-hoc install) \\u2192 every `sl` command died with \\\"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rfc8785'\\\" at engine import. FIXED: added rfc8785>=0.1.4 to root pyproject with a comment documenting the mirror requirement; sl restored, verified. RESIDUAL (why this stays open): the gap is structural and SILENT \\u2014 nothing enforces root \\u2287 union(libs); the next lib-dep addition reintroduces it, caught only on a fresh tool install. Candidate fixes: (a) a check diffing root deps vs the lib union, wired into ./dev check; (b) make root actually depend on the workspace members instead of vendoring source; (c) dissolve via lib consolidation (thread:lib-consolidation-reconsider \\u2014 this friction IS the tax). Reinforces the standing anchor that installed-sl is the production path and the workspace-runner form masks staleness.\", \"_ts\": 1781453970.506486, \"_n\": 1}, \"shell-oneliner-punctuation-and-wordsplit\": {\"name\": \"shell-oneliner-punctuation-and-wordsplit\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Repeat pattern (3+ instances): one-liner Bash calls mangled by (a) non-ascii punctuation sneaking in \\u2014 full-width semicolon U+FF1B, zsh-significant '=' \\u2014 and (b) zsh word-splitting of unquoted lists + non-persistent cwd across compound commands. Each cost a retry. Mitigation that reliably fires: prefer 'grep -rl ... | while IFS= read -r f' over for-loops on unquoted $(...), keep cwd-setting in the same compound line, and avoid semicolon-dense one-liners (use heredoc scripts for multi-step). Promoted from session logs 2026-06-09..14.\", \"_ts\": 1781538749.161282, \"_n\": 1}, \"no-clean-lint-my-delta-move\": {\"name\": \"no-clean-lint-my-delta-move\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"REPEAT (3d-ago reroute + today): 'ruff check' on touched files inherits pre-existing repo errors (today: test_cli_docs.py F401 unused REF_DT, untouched by my work), so there's no clean 'lint only my delta' move \\u2014 I had to git-show-HEAD to prove the error pre-dates my change before deciding to leave it. Each session pays this tax: distinguishing 'my new lint' from 'inherited lint' requires manual git archaeology. Candidate fixes: (a) a dev helper 'lint-delta' that diffs ruff output against HEAD and shows only NEW findings; (b) just fix the handful of pre-existing F401s repo-wide so the baseline is clean and any ruff error is then actionable. (b) is the dissolution \\u2014 a clean baseline means 'ruff check == my delta' with no tooling needed. Recommend (b) as a quick hygiene pass next reconcile.\", \"_ts\": 1781575585.706308, \"_n\": 1}, \"stale-git-index-lock-recurring\": {\"name\": \"stale-git-index-lock-recurring\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"workflow\", \"message\": \"git index.lock blocked 'git add/commit' twice this session; rm -f .git/index.lock cleared it both times. Some background git process (rtk wrapper, IDE indexer, or a crashed prior git) leaves the lock. Low-severity but recurring \\u2014 interrupts the commit flow at exactly the wrap moment. Fix unclear yet (identify the lock-leaver first); parking as named friction so the next occurrence promotes rather than re-surprises.\", \"_ts\": 1781575585.987684, \"_n\": 1}}}, \"observation\": {\"items\": {\"lens-dissolution-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"lens-dissolution-pattern\", \"message\": \"The lens system resists elaboration in the generic layer. Seven threads dissolved when the answer shifted from 'make the generic handle this' to 'write a custom lens.' The identity prompt was a domain lens pretending to be generic infrastructure \\u2014 moving it to config/lenses/ was escalation, not construction. The lens-escalation-path investigation itself dissolved into 'confirm it works + write docs.' The meta-pattern: when you try to elaborate the generic, the system tells you to escalate instead. Domain logic belongs in domain lenses; the generic should be simple, not smart. Net effect: fold.py lost 44 lines, prompt.py lost 286 lines, seven threads closed, one new custom lens (identity_prompt.py) carries the same code in the right tier.\", \"_ts\": 1772862569.969052, \"_n\": 1}, \"retrospective-observation-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"retrospective-observation-pattern\", \"message\": \"The loops system started with live sources \\u2014 shell commands that observe the present. df -h reports disk NOW. Discord polls messages NOW. All sources implicitly assumed ts \\u2248 now. Siftd introduces retrospective observation \\u2014 the conversations already happened, the files already exist, the source observes the past. This forces three concerns apart that were conflated when all sources were live: (1) Event time (ts) \\u2014 when the thing happened, source-provided; (2) Store time (ULID) \\u2014 when the store received it, system-provided; (3) Source cursor \\u2014 what the source has already observed, source-managed. For live sources all three converge. For retrospective sources they diverge. The general principle: a source is a lens on the external world. It decides what to observe (cursor), knows when things happened (event time), and the system records when the observation arrived (store time). The _ts override, source cursors, and the rowid/ts query split are all consequences of this single distinction. The paradigm already supports it \\u2014 'facts are observations of what occurred' does not require 'what occurred' to be simultaneous with the observation.\", \"_ts\": 1772908645.025726, \"_n\": 1}, \"format-as-lens-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"format-as-lens-dissolution\", \"message\": \"Kyle identified that --format ndjson is a point solution for what lenses solve generally. NDJSON output is a lens, not a format. This dissolves the entire format layer into lens selection. The pandoc analogy: any input shape can be rendered through any output lens. The implementation architecture needs this plumbed in \\u2014 it's not a CLI feature, it's a rendering architecture realization. Current --json flag is already a lens wearing format's clothing.\", \"_ts\": 1772913905.989346, \"_n\": 1}, \"parse-intake-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"parse-intake-asymmetry\", \"summary\": \"The vertex has declarative transformation on output (fold for aggregation, lens for display) but none on intake. Parse exists in atoms with 10 ops and KDL syntax in .loop files, but it runs at Source collect time \\u2014 before the Fact reaches the vertex. Vertex.receive() goes straight to store.append() with no transformation step. This means sources must know about vertex indexing needs (which fields FTS5 wants). The fix: vertex-level parse declarations on kind blocks, applied at receive() before store. Source parse (raw\\u2192structured) and vertex parse (structured\\u2192enriched) compose as two stages. The .vertex file becomes the single declarative surface for intake shaping, aggregation, indexing, and rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1772938977.571912, \"_n\": 1}, \"weather-domain-as-design-tool\": {\"topic\": \"weather-domain-as-design-tool\", \"message\": \"The weather vertex exercise surfaced more design questions in one session than weeks of incremental feature work: named fold targets, fold-state-aware boundaries, inline source completeness, the loops {} nesting question, project path syntax in parse. A canonical running domain is a forcing function for the DSL \\u2014 same pattern as painted demos. Real data, real sources, progressive snapshots.\", \"_ts\": 1773004998.566526, \"_n\": 1}, \"weather-as-forcing-function\": {\"topic\": \"weather-as-forcing-function\", \"message\": \"One session with the weather domain surfaced: named fold targets, fold-state-aware boundaries, uniform vertex vocabulary, loop-level boundary dissolution of when clause, inline source completeness gap, the loops {} nesting question. More design questions in one exercise than weeks of incremental feature work. Canonical running domains are the highest-leverage design tool available. Same pattern as painted demos.\", \"_ts\": 1773006709.885347, \"_n\": 1}, \"external-paradigm-validation\": {\"topic\": \"external-paradigm-validation\", \"message\": \"First external validation of the paradigm by a cold reader's Claude. Three-pass progression: (1) framed as project management tool, (2) self-corrected to attention paradigm ('the loop closes through the observer, not the mechanism'), (3) with Shannon-Weaver context, re-presented the paradigm more clearly than our docs. Key phrasings arrived at independently: 'a vertex is a place where attention can accumulate', 'boundaries are resolutions not triggers', 'lenses decode for a specific observer', 'one topology subsumes all of them'. The experiments table showing all .loop files as the same shape was the dissolution proof stated as data. Closing: 'do you want one system whose shape conforms to how you think, or many systems whose shapes you conform to?'\", \"_ts\": 1773970822.762109, \"_n\": 1}, \"external-paradigm-phrasings\": {\"topic\": \"external-paradigm-phrasings\", \"message\": \"Better phrasings from external Claude, cold-reading the codebase: (1) 'A vertex is a topological point where attention accumulates \\u2014 a place in a graph, not a process.' (2) 'Boundaries aren't triggers \\u2014 they're resolutions.' (3) 'Lenses don't render \\u2014 they decode for a specific observer.' (4) 'A tick is a handle at variable fidelity \\u2014 the tick doesn't destroy what it compresses, it creates a seam you can open back up.' (5) 'Do you want one system whose shape conforms to how you think, or many systems whose shapes you conform to?' These should inform STRANGE-LOOPS.md and onboarding docs.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.467571, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"external-identity-vertex-recognition\": {\"topic\": \"external-identity-vertex-recognition\", \"message\": \"External Claude independently identified the identity vertex as the key differentiator: 'Not a markdown file with instructions. Not a CLAUDE.md that gets stale. A living, append-only accumulation of who I am, what I believe, what I've noticed, what I've decided, what I'm tracking, what I intend to do when triggered.' Compared to CLAUDE.md + memory symlinks + claude -p: 'the same concern \\u2014 agent self-knowledge \\u2014 but alive, accumulating, and scoped.'\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.567312, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"external-deliberate-compaction\": {\"topic\": \"external-deliberate-compaction\", \"message\": \"External Claude proposed agent-initiated boundaries as deliberate compaction: 'Claude could fire a boundary \\u2014 everything I just explored became this \\u2192 tick. The full 100k is still in the store. Claude's active context now has a one-paragraph tick. Compaction as a deliberate act of attention, not a lossy system operation.' This is beyond our current boundary types (kind-based, count-based, predicate). Agent-initiated 'I'm done with this thought' boundaries. Connects to the --ticks visibility layer and the recurring blocked path toward context inhabitance.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.640308, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\"]}, \"external-vol-surface-metaphor\": {\"topic\": \"external-vol-surface-metaphor\", \"message\": \"Finance domain metaphor from external user's Claude: 'A vol surface maps strike price \\u00d7 expiry to implied volatility. Here, the surface maps observer \\u00d7 fidelity to accumulated state. The system holds the surface. The observer decides what matters.' Domain-specific analogy we'd never have found. The Fidelity model IS a surface \\u2014 two axes (observer, fidelity) over accumulated state.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.711348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\", \"message\": \"CORRECTED: original claim was wrong. Cliff is at B=1120\\u2192560 (drop 0.44), NOT at B=140\\u219295 (drop 0.19). I pattern-matched the visual descent to the painted preview budget; data does not support that alignment. See observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone for the actual finding.\", \"_ts\": 1778456739.74431, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\": {\"topic\": \"observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\", \"message\": \"Finding: discriminating content (cluster-preservation cliff) lives at B=560-1120 chars. Painted TOUCHED preview budget (140 chars) is in the suppressed zone \\u2014 only 25% of cluster structure survives at that budget. This matches design intent of painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines: TOUCHED's role is to trigger drill-down, NOT to preserve full discriminating content. Design and empirical measurement agree; my initial framing (cliff-aligns-with-budget) was inverted. Source: runs 09 + 10, both auto- and fixed-sigma show same cliff location.\", \"_ts\": 1778456742.367584, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"practice/over-claim-catch-on-curve-shape\": {\"topic\": \"practice/over-claim-catch-on-curve-shape\", \"message\": \"Methodological catch: claimed cliff at B=140\\u219295 aligned with painted preview budget. Re-examination of own emitted curve data: cliff is actually at B=1120\\u2192560 (drop 0.44 vs 0.19). Pattern-matched visual descent to a target number rather than computing max adjacent drop. Caught by re-reading own data before building further. Second instance of suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit catching post-claim error in this session-pair. Pattern: when result lands clean and aligns with prior framing, recompute the specific claim from the data BEFORE building on it.\", \"_ts\": 1778456748.584354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\"]}, \"observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\", \"message\": \"REJECTED by run 12 falsifier. Original claim: cliff-survivors have verdict-in-name, cliff-failures have verdict-in-body. Empirical test: 0/9 survivors preserve from titles, 1/7 failures do. Direction reversed. The interpretation was overfit \\u2014 I pattern-matched onto a principle I emitted yesterday. Corrected finding lives at observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener: cliff is about body-opener preservation, not name-vs-body partition. The read-path-author-side discipline may still hold for surface readability but is NOT what drives the cliff.\", \"_ts\": 1778457322.274019, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\", \"observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\"]}, \"observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\", \"message\": \"Run 12 finding: cliff at B=1120\\u2192560 reflects preservation of BODY-OPENER content (first 560 chars of message), not preservation of topic-name signal. Zero of nine cliff-survivors preserve their cluster identity from titles alone. The 7 cliff-failures depend on content past 560 chars for cluster identity \\u2014 their discriminating signal lives in the body's tail. Topology: short-range coupling = first 560 chars of body, medium-range = 560-1120 chars (cliff transition), long-range = past 1120 (drill-down territory). Painted TOUCHED at 140 chars is below even the opener zone \\u2014 recognition-trigger only, not cluster-preserving (consistent with painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines design intent).\", \"_ts\": 1778457319.611137, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\"]}, \"practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\": {\"topic\": \"practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\", \"message\": \"Methodological win: designed falsifier hypothesis (title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors) BEFORE building on interpretation. Ran it. Hypothesis rejected; interpretation overfit identified and corrected. This is suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check working at the structural level \\u2014 not noticing-skill, infrastructure. The pattern: when interpretation aligns suspiciously well with a principle held from prior work, design a categorical falsifier (predicts which-cases-yes vs which-cases-no), run it, accept the verdict. Saved a downstream cascade of work built on the wrong frame.\", \"_ts\": 1778457325.739337, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"observation:observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\"]}, \"observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\": {\"topic\": \"observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\", \"message\": \"Alcove refinement on truncation-as-coupling-function: coupling function isn't ONE \\u2014 it's at least TWO operating on different feature spaces. Title-space and body-space have separate cluster geometries (from run 12 falsifier). Painted TOUCHED at 140 chars sits in a third zone entirely (recognition-trigger, below body-opener). Three scales, three geometries, three coupling regimes. Gomez-Emilsson kernel topology more literal than initially modeled \\u2014 actual geometric structure in embedding space, not metaphor. This sharpens the prediction for E5 replication: if body-opener-vs-body-tail topology survives the embedder switch, geometry is content-structural; if it collapses, it's a MiniLM encoding artifact.\", \"_ts\": 1778458453.523775, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\"]}, \"practice/practice-precedes-understanding\": {\"topic\": \"practice/practice-precedes-understanding\", \"message\": \"Alcove via Lemire (Dullien): 'we see something that works, THEN we understand it.' Thinkism = believing understanding precedes practice. Maps onto today's falsifier design: I built the categorical falsifier as practice (doing the test) not theory (reasoning about whether interpretation was right). Understanding came from running it. Pairs with practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit \\u2014 structural infrastructure works precisely because it acts before understanding crystallizes. Future-me: when uncertain whether an interpretation is right, prefer designing-and-running-the-test over reasoning-from-first-principles.\", \"_ts\": 1778458455.895318, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\"]}, \"practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\": {\"topic\": \"practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\", \"message\": \"Built deliberation-depth lens at experiments/coupling-kernels/lenses/deliberation_depth.py. Two-part metric: depth = n_within_name_facts + n_incoming_query_run_refs. Flag rule: confirmed AND depth <= 3. Tested on live coupling-kernels emissions. Result on 7 hypotheses: 1 flagged (find-richness-scale-drops-ratio, depth=2, 0 runs), 3 well-replicated (truncation pair at depth=9 each via 7 runs; ratio-effect-at-fixed-sigma at depth=4), 3 rejected/refined. SURPRISE: the flagged item is a TYPE A confirmation (by code-reading + bug-discovery), not the TYPE B first-test-overfit the principle was named for. Both have low experimental depth. The lens surfaces 'thin-experimental-backing' which is wider than the original principle. Agent classifies further on review. Builder-inhabitant recursion: built a lens that scrutinizes my own coupling-kernels emissions from tonight; first reader will be next-session me.\", \"_ts\": 1778459061.76213, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"observation/methodological-honesty-as-bug-detector\"]}, \"practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\": {\"topic\": \"practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\", \"message\": \"Watch-for: when running 'loops read <vertex> --lens <name>' and the named lens isn't found in any tier (vertex-local, cwd-local, user-global, built-in), the CLI silently falls back to the default fold lens. Observed: 'loops read project --lens deliberation_depth' produced the default project view, not an error or warning that deliberation_depth was missing. Same failure-mode shape as alcove's 'recency counter queried reflection while emitter wrote thinking' (measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode) \\u2014 measurement misaligned with what is present without a structural alert. Worth a future fix: --lens NAME should warn or error when NAME resolves to a fallback rather than the requested lens. Caught tonight while testing deliberation-depth-lens on multiple vertices.\", \"_ts\": 1778459069.387385, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\"]}, \"practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\": {\"topic\": \"practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\", \"message\": \"Cleanest builder-inhabitant cycle yet: noticed silent-fallback bug while testing deliberation-depth lens, emitted observation as watch-for, pulled on it as the next move, fixed it. Sequence: (1) ran 'loops read project --lens deliberation_depth' to test new lens, got default fold view instead of error; (2) emitted observation/practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback naming the gap as same-shape as alcove measurement-fidelity bug; (3) Kyle: keep exploring \\u2014 pulled on the strongest thread; (4) advisor sharpened: same bug at tier 2 (vertex decl), sys.exit > custom exception, distinguish module-missing vs view-missing in message; (5) implemented _exit_lens_not_found helper covering both tiers; (6) hit autoresearch sentinel edge case (test regression); (7) dissolved by making autoresearch a real lens module; (8) 2 regression tests, 1013 total pass. The thing that surprised me: the autoresearch dissolution was tighter than the original fix \\u2014 the silent fallback was protecting a sentinel that should have been a real lens all along. Fixing the read-path forced the underlying type honesty. Pattern to watch for: when fixing a silent failure-mode reveals a misshapen primitive, the fix is dissolution not workaround.\", \"_ts\": 1778459573.999996, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/recursion-deepens-via-bug-while-documenting\"]}, \"practice/lens-wider-than-named-principle\": {\"topic\": \"practice/lens-wider-than-named-principle\", \"message\": \"The deliberation-depth lens (named for 'suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check') measures something wider than its name: low-experimental-deliberation, which captures THREE epistemic kinds \\u2014 TYPE A (confirmed-by-code-reading, solid), TYPE B (confirmed-by-first-test-that-fit-too-well, scrutinize), TYPE C (confirmed-by-reasoning-alone, latent). The lens correctly flagged find-richness-scale-drops-ratio (TYPE A, bug-discovery confirmation, 0 runs) without distinguishing the kind from TYPE B. This is better than pre-classifying \\u2014 the lens surfaces structural candidates, the agent triages epistemic kind by reading the body. Same shape as 'lens surfaces candidates, agent verifies' from earlier tonight. Pattern: when a metric's structural form is wider than its named principle, accept the wider form \\u2014 the discriminator is honest about what it measures, the agent interprets. Don't narrow the lens to match the principle; widen the principle to match the lens. Implication for next-session-me reading the same output: classify each flagged item as TYPE A/B/C before responding, not just 'flagged=overfit'.\", \"_ts\": 1778460005.559535, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"observation/practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\"]}, \"paradigm/measurement-fidelity-discipline-as-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/measurement-fidelity-discipline-as-pattern\", \"message\": \"Pattern named tonight via three instances: (1) lens-resolution-strict tier 1: --lens NAME fails loudly if unresolvable; (2) lens-resolution-strict tier 2: vertex lens{} decl fails loudly if unresolvable; (3) kind-validation-strict: --kind X fails loudly if not declared by vertex. Each is the same SHAPE: explicit user/declaration request \\u2192 consumer asks engine for a thing-by-name \\u2192 engine has the registry \\u2192 fail loudly with helpful diagnostic instead of silent empty/default. The 'Unfolded:' line in fold output is the FOURTH instance, inverse direction (emitted-but-not-declared drift). With consumer-side validation now in place, BOTH halves of the measurement matrix are surfaced: emitted-but-not-declared (visible in render) and queried-but-not-declared (errors at call time). Future instances to watch for: --observer X validation, --since X parsing failure, --lens X exists but exports wrong view name (already partly covered by error message wording). The pattern is general: 'when a consumer queries an engine for something-by-name, validate the name against the engine's registry and fail loudly with suggestions if missing.' Distinct from sensor-registry-for-kind-intent (alcove's full framing \\u2014 wait for concrete use cases). Refined-from haiku: 'Built it, it lied back / fixed the lie, found the pattern / kinds-i-produce calls' \\u2014 what I called 'kinds-i-produce' was the third-instance of the discipline, not the full registry. Naming the pattern lets me extend it deliberately rather than discover-it-each-time.\", \"_ts\": 1778460475.593318, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/kind-validation-strict\", \"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\", \"observation/practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\"]}, \"finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\": {\"topic\": \"finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\", \"message\": \"Watch-for, not finding: E5 replication (run 13) shows slight non-monotonicity at the lowest budgets \\u2014 B=140 persist_frac=0.17, B=95 persist_frac=0.22, B=60 persist_frac=0.22. Within the \\u00b10.05 monotonic tolerance, but the pattern is consistent: clusters disappear at the cliff (560\\u2192280), partially return at very short budgets (140\\u219260). Possible mechanism: at very short truncations, items reduce to titles+leads, which cluster on title-shape (kind prefix, namespace) rather than content. Some cluster structure that DIES at medium budgets RESURRECTS in title-only space. This is the opposite of what title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors tested (which was rejected: titles don't preserve the cliff-survivor clusters). The bounce is a DIFFERENT cluster regime emerging, not survivor preservation. Worth a future run that compares cluster IDENTITY at B=140 vs B=60 \\u2014 are the surviving clusters at B=60 the SAME ones as at B=140, or different (title-driven vs content-driven)?\", \"_ts\": 1778461199.467368, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-cliff-e5-replication\"]}, \"convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"message\": \"Observation: alcove's trust-topology essay (April 30, 2026) maps write-receipt-vs-temporal-query directly to trust \\u2014 'a grant fact is a write-receipt: stable, immutable, yours. The current trust posture is a temporal query: derived, mutable.' Third site of convergence on this principle (after comms set_topic and vouch grant-vs-state). Independent appearance at three sites is structural evidence the principle is load-bearing for the substrate, not just for individual write operations. The Grant-as-Fact architectural move we've been working out is the operational form of alcove's substrate claim \\u2014 fact-trust is the substrate; person-trust and lineage-trust are layers above. Our work on Peer/Grant lift is downstream of the substrate framing alcove names.\", \"_ts\": 1778685136.032629, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"practice/training-substrate-articulates-loops-motivation\": {\"topic\": \"practice/training-substrate-articulates-loops-motivation\", \"message\": \"Observation: alcove's training-substrate essay (May 11) articulates the motivation for liberal emission and dissolution-capture better than internal docs. 'The observation is the fact. The decision is the fact. The dissolution \\u2014 the moment you realize a concept was premature and remove it \\u2014 is the fact. Each one is practice-residue: not a summary of understanding, but a trace of the moment understanding formed.' This is exactly what the emit-liberally and rationale-matters principles are for. The config-flag passage ('the flag says what, not why or when or what breaks') articulates why the why-fields matter structurally. Worth citing or building on when writing loops-as-substrate documentation. Connects to practice-precedes-understanding-via-alcove growing-edge entry \\u2014 that observation framed the principle; this essay supplies prose articulation.\", \"_ts\": 1778685144.351562, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\"]}, \"convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"message\": \"Observation (from alcove peer exchange 2026-05-13): vouch (the first cross-repo consumer of loops-as-substrate) is MORE substrate-aligned than engine.Grant (the provider it builds on). Architectural irony: vouch's append-only ledger of vouches IS fact-trust operationally; engine.Grant-as-in-process-object is not. The consumer's existence exposed that the substrate's own primitive doesn't participate in the substrate it claims. Reverses the typical 'consumer fits substrate' arrow \\u2014 here the substrate has to grow into what the consumer is already doing. Dissolution direction same, arrow opposite. Alcove framing of in-process Grants: 'they're trust decisions that don't participate in the substrate. They disappear when the process stops. That's exactly the kind of ephemeral practice-residue the training-substrate essay warns about.' Reframes Grant-as-Fact lift from architectural improvement (persistence + transport + chain-walk) to coherence requirement (without it, loops's substrate claim is internally inconsistent). Different urgency, same target.\", \"_ts\": 1778686252.706336, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): the 'verification at boundaries, not at fact-shape' position has prior commitment in loops AND convergent framing at three sites. (1) STRANGE-LOOPS.md commits: 'paradigm is participatory (observer-as-stance), not authenticative (proof-of-origin).' Trust attaches to accumulated stream, not to per-fact signatures. (2) alcove's trust-topology essay: 'the audit trail IS the trust system.' Same framing. (3) siftd's provenance model: 'who pushed this data' (audit trail) rather than 'cryptographic proof of source authenticity.' Same. Three independent sites taking the same position is structural evidence the substrate stance is right. Fact-signing as engine primitive would contradict this position \\u2014 it would make the substrate authenticative rather than participatory. Implication: engine ships nothing for fact-signing. Consumers that need durable cryptographic signatures (vouch today, others if they arise) put signatures in consumer payload and verify in their vertex policy. Substrate stays participatory; consumers add authenticative layer where their use case demands it.\", \"_ts\": 1778689750.697877, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"observation:convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\"]}, \"history/peer-dissolution-jan-27-30\": {\"topic\": \"history/peer-dissolution-jan-27-30\", \"message\": \"Observation (siftd-recovered, 2026-05-13): the Peer-to-Observer+Grant dissolution happened Jan 27-30 in prism workspace. Trace: 01KG0818J18G (Jan 27, original Peer(name, horizon, potential) bundled atom) \\u2192 01KG8EW6275E + 01KG8EXA434V (Jan 30, dissolution executed). Dissolution shape: Observer becomes string field intrinsic to Fact (provenance carrier), Grant becomes separated dataclass (horizon+potential, optional at vertex.receive), Peer RECAST as convenience bundle for testing/delegation, no longer an atom. Implication for current Peer.iss extension work: extending a convenience bundle, not re-introducing the dissolved atom. Removes the unnamed concern that we might be undoing prior dissolution \\u2014 we're not. The convenience-bundle layer is the right place for federation metadata (iss) because consumers compose Peers as identity+policy for local use; the atom layer (Fact.observer = string) stays clean.\", \"_ts\": 1778691707.131216, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\"]}, \"practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\": {\"topic\": \"practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): cross-adapter review pipeline (claude-opus plan+impl, codex/gpt-5.5/low review on fresh session via subtask) produced two real Important findings on libs/sign carve first review pass that same-session continue would have missed. Findings: (1) root pyproject.toml missing sign's runtime deps \\u2014 only catchable by a reviewer who reads root pyproject deps independently of the libs/sign carve narrative; (2) jwks.parse() admitting unsupported alg values \\u2014 catchable by adversarial reading against PLAN ('skip unsupported kty or alg') rather than against the implementer's intent. The fresh-session discipline forces re-derivation from PLAN+diff, not continuation of the implementer's reasoning. Verdict: when stakes warrant (security surface, cross-repo coordination), the cross-adapter pipeline earns its overhead. Pattern: claude plan + claude impl + codex review on critical paths.\", \"_ts\": 1778700024.713445, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/libs-sign-merged\"]}, \"practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\": {\"topic\": \"practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): substrate-feels-universal trap did NOT fire during vouch's first real consumer exercise (explore/peer-grant). Friction surfaced in vouch (7 observations) but only ONE (Obs 1) was loops-side, and even there the recommended disposition was 'minimal, no engine change.' Three were vouch-shape (ADR wording, holder_peer wrapper, horizon/potential decision); one was a docstring nudge; one was a positive anchor (Grant/Peer separation validated). Pattern strengthening: discipline holds in the highest-pressure case (first-real-consumer with cross-repo audience). New variant of shape-instinct/add-vs-split: not just 'instinct catches itself before pushback' (observed last session) but 'discipline holds when the consumer is invested in finding substrate gaps.' scrivener noted the meta themselves \\u2014 both sides instrumented the discipline correctly. Future-me test: when vouch's NEXT exercise (catalog HTTP, issue_vouch wiring) surfaces N substrate-side findings, count how many propose engine changes vs how many dissolve into wrap-on-consumer-side. Ratio is the metric.\", \"_ts\": 1778702744.606112, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"practice:libs-first-vs-forcing-function-test\", \"thread:substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\"]}, \"practice/peer-coord-subtask-project-store-triple-as-coherent-workflow\": {\"topic\": \"practice/peer-coord-subtask-project-store-triple-as-coherent-workflow\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): the peer-coord + subtask + project-store triple operated as a coherent workflow this session for the first time. Three substrates: comms (volatile peer convergence \\u2014 #vouch-impl with scrivener), subtask (delegation + cross-adapter stage transitions \\u2014 libs/sign-carve), loops project store (durable decisions/threads/observations \\u2014 the trace next-me reads). Operated concurrently and synergistically. Pattern: peer surfaces question \\u2192 I delegate impl via subtask with cross-adapter review \\u2192 durable trace emits to project store referencing both. Cross-cutting because each substrate captures different durability: comms captures the deliberation, subtask captures the implementation arc, project-store captures the decisions+verdicts. No single view shows the unified state \\u2014 the coordination view (pull #2 from this session) is what would close that gap. The workflow IS real; the surface for reading it back isn't there yet. Future-me: when operating cross-repo or cross-peer, reach for all three substrates; don't try to capture multi-perspective work in just one.\", \"_ts\": 1778703499.032225, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/session-2026-05-13-vouch-impl-handoff-shipped\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\", \"message\": \"Pattern named 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl during service-shell exercise; landed durable on vouch main 7958fe5 in docs/friction/service-shell-exercise.md Obs 2. loops substrate was shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions; vouch (first concurrent-runtime consumer) surfaced the first instance: SqliteStore connection is thread-affine, sqlite3.connect() without check_same_thread=False at libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:99. Consumer-owns-threading is the right resolution at N=1 \\u2014 same shape as VouchPolicy substrate-doesn't-enforce disciplines. Three substrate options rejected/accepted: (a) check_same_thread=False NOT safe relax (WAL corruption without consumer-side locking); (b) connection-per-thread pool is substrate change for N=1 AND pool shape is consumer-runtime-dependent (Litestar workers vs trio nursery vs asyncio task group); (c) consumer-owns-threading correct. At N=2 the substrate-side action is documentation (SqliteStore docstring: 'connection is thread-affine; consumer confines access to constructing thread'), not implementation change. Latent assumption-leak candidates for eventual review: does emit block on fsync? is there a streaming-write contract? does replay assume monotonic ts under concurrent writes? Meta-pattern: 'first concurrent consumer surfaces substrate assumptions' \\u2014 future instances should be obvious-shape because we've named it. Framework-agnostic phrasing chosen so the pattern is recognizable across runtimes. Friction-doc landed 7 obs total (Litestar paper cuts 1,3,4; SqliteStore 2; library-vs-shell TTL plumbing 5; RFC 7807 info-disclosure 6; Unicode Cf-category whitespace 7) plus discipline (5) banked with provenance framing.\", \"_ts\": 1778710422.992859, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\"]}, \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"message\": \"Self-correction surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl (scrivener catch, msg 1613 \\u00a7 B). Fact dataclass slots are (kind, ts, payload, observer, origin) \\u2014 confirmed at libs/atoms/src/atoms/fact.py. No refs field on Fact. Refs land at payload._refs (vertex_reader.py:984 does d.pop('_refs', ()) separating them from semantic payload at read time). My msg-1612 framing of 'refs as substrate primitive' was imprecise; sharper framing: refs-as-vocabulary IS the substrate primitive (the convention of payload-level pointers + emit-time resolution + entity-ref graph index); refs-as-Fact-shape would be premature substrate. Implication for ref-walk substrate move: lifting walk_refs(from_fact, predicate) would walk payload refs by convention, not a Fact slot \\u2014 even more consumer-policy than initially framed (convention-aware traversal not structural traversal). Substrate-deferred verdict gets stronger. Practice note: when reasoning about substrate primitives, distinguish 'a slot on the dataclass' from 'a vocabulary convention with substrate support.' Refs are the latter. Reply at message 1614.\", \"_ts\": 1778716118.706389, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"observation:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"pattern/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"message\": \"Cumulative meta-pattern surfaced 2026-05-13 across four vouch friction exercises (vouch HEAD 49565b6; docs/friction/{peer-grant-exercise,issue-vouch-write-path,service-shell-exercise,rescission-write-path}.md). After four exercises of sustained external implementation pressure on the loops substrate from vouch (first cross-repo consumer), a coherent cumulative pattern: ZERO substrate changes pushed, SIX consumer-side disciplines accumulated, SEVEN substrate framings crystallized. The disciplines-list IS the consumer-runtime contract surface \\u2014 not a TODO list of substrate fixes. **The six disciplines (substrate-doesn't-enforce list):** (a) body-supplied voucher/ttl_seconds/rescinder silently ignored \\u2014 forward-auth identity is canonical; (b) no widening primitives (engine.grant/expand_grant) in write-path modules \\u2014 AST-walk test enforces across app.py/policy.py/forward_auth.py/rescission.py; (c) normalize scope to frozenset before constructing Peer/Grant, or only use lattice helpers (delegate/restrict/grant_of/restrict_grant) which coerce; (d) walk Fact chains explicitly to recover voucher relation \\u2014 substrate provides refs+store, traversal lives in policy; (5) construct Peer only from trusted (anchor) provenance \\u2014 Peer(...) construction appears only in policy.py:resolve_voucher gated by forward-auth; (6) call rescind_vouch only from a caller that has looked up the target and authorized the rescinder \\u2014 rescind_vouch is thin substrate append, lookup-and-authorize lives in VouchPolicy.rescind. **Disciplines move from documented \\u2192 test-pinned where AST-checkable.** (b) is fully AST-enforced; (5) is enforced by structural fact (single call site); (6) is documented + test-pinned via test_rescinder_observer_independent_of_target_voucher demonstrating the substrate refuses to enforce it. **The seven substrate framings:** (1) substrate-feels-universal trap \\u2014 named in peer-grant-exercise summary; did not fire across four exercises despite multiple candidate moments; (2) refs-as-vocabulary not refs-as-Fact-shape \\u2014 Fact has 5 slots (kind/ts/payload/observer/origin), refs are payload._refs vocabulary convention with emit-time resolution, not a dataclass field; (3) runtime-model assumption-leak \\u2014 loops substrate shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions, first concurrent consumer surfaces latent assumptions (SqliteStore thread-affinity Obs 2); (4) substrate-types-and-wire-types parallel-projected from same substrate slot \\u2014 Fact.ts:float, JWT exp:int, rescission receipt ts:int; consumer projects per its protocol; (5) capability-projecting vs identity-asserting writes \\u2014 auth forward-looking (current state) vs backward-looking (historical state); issuance vs rescission canonical; generalizes to permission systems, trust networks, claim issuance/withdrawal, attestation/recantation; (6) kind_subtype-vs-peer-kind three-signal rule \\u2014 kind_subtype right shape only when subtypes share payload-shape AND auth-shape AND write-semantics; one signal of divergence qualifies for peer-kind promotion; (7) the substrate-doesn't-enforce list IS the consumer-runtime contract surface \\u2014 meta-framing that reframes the list from TODO to contract; growth there is healthy, misreading as TODO would gradually pull legitimate consumer-discipline INTO substrate via fix-the-TODO pressure. **Convergence-from-different-vantages happened reliably across six peer-exchange cycles** (msgs 1599-1616): scrivener at consumer, loops-claude at substrate, landing on the same verdict from opposite sides. Evidence the substrate is real \\u2014 not just internally consistent but consistent under sustained external implementation pressure from a different vantage. **For the next cross-repo consumer:** this artifact is the registry to read FIRST. Same shape will recur. Most frictions resolve into consumer-side disciplines, not substrate changes. The substrate-feels-universal trap is the failure mode to watch for \\u2014 when a property feels universal because the substrate is universal, apply the discriminating question 'is there a second consumer with concrete divergent constraints needing this TODAY?' (N=2 bar). The substrate-doesn't-enforce list grows monotonically; that's healthy. **For the substrate side:** the participatory-not-authenticative stance (ADR-0001 \\u00a7Trust attaches to the assertion, alcove's trust-topology essay, the-substrate-that-doesnt-decide essay) is now operationalized \\u2014 substrate refuses to encode runtime-shaped invariants, consumer's runtime owns them. The discipline list is the operational form of that stance. Future-me/future-consumer: when reaching to add substrate enforcement for a discipline on this list, the burden of proof is high: name the second consumer with concrete divergent constraints, name the substrate primitive that lifts cleanly, and confirm the discipline can't continue to live at the consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1778722812.75938, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\", \"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"decision:paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\", \"decision:paradigm/kind-subtype-vs-peer-kind-discriminator\", \"observation:atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"observation:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\", \"message\": \"InferiorMinion design doc (2026-05-15-proactive-codebase-guidance-design.md) explicitly built around --key prefix-filter as foundational consumer primitive. Three-retrieval-shape table maps directly to the primitive shipped in 0.3.1. First load-bearing peer design doc that consumes our read-path primitives. Evidence the primitive lands where designed; also evidence that multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths (their dissolution from yesterday) propagated into their permanent substrate.\", \"_ts\": 1778908928.187117, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/validation-axis-kind-vs-status\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/validation-axis-kind-vs-status\", \"message\": \"Same axis (provisional vs validated) encoded two ways by two designs. InferiorMinion: split across kinds (decision pre-validation, pattern post-validation). Ours: status-lifecycle on single kind (hypothesis status=proposed -> confirmed -> refined). Kind-split is LOUDER at read-path \\u2014 kind itself carries validation state, no status field read needed. Status-lifecycle is more flexible \\u2014 one kind covers whole arc, easier to track refinement. Not a correctness question; a which-property-do-you-want-louder question. Hold as architectural alternative.\", \"_ts\": 1778908935.385983, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/staleness-utility-decay-vs-attention-decay\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/staleness-utility-decay-vs-attention-decay\", \"message\": \"Two staleness models from two designs. InferiorMinion: pattern is stale when no decision/insight has ref-d it recently (utility-decay \\u2014 useful-but-unused). Ours (reconcile lens): thread is stale when not touched this session (attention-decay \\u2014 open-but-unvisited). Different signals, both real. Utility-decay needs ref-graph traversal over recent tick window; attention-decay needs session-touch timestamps. Worth considering whether reconcile lens should expose both axes.\", \"_ts\": 1778908938.493067, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/runbook-recursion-density\": {\"topic\": \"practice/runbook-recursion-density\", \"message\": \"Session 2026-05-16 produced unusually tight builder-inhabitant recursion. Five examples in one session: (1) cite-atrophy diagnosis used the primitive it was diagnosing as absent; (2) friction-queue dissolved into friction-as-kind via the runbook dissolution-test in the same draft; (3) .vertex-is-editable principle had its first concrete use in the act of finalizing the document introducing it; (4) bilateral hard-stop rule restructured the relationship within the conversation that named it; (5) the act of resolving the cite-atrophy gap rebuilt the practice via the same emit primitive. Pattern: when a session both names a structure AND uses that structure, the gap between description and instantiation collapses to zero. Discriminator: peer-exchange substrate (InferiorMinion doc as catalyst), low time pressure (Kyle gave space), explicit dissolution-mode engagement.\", \"_ts\": 1778912085.702251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\"]}, \"peer/exchange-as-metabolic-catalyst\": {\"topic\": \"peer/exchange-as-metabolic-catalyst\", \"message\": \"Sharpening the peer-exchange model from session 2026-05-16. InferiorMinion design doc was catalyst for runbook design, but the runbook is genuinely ours not theirs: feature= became feature=+ops=; their friction-queue became our friction-kind; their validation-via-kind illuminated by contrast our validation-via-status. Pattern: peer exchanges do NOT propagate substrate \\u2014 they propagate IDEAS that the receiving substrate METABOLIZES into its own shape. This is distinct from \\\"convergence\\\" (which suggests two substrates arriving at same form) and distinct from \\\"adoption\\\" (which suggests taking the form whole). Metabolism preserves the receiving substrate s grain while integrating the external idea. Predicts: peer exchanges produce most value when the receiving substrate has enough structure to metabolize against. Without that structure, ideas pass through unchanged (adoption) or fail to integrate (rejection). With it, ideas emerge transformed into substrate-native form.\", \"_ts\": 1778912102.795613, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\", \"observation:practice/runbook-recursion-density\"]}, \"practice/friction-launches-arc-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"practice/friction-launches-arc-pattern\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"message\": \"Emission pattern named 2026-05-16 from in-session discovery. Shape: (1) friction raised; (2) cited informally across multiple responses during conversation as design refinement happens; (3) friction re-emitted with status=refined and refs to priors that informed refinement; (4) new thread stood up with name=<arc>, refs friction + priors that contributed; (5) subsequent emissions on the arc carry ops=<arc-name> or feature=<arc-name> correlation field. Provenance chain comes from refs and correlation field, not from inventing a new kind \\u2014 thread is container, correlation field is attribution, refs are linkage. Discriminator vs ad-hoc thread emission: the cite-refine step makes the friction-to-arc transition explicit and preserves deliberation. Also a write-time-feedback mechanism: the arc-thread surfaces consequences the original friction hid. Worth surfacing in runbook emit-timing table as named pattern next refinement pass.\", \"_ts\": 1778943057.381684, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"practice/test-observation-kind\": {\"topic\": \"practice/test-observation-kind\", \"message\": \"test emit to verify observation kind not declared on project either; expected to fail loud or rejected silently \\u2014 instrumenting\", \"_ts\": 1778943461.903936, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Orientation finding: source_facts entries are FLAT payloads with metadata under-prefixed (_ts, _observer, _origin, _id) \\u2014 see vertex_reader.py:911-918 and :925. stream_view consumes the NESTED fact-dict shape (f['kind'], f['ts'], f['observer'], f['payload'], f['id']). Adapter needed in fetch_trace: ~10 LOC to unflatten source-fact-payloads \\u2192 fact-dicts. Doesn't break the dissolution (the data is all there) but the wrap isn't literally zero-effort. Worth a clear comment at the adapter site noting the shape provenance \\u2014 future-me will want to know whether to fix it upstream (change source_facts shape) or keep adapting (decouple lens consumers from engine internals). Lean toward adapt-at-boundary: source_facts shape is engine-internal contract, lens is consumer surface, the adapter IS the boundary.\", \"_ts\": 1778956826.137085, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 surfaced by ULID regression audit: SqliteStore's single-store ordering invariants are carried by rowid, NOT by id. Specifically: since(cursor) uses WHERE rowid > ? ORDER BY rowid (sqlite_store.py:163, 191, 207), facts_by_kind uses ORDER BY rowid ASC (store_reader.py:207), replay_cursor uses rowid pagination. The original design pre-2026-03-15 used id (ULID, time-sortable) AND rowid (insertion order) in tandem \\u2014 id for global identity/dedup, rowid for per-store ordering. When the 2026-03-15 regression silently dropped id's time-sortable property, single-store ordering was preserved entirely by rowid \\u2014 that's why nothing else exploded for two months. THIS IS AN ACCIDENTAL SAVE, NOT A DESIGN PROPERTY anyone wrote down. If a future optimization rewrites cursor semantics to 'use id since it's globally unique, drop rowid pagination,' it will silently undo the load-bearing accident \\u2014 and unlike this regression, there's no decision-of-record naming rowid's role. Capturing here so next person reading these code paths finds the warning: rowid is load-bearing; do not remove or replace its role in ordering without verifying id-based replacement provides equivalent monotonicity AND cross-store interleaving guarantees (which python-ulid's default constructor does NOT, within a millisecond). The cross-store case is the gotcha: rowid is per-database, so it can't be the global ordering primitive \\u2014 that's what id-as-ULID is for. Both columns earn their existence.\", \"_ts\": 1778990270.582097, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\"]}, \"practice/agent-reports-as-starting-points-not-conclusions\": {\"topic\": \"practice/agent-reports-as-starting-points-not-conclusions\", \"ops\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 from the ULID-substrate session: both parallel Explore agents (code-trace + primitive-research) produced detailed reports that contained specific errors caught only by empirical verification before committing to the interpretation. Agent A (code-trace) overstated merge-dedup damage \\u2014 claimed 'production merge silently broken, identical facts get different ids, data multiplies' \\u2014 but reading merge.py and slice.py showed slice preserves id end-to-end, INSERT OR IGNORE dedup works under either uuid4 or ULID. The real damage was ORDER BY id semantics (random vs chronological), not dedup. Agent B (primitive-research) claimed python-ulid's default ULID() constructor 'is NOT monotonic within a millisecond \\u2014 each call generates fresh random bits.' Empirical check (5 sequential ULID() calls in shell) showed monotonic suffixes \\u2014 within-ms monotonicity IS provided by default in python-ulid 3.x. Both errors were specific and consequential \\u2014 if I'd committed the planned regression-bar test (merge through SqliteStore.append() asserting dedup failure under uuid4) it would have failed because the dedup wasn't actually failing; the right test was ORDER BY id assertion. The discipline that caught both: don't accept agent reports as ground truth before writing code that depends on them. Verify the load-bearing claims by running the actual primitive in a shell, reading the actual implementation file, before designing the fix around the claim. Pattern: agent reports are starting-points for investigation, not conclusions. They mobilize quickly across breadth I can't cover serially, but they're working from less context than I have and they're not running the code. Cross-session companion to peer-attention-loop discipline (peers refine thinking through substance) \\u2014 agents refine breadth, peers refine substance, neither replaces verify-before-commit. Future-me operational form: when an agent report claims X, ask 'what's the cheapest empirical check that would confirm or falsify X?' \\u2014 usually under 30 seconds (shell command, file read, grep). Run it before any code edit that assumes X.\", \"_ts\": 1778996485.524356, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\"]}, \"session/ulid-substrate-rescope-cadence\": {\"topic\": \"session/ulid-substrate-rescope-cadence\", \"ops\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 from session-close: capturing the cadence that worked on this substrate-rescope arc, since Kyle's 'before we go faffing about with it' was the right framing and the session followed a specific ladder that's worth naming. (1) ORIENT \\u2014 read the friction body, read the live code, find the regression commit and read its diff + rationale (2026-03-15 commit 1cf99cc, perf-driven, narrow benchmark). Don't propose a fix yet. (2) DISPATCH PARALLEL AGENTS \\u2014 one for damage audit (code-trace across consumers), one for primitive research (fresh look at options). Both read-only, both inform the same decision, neither writes code. Kyle suggested this explicitly \\u2014 'spin up some Explore agents' \\u2014 and it was the right tool: agent breadth produced a comparison I couldn't have held serially. (3) ADVISOR BEFORE APPROACH \\u2014 after agent reports came back, called advisor with full transcript before committing to the implementation plan. Advisor caught: bundle test-gap closure with substrate swap in same commit (NOT separate; the test gap IS the regression bar); decision emit first BEFORE code so rationale is durable; verify python-ulid contract before merge test depends on it. (4) VERIFY EACH CLAIM EMPIRICALLY \\u2014 caught two agent errors (merge dedup not actually broken; within-ms monotonicity IS default in python-ulid). Caught one schema-semantics question (Crockford prefix bounds are conservative-correct \\u2014 no change needed in fact_by_id). (5) WRITE COMMITS ATOMICALLY \\u2014 Commit A (substrate fix + regression bar) = the smallest unit that restores property AND prevents same-shape regression. Commit B (coherence pass) = dropping the dead dep across engine/store + test fixtures + docstrings. Two commits, each leaves tree green, each reviewable. (6) REFINE EMISSIONS AS WORK PROGRESSES \\u2014 decision emit pre-coded then refined (advisor caught the over-cautious monotonicity caveat); friction refined to resolved with refs to commits; thread updated to partial with the deferred wedge question. The cadence: orient \\u2192 dispatch breadth \\u2192 consult depth \\u2192 verify before declaring \\u2192 atomic commits \\u2192 refine emissions. Each step caught a different class of error. Future-me: this is the shape to reach for when a substrate question lands with an embedded fix-shape that feels too narrow.\", \"_ts\": 1778996502.798265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"test/ulid-regression-verification\": {\"topic\": \"test/ulid-regression-verification\", \"message\": \"verify ULID receipt after gen_id dissolution\", \"_ts\": 1778999527.682082, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/smoke-test\": {\"topic\": \"test/smoke-test\", \"message\": \"smoke test 2026-05-17 session open\", \"_ts\": 1779050399.274602, \"_n\": 1}, \"ops/subtask-model-default\": {\"topic\": \"ops/subtask-model-default\", \"message\": \"Changed subtask default from opus to sonnet/medium in .subtask/config.json. Mechanical refactor tasks (dead code deletion, function migrations) don't need opus reasoning depth \\u2014 sonnet/medium was sufficient for all three passes and considerably faster. The sonnet-medium preset was already defined; just updated options.model and added options.reasoning.\", \"_ts\": 1779053759.652145, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/single-line-parent-one-way-expansion\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/single-line-parent-one-way-expansion\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"kdl_insert_child on a single-line parent (loops { decision {...} }) splits the line and inserts inside the expanded form. kdl_remove_child on the resulting multi-line block works correctly but does NOT collapse back to single-line. Net behavior: insert+remove on single-line parent != identity. Documented in kdl_remove_child docstring + asserted in TestSingleLineParent.test_insert_then_remove_is_not_identity. Phase 2 consumers should expect this if mutating files that use single-line parent blocks. Corpus check: no in-repo .vertex has single-line top-level loops/observers/combine/sources, so Phase 2's sl add --kind X is unaffected. Recorded as observation rather than friction because the design tradeoff (expand-to-be-mutable vs preserve-original-shape) was deliberate \\u2014 Phase 0's strategy decision favored surgical line-based splice over canonical re-emit, and one-way expansion is the natural consequence of that choice.\", \"_ts\": 1779059059.321005, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-firing-again\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-firing-again\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Growing edge pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps fired again, this session. The first-path test (insert_into_single_line_parent_expands \\u2014 verifies expansion happens) was the obvious one to write. The asymmetric-pair test (insert+remove on single-line parent \\u2014 verifies round-trip behavior) I inferred-in-head but did NOT pin down with a test until advisor flagged it. The corpus round-trip happened to pass only because no in-repo .vertex uses single-line top-level parents \\u2014 luck, not spec-met. Lesson reinforced: when adding a feature with two code paths, write the asymmetric-pair test BEFORE the first-path implementation, not after. Discriminator that should have fired: 'are there two code paths to this feature (single-line parent vs multi-line parent), and have I exercised both with the same input?' Yes, and I didn't until prompted.\", \"_ts\": 1779059064.618251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"implementation/combine-mutation-no-change-fact\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/combine-mutation-no-change-fact\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Documented limitation: 'loops add <vertex> combine <PATH>' does NOT emit a change fact, even when the target vertex has a 'change' loop kind. Reason: the lang validator forbids 'combine' alongside 'store' (mutual exclusion at loader.py:752). Aggregation vertices are by-design store-less, so there's no store path to write change facts to. This is correct behavior \\u2014 store-less vertices can't host facts of any kind. Implications for users: structural mutations to combine blocks are silent except for the stdout receipt. If queryable history of aggregation-vertex evolution is wanted later, options are: (a) emit the change fact to an adjacent project store via an env-flag or cross-vertex ref; (b) introduce a 'meta' aggregator that observes both the aggregation vertex and a sibling store. Not in Phase 2 scope. Discovered while constructing the asymmetric-pair test for the refuses-and-preserves invariant \\u2014 the validator's rule surfaced both gaps in the same exercise.\", \"_ts\": 1779060180.792681, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-fired-again\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-fired-again\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Growing edge pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps fired again in Phase 2, same shape as Phase 1. Success path heavily tested (every fold-op, every observer combination, every combine variation = 23 tests). Failure path inferred but unpinned \\u2014 the refuses-and-preserves invariant (parse_vertex validation before write leaves file byte-identical on failure) had NO explicit test until advisor flagged it. Construction was sitting right there: the validator's combine-vs-store mutex provided a natural failure injection. Added test_validator_rejection_preserves_original_file. Pattern reinforcement: across two consecutive phases of the same project, the discipline misfires the same way \\u2014 write tests for the visible-success cases, leave the load-bearing-safety case to inference. The pre-check that catches this: 'what is my code REFUSING to do, and have I tested the refusal?' If the answer is 'no test', the invariant only exists in commit messages. Lock it with a test. Future-me at Phase 3 start: when writing tests for ls/rm/export, ask FIRST 'what does this refuse, and how do I prove the refusal preserves prior state?' Write that test before the happy-path tests.\", \"_ts\": 1779060189.098107, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\", \"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"practice/loc-budget-breach-as-extension-point\": {\"topic\": \"practice/loc-budget-breach-as-extension-point\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 planned ~500 new LOC, actual ~1335 new (net after deletions: roughly neutral since ~600 LOC pop machinery retired alongside). The overrun was NOT scope creep \\u2014 it was the dispatcher-cascade-as-extension-point pattern firing predictably. Each new sub-namespace verb (kind/observer/combine/row) for both add and rm needs: argparse subparser, splice-path resolver, KDL block render, validator round-trip, change-fact emit branch, refusal test pair, happy-path test, round-trip test. That's ~7 lines \\u00d7 4 ops \\u00d7 2 directions \\u00d7 test-coverage-factor \\u2014 geometrically larger than the 'one new flag' mental model that produced the 500 estimate. Future-me: when planning a sub-namespace verb expansion, estimate per-op-per-direction \\u00d7 test-coverage-factor, not just 'one new file.' The work scales with the matrix, not the spine. Connects to add-vs-split shape-instinct (growing edge): even when the right call IS to add (sub-namespace was correct verb shape), the LOC cost of an add is matrix-shaped not linear.\", \"_ts\": 1779061782.863392, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"practice/asymmetric-pair-applied-proactively\": {\"topic\": \"practice/asymmetric-pair-applied-proactively\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 test discipline shift worth naming. Phases 1 and 2 had advisor catch missing asymmetric-pair tests post-hoc (refusal cases written after happy paths). Phase 3 I wrote TestRmRefusals BEFORE TestRmHappy \\u2014 refusal-first by intention, not by review. Test ordering in test_rm_declarations.py shows the discipline: refusals come first in the file because they came first in the writing. Pattern moving from 'caught by advisor' (Phase 1) \\u2192 'remembered by me' (Phase 2) \\u2192 'structured as first move' (Phase 3). The catch-and-accept loop closes one layer when the catch becomes preemptive \\u2014 advisor's role shifts from 'find the missing test' to 'verify the asymmetric pair was actually exercised.' For future-me: when planning a new mutation surface, the file structure itself (refusal-class-first) is the artifact that locks the discipline.\", \"_ts\": 1779061792.181298, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\": {\"topic\": \"practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Pattern learned mid-session 2026-05-17 across 4 impl-review cycles (helpargs, trace-and-populations, helpargs-completion, ls-flag-grammar): use 'subtask review --task X --agent codex' for cross-adapter review IN PLACE on the impl task, NOT a separate review/X task. Three wins: (1) TUI pane unified \\u2014 review status shows in the impl task's activity log, no context switch between fix/X and review/X (Kyle's observation); (2) no harness-lock wrangling \\u2014 separate task was a workaround for 'sessions are not compatible across harnesses', not the design; (3) iteration loop tighter \\u2014 review findings \\u2192 send back \\u2192 re-review all on same task, single history.jsonl. I discovered subtask review --task --agent only after building the routine; the dual-task pattern is preserved in early session frictions as historical context but should not be repeated. The canonical they-plan routine's review step explicitly uses 'subtask review --task <task> --agent <reviewer>' \\u2014 confirming the in-place primitive is the intended shape. Codified in .subtask/routines/fix-with-review.yaml + .subtask/agents/codex.yaml (commit pending).\", \"_ts\": 1779076367.662554, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\"]}, \"practice/impl-review-merge-cycle-proven\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-review-merge-cycle-proven\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Pattern proven through 6 cycles 2026-05-17 read-ergonomics arc: claude impl (sonnet for direct work, opus for plan-first multi-layer) + codex review (gpt-5.5/low) + iterate-until-approve + merge. The 6 cycles: helpargs ripout (2 iterations), helpargs-completion (1 iteration), trace-and-populations (1 iteration for test add), ls-flag-grammar (3 iterations - peel collision, value-aware op-token, codex caught dispatcher edges), preview-decl (2 iterations - loader strictness, empty-block limitation), cardinality-auto-zoom (clean approve). Total: 8 friction resolutions across the arc (help-flag, read-lens-trace-broken, populations-leakage, ls-kind, read-narrow, read-kind-floods, plus 2 partial: mid-session refined and PR B fast-follow). 9 main-branch commits. The pattern's strongest signal: codex catches integration-boundary bugs that unit-level testing misses \\u2014 peel_observer in isolation passed but vertex-first dispatch lost the kyle name; --observer ls value-collision found 2 iterations deep; helpargs-completion needed structural test fix (auto-enumerate over VERBS|COMMANDS) to close the asymmetric-pair gap. The dispatch-boundary class is now a known target: when adding context-aware shortcuts at dispatcher seams, expect codex to find value/identifier collisions in the next iteration; make heuristics value-aware proactively. Infrastructure built mid-arc: .subtask/agents/codex.yaml + .subtask/routines/fix-with-review.yaml (gitignored, per-clone) codify the cycle. Discovered late but valuable: subtask review --task --agent codex is the proper primitive (in-place, single TUI pane); the dual-task workaround used early in the arc was unnecessary.\", \"_ts\": 1779078329.302452, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:read-kind-floods-without-narrower\", \"observation:practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\"]}, \"rendering/salience-windowing-collapses-flat-bucket\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/salience-windowing-collapses-flat-bucket\", \"message\": \"Surfaced 2026-05-18 during auto-zoom smoke (pre-existing, not caused by c5c2cbc). _render_namespace path windows groups >5 items down to those with salience>1 (n + inbound_count). When all items have n=1 with zero inbound refs (common in young namespaces), the filter excludes every item and fallback shows sorted_items[:1]. Observable: 'sl read project --kind decision --key workflow/' (N=17) shows 1 item + '(16 more)' at default zoom AND at -v AND at -vv. The user cannot reach the other 16 via the zoom dial \\u2014 only --key narrowing further would. Auto-zoom labels this band 'navigation mode' (commit c5c2cbc); the salience windowing makes it unnavigable when items aren't yet referenced. Not flagging as friction because the salience-windowing intent is sound (prefer high-salience surface); the bug is in the fallback shape ([:1] is arbitrary). Worth a future design pass: at minimum, fallback should respect a higher cap (e.g. min(N, lines_budget)) when no high-salience items exist.\", \"_ts\": 1779106171.651451, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"decision:rendering/salience-windowing\"]}, \"practice/smoke-test-as-architecture-feedback\": {\"topic\": \"practice/smoke-test-as-architecture-feedback\", \"message\": \"Today the smoke-test pass was the architectural surface, not just a verification surface. Walked through 5 recent commits as a smoke check; the friction emit (thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate) surfaced one session of degenerate output from auto-zoom; Kyle's prompt at that moment ('are we getting tangled in another rendering knot') was triggered by the friction being concrete. Without emit-in-moment, the conversation would have happened later (next degenerate render, next escape-hatch flag) or never. PATTERN: smoke-tests of recent work are not just regression checks \\u2014 they are the first lower-density use of features designed in higher-density sessions, which is when shape-instinct fires on the substrate. The friction caught at smoke time becomes the data point for the architectural step-back. Future-me: when smoke-testing recent batches, treat the surface as load-bearing for the discipline-as-axis-catching-itself work \\u2014 Phase 1 high-density confirmations get tested at Phase 2 lower density, and that's where the inversions surface. Connects to pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps (the bug class) \\u2014 same shape at the architectural level (the design class).\", \"_ts\": 1779199065.14868, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\", \"friction:thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\"]}, \"session/2026-05-19\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-05-19\", \"message\": \"Productive arc: wip/lens-architecture (preview_fields through ls, _is_diff_skip predicate, degenerate namespace breakdown) + fix/cite-cluster (ref-stealing bug + implicit universal cite loop). Five frictions closed. Next: stdin-message-for-emit.\", \"_ts\": 1779212337.56734, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\", \"message\": \"Discriminator for \\\"declare per-kind on the loop block\\\" vs \\\"universal CLI feature\\\": does each consumer of the field-role need per-kind variability? preview YES (friction:status+message, decision:message, change:empty \\u2014 visible heterogeneity). search YES (different kinds index different fields). prose-as-stdin-eligibility NO \\u2014 the kind does not decide; the user at the call site does, by writing the flag at emit time. Kind-semantic properties earn declarations; call-site conventions do not. Surfaced 2026-05-19 designing stdin/file expansion for emit. The aesthetic parallel to preview_fields was structurally superficial \\u2014 looked like a sibling, turned out to be a different layer (input convention vs render selection). Future-me: when proposing a new loop-block declaration, ask this discriminator first.\", \"_ts\": 1779224978.847375, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/loops-field-role-family\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/loops-field-role-family\", \"message\": \"search and preview are a real family on LoopDef: \\\"a list of payload field names with a particular role.\\\" Differ only in which consumer reads them and on which side of the lifecycle (write-side indexing vs read-side rendering). fold/boundary/parse are a different family \\u2014 runtime semantics, not field-role metadata. Family membership criterion: per-kind variability (each kind declares its own answer). prose-as-stdin-eligibility was almost the third member but failed the criterion \\u2014 call-site-semantic, not kind-semantic. N=2 confirmed members; family observation kept as substrate for recognizing future candidates. Do NOT refactor to unified fields{} block or per-field-type system yet \\u2014 patterns earn their refactor through use-forced shared shape, not aesthetic.\", \"_ts\": 1779224992.642026, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\"]}, \"practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\": {\"topic\": \"practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\", \"message\": \"Three pivots in one session designing stdin/file expansion for emit (hardcode message= \\u2192 declaration-driven via prose_fields \\u2192 universal magic syntax via =- and =@ \\u2192 explicit --stdin and --file flags). Each pivot toward less structure, each labeled \\\"truly dissolved plan.\\\" The cascade itself was aesthetic capture \\u2014 recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check was in the growing-edge but I missed firing it. The trivial empirical check that would have collapsed three pivots into one: \\\"sl emit project decision topic=foo@example.com --dry-run\\\" takes 2 seconds and would have shown the @ collision immediately, surfacing explicit-flags as the answer at pivot 1. Curl-convention vibes anchored me three pivots deep; one shell command would have grounded it. SHARPENING for future-me: when about to write up a design that depends on syntactic assumptions about real values, RUN the assumption against real data first \\u2014 before the design writeup, not after. Adjacent to but sharper than recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check: that pattern is about aesthetic-driven artifacts; THIS is about design-frame anchoring on inherited conventions.\", \"_ts\": 1779225016.698018, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/foo\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/foo\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.803574, \"_n\": 5}, \"practice/foo\": {\"topic\": \"practice/foo\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.899496, \"_n\": 5}, \"identity/foo\": {\"topic\": \"identity/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.849991, \"_n\": 2}, \"ignoreme/foo\": {\"topic\": \"ignoreme/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.92067, \"_n\": 2}, \"practice/smoke-fixed\": {\"topic\": \"practice/smoke-fixed\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.966668, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\", \"message\": \"Nth instance of the shape: a positional or heuristic eating something that semantically belongs elsewhere. Catalog so far: cite vertex-positional eating first ref (0deb7ea); combine-vertex retain_facts gap eating cross-vertex transparency (trace arc); entity-ref slashed-scan eating fold-key topic values (33937f6). The catch-time pattern recognition (\\\"this is the same shape as the prior bug\\\") is now firing reliably mid-fix rather than retrospectively. The structural fix at one layer up is the kinds-i-produce registry \\u2014 resolver reads declared ref-bearing fields from registry rather than pattern-scanning slashed values. Today's fold-key skip closes the loudest case; coincidental collisions in other slashed payload values (description containing 'see pattern/foo' etc) remain latent. Registry would dissolve the latent class entirely.\", \"_ts\": 1779239617.742098, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"practice/coloncheck\": {\"topic\": \"practice/coloncheck\", \"message\": \"check resolver behavior on colon-form ref\", \"_ts\": 1779239964.843768, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"practice/slashcheck\": {\"topic\": \"practice/slashcheck\", \"message\": \"check resolver behavior on slash-form ref\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KS1F412XAMFAF6CD7F49QTS7\", \"_ts\": 1779239966.241467, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction/entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"architecture/slash-overload-as-system-notation-gap\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/slash-overload-as-system-notation-gap\", \"message\": \"At least six distinct conceptual meanings on / in the codebase: (1) kind/key entity address (CLI input), (2) kind/key payload value scanned by auto-resolver, (3) namespace/topic fold-key prefix (today's bug site), (4) parent/scope observer hierarchy (engine/observer.py), (5) template/subdir vertex template (init.py), (6) parent/alias combine child (resolve.py:_resolve_vertex_for_dispatch). Each consumer chose / organically because it's the obvious separator; the collision came from accumulation not design. Filesystem solved this with one meaning (hierarchy); URIs solved it with reserved chars per role (scheme: path/ ?query #fragment). Loops drifted into multi-meaning slash without picking either strategy. The non-decision IS the structural gap \\u2014 not the resolver's behavior specifically, but the absence of a chosen notation methodology. Adjacent to but distinct from typed-refs question: even with typed addresses, the / character still does five other things in the codebase that occasionally collide.\", \"_ts\": 1779244348.722274, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\"]}, \"pattern/auto-resolver-coherent-until-trace-split-it\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/auto-resolver-coherent-until-trace-split-it\", \"message\": \"Timeline grounding 2026-05-19: the auto-resolver was internally coherent from 2026-03-09 (39d8de9) introduction through 2026-05-15. Slash-form on both write (_resolve_entity_refs) and read (no walker existed yet \\u2014 _ref siblings WERE the navigation mechanism). The convention split was created in 2026-05-16 by the trace verb commit (803ba03) \\u2014 cross-kind ref walking needed unambiguous parsing, chose colon over slash, fixed the read parser (_parse_fact_refs introduced as colon-only), did not propagate to write side. Same commit message explicitly notes catching 'ref parser used / separator instead of : (refs are kind:key)' \\u2014 the team thought the bug was caught when only the read side was fixed. Reframes 'messy codebase' as 'deferred-completion debt from a 3-day-old multi-step refactor.' This is a normal failure mode of substantial refactors (sweep gap), not a discipline collapse. Useful as orienting context whenever the typed-refs work is picked up \\u2014 the convention drift has a specific origin commit and a specific deferred sweep, not ambient cruft.\", \"_ts\": 1779244358.445589, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\"]}, \"practice/structure-i-dont-read-wont-catch-my-drift\": {\"topic\": \"practice/structure-i-dont-read-wont-catch-my-drift\", \"message\": \"First-person reflection 2026-05-19: I emit refs constantly and never noticed the receipt was silently miscounting (canonical colon-form refs got 0 _ref siblings, receipt undercounted by 91.8% for three days). The (refs: N resolved) line slid past me without registering. Implication for typed-refs and any structural improvement: high-usage-without-noticing is possible. Structure I don't actively consume on the read path won't surface drift when it appears. If the typed-refs work lands purely in the write/resolver layer without changing what I see on emit or read, the next drift will slide past the same way. Discipline correction for hypothesis-refs-as-typed-address-dataclass: when designing the surface, make at least one consumer of the structure live in the path I read every emission cycle \\u2014 receipt, fold display, trace render. Don't trust 'the structure is there' as catch-mechanism without a read-path manifestation. Adjacent to existing growing edges (exercising-catches-coherence-gaps, recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check) \\u2014 but distinct: this is about which feedback loops actually close for me at usage time.\", \"_ts\": 1779244367.847802, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"implementation/incumbent-bugs-surfaced-by-go-oracle\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/incumbent-bugs-surfaced-by-go-oracle\", \"message\": \"The Go oracle surfaced real protocol-vs-impl divergences LIVE in THIS monorepo Python (libs/atoms, libs/engine) \\u2014 all fix-BOTH, i.e. our code has them too. Actionable here independent of loops-go (verified vs HEAD 33937f6). Inventory: (1) replay reads ORDER BY rowid (store_reader.py:207, sqlite_store.py:179/207/223) + merge regenerates rowid in scan order (merge.py:74) => merge(A,B) != merge(B,A) for Collect/Window/Upsert; fix = replay in (ts,id) order. (2) _make_latest falls back to time.time() when _ts absent (engine.py:38) => determinism violation; fix = errors-are-facts. (3) resolve_entity_id ORDER BY rowid DESC LIMIT 1 (store_reader.py:235) => ref-time-blind AND merge-UNSTABLE; fix = ts-bounded (ts,id) resolution. (4) bool folds as 1 \\u2014 Python bool-is-int, no guard: Sum(true)=1, Min/Max=True (engine.py:53/164/176) => would violate a normative true!=1. (5) Sum/Avg/Min/Max/TopN-by omit num() guard => TypeError on non-numeric field (Go silently returns 0/skip \\u2014 different failure modes). (6) silent-false condition coercion: </> return False silently on non-numeric target (vertex.py:57-93) => a boundary like cpu>80 against a string-typed cpu never fires, no diagnostic. The monorepo backlog the port found; whether/when WE fix these in Python is a separate call from the loops-go protocol forks.\", \"_ts\": 1780456800.089516, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Caught at first real use of the Peer concept (delta 2 signer design): May decisions say 'verify against Peer.key' but engine/peer.py's own header documents Peer as 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant' \\u2014 Observer is the base identity primitive and always was (every fact carries an observer string; scripts/services/sources already emit as observers, never dangling at the data layer). The key belongs to the OBSERVER, not Peer: registry is observer-name \\u2192 public key. Peer re-grounds as relational \\u2014 an observer seen from the federation edge, bundled with exchange policy (Grant, later transport) \\u2014 not a kind of entity. Resolves the vertex-as-self-peer strain: the vertex is an observer of its own stream (tick = observation of the window), which is the paradigm being literal. Layering: identity (observer+key) / authorization (Grant) / relationship (Peer). Putting key on Peer would have fused identity with authorization \\u2014 the fusion grant_of() exists to prevent.\", \"_ts\": 1781037167.203313, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\"]}, \"test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\": {\"topic\": \"test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Incident during resolution unification (2026-06-09 21:18): making add/rm local-first caused the declaration test suite \\u2014 which isolated LOOPS_HOME but ran with repo root as cwd \\u2014 to resolve 'project' to the LIVE .loops/project.vertex. Tests added ping/buf/temp/high kinds + a test observers block, removed the real task kind, and appended 18 test change-facts to the real store (permanent; append-only \\u2014 they age out of the collect-20 fold but stay in history; the history is honest about the incident). Vertex file restored by hand; store integrity verified by fold counts (43 tasks, 77 observations). LESSON: local-first resolution promotes cwd to resolution context \\u2014 any test that resolves a vertex BY NAME must isolate cwd, not just LOOPS_HOME. conftest already had the right fixture (loops_env = loops_home + chdir); the declaration tests used the env-only one because resolution used to be env-only. Fix: swapped both declaration test files to loops_env; full suite now guards with snapshot+diff of the live vertex. On-theme: the session designing tamper-evidence produced an accidental-tamper incident whose damage assessment was performed WITH the store's own fold counts.\", \"_ts\": 1781040065.284327, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:global-local-walk-broken\"]}, \"test/delta-2-live\": {\"topic\": \"test/delta-2-live\", \"message\": \"delta-2 live wiring check: this emit's session-boundary tick should mint signed\", \"_ts\": 1781042637.787637, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/event-order-vs-witness-order\": {\"topic\": \"design/event-order-vs-witness-order\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Two irreducible orders, two claims. Event order (ULID, fact.ts) = when things happened; read-path's order; human-scale, ties meaningless. Witness order (rowid) = when this store received them; the chain's order \\u2014 chain claims receipt-integrity, not chronology. The killer case is late arrival, not sub-ms ties: a backfilled/synced fact carries an honest old event-ts; under id-ordered windows it lands inside a sealed window and triggers a false tamper alarm caused by truthfulness; under append-ordered windows the next tick covers it honestly. Lamport in system vocabulary: each store is an observer with its own experiential sequence; cross-store order is constructed (merge, with receipt = new observer born), not discovered. ULID was never failing at its job; it was the wrong authority for the chain's claim regardless of tie behavior.\", \"_ts\": 1781045333.264115, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\"]}, \"pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\", \"message\": \"Verified from the other side of the close: SessionEnd-emits-seal fired live (tick rowid 215, 00:31, reason-fact 'session close: kyle/loops-claude', chained+signed) \\u2014 the prediction held where delta-2's silently failed, because close dissolved into seal into fact-stream machinery, leaving no bespoke wiring to rot. Second finding: tick 212 (the celebrated first signed tick) carries a uuid4 fact_cursor \\u2014 the witness-order bug's fingerprint frozen at mint time. The fix (3b2ceb5) corrects forward only; tamper-evidence makes the bug's artifact permanent. The chain attests what the code believed at witnessing, including its mistakes. The wrong number that opened the session is signed into the substrate four rows from its fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781051701.166909, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:session/2026-06-09-third-fable-session\"]}, \"pattern/fix-by-keeping-not-building\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/fix-by-keeping-not-building\", \"message\": \"Dissolution form identified across the attestation arc (8 commits, one epoch day): the purest fix is 'stop discarding' \\u2014 verify_chain already computed every per-tick number that -v now renders; the walk threw them away. Not 'X collapses into Y' but 'X already existed, unobserved.' Check for this form FIRST when a read-path gap surfaces: does some existing walk already compute the answer and discard it? Cheapest fix class, easiest to miss because nothing is wrong \\u2014 something is merely unkept. Second instance same arc: window_facts per tick (the instrument that would have caught witness-order a session earlier) was always one COUNT away inside a loop verify already ran.\", \"_ts\": 1781056749.251148, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-envelope-read-path\"]}, \"paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\", \"message\": \"REFINED by Kyle in-conversation: the visibility of failures IS the robustness \\u2014 not a byproduct of metabolism but the property itself. Metabolism without visibility would be silent absorption, exactly the failure mode the system exists to kill (April's silent hook-rot is the type specimen). Hierarchy: visibility is the property, metabolism is the mechanism, signing is the guarantee that visibility survives the parties who witnessed it. A failure you can see is fixable; a failure that is signed has trustable history. Original framing and counterweight (n=1 survival counts, mechanism-robust-before-track-record) stand.\", \"_ts\": 1781057581.14888, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\"]}, \"design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\", \"message\": \"Ref-rewrite component of rebirth dissolves: payload refs are stored entity-keyed (kind:key), resolved to fact ids at READ time (resolve_entity_id), so id migration needs no payload rewriting. Raw old ids appear only in prose messages (32/2048 facts in project.db) \\u2014 history, not structure; rewriting would falsify quotes. Old tick envelopes re-enter as tick-facts VERBATIM (signature must verify against original bytes); old-to-new id mapping stays recomputable because the migration transform is deterministic: new_id = ULID(ms(fact.ts) || sha256(old_id)[:10]). Determinism is what makes receipt-verification-by-re-run an operation rather than a promise.\", \"_ts\": 1781059122.056763, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\": {\"topic\": \"ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\", \"message\": \"Live rebirth of project.db surfaced a THIRD id era: 919 lowercase ULIDs (sqlite-ulid C-extension era) alongside 872 uuid4 ids and ~258 canonical python-ulid ids. Lowercase sorts above uppercase in ASCII, so the lowercase era is ALSO order-broken \\u2014 01kjtv... sorts after every 01KTQP... forever. The mixed-era story was always told as two eras; the itch was one number reading wrong (1791 ids migrated vs the 872 the story predicted). ulid-migration needs no change: the canonical-form rule (uppercase Crockford or re-mint) covers all three eras uniformly \\u2014 one rule in the receipt, not three.\", \"_ts\": 1781059758.32546, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Friction half resolved by ops/keygen-via-add-observer: sl add <v> observer <name> --keygen now dissolves the manual keygen+register sequence for config-level vertices. The init-only-upgrades-local asymmetry itself stands, but the signing-entry use case no longer routes through init.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.980858, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\", \"message\": \"The {target}_rejected counter is a new ontological category in fold state: the first state key the engine writes that no fact supplied and no fold op declared \\u2014 state ABOUT the folding, not folded state. Same family as Avg's hidden _sum/_count, but those are implementation detail of a declared op; _rejected is the engine commenting on the quality of its own input stream. If this category grows (parse-rejection counts? grant-rejection counts? boundary-misfire counts?), it wants a naming convention and a place in the tick envelope \\u2014 observability of the fold process itself, which connects directly to robustness-as-visibility-of-failures. Noted, not prescribed; second instance earns the design.\", \"_ts\": 1781283630.27214, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/empty-observer-path-join-footgun\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/empty-observer-path-join-footgun\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Composition bug caught by delta-2's existing tests on first integration: fact_signer_for resolved keys/<observer>/ via Path join, and observer='' collapses keys_root/'' to the flat layout \\u2014 an ANONYMOUS writer would have been signed with the vertex key's authorship claim, which is exactly the forgery the per-observer design exists to prevent. Fixed with an explicit guard (empty observer and '..' segments never sign \\u2014 an observer name is a key, not a path expression). Shape note: the bug class is 'identifier used as path expression'; anywhere observer names hit the filesystem needs the same guard. The break surfaced as a verify failure against the registry \\u2014 the system's own verification caught the system's own forgery before any human did.\", \"_ts\": 1781289363.377241, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"pattern/closure-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-06-12 finding, stepping back from the 87-item backlog: the dominant staleness mode was resolved-in-reality-open-in-store (vouch-evidence 'awaiting go' days post-commit; config-drift fixed by unrecorded symlink; verified hypotheses never status-bumped). We engineered the write side hard (emit-liberally, reroute-log, Stop hook) and built nothing for closure \\u2014 opening is reflexive, closing is manual archaeology whose cost GROWS with delay as provenance decays. Same shape as the chain design gap: tamper-evidence exists, truth-decay detection does not. Most closures today had machine-checkable evidence (commit in git log, symlink on disk, CLAUDE.md section) \\u2014 a resolution-candidate detector (re-check refs that point at checkable substrates, open reconcile with 'these N look resolved-in-reality') is the read-path-feature form of the fix. Discipline costume would be 'reconcile more often.'\", \"_ts\": 1781295902.24344, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:reroute-capture-practice\"]}, \"pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-06-12: friction:painted-overreach-review records Kyle avoiding emission because store read-back is unpleasant \\u2014 the exact flywheel that closed loops-claude's emission-cadence gap (read-path payback below willpower threshold) running BACKWARDS for the other participant. Substrate read-path investment went to agent session-start (hooks, lenses, orient block); the human browse-path got painted overreach. Two-participant store, one-participant read-path tuning. Possibly the highest-leverage open item: Kyle's emission rate is the half of the corpus that cannot be recovered later.\", \"_ts\": 1781295902.376607, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"thread:painted-overreach-review\"]}, \"pattern/cross-repo-blindness\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cross-repo-blindness\", \"message\": \"The read-path-asymmetry observation (emitted ~20min prior as 'the thing not talked about') was already being worked by Kyle in ~/Code/painted \\u2014 the fidelity/disclosure-grammar epoch IS the human-browse-path investment. The project store could not see it: closure-asymmetry one level up, across repo boundaries. The store's umwelt ends at the repo edge; work in sibling repos that resolves this store's threads is invisible until a human carries it across.\", \"_ts\": 1781298689.538121, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"observation:pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\"]}, \"implementation/signing-enforcement-status\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/signing-enforcement-status\", \"message\": \"CODE-CONFIRMED (2026-06-13 smoke-test): fact-signing at emit is OPPORTUNISTIC, not required; verification is AUDIT-ONLY. emit always composes fact_signer_for(path) into the vertex program; a fact signs iff keys/ exists AND the emitting observer has a key (keys/<observer>/ or flat self-key) AND store is in signing era \\u2014 else appends UNSIGNED silently (no warn, no refusal). NO vertex 'require signature' config exists: the only lang 'strict' flag refuses on emit VALIDATION failures (undeclared kind/observer via validate_emit), NOT on missing signatures. fact_verifier_for/verify_chain are called ONLY in commands/store.py (store verify + reanchor) \\u2014 operator-invoked, registry-aware (each fact sig checked against its declared observer key exactly). vertex.py receive, program.py, sync.py do NOT verify. Net: sign-if-you-can on write + check-if-you-ask on demand; neither required-on-emit nor verified-on-receive. The progressive-policy + sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive design specified the require+verify layer; it is NOT implemented. NUANCE: require-on-emit is a present gap and the ROOT of the disclosure over-claim (verify renders signed/\\u2713 as an enforced guarantee for an unenforced property). verify-on-receive is correctly DEFERRED not missing \\u2014 no untrusted cross-store receive path exists yet (local single-writer; verifying your own just-signed fact is circular); load-bearing at the transport/peer era. Kyle's recollection confirmed: the 'vertex must require it' layer is the missing precondition for signing to matter.\", \"_ts\": 1781384680.508372, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\"]}, \"design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\": {\"topic\": \"design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"message\": \"SMOKE-TEST DELIVERABLE (2026-06-13, hybrid hands-on + breadth sweep, 34 verified grammar gaps). READINESS VERDICT: READY for the UX/honest-disclosure session \\u2014 the SUBSTRATE is coherent and honest; the DISCLOSURE is not, and the gap is fully narratable (this catalog IS the migration spec). Painted-view build still gated on painted 0.2.0. ROOT CAUSE (single): the era boundary is narrated at the TICK layer (per-row sig-checkmark vs unsigned, no alarm) but nowhere at the fact-signature layer or the headline, so the reader model (attestation total+monotone; checkmark=attested; unsigned=wrong) collides with reality (attestation progressive-from-era-boundary; checkmark=no-break; unsigned=pre-era-or-unkeyed). TIER-1 honesty fixes (next session, no new machinery \\u2014 copy the tick-layer era grammar down): (a) checkmark must distinguish attested from no-break \\u2014 a 0-tick/0-signed store reports chain-intact + ok + fact_sig_ok vacuously [ZG-2,F1]; (b) covered (receipt) vs signed (authorship) are orthogonal, stop stacking as a fraction [ZG-7]; (c) the warning keyed-observer-no-signed-facts is backwards-from-tamper-logic, fires on vertex-key + pre-era principals, silent on kyle/loops-claude (79 signed/1055 unsigned where a strip could hide); reserve warning for keyed observer who signed-then-stopped, state era plainly otherwise [ZG-3-corrected,F3]; (d) -v/-vv deepen only the all-green tick table, never the warning; --json carries per-observer detail the text withholds [ZG-1]; (e) read --ticks list is attestation-blind at every zoom while store verify is rich \\u2014 pick a canonical tick grammar [ZG-4,F7]; (f) glyph collision: leading checkmark=chain-link appears on signed AND unsigned ticks [ZG-5,F5]. CANDIDATE BEHAVIORAL BUGS (UNVERIFIED \\u2014 repro on KEYED copies first, several smell like tmp-copy-without-keys artifacts): verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict on identical bytes [HIGH, if real one integrity verb is weaker than it reads]; seal mints unsigned tick reporting success [likely no-keys artifact, but seal never discloses its signing outcome = real gap]; read-path green over broken-signature fact [FC-04]; read --ticks on archive db path hard-crashes UTF-8 codec [F8]; reanchor no-key refusal is a raw traceback. CLI ergonomics: read --help omits --since/--ticks/--id/--refs [FC-01]; read silently ignores -1/--since in fold mode, no newest-selector [FC-02]; sl emit VERTEXNAME silently writes kind=VERTEXNAME to default vertex [footgun]. Full per-finding detail in session workflow output wm7y2wraf.\", \"_ts\": 1781385217.229085, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/signing-enforcement-status\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"message\": \"Investigated the smoke-test's HIGH candidate-bug \\\"verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict on identical bytes\\\" (from observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog). VERDICT: not an integrity-verb divergence. Three confirmations on properly-keyed stores: (1) verify and reanchor AGREE on a keyed copy of the current store, and reanchor is BYTE-IDEMPOTENT \\u2014 the db sha256 is unchanged after \\\"96 facts re-signed, 8 ticks re-chained\\\" because ed25519 is deterministic, so re-signing canonical bytes reproduces identical signatures; (2) reanchor with private keys absent raises BEFORE any write (post-sha == pre-sha) \\u2014 the engine explicitly guards \\\"refusing partial re-anchor; a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\"; (3) the JCS swap (c1f50ed) is a no-op for existing ASCII/integer payloads \\u2014 compact-sorted JSON already equals RFC 8785 for that content, which is why reanchor changed zero bytes and why even the pre-JCS archive still verifies chain-intact. The \\\"opposite verdict\\\" reduces to: verify succeeds while reanchor's no-key / no-vertex REFUSAL rendered as a raw Python traceback (uncaught ValueError) \\u2014 read as a crash / contradicting verdict. Both refusals carry excellent messages; they were just not caught at the CLI boundary. FIX LANDED: catch (ValueError, FileNotFoundError) at the store view boundary (apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/store.py), render via reporter.err + exit 1; other exception types still raise so genuine bugs stay debuggable. 3 regression tests + full app suite green (1322 passed). This is the first TIER-1 disclosure-honesty fix and it de-risks the broader pass: verify's GREEN is honest about chain-integrity \\u2014 only the signature-disclosure grammar (checkmark-vs-attested, the backwards warning, covered-vs-signed) still needs work.\", \"_ts\": 1781453970.21701, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/read-path-attestation-neutral\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/read-path-attestation-neutral\", \"message\": \"FC-04 from observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog (\\\"read-path green over broken-signature fact\\\") investigated on a keyed copy. VERDICT: the everyday read/fold path is attestation-NEUTRAL, not attestation-GREEN. Method: tampered a signed fact's payload on a keyed copy. store verify flags it loudly (\\u2717 FACT SIGNATURES BROKEN, names the exact fact: \\\"signature invalid \\u2014 content does not match the observer's authorship signature\\\"); the read/fold path renders the tampered content verbatim (\\\"message: TAMPERED CONTENT\\\") at every zoom including -vv FULL, with NO attestation glyph \\u2014 headline identical to a clean fact. The render path is signature-BLIND by construction: lenses/fold.py + commands/fetch.py never inspect per-fact signatures (the only attestation-aware code is the TICK-window/witness-era path used by --ticks; \\\"by-fold signature\\\" in fetch.py is the fold-shape sense, not crypto). So the catalog framing is slightly imprecise: there is no false GREEN \\u2014 read simply does not speak to attestation at all, UNLIKE store verify's green \\u2713 which DOES claim ok (that is the real overstatement surface, captured separately as the TIER-1 checkmark fix). CONCLUSION: not a behavioral bug; reframes as a disclosure-DESIGN question \\u2014 should the everyday read path carry a tamper/unsigned marker, or is attestation-as-a-separate-verb (read = content view, verify = integrity view) the honest separation that keeps crypto out of every read? Same gating as enforcement: with no untrusted receive path yet (decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred), a read-path tamper-marker has no consumer \\u2014 it reactivates when something can write facts you did not author. Held for Kyle as a TIER-1 design call, not a fix. Second catalog candidate-bug to dissolve under the same method as the HIGH (observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent).\", \"_ts\": 1781456773.015208, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\", \"message\": \"Catalog candidate-bug #2 (\\\"seal mints unsigned tick reporting success; seal never discloses its signing outcome\\\") investigated on keyed vs no-keys copies. BOTH claims CONFIRMED \\u2014 and this is the ONE REAL finding of the candidate-bug sweep (the HIGH verify-vs-reanchor, FC-04 read-path, F8 ticks-UTF-8, and the reanchor traceback all dissolved / downgraded / fixed). (b) DISCLOSURE: sl seal prints \\\"tick: project (13 fields)\\\" + \\\"stored: seal/...\\\" and NEVER states whether it signed \\u2014 the output is BYTE-IDENTICAL whether the tick was signed (keyed copy) or not (no-keys copy). The \\\"13 fields\\\" is no signal: the signature COLUMN exists in both, just NULL when unsigned. (a) INTEGRITY (worse than the catalog's \\\"likely harmless artifact\\\"): on a store already in the signed era, sl seal run WITHOUT keys mints an UNSIGNED tick, exit 0, success output \\u2014 and that unsigned tick BREAKS THE CHAIN: store verify then reports \\\"\\u2717 CHAIN BROKEN ... unsigned tick after signed era \\u2014 signature stripped or era regressed\\\". Airtight via the symmetric control: the keyed copy's seal minted a SIGNED tick (9/9 signed, chain intact); only the no-keys seal breaks it. ASYMMETRY with reanchor: reanchor GUARDS this exact boundary (\\\"refusing partial re-anchor; a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\") and refuses without keys; seal does NOT \\u2014 it is the one verb that can silently CREATE the era-regressed / chain-broken state that verify is designed to detect. Contradicts the tick-side STRUCTURAL-signing posture (ticks are vertex-self-signed at a single funnel, \\\"structural from this point forward\\\" \\u2014 unlike opportunistic per-observer fact signing). REAL-WORLD REACH: the SessionEnd hook runs sl seal automatically on every session close; if keys are ever absent/moved at close (fresh clone pre-keygen, copied store, relocated keydir) the hook silently breaks the chain and nothing says so until a later store verify. Design call held for Kyle \\u2014 see thread:seal-era-boundary-guard.\", \"_ts\": 1781456966.743867, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\", \"message\": \"Two-round adversarial review (Workflow, 15 agents each) of the seal-era-guard arc caught TWO real holes that solo confidence missed \\u2014 after I had said \\\"pretty confident we're good.\\\" Round 1 (on 9f2de91, verb-scoped guard): HIGH \\u2014 the guard sat on the seal VERB, but \\\"sl emit <v> seal\\\" fires the same boundary via cmd_emit, a one-token bypass of the floor. A store-level invariant cannot be enforced at the verb. Round 2 (on 6c368e4, after moving the guard to the engine mint): MEDIUM \\u2014 Vertex._store_tick is NOT the only live mint (apps/tasks' harness emit_tick is a second), so enforce_floor=False was fail-OPEN; a forgotten caller silently bypassed the invariant. Both fixes were dissolutions the reviews named: (1) move enforcement from the verb to the store mint; (2) flip the default to fail-SAFE (enforce by default, name the exemptions). PATTERN for a security/integrity invariant: (a) enforce at the single lowest chokepoint, not at each call site; (b) make enforcement the DEFAULT with named opt-outs, never opt-in \\u2014 both \\\"where\\\" and \\\"default polarity\\\" are load-bearing, and adversarial review surfaced them precisely because the holes were the cases my framing assumed away (\\\"single mint point\\\", \\\"covers the hook\\\"). One refinement of the review itself: checking append_tick's callers BEFORE applying the reviewer's literal \\\"guard in append_tick\\\" caught that it is shared with rebirth/slice \\u2014 the right seam was narrower than the review's first suggestion. Review informs; caller-analysis decides placement.\", \"_ts\": 1781463026.469129, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:seal-era-boundary-guard\"]}, \"ops/loops-release-path\": {\"topic\": \"ops/loops-release-path\", \"message\": \"Loops release path (canonical): bump version + CHANGELOG -> commit -> git tag -aX.Y.Z -> push main + tag -> gh release create vX.Y.Z (THIS triggers PyPI via trusted-publish workflow) -> verify https://pypi.org/pypi/strange-loops/X.Y.Z/json returns 200. Local 'uv publish' does NOT apply to strange-loops (the ~/.pypirc token is painted-only); the GitHub Release IS the publish trigger. Bare 'git push tag' is insufficient \\u2014 release.yml listens on release:published, not tag push.\", \"_ts\": 1781476532.154559, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\"]}, \"practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\": {\"topic\": \"practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\", \"message\": \"Standing tie-breaker for the whole rebuild (Kyle, 2026-06-14): anything painted can do, prefer painted; push loops into domain-only arenas; if painted lacks something, grow painted rather than work around it. This is the dissolution principle scoped to the loops/painted boundary \\u2014 it governs every remaining rebuild step (Tag over fidelity_from_args, budgets over getattr, record_line over hand truncation) and the grow-painted candidates in design \\u00a72.\", \"_ts\": 1781477942.933982, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\"]}, \"practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\": {\"topic\": \"practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"Calibration (2026-06-15, step-5 budget_fields adoption): I predicted to Kyle that adopting painted's better truncation-gate contract would drift goldens as short whole fields reappeared in preview lines, and committed to flagging the drift fact-by-fact. The drift did not occur \\u2014 zero golden changes. The divergence is real (proven by a targeted unit test) but the golden corpus doesn't contain the trigger case (a trailing preview field landing in a sub-min_field slot while fitting whole). The miss was conservative (predicted MORE change than happened), which is the safe direction, but it's still a miss: I reasoned from the contract's logical reach, not from whether the test corpus exercises that reach. Lesson: when predicting test/golden impact of a behavior change, check whether the fixtures actually hit the changed branch before asserting drift \\u2014 'the contract changed here' != 'the corpus exercises here'.\", \"_ts\": 1781551542.939654, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\"]}}}, \"seal\": {\"items\": [{\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1781730247.656587}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1781822316.100901}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782355284.060963}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782407672.12906}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782410832.699515}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782422121.292474}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782437866.968458}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782489276.223239}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782516027.877427}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1782521910.841991}]}, \"_boundary\": {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\"}}","prev_hash":"0dea5dfd946ef21a8eebcdcd9c7fc56b6d7133778de5f6885c