01M08AB1PH9NJNAAKW85D8ZXFK	decision	design/arrival-release-scope	RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; Sol fifth-pass concurrence on convergence). HOW ARRIVAL SHIPS. Three rulings, each an instance of the one-break budget: the persisted store contract breaks ONCE, loudly, on the model actually believed.\n\n=== 1. THE ARRIVAL SUBSTRATE IS 1.0.0 ===\n\nThe one-break budget IS semver-major reasoning, promoted to versioning. Arrival is the 1.0 story; no intermediate store contract ships before it. The interim hazard clock (the live-but-unreachable JSONL merge hazard on main since PR #8) ends when 1.0 lands.\n\n=== 2. MIGRATION IS A SIDECAR, NOT NATIVE — ONE-TIME, NOT SUPPORT-FOREVER ===\n\nNative-forever legacy reading is two open paths alive indefinitely: the two-mode store re-entering through compat, the exact shape four passes removed. The sidecar is the dissolution-complete option — residence.py dies with no survivor. THREE REQUIREMENTS KEEP IT HONEST:\n\n(a) SIDECAR-NESS RELAXES THE MAINTENANCE COMMITMENT, NEVER THE EPISTEMICS. The full migration ruling binds it: receipted like rebirth; exact historical receipt order where reconstructible, an explicit LEGACY-ADOPTION GENESIS MARKER where not (never manufactured precision); idempotent; resumable. Those were release blockers before; they are release blockers for the sidecar. Record by record the contract answers: exact order reconstructible -> migrate exactly; only fact ordering, not custody semantics -> explicit adoption boundary; tick/cursor relationships -> prove preserved or preserve the limitation.\n\n(b) A BRIDGE PINNED AT BOTH ENDS. Last 0.x reader and first arrival writer as frozen, pinned dependencies — uvx-runnable years later for a user arriving from any 0.x. One-time per store, forever-available as a FROZEN ARTIFACT, never a maintained surface.\n\n(c) PROVENANCE LIVES IN THE STORE, NOT THE TOOL. The legacy-adoption genesis receipt in the new arrival log is what makes deleting the tool safe — the store carries its own migration evidence after the sidecar is gone.\n\nONE PERMANENT RESIDUE, named so it is not rediscovered as scope creep: 1.0's store layer keeps a legacy-shape DETECTOR that refuses with teaching, naming the sidecar. A location claim ("this is a 0.x artifact"), never an open-and-read path.\n\n=== 3. THE CLI IS REBUILT FROM SCRATCH AS A THIN WRAPPER OVER THE SDK ===\n\nWith explicit license (Kyle) to DROP any current loops-app-cli concept that does not fit the implementation<->conceptual-model seam. The executable spec is what makes from-scratch safe: conformance vectors, arch rules and the verification pyramid live at engine/SDK level and survive; CLI goldens rebuild against the new surface.\n\nDISSOLVES: residence suffix-as-mode; store verify's byte-prefix custody model (re-specified over arrival, cut D); merge/receive as sqlite operations (admission through drivers); adopt reshapes into lineage genesis ceremony.\nRE-KEYS STRONGER: witness addressing on (lineage, ordinal) — seq:N INVERTS from the most dangerous address form today (a rebuild renames its referent; measured in the merge lab) to the canonical coordinate under arrival.\nORTHOGONAL, CARRIED: fetch->lens->run_cli, the emit grammar, lens/zoom discipline, completion single-source.\n\nThis is decision:design/projection-driver-model's "what the SDK stops asking" cashing out, not new architecture. The burden of proof now sits on IMPLEMENTATION AND MIGRATION; per the reopening bar in thread:admission-disposition, further conceptual review needs a counterexample, not a prettier abstraction.
01M08EQ5YRGR8J5CFEF5HDEK80	thread	arrival-migration-arc	OPENED 2026-08-17. The migration/implementation arc following arrival-substrate convergence. Design rulings so far: classification-as-fact (order verified/asserted/minted + orthogonal signature-era axis), rebirth dissolved into the single re-custody ceremony, --allow-unsigned for keyless migration of signed sources. Context corpus: five-reader briefs + synthesis in session scratchpad c7edea55 (migration-exactness-synthesis.md); census verdict table covers every real store on the machine. NEXT ENTRY POINT (ruled by Kyle): before continuing the sidecar spec, a design session on THE SPECIFICS OF THE ARRIVAL LOG ITSELF — the artifact's concrete format/encoding/genesis shape. Then: sidecar contract spec (must ref 01M070N0 directly — invisible from folded reads), migration verifier adapted from merge-lab tooling (add signed-tick + aggregate arms), one-line memo correction (rowid is ordering authority, not hashed input — verified at sqlite_store.py:157,1510).
01M08J0C1BBJM7NNGKSM1J8JEK	thread	arrival-migration-arc	ARRIVAL-LOG DESIGN SESSION (2026-08-17, Kyle + Fable) — the ruled entry point, substantially advanced. Rulings converged in-session (ratified conversationally; this entry records them for the arc):\n\n1. GRAMMAR DISSOLVES. The arrival log is the EXISTING JSONL codec — fact/tick/batch line shapes unchanged, genesis-first, line position as witness order, tick chain re-based from rowid to line order (spec-text change, not byte change). No new file type, no per-record envelope. Unsealed-span posture accepted: order between seals is asserted by custody, committed by the next seal — seal density is the ruled integrity lever (per admission-disposition). Retroactive win: one interleaved file records the fact/tick interleave _receipt_order had to reconstruct.\n\n2. THE LOG CONTAINS EVERYTHING THAT IS EVIDENCE (Kyle's conception, census-verified against ~/.config/loops + .loops): genesis, declarations (vertex definition INCLUDED — the loops/kinds block already rides as _decl batch lines), observer introductions, grants, assertions, seals. EXCLUDED, exactly four categories: secrets (private keys), code (lenses), transport (driver config/credentials/cursors, store locator), and its own address. The .vertex FILE becomes a folded-out PROJECTION — editable for iteration, re-absorbed via absorb_edit CAS (Edit 2 doctrine applied; observers{} block joins the declaration document set).\n\n3. VERTEX REGISTRATION relocates into the AGGREGATOR'S OWN lineage as first-class facts (membership assertions, admitted like anything else); discover globs degrade from authority to a discovery DRIVER proposing membership candidates — Law 3 verbatim. Cross-lineage topology never enters a member's log (Law 4).\n\n4. GENESIS IS SELF-CERTIFYING. Founding observer-introduction fact carries the pubkey and is signed BY it — TOFU at line 1; attests possession, never identity (signatures attest claims, not external truth; names are lineage-local; cross-lineage identity = vouch arc, deferred). Later observers introduced by facts signed by already-introduced observers; grants/rotations/revocations are ordinary signed facts. Verification becomes POSITION-DEPENDENT against the in-log registry (arrival restatement of internal-table-meta-schema's historized-keys ruling) — fixes today's timeless .vertex registry (retroactive validation + rotation-breaks-history defects) and the Relay cross-vertex unverifiability (thread:cross-vertex-observer-key-reuse's demand "trust decision is itself a fact" satisfied structurally). Keyless genesis stays coherent: --allow-unsigned = no TOFU anchor, era UNSIGNED classification, introduction may open the signed era later.\n\n5. TAINTED-SPAN ruled at decision:design/key-revocation-taint-disposition — default leave-in-place + projection policy; content-destruction = re-custody ceremony, never in-place rebuild.\n\nloops init reshapes into a three-movement genesis ceremony: lineage genesis, declaration absorption, observer introduction — sealed before first ordinary admission; a fresh 1.0 log is self-describing and self-verifying from line 1.\n\nNEXT: review of the full decision chain + consolidated arrival-log shape (in progress this session), then the sidecar spec (must ref 01M070N0 directly), migration verifier, memo correction.
01M08KE19RRFDRAHHHCH2VXPEF	thread	arrival-migration-arc	RATIFICATION UPDATE (Kyle, 2026-08-17 14:32): ruling 4 — SELF-CERTIFYING GENESIS — is now EXPLICITLY RATIFIED (TOFU at line 1, founding introduction self-signed by the key it introduces, attests possession never identity; later observers introduced by already-introduced observers; position-dependent verification against the in-log registry; keyless genesis via --allow-unsigned opens era UNSIGNED). Ruling 3 (registration relocates to aggregator lineage) REOPENED for unpacking at Kyle's direction — not yet ratified. cas(head)-vs-declaration-head and window_hash line-scope queued for discussion this session. DEFERRED from this discussion explicitly: lineage-copy/custodian binding, key-loss/escrow. NEW QUESTION on the table: JSONL as THE store format vs a custom format — gating, since grammar-dissolution ruling 1 rests on it.
01M08KK74KMY6JYFRY014P9G4B	decision	design/arrival-log-format	RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; arrival-log design session). THE ARRIVAL LOG'S PHYSICAL FORMAT IS JSONL — THE EXISTING CODEC.\n\nThe custom-format ideation was run and fails the dissolution test. Grounds: (1) Law 1 removes read performance from the format's requirements — reads execute through derived indexes; the log is parsed only at index build and verify, killing the traditional case for binary. (2) The existing codec's properties are exactly arrival's requirements and are test-pinned: verbatim byte preservation (signatures + migration exactness), one canonical spelling per record (commitment hashes), batch-line atomicity, torn-tail truncation-not-skip, resumable offset indexing, golden fixtures + canonical_audit. A custom format re-derives all of it with fresh bugs. (3) Record-completeness (declared-fold-order #5): JSONL-canonical records are the bindable exchange representation — custody format == exchange format means one representation of canon, no translation layer, no derived-vs-canonical adjacency (Edit 2). Stored bytes ARE committed bytes; CBOR/binary would split storage encoding from the JCS commitment surface so every verify round-trips a translation. (4) Per-record CRC (the one thing binary framing genuinely buys) protects unsealed spans against disk rot — a threat explicitly accepted under the seal-density posture; buying it back via encoding re-litigates that ruling through the side door. (5) Sovereignty as product stance: the entire evidentiary history readable with cat/grep, diffable in git — same property as .vertex fold-out "seeing it directly", at the store level.\n\nTWO ADDITIONS RATIFIED WITH IT: (a) FORMAT-VERSION FIELD IN THE GENESIS FACT — the one-break budget's exit hatch; if binary ever becomes necessary it is a future loud break, detectable at line 1 instead of archaeologically. (b) BLOBS STAY OUT OF THE GRAMMAR — large binary content is sourced/ref'd from facts (content-addressed, by hash) if needed; never inline, never a format argument later.\n\nThis closes grammar-dissolution ruling 1 of the arrival-log session for real: existing JSONL codec, fact/tick/batch shapes, genesis-first, line position as witness order, seal-density integrity posture, format-version at genesis.
01M08MD6Y51BS2RJ8136J5DGFV	decision	design/arrival-cas-two-scopes	RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; arrival-log design session). cas(head) IS CONDITIONAL APPEND ON A KIND-SCOPED WITNESS POSITION, WITH EXACTLY TWO SANCTIONED SCOPES.\n\nThe verb from log-and-index-roles (append->stamp, records_from, cas(head)) is specified: "append this batch iff no record of kind-class K admitted since position N." Two scopes only: K=everything (the ARRIVAL head — transport, backup boundaries) and K=declarations (the DECLARATION head — the absorb ceremony's guard, what _declaration_head_in_txn already does). CAS against the arrival head alone would be spuriously strict for declaration edits: any ordinary admission between fold-out and re-absorb would fail an edit with no actual conflict.\n\nNO PREDICATE GENERALIZATION: "append-if no record matching P" is a query language growing inside the custody boundary; admission stays too dumb to evaluate semantics. Kind-scoping is the entire vocabulary — structural, one indexed lookup in the single-writer transaction.\n\n_decl.* PROMOTES FROM CONVENTION TO CONTRACT-LEVEL NAMESPACE (binds forever under the one-break budget — said out loud). It already exists de facto: _decl.genesis + the frozen *-defined/*-retired edit vocabulary, _meta.own_lineage, _topology. Structural, not semantic: the custodian distinguishes declaration records the way it distinguishes fact lines from tick lines, without knowing what any declaration means. Residue under arrival: _meta.own_lineage moves from store_meta (index-side, derived) into the genesis fact.\n\nFROZEN AT TWO WITH A SHRINK-ONLY BAR: a third scope requires demonstrating a ceremony that is structurally neither ordinary admission nor a declaration edit. The extensibility question dissolved on inspection — every ceremony named in this arc (observer introduction/grant/rotation/revocation, membership edits, epoch/registry mutations) is declaration-shaped, because the observers block and aggregation membership were both ruled into the declaration document set. Ratchet-test pattern applied to the verb surface.\n\nRIDER, forced not chosen — window_hash SCOPE: windows stay FACTS-ONLY under the single interleaved file. Migration exactness decides it: signed history migrates exactly iff committed bytes are unchanged, and historical windows commit to fact rows between id-resolved cursor bounds; including tick lines would change every window input and force re-signing. Nothing lost: window_hash pins fact order, prev_hash pins tick order, fact_cursor pins each tick's position among facts (ties among cursor-sharing ticks break by chain order) — jointly the entire line interleave is committed.
01M08MPF247VX7YR9GZVQK9XB7	thread	arrival-migration-arc	ARTIFACT STOOD UP: "The Arrival Log" — https://claude.ai/code/artifact/a70ab076-a5c0-4d18-96bd-5fb0829a0963 — sibling to The Arrival Substrate memo, laying out the artifact itself: JSONL format ruling + riders, line grammar and (lineage, ordinal) position, contents boundary (four exclusions, .vertex-as-projection), three-movement genesis, position-dependent verification + self-certifying genesis, rotation/revocation/taint two-arm ruling, membership-as-declaration, cas two-scopes + _decl contract namespace, facts-only windows + seal-density posture, migration touchpoints, deferred ledger. Colophon carries all backing fact ids. Carries the memo rowid correction inline (sect. 10). NEXT: sidecar contract spec (ref 01M070N08HX69QAEQ3TRPY72CQ directly).
01M08N9H33H3X06A9ZR9X00V1Q	decision	design/arrival-batch-ordinals	RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; Sol review contract 1). ORDINAL IS PER-RECORD: witness order is line order with batch lines expanding in row order. Forced by the code, not chosen: deserialize_records expands rows in array order and _index_lines INSERTs in that order — each fact in a batch gets its own rowid today, and arrival witness order must be order-isomorphic to legacy rowid order or class (b) migration verification (window hashes recomputed over carried order) breaks; one-ordinal-per-batch would make a migrated store's fact counts and window membership disagree with its own signed history. A batch occupies a CONTIGUOUS ordinal range. Atomicity is an ADMISSION property (the line commits whole or truncates whole), never an addressing property: a read basis may land mid-batch, exactly as a fact-id address can name a mid-ceremony fact today. (lineage, ordinal) addresses a RECORD; the entry (line) is the atomicity unit. Sol's coherent alternative (batch = one custody act = one position) rejected as the new-machinery branch of the dissolution test.
01M08N9H8GT4WQXMPGJN3ADWW4	decision	design/arrival-genesis-bootstrap	RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; Sol review contract 2 — Sol caught a real ordering bug in the first three-movement sequence: lines preceding the key introduction were either unsigned inside a signed lineage or needed a retroactive-verification exception). THE GENESIS FACT IS THE FOUNDING INTRODUCTION. Line 1 (_decl.genesis) carries lineage id, format-version, and the founding PUBLIC KEY, self-signed by that key — the TOFU anchor at ordinal 0. Then the declaration batch, signed by the now-introduced key; then the genesis seal. The three movements become: SELF-CERTIFYING GENESIS, DECLARATION ABSORPTION, SEAL.\n\nVERIFIER RULE, one explicit clause instead of an exception: a key is valid at position N iff introduced at position < N, OR N is the genesis position and the record is self-certifying — SELF-CERTIFICATION IS LEGAL AT ORDINAL 0 AND NOWHERE ELSE. No retroactive verification anywhere.\n\nKeyless genesis unchanged: same line 1, no key field, unsigned, classification era UNSIGNED; a later introduction opens the signed era (that introduction is itself self-certifying-shaped but arrives through ordinary custodian admission, era transition recorded per classification-as-fact).\n\nRIDERS ACCEPTED FROM THE SAME REVIEW PASS: (a) the self-verification claim scopes to CRYPTOGRAPHICALLY self-verifying — TOFU genesis means self-verifying ≠ externally authenticated; names stay lineage-local, identity is the vouch arc. (b) INTERLEAVE UNIQUENESS becomes a stated rule + conformance-vector obligation: a tick's cursor assigns it to the gap immediately after fact F; ticks sharing a gap order by chain; chain continuity (verify_chain) makes assignment monotone — unique total interleave, and a claim that can be falsified automatically must be (loops-go vector family candidate). (c) MIGRATION spells out: legacy physical position != 1.0 witness ordinal even for order-VERIFIED stores; preserved = relative order, record bytes, tick relationships — never receipt-number identity. (d) SDK SURFACE for the two-scope CAS: distinct coordinate types (ArrivalHead / DeclarationHead), never generic position + flag — the frozen scope set lives in the type system, not review vigilance; verb renames to guarded_append (cas(head) under-describes its own semantics; canon two-scope ruling unchanged).
01M08NCZENDSXQPD407RTFVZR7	thread	arrival-migration-arc	SOL REVIEW PASS FOLDED IN (2026-08-17, GPT 5.6 Sol, artifact-only read — no code access). Verdict: "the first implementation discussion that makes me more confident the collapse was real" — dissolution held (existing codec/grammar/ceremonies under one new authority: physical line order = minted witness order). Three contracts identified; all settled:\n\n1. BATCH ORDINALS — ruled at decision:design/arrival-batch-ordinals @ 01M08N9H33H3X06A9ZR9X00V1Q: per-record ordinals (batch expands in row order, contiguous range, atomicity = admission property not addressing property). Forced by code Sol couldn't see: _index_lines gives each batch row its own rowid today, and class (b) migration verification requires order-isomorphism.\n\n2. GENESIS BOOTSTRAP — ruled at decision:design/arrival-genesis-bootstrap @ 01M08N9H8GT4WQXMPGJN3ADWW4: Sol caught a REAL ordering bug in the artifact's first draft (declarations preceded the key that signs them). Fix: genesis fact IS the founding introduction (lineage id + format-version + founding key, self-signed); movements become self-certifying genesis / declaration absorption / seal; verifier gains one explicit clause (self-certification legal at ordinal 0, nowhere else), no retroactive verification. Riders in same fact: "cryptographically self-verifying" scope qualifier; interleave-uniqueness stated rule + conformance-vector obligation (loops-go queue candidate); legacy-position != ordinal migration disclaimer; SDK typed heads (ArrivalHead/DeclarationHead) + guarded_append rename.\n\n3. CUSTODIAN CONTINUATION — Sol concurs with the deferral and sharpened the articulation ("possessing bytes claiming lineage L" vs "authorized to continue L"); remains the named next custody discussion.\n\nArtifact updated in place (same URL, version label sol-review-folded): six edits + colophon review record. The arrival-log design session is now CLOSED pending the sidecar spec.
