01M0AXTAG45GNPFED1Q2XB8BJC	task	arrival-slice-A	CUT A — AUTHORITY launched (2026-08-18, Fable arbiter, Kyle present). Stage 0 per impl-pipeline ratify-gate-one-level-down: design agent drafting the cut-A design proposal — the ONE open contract decision is adoption-genesis content for a store with real history (assigned to slice A by Kyle's ruling 2 in decision:design/arrival-slice0-record-grammar @ 01M09GNGW7), with the live-store-ceremony vs sidecar-migration-genesis seam drawn explicitly against design/sidecar-containment-genesis @ 01M08Q6P3P and design/arrival-genesis-bootstrap @ 01M08N9H8G. Everything else instantiates ruled ground: residence suffix flip (plan @ 01M090QW6Z), probe.py dispatch arm first, Rule 18 _SCAN_TARGETS growth + allowlist shrink, late_arrivals rename as a one-line recommendation. Impl+gate launch only after Kyle ratifies.
01M0B0Z14T9ATPRAJTKBBMCQQT	decision	design/arrival-sliceA-authority	RATIFIED (Kyle, 2026-08-18 session with Fable — the cut-A ratify gate per impl-pipeline stage 0 is now OPEN for implementation). The cut A (AUTHORITY) design fact; proposal doc docs/dev/arrival-sliceA-authority-design-2026-08-18.md (authored by a Claude design agent, all load-bearing citations arbiter-spot-verified against source at HEAD; agent self-corrected one cost claim mid-review — key locality, not an unsigned era — and demoted its own gate overclaim, both kept in the ratified record).\n\nCORE: adoption genesis body = {protocol, lineage, key} — founding public key self-signed at ordinal 0 per bootstrap fact 01M08N9H8G movement 1; slice 0's minimal body was slice-0-scoped, the bootstrap fact ruled the destination. protocol = the founding key-holder's SIGNED claim of the arrival grammar the lineage speaks (forward-versioning of arrival itself, NOT legacy-store support; per-record v is unsigned framing, the genesis copy is the attested one). Document set stays at ordinal >= 1 as movement 2 (declaration absorption) — never in the genesis body. fact_cursor DISSOLVES (ord < N is structural); chain_head OUT (a sqlite tick-row hash frozen into a signed immutable record rests an integrity claim on a projection — Law 1's first prohibition). Cut A builds arrival.py's FIRST VERIFIER implementing the ruled rule: key valid at N iff introduced at < N, or N is genesis and self-certifying.\n\nKYLE'S TWO RULINGS THIS SESSION: (1) Q1 as above. (2) Q2 = the gate's libs/sign + observer-key registry file-position trace is an EXCLUSIVITY claim (reading 2): the arrival verifier resolves every verifying key from (lineage, ordinal) coordinates ONLY, no libs code consults the .vertex for arrival keys; G2 gate artifact = (key, lineage, ordinal) rows produced with every projection deleted after a second key is introduced at a stated ordinal. BOUNDARY: the apps-composed tick-chain verifier and the .vertex observers{} block