b with BOTH .arrival and .jsonl siblings) named: arrival wins per Law 1, .jsonl classifies as projection — the one place cut A could silently mint two custody holders; own_lineage becomes a PROJECTION of the arrival genesis (written from ArrivalLog.lineage(), read from sqlite, rebuildable by cut B) — six sqlite readers incl. a raw SELECT at apps/loops store.py:942 ride unchanged; adopt_lineage in arrival mode REFUSES (restamp is projection repair = cut B's verb; delete breaks legacy stores per seam rule S3); late_arrivals KEEPS its name (user-visible JSON key, witness-time sense already labeled at witness.py:584-594, rename needs a CLI-surface cut + CHANGELOG); Rule 18 _SCAN_TARGETS gains residence.py + probe.py ONLY (custody has not left jsonl_store et al. until cut B); the shrink-only mechanism that moves is Rule 17's _ALLOWLIST via test_allowlist_has_no_stale_entries (Rule 18's _ALLOWED is empty — brief's shrink premise corrected by the agent).\n\nSEAM (three rules): S1 a live-store genesis NEVER carries a containment claim — containment belongs to the sidecar's frozen content-addressed genesis (01M08Q6P3P); S2 migration pins resolve to the sidecar's containment evidence — cut A's answer is dissolution, not relocation; S3 cut A converts NOTHING — every ceremony change is conditional on the declared locator being .arrival, .jsonl and sqlite ceremonies stay byte-identical.\n\nGATE: G1 authority test literally (build, exercise incl. declaration absorb + seal, delete .db/-wal/-shm and any .jsonl, everything answers from .arrival alone incl. own_lineage with store_meta gone, via walk()); G2 the exclusivity trace as ruled above; G3 apps/ diff-empty. Carried: every new reader that ADOPTS an on-disk record validates at the adoption site (_authority_fault); the O(n) residual stays at confirmed width, any narrowing is Kyle's flagged call.
