  1436	        the head. Truncation lives here and only here — the lock is what
  1437	        makes "no append is in progress" knowable, and it is the only
  1438	        condition under which an unterminated tail can be called torn
  1439	        instead of in flight. The lock is per open-file-description, so it
  1440	        releases exactly when this ``with`` closes the descriptor; every
  1441	        byte a caller writes must land inside the block.
