  1451	        byte offset just past its newline, both read under the lock.
  1452	
  1453	        Acquire and read the head (:meth:`_locked_head`), then build,
  1454	        validate, encode, write, fsync, release.
  1455	
  1456	        fsync and not merely flush: the record must outlive a power cut, not
  1457	        merely a process crash. That was strong reasoning when the line was
  1458	        one of two copies; it is not optional now that it is the only one.
  1459	        """
