01M0BMF0BBAHTZGVS63V506Z0B	retrospective	arrival-cutB-pipeline-round	CUT B — PROJECTIONS pipeline round retro (2026-08-18, one session, Kyle present at both gates). SHAPE: full antigravity pipeline — Stage E (6 flash-low explorers, all citations spot-checked) -> opus design agent -> Kyle ratified with 2 explicit rulings (restamp dissolution; Q9 Rule-18 departure) -> opus impl 8 commits, 9 disclosed deviations -> opus gate FINDINGS NON-BLOCKING with own oracle + own mutations (refuted 2 of the arbiter's brief claims — the gate gating the arbiter works) -> Kyle ruled #9 ratified + F1 fix-now -> 3 remediation commits, gate re-check CLEAN -> 3 flash-high scoped reviews, 2 findings, both fixed -> 4-angle seeded simplify, 5 moves (1 composed from 2-angle convergence, 1 load-bearing perf restoration mutation-proofed 33-red) -> gemini-3.1-pro readiness CONVERGED 7/7 PASS. Arbiter independently re-executed the discriminating M5 mutation (19+14 red) per the cutA read-heavy-readiness precedent. WORKED: deviation-disclosure culture (9 deviations all survived scrutiny, several strictly stronger than the contract — the id-guard on the own_lineage licence prevented a real corruption B6 would have enabled); the seeded-angle simplify returned a composed finding and a genuine perf regression the review rounds missed; findings-as-store-facts made the final reconciliation a one-liner (12 findings, 0 open). LESSONS: (1) jq '//' fallback suppressed pro's coverage field — nearly ordered a 60m rerun for evidence that existed unread; read the full structured object before judging proof-of-work. (2) Rule 17 scans docs/scratch and bit THREE agent drafts this round — briefs must paraphrase retired vocabulary; consider the git-ls-files scope fix (finding:rule17-scans-untracked-docs) before cut C. (3) The impl's fence departure pattern (Rule 17 allowlist, guard unification into receive.py) was right both times BUT only because each carried a both-sites-red proof — proof-of-work justifies scope calls, prompts should say so explicitly. (4) agy idle pings race SendMessage reports; verify branch state before acting on any ping. RESIDUE CARRIED: perf benchmark (O(n) derived-log regen per merge) still unmeasured — named pre-ship; _create-self-enforce guard question awaits a Kyle ruling; JsonlStore.catch_up twin race waits for its cut; sol belt-and-braces round remains Kyle's standing option after the codex reset (Aug 19 23:00).
01M0EJ9DVDA53DZBQKCAVPRH6F	decision	design/arrival-sliceC-ordering	RATIFIED (Kyle, 2026-08-19): Cut C — ORDERING design contract. Full body: docs/scratch/arrival-sliceC/design-proposal.md (committed on feat/arrival-libs). Spine: ordering is DECLARED, never inferred — atoms Ordering union Arrival()|ByKey(field) + ONE totalization beside it, every reader consumes that primitive; .arrival is the only real store, legacy families frozen byte-for-byte. Q1 totalization: ByKey sort key (K(record), record.id ASC), id NEVER semantic time (NON-NEGOTIABLE); missing-K = non-membership in the projection (Kyle-ratified posture, vector-pinned); type-mixed K REFUSES loudly (no coercion); flat payload field this cut; no lang grammar change (LensDecl key attr = later thin constructor, dissolution test). Q2 'arrival' is SINGLE-STORE-ONLY (ordinals dense per-log): aggregates must ByKey, default ByKey('ts'); aggregate+Arrival refuses loudly; _combined_read store-count fork DISSOLVES into declared ordering ("interim state" comment retires — this is the ruling it awaited); single-store Arrival ≡ old rowid sequence byte-identical (gate pin). Q3 CAS token = arrival head (record_ordinal, fact_id), batch rows share record ordinal; predicate keeps lineage-filtered _decl.*-only semantics verbatim; _INTENT_VERSION BUMPS, old intents refuse via IntentCorrupt posture; legacy declaration_head FROZEN untouched; test axis rewrite: cas-token test pins ARRIVAL apart from (ts,id); gate: token agrees with from-scratch log walk. Q4 ordered(prefix,key) on StoreReader, read-time sort, NO new index (benchmark-justified later); perf benchmark item extends to ordered() pre-ship. Q5 dissolution takes the WHOLE bridge module store/jsonl.py (_receipt_order + export_jsonl + rebuild_jsonl + ORDERING RULE docstring + tests) — exporting under substitute order would rewrite receipt history on rebuild; residue swept same change: __init__ exports, sl store export CLI arm (apps/ NOT diff-empty this cut, Kyle-ratified departure from B), refusal-message pointers merge.py:120 + jsonl_store.py:689/755, RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md R2/R3; JsonlStore engine class UNTOUCHED; planned frozen last-0.x sidecar keeps its own copy (e1: no sidecar exists yet — future home named, nothing to fence). Q6 generate_lens grows key axis against the atoms primitive; existing ts vectors become ByKey('ts') family BYTE-IDENTICAL (normative, loops-go reads them); new families: non-ts key + adversarial missing-K/mixed-type/id-tiebreak; checkpoint dispatch tests enumerate Ordering variants — Arrival licenses checkpoint+replay_from suffix, ByKey cold-folds. Q7 Rule 17 scan scope = slice C0 first commit: git ls-files selection + docs/scratch exclusion, shrink-only. KEEP (NON-NEGOTIABLE): Spec.replay_from, VertexHandle checkpoint machinery, benchmark arms, Rule 17 semantics, ArrivalStore write path (except CAS coordinate), legacy families. Commit seams C0-C5, C1→{C2,C4,C5}. GATE items 1-7 in proposal incl. main-checkout full suite post-merge.
01M0EJHPHX34MZ2ET1QY05QHGD	observation	session/2026-08-19-arrival-sliceC-design	Cut C ORDERING design session, ratified same-evening (antigravity-impl-pipeline Stage E + stage 0; no implementation). Shape: six flash-low explorers (all citations spot-checked verbatim, 6/6 exact) fed a design brief; six sequential arbiter-gate questions to Kyle produced the contract; decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering RATIFIED + receipts committed a49997cd. CALIBRATION NOTES: (1) Kyle's Q6 pushback ("there's a set of primitive work that would make everything else easier") reframed the cut around ONE atoms Ordering primitive + shared totalization — the arbiter had been answering the six questions locally; the primitive-first composition came from the human gate. Sequential one-question-at-a-time gating is what created the room for that catch. (2) Kyle challenged Q2's premise (mode-qualified CAS token) — grounding the answer in the tree (three families still execute pre-migration) converted a premise dispute into a clean freeze-the-condemned ruling. (3) Advisor post-completion check caught that Rule 17 needed running after the docs commit — red, but ALL offenders pre-existing untracked docs/dev files (the receipted Cut B finding), committed receipts pass; verified before declaring done rather than assumed. (4) Plan-fact line anchors were stale vs the branch (CAS predicate drifted 1411->1448); re-pinning every anchor in the proposal is now the standing brief practice. NEXT ENTRY POINT: implementation session — pipeline stage 1, slices C0 (Rule 17 scan scope, first commit) then C1 atoms primitive feeding C2/C4/C5, C3 CAS independent; opus gates via pointer branches; flash-high scoped reviews; proposal's anchor table is the map.
