     1	"""canonical_audit — does the derived index still agree with the canonical log?
     2	
     3	A JSONL-canonical store (design/architecture/jsonl-canonical-store) has two
     4	artifacts: the ``.jsonl`` log, which IS the store, and the sibling ``.db``,
     5	which is an index derived from it. Every verification surface before this
     6	module walked the *index* only, so an out-of-band sqlite row — a row the log
     7	never carried — still rendered ``✓ chain intact`` at rc=0. That is a false
     8	attestation of exactly the lie-class the chain exists to prevent
     9	(design/store/verify-canonical-agreement).
    10	
    11	This module is the reader that judges the two artifacts against each other.
    12	
    13	**Pure reader, by contract.** Nothing here constructs a :class:`~engine.
    14	jsonl_store.JsonlStore`. That constructor *repairs* — catch-up, torn-line
    15	truncation, rebuild-on-divergence — and repair destroys the evidence
    16	verification exists to inspect. Open-time recovery and verification are
    17	opposite contracts, so they never share a code path: the log is read with
    18	plain file IO through :mod:`engine.jsonl_codec`, the index with a read-only
    19	sqlite connection, and neither offset nor count marker is ever written.
    20	
    21	Two depths:
    22	
    23	``audit_agreement``  (L1, the default gate)
    24	    Three O(1)-ish checks: the stamped byte offset equals the log's size, the
    25	    stamped row counts equal ``COUNT(*)`` per table, and the last complete log
    26	    line agrees field-for-field with the index row it names. Cheap enough to
    27	    run in front of every store read verb.
    28	
    29	``audit_deep``  (``--deep``)
    30	    Streams every log line — bounded memory, never the whole 111MB-class log
    31	    at once — comparing fields *and* order against the index rows in rowid
    32	    order, then re-derives the tick hash chain FROM CANONICAL CONTENT rather
    33	    than from the index it is judging.
    34	
    35	SCOPE BOUNDARY, stated rather than implied: a *coordinated* edit of an
    36	unsealed fact in both artifacts is uncaught here, because nothing yet commits
    37	to that fact's content — the witnesses at the live edge are the fact's own
    38	signature and the next seal, not this audit. Pinned by
    39	``test_interior_tamper_of_an_unsealed_fact_is_caught_by_nothing``.
