    91	    """Does this divergence lie past the prefix the index claims to have consumed?
    92	
    93	    A SCOPE STATEMENT, NOT AN INNOCENCE CLAIM. ``JsonlStore`` fsyncs the log
    94	    BEFORE it commits the index rows and the markers (``jsonl_store.py``), so
    95	    a crash in that window leaves a durable log ahead of a truthful-but-behind
    96	    index — and an interrupted append leaves a torn final line the next open
    97	    truncates. Both states put their divergence here. But so does an attacker
    98	    who rewinds the marker and then edits the suffix: L1 corroborates only the
    99	    FIRST line past the offset (:func:`_suffix_unindexed`), which is enough to
   100	    refuse the marker's bare word and no more. Full corroboration of an
   101	    unindexed suffix is definitionally :func:`audit_deep`'s job, so no caller
   102	    may turn this flag into "not tampering" — only into "the disagreement is
   103	    in bytes the index never claimed, which an interrupted append also
   104	    produces; run ``--deep`` to rule the rest out".
