    12	# The ratified glossary (decision:design/arrival-slice0-record-grammar §4.1)
    13	# is small on purpose: arrival log, record, lineage, ordinal, coordinate,
    14	# genesis, head, append, resume mark, torn tail, projection, body. §4.2
    15	# ratifies a seed denylist alongside it — terms from the model the arrival
    16	# substrate replaces. They are banned here because a name is how a retired
    17	# model gets rebuilt in the next reader's head: the resume mark is
    18	# `arrival_*` rather than a rename of the old meta keys precisely because
    19	# renaming would have carried the two row counts along, and starting from the
    20	# arrival axis is what showed they dissolve.
    21	#
    22	# Scope note (deliberately narrow — "scope the claim before widening the
    23	# detection"). This judges the ARRIVAL surface only: the arrival module and
    24	# every shipped source file under `libs/sdk/src`, which the design fact names
    25	# as the eventual public surface. Legacy modules keep their vocabulary until
    26	# their own cuts dissolve them — scanning them would turn this rule into a
    27	# standing failure that gets suppressed rather than a gate that holds. When a
    28	# later slice moves custody into a module, that module joins _SCAN_TARGETS in
    29	# the same change. Tests are out of scope for the same reason Rule 17 excludes
    30	# them: a test states the banned vocabulary in order to assert it is gone, and
    31	# folding those into an allowlist dilutes it.
    32	
    33	# Paths, relative to the repo root, whose names are held to the arrival
    34	# glossary. GROW as arrival slices land; never shrink to make a failure go
    35	# away. Cut A moved custody into the funnel (residence, probe) and built the
    36	# arrival write path (arrival_store — a new module born on the arrival
    37	# surface, so it joins at birth).
    38	#
    39	# Cut B adds four. `arrival_projection` and `derived_log_merge` are NEW and
    40	# born on the arrival surface, so they join at birth. `store/merge.py` and
    41	# `store/receive.py` join because CUSTODY MOVED INTO THEM: they stopped being
    42	# direct index writers and became arrival appenders, which is this rule's own
    43	# stated trigger.
    44	#
    45	# `jsonl_store.py` does NOT join, departing from
    46	# `plan:arrival-vocabulary-ratchet`'s "jsonl_store until cut B". Custody has
