   462	    def _ceremony_persist(self, rows: list[tuple]) -> None:
   463	        """Make a declaration ceremony canonical: ONE arrival record, stamped.
   464	
   465	        Runs inside the ceremony's open transaction after every check
   466	        passed, immediately before the caller's COMMIT. One row rides as a
   467	        ``fact`` record; several as one ``batch`` record — one record is the
   468	        log's atomicity unit, so recovery can never expose a partial
   469	        ceremony.
   470	
   471	        ``following`` pins the append to the head the ceremony reconciled
   472	        against: a record another writer lands mid-ceremony REFUSES the
   473	        append before any byte is written (``AppendRejected``), the
   474	        caller's transaction rolls back with the log byte-identical, and
   475	        the ceremony is simply retryable — unlike :meth:`_write`, this path
   476	        cannot resolve a gap after the fact, because the record it would
   477	        have made durable is the ceremony itself.
