facts`, `generate_lens`, `test_conformance_lens`) delegate to it.\n  - Strict type identity (`type(value) is not key_type`) rejects any coercion (including `bool` vs `int` and `int` vs `float`).\n  - Missing K and `None` are non-membership (excluded before sorting).\n  - Fact `id` is ascending and acts as tie-break only.\n- **Probe Command:**\n  ```bash\n  cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-3805-4241-87e6-8928f83ad939/scratchpad/wt-review \u0026\u0026 uv run python /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-3805-4241-87e6-8928f83ad939/scratchpad/agy-scratch/probe_category1_totalization.py\n  ```\n- **Probe Output:**\n  ```\n  Running Category 1 Probes...\n  ALL Category 1 Probes PASSED successfully!\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### Category 2: `ordered()` SEMANTICS \u0026 FIX COMMIT RE-VERIFICATION\n\n- **Lines Read:**\n  - [`libs/engine/src/engine/store_reader.py:198-260`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-3805-4241-87e6-8928f83ad939/scratchpad/wt-review/libs/engine/src/engine/store_reader.py#L198-L260)\n  - [`libs/engine/tests/test_store_reader.py:808-958`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-3805-4241-87e6-8928f83ad939/scratchpad/wt-review/libs/engine/tests/test_store_reader.py#L808-L958)\n- **Analysis:**\n  - `StoreReader.ordered(prefix, key)` cleanly decouples selection and ordering: SQL query selects `[0..prefix)` rows using `ORDER BY rowid ASC LIMIT ?` (with `_decl.*` excluded by default before limit), and Python `totalize()` reorders the selected prefix under declared `key`.\n  - Fix commit `c314a3e7` (gate finding A1) added `test_prefix_rides_arrival_not_event_time` with inverted `ts` vs `rowid` ordering.\n  - Re-verified the mutation: changing `ORDER BY rowid ASC` to `ORDER BY ts ASC` causes the SQL selector to pick `['d', 'c']` instead of `['a', 'b']`, failing the test.\n- **Probe Command:**\n  ```bash\n  cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-38