pad/wt-review/spec/conformance/vectors/lens/lens-by-key-mixed-types-refused.json#L1-L45)\n- **Analysis:**\n  - `git diff a49997cd..074a1860 -- spec/conformance/vectors/lens/lens-timestamp-tie-id-asc.json spec/conformance/vectors/lens/lens-sub-millisecond-timestamp-precision.json` is completely empty (0 bytes delta) — the historical `ts` vectors are byte-frozen.\n  - The four new vector files' expected outputs were independently computed from input fixtures and verified to match the JSON golden outputs:\n    1. `lens-by-key-payload-seq.json` -\u003e `[\"01TESTULID0000000000000003\", \"01TESTULID0000000000000002\", \"01TESTULID0000000000000001\"]` (seq 1 \u003c 2 \u003c 3)\n    2. `lens-by-key-tie-id-asc.json` -\u003e `[\"01TESTULID0000000000000001\", \"01TESTULID0000000000000002\", \"01TESTULID0000000000000003\"]` (tie on seq=7 broken by ULID ASC)\n    3. `lens-by-key-missing-field-excluded.json` -\u003e `[\"01TESTULID0000000000000004\", \"01TESTULID0000000000000001\"]` (missing and `None` keys excluded)\n    4. `lens-by-key-mixed-types-refused.json` -\u003e `{\"error\": \"OrderingError\"}` (`int` vs `str` key refused)\n  - Conformance schema: `input.ordering` is optional and omitted for the default `ts` family. Any loops-go reader expecting the default `ts` vector format will continue to read historical vectors without breaking changes.\n- **Probe Command:**\n  ```bash\n  cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-3805-4241-87e6-8928f83ad939/scratchpad/wt-review \u0026\u0026 uv run python /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kaygee-Code-loops/c86ef4b9-3805-4241-87e6-8928f83ad939/scratchpad/agy-scratch/probe_category3_vectors.py\n  ```\n- **Probe Output:**\n  ```\n  Running Category 3 Probes for Conformance Vectors...\n  Discovered vectors: ['lens-by-key-missing-field-excluded.json', 'lens-by-key-mixed-types-refused.json', 'lens-by-key-payload-seq.json', 'lens-by-key-tie-id-asc.json', 'lens-sub-millisecond-timestamp-precision.json', 'lens-timestamp-tie-id