    10	# The ratified semantic (docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md): fold replay order is
    11	# RECEIPT order (rowid, store-local). `(ts, id)` survives only as an explicit
    12	# read lens. The code moved in S1/S2; this rule is what keeps the PROSE from
    13	# drifting back, because a stale docstring is how the old model gets rebuilt in
    14	# the next reader's head.
    15	#
    16	# Scope note (deliberately narrow — "scope the claim before widening the
    17	# detection"). This scans SHIPPED prose only: `libs/*/src`, `apps/*/src`, and
    18	# every `.md` under `spec/` and `docs/`, plus the conformance generators, whose
    19	# case descriptions are normative text. Test files are OUT of scope on purpose:
    20	# tests state counterfactuals constantly ("what would break under a (ts, id)
    21	# replay") and folding those into the allowlist would dilute it from "these are
    22	# genuinely lens" into "these are lens or hypothetical", which is exactly the
    23	# overclaim this rule exists to prevent. `libs/engine/mutants/` is an artifact
    24	# tree and is excluded everywhere.
    25	#
    26	# Two further narrowings, same principle. Only TRACKED files are judged — what
    27	# git ships is what "shipped prose" means, so an untracked local scratch file
    28	# is not a claim the repo makes. And `docs/scratch/` is excluded outright: it
    29	# is the working-notes tree, where briefs and receipts must be able to QUOTE
    30	# retired vocabulary verbatim to record what was superseded. Both are shrinks
    31	# of the judged set; the rule text and its semantics are unchanged.
    32	
    33	_TS_ORDER = re.compile(
    34	    r"\(ts,\s*id\)|\(ts,\s*fact_id\)|\(ts,id\)|ORDER BY ts\b|"
    35	    r"ts ASC,\s*id ASC|ts DESC,\s*id DESC"
    36	)
    37	_FOLD_VOCAB = re.compile(r"\bfold|\breplay|\bFold|\bReplay|\bREPLAY")
    38	
    39	# How far either side of the ts-pattern line the fold vocabulary may appear and
    40	# still count as the same claim. Two lines is a wrapped sentence; wider starts
    41	# pairing unrelated paragraphs and crying wolf.
    42	_WINDOW = 2
    43	
    44	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    45	# Allowlist — SHRINK ONLY.
    46	#
    47	# Each entry is (path relative to repo root, a substring that must appear on
    48	# the matched line). Content markers, not line numbers: prose gets reflowed,
    49	# and a line-numbered allowlist would churn on every unrelated edit while
    50	# silently re-admitting a moved claim.
    51	#
    52	# Every entry needs a comment saying why the site is GENUINELY a lens (or a
    53	# labeled historical record). "It has always been there" is not a reason. The
    54	# only legal edits to this list are deletions.
    55	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    56	_ALLOWLIST: set[tuple[str, str]] = {
    57	    # _combined_facts' ORDER BY: a combined view has no receipt axis (rowid is
    58	    # per-store), so this genuinely IS the lens, and the comment says so.
    59	    (
    60	        "libs/engine/src/engine/vertex_reader.py",
    61	        "ORDER BY ts, id here is the explicit (ts, id) READ LENS ordering",
    62	    ),
    63	    # facts_by_kind's docstring states the ratified rule and names (ts, id) as
    64	    # the thing that does NOT order the fold. Stating the negation is the
    65	    # opposite of the claim this rule forbids.
   130	    """Repo-relative posix paths git tracks — the definition of "shipped"."""
   131	    out = subprocess.run(
   132	        ["git", "-C", str(REPO_ROOT), "ls-files"],
   133	        capture_output=True,
   134	        text=True,
   135	        check=True,
   136	    )
   137	    return set(out.stdout.splitlines())
