     5	disambiguation, because under three modes a bare ``.db`` cannot answer its
     6	own mode from its path):
     7	
     8	===========  ================================================================
     9	``sqlite``   Unchanged, byte-identical to the pre-arrival ceremony: ATTACH +
    10	             ``INSERT OR IGNORE``. Every change in this cut is conditional on
    11	             the declared locator.
    12	``arrival``  The arrival log is the store, so a merge APPENDS INTO IT and
    13	             then re-derives the projections. Nothing here ever INSERTs into
    14	             the index.
    15	``jsonl``    REFUSED, naming the export-and-reopen recovery. A merge into a
    16	             log-canonical store succeeds today and then bricks the store at
    17	             its next open; refusing at the site is the same verdict,
    18	             delivered where it is attributable, and it destroys nothing.
    19	===========  ================================================================
    20	
    21	The id primary key is the globally unique identity — a fact retains its id
    22	through slice/merge round-trips, so a row whose id the target already holds
    23	appends nothing. Independently-emitted facts (same content, different stores)
    24	get different ids and are correctly NOT deduplicated.
    25	
    26	What a merged store claims about order
    27	--------------------------------------
    28	For an arrival target: **the target's arrival ordinal — the order records
    29	arrived at the target — and nothing else.** No claim is made about event
