    31	``merge(A,B)`` and ``merge(B,A)``. The two merges are different custody
    32	events and the ordinal says so; what survives is determinism per direction
    33	and equality of content.
    34	
    35	An arrival source replays in ORDINAL order — merging is replaying the
    36	source's arrival into the target's, and it consumes no event-time input at
    37	all. A sqlite/jsonl source (the transport case, where ``slice_store`` emits a
