01KX9S7YZDYN04CXTN8G41KMFZ	design/declaration-document-subjects-and-order			S0 review round (Codex gpt-5.6-sol on f82e9e3: 1 blocker, 5 majors — all confirmed) forced two protocol calls on the document form. (1) SOURCE SUBJECTS: human-meaningful base (template path / bare path / command) + deterministic collision suffix in encounter order (base, base#2, base#3) — reorders of distinct sources stay stable, duplicates disambiguate deterministically; picked over content-hash subjects (edit=retire+define churn) and pure ordinals (reorder=spurious redefinition of every subject). (2) ORDER IS MEANING: every multi-instance document payload (kind-defined, source-defined, member-defined, observer-defined, lens-defined) carries integer order=; projection sorts by (order, subject). Rationale: sequential source blocks, boundary match order, and kind declaration order (salience rendering) are all meaning the per-subject Latest fold would otherwise destroy; a reorder edit re-emitting affected subjects is honest because order is meaning where declared. Also enforced at serialization: float finiteness + recursive JSON-safety (str keys, JSON values) — JCS canonicalization must never be the first thing to notice. Empty-present vs None collections: preserve via vertex-defined presence markers where loader-reachable (empty sources block IS: loader.py:595), else normalize+document.
