01KYG3Y67QQK3A3J8PNFQCR5EF	architecture/surfacing-layer-charter	proposed		SURFACING HOME = LAYER DESIGNATION, NOT PACKAGE (Kyle ruled shape 2026-07-26, wave-open discussion). The home the instrument-family survey says is missing arrives the way the record layer exists: a named layer in ARCHITECTURE.md + membership and boundary rules in the import DAG (test_architecture.py _LIB_ALLOWED_RUNTIME), spanning multiple packages by role. Charter content: (1) surfacing = Level C per shannon-weaver mapping — conduct/authority/host orchestration, relational, reliable-not-correct; (2) members by assignment, zero file moves: libs/sign + libs/custody (authority), loops-go protocol artifacts (coordination); (3) TUI shell = first NATIVE occupant, app-side per ratified rendering/tui-shell-integration; (4) discipline = relocation-on-pull — the CLI-host extraction from painted (run_cli/add_cli_args/run_app, leaving painted pure Level-A view) happens when the TUI shell actually pulls on that seam, gated separately as a painted-major coordination; (5) the misfiling fix is the NAME + DAG rules — the filing function failed for lack of a name, and a mega-lib would just be a third place to misfile into. Status proposed until ARCHITECTURE.md section + DAG rule shape are drafted for ratification.
