01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS	architecture/libs-handoff-scope	proposed		Contract basis for the libs handoff derived from Sol's LIBS_CHANGES (branch cli-v2-proposal), triaged 2026-08-13. IN SCOPE as tasks (P0): jsonl-declaration-ceremonies (absorb_genesis/absorb_edit on JSONL-canonical — atomic multi-row ceremony in the log, stale-head refusal leaves log+index byte-equivalent, index stays pure derivation); declaration-plan-apply-api (plan_declaration_update/apply — one high-level op owning head-capture, diff, residence, signing; today every client re-assembles an 8-step protocol); declaration-file-store-recovery (durable intent + idempotent recover for the store-first-then-file-cache gap). IN SCOPE (P1): observer-grant-engine-resolution (THE HOLE — engine gates only caller-supplied Grant, declared ObserverDecl.grant.potential silently bypassable; fix at the engine boundary, bypass must be explicit); receipt-attestation-state (persisted signed-state on Receipt/ReceiveResult from the committed row — passes write-receipt-vs-temporal-query, your write's attestation is your write's identity); bounded-fact-query (cross-kind limit+cursor query — MUST spec against the shipped 0.8.0 temporal-cursor contract and A3 ids-never-ordered, not Sol's FactCursor sketch); strict-contract-ruling (MODIFIED from Sol: strict IS enforced, at the CLI (commands/emit.py three-source precedence); ruling needed on whether enforcement moves to engine receive — same push-admission-into-engine motion as observer-grant — Sol's 'unenforced' premise was half wrong); lang-kdl-mutation-api (export add/edit/remove_vertex_kind over existing kdl_insert_child/kdl_remove_child + loops{}-creation + LoopDef-to-KDL serializer); target-probe-api (probe_target -> TargetInfo, dissolves per-client residence/suffix logic); canonical-audit-preflight (typed audit-only/audit-then-open/recover-then-open, never conflate verify with repair). DEFERRED (P2, promote on forcing consumer): lifecycle-projection helper, shared result codec, search coordinator, maintenance backend matrix. SEQUENCING: VertexHandle S5 checkpoint precedes any consumer cutover; the throwaway probe (task:cli-v2-probe) is the independent forcing consumer that exercises these APIs as they land. Collisions honored: exit-code/machine-codes work stays with thread:cli-error-surface-unification, not duplicated here.
01KZYQ5PQXSQ1N6E4BB19ZJRE7	libs-handoff-s5	completed		S5 MERGED (gate PASS + blocking 5d fixed: allow-mode pinned by mutation-verified multi-row ceremony test 03f4d36f). Gate highlights: independent pagination equivalence on adversarial mixed-era ids; evasion probe confirmed mid-ceremony cursor refused at fold apply (declaration.py receipt_group_span re-check) — defense in depth. Deviations for sol brief: aggregate RAISES WitnessAggregateUnsupported vs contract's typed-result wording (matches 0.8.0 at= precedent, CLI must catch-and-render; state to Sol); order=str not Literal (cosmetic, skipped).
01M03SZAKGQJXWNA8XERJPDB0J	fold-replay-semantics	open		THE DESIGN FORK, at Kyle's gate — next session's headline topic. VertexHandle.receive commits a fact then calls _refresh_locked, which falls through to _reconstruct: 'full replay in (ts, id) order' (handle.py:909). The fast paths are guarded on 'not has_new_facts' and a receive always adds one, so every write re-folds all history. Deliberate and documented (handle.py:1300): a backdated fact must fold at its (ts,id) position, not at the live tail. THREE FINDINGS THAT RESHAPE THE DECISION: (1) Reconstruction runs PRAGMA query_only=ON, so it cannot fire or retract a tick — the O(n) per write buys canonical STATE, not canonical HISTORY. A backdated fact that should have changed whether a boundary fired in an earlier cycle leaves that persisted tick untouched. The cost is paid for a narrower property than it appears to buy. (2) Most fold operators do not need replay at all: Count/Sum/Min/Max/Avg are commutative (order irrelevant by construction); Upsert is decidable in O(1) against the stored entry's (ts,id); Collect(max=N>0)/Window/TopN are order-sensitive but BOUNDED (re-derive from N items, not n facts). Only Collect(max=0) genuinely needs full history. (3) The append fast path is behaviour-preserving BY CONSTRUCTION — for a fact whose (ts,id) sorts after everything folded, replay-from-zero and fold-in-place are identical, and the handle already holds the head so the test is O(1). THE FORK: refuse backdating / accept eventual-state-with-append-only-history / build tick retraction. That choice decides whether the slow path needs to exist at all. Complication: reset=true cycles and count-based every/after boundaries mean a backdated fact shifts cycle membership, which full replay does not fix either. UNVERIFIED: whether (ts,id) is a total order with monotonic gen_id within a store — the fast path rests on it.
01M070N08HX69QAEQ3TRPY72CQ	design/declared-fold-order			AMENDMENT 2026-08-16 #4 — RATIFIED (Kyle, in-session with Opus 5, cross-family with GPT 5.6 "Sol", grounded by a 5-lens code audit, workflow wf_5c2a2768-b76, 22 agents). THIS SUPERSEDES THE TWO-MODE DESIGN ENTIRELY, including amendments #1 and #3 of this decision and load-bearing sentences of decision:design/log-and-index-roles. The store is no longer a thing with modes.\n\n=== THE COLLAPSE ===\n\nTHE STORE IS AN APPEND-ONLY, LINEAGE-LOCAL ARRIVAL LOG. It holds complete canonical records plus a minted arrival lineage genesis. Its position is the witness position. It is never merged, never rebuilt, never rewound. EVERYTHING ELSE IS A PROJECTION OF AN ARRIVAL PREFIX: fold state, FTS/search, graph views, lenses, the sqlite index, AND the git-tracked JSONL, which becomes a deterministic canonical-set synchronization projection. Authority INVERTS from today, where JSONL is canonical and custody order is implicit in line order.\n\nOne sentence: THE STORE IS WHAT THIS CUSTODIAN RECEIVED. Everything else is a question asked of it.\n\n(thing, id) AS A SUBSTRATE PRIMITIVE — Kyle's generalization, which is what finished the collapse. "Event order" was only ever (ts, id), with ts the first and most obvious key; fiction_time, effective_date, priority, (chapter, scene) are peers. So "event" leaves the vocabulary and the substrate exposes ONE read primitive:\n    ordered(prefix=W, key=K) = stable total ordering of arrival[0:W] by (K(record), record.id)\nwith `order` declaring `arrival` or `by KEY`. Requirements on K: deterministic under its declaration generation, historically reconstructible, replica-independent, totally comparable. That is sufficient to make it substrate-level WITHOUT teaching the substrate what ts or fiction_time mean — domain meaning stays in declarations. id remains identity/dedup plus deterministic totalization and is NEVER semantic time; protecting that is more important now than before, because most keys are not time at all.\n\nPROJECTION TAXONOMY — the real descendant of the trilemma, which was never a property of stores. It classifies any maintained projection, not just folds:\n    arrival-stable          new observations only extend it -> resume from head\n    key-ordered/insertion-sensitive   a new observation may sort into prior material -> checkpoint + replay from insertion\n    order-independent       visitation order does not matter -> incorporate directly\nThe checkpoint ladder is therefore projection-maintenance infrastructure, not an event-store feature. FTS is the clarifying case: it exists today partly because sqlite happens to provide FTS5 — an accidental capability of the storage engine promoted to a capability of the system. The .vertex `search` directive is already a projection spec, mislabeled.\n\nWITNESS POSITION = (arrival_lineage, ordinal). NOT (replica, position) — the naming matters and Sol's correction is adopted. "Replica" names machine/worktree/runtime identity; what makes a persisted position meaningful is the MINTED GENESIS LINEAGE of the arrival log. Renaming or moving a worktree must not change a position's identity, and copying bytes must not silently establish continuity with a lineage — which is exactly the hijack AmbiguousGenesis already refuses. The type states the law: POSITIONS COMPARE ONLY WITHIN ONE ARRIVAL LINEAGE, and cross-lineage comparison is not false but UNDEFINED, failing structurally rather than answering wrongly. One coordinate carries CAS token, tick chain basis and witness cursor simultaneously; they must not be three notions of head.\n\nCAS IS A QUALIFIED PREDICATE OVER THE ARRIVAL AXIS, not a second species. Contract: "no fact matching the declaration-basis predicate arrived in lineage L after position P" — preserving today's lineage-filtered, _decl.*-only semantics (sqlite_store.py:1411-1438) while riding the new axis. An UNQUALIFIED arrival-head compare was verified to break ordinary use: any `sl emit` landing in the plan->apply window would raise StaleDeclarationHead across six call sites (libs/sdk/src/sdk/kind.py:148/152,194/198,239/243,314/318,361/365; apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py:1257->1356) with an error message that would have become false. Digest CAS stays RETIRED — demoted to a possible conflict-narrowing optimization, not protocol.\n\nFEDERATED READ AND ADMISSION STAY DISTINCT, and the audit confirms the code already holds this line — the rewrite does NOT need to absorb aggregation.\n    federated read: inspect evidence resident in independent stores; witness axes remain separate. combine/discover use read-only ATTACH, copy nothing (vertex_reader.py:9-11, :335-341), and REFUSE to fabricate a global witness order across stores (WitnessAggregateUnsupported, plus the A10 cross-store lineage refusal).\n    admission: this lineage receives a foreign observation; canonical bytes append to this arrival log; this lineage now holds a receipt position for it. A DISTINCT CUSTODY ACT, separate from merge. Signature verification at admission is NEW CODE — no current receive path has it.\nProtect this distinction in the new store API.\n\nTHE SHARED PROJECTION AND GIT. Git-tracking the store IS the intended workflow (Kyle, confirmed) and has been the intent since the JSONL work began; .gitignore:9 (*.jsonl) and :37 (.loops/) are RESIDUE to sweep in the same change that lands arrival, at which point .loops/project.vertex:5-7's claim becomes true instead of aspirational. CORRECTION TO A CLAIM MADE IN-SESSION AND WITHDRAWN: materializing the projection in canonical id order does NOT mostly eliminate git tail conflicts. ULIDs are time-ordered, so records newly emitted on two branches both sort after their common base — both branches still change EOF from the same base, which is the classic append-conflict shape. WHAT SURVIVES, and it is the part that matters: a given fact set has EXACTLY ONE canonical byte representation, giving deterministic projection generation, cheap digest equality, and the removal of representation order as semantic information. THE RIGHT ANSWER for merge is available precisely because the projection is derived: give git a SEMANTIC MERGE DRIVER (parse ours/base/theirs, union by id, conflict on same-id-different-bytes, validate policy, sort canonically, rewrite). The audit found NO .gitattributes and no merge driver anywhere in the tree, so this is greenfield, not a compatibility constraint. Loops defines the semantics of merging its own representation; git remains the PR/concurrency workflow.\n\n=== WHY THIS IS NOT MERELY AESTHETIC: REPO EVIDENCE ===\n\nThe audit did not just agree with the collapse; it found a CORRECTNESS WEAKNESS exactly where the new model says authority is misplaced.\n\nTHE AUTHORITY TEST, ANSWERED LITERALLY: delete project.jsonl today with a complete valid arrival log present and NOTHING can be answered — not one local semantic or integrity claim. catch_up refuses to open (JsonlCanonicalUnsupported), audit_agreement fails, preflight gates stats/ticks/verify (preflight.py:67-72).\n\nLATENT DEFECT ON MAIN: line order IS custody order and is CRYPTOGRAPHICALLY COMMITTED TO — prev_hash, window_start, fact_cursor and window_hash all derive from rowid (sqlite_store.py:1595-1603, window SQL :1531-1534; declared authority at :85-88 and :12-13). But _rebuild does DELETE FROM facts, resetting sqlite's rowid counter, and the code says it plainly (jsonl_store.py:931-934): "re-indexed rows take rowids that previously named other facts." CHAIN COMMITMENTS REST ON AN AXIS A REBUILD REGENERATES. Separately, byte offset is the custody watermark and is NOT confined to --deep: the default L1 gate is a byte-prefix model (_check_offset canonical_audit.py:429-460, _suffix_unindexed :400-427, _check_last_line :495-540), so a mid-file insertion invalidates it with no deep verification run.\n\nTHE DESIGN ANTICIPATED THIS. engine/witness.py:25-30: "A store-wide receipt ordinal (GlobalReceiptPosition) is a queued protocol amendment, not smuggled in here." ARRIVAL IS EXACTLY THAT QUEUED AMENDMENT; witness.py:3-4 and :22-24 already carry the inclusive-witness-prefix vocabulary.\n\n=== PR #8: MERGE, DO NOT RELEASE, DO NOT LEAVE IT ALONE ON MAIN ===\n\nFar less superseded than assumed. It introduces NO per-store receipt-mode flag: it unconditionally makes fold order = the order this store received facts and demotes (ts,id) to an explicit read lens. That IS the arrival model's semantics, implemented one layer too low — its authority for "order received" is rowid, which today equals line order. Not merging costs more: the rewrite would have to re-fight every (ts,id)-as-fold-order pin still on main (conformance replay vectors, test_properties_replay.py, test_fold_diff.py, libs/store/tests/test_merge.py:452) and rebuild replay_from plus checkpoint dispatch from zero with no base-arm benchmark evidence.\n    KEEP: Spec.replay_from (atoms/spec.py:128 — arrival order IS append order, so only a docstring word moves); the VertexHandle checkpoint machinery (handle.py:792, :1225) with same-snapshot seeding, epoch invalidation and StoreReplaced-over-reinterpretation already solved; the benchmark arms (engine_receive_held -69.2%/-86.5%, same-runner A/B/A/B/A) with their honest self-stated boundaries; the lens conformance area (spec/conformance/generate_lens.py — hardcoded to ts, i.e. ONE INSTANTIATION SHORT of the (key,id) generalization, so extend rather than rebuild); Rule 17's prose ratchet, which holds verbatim under arrival.\n    REWRITE: the CAS token coordinate ((rowid,id) -> arrival head) — LARGER than the branch notes, since the token escapes into a PERSISTED intent record (ceremony.py:432); the combined-read fold fork (vertex_reader.py:390,:403-406 and libs/sdk/src/sdk/read.py), which the target answers directly — a combined read has no single arrival axis, so it must DECLARE a projection ordering and the member-count fork disappears; authority prose across store_reader.py, witness.py, declaration.py, docs.\n    DISCARD: R1 as doctrine only (merge.py:83 "the ceremony DEFINES the merged store's receipt order" and test_merge_direction_sets_fold_order_by_receipt). Under the target, merge never touches custody. Keep test_merge_direction_is_deterministic.\n    INTERIM HAZARD, operationally binding: merged alone, fold results depend on git's line interleaving of the still-canonical JSONL and the branch adds no guard; detection exists at verify time only. So PR #8 MUST NOT SPEND MEANINGFUL TIME ON MAIN BY ITSELF — land it with arrival, or accept that multi-replica JSONL merges are fold-affecting in the interim. No tag, no release, no user-visible intermediate store contract; the one contract break is spent on the model actually believed.\n\n=== THE FOUR CUTS (replacing the dead 8-slice plan) ===\n\nA AUTHORITY — arrival becomes canonical; lineage genesis moves into it; records become complete. residence.py:56-62 is the whole mode switch (a suffix test), ~225 non-test call sites funnel through it. Sweep hardcoded .db sites, especially init.py:141-142 whose regex SILENTLY NO-OPS on a non-.db locator. Reuse _read_lines/_truncate_torn_line, which migrate to arrival WHERE THEY ARE CORRECT since arrival is the genuinely append-only artifact. own_lineage is written by exactly two ceremonies (absorb_genesis sqlite_store.py:932-935, adopt_lineage :1392-1395).\nB PROJECTIONS — catch_up/_rebuild are already the right primitive; re-point the source and add .jsonl as a SECOND derived output. The offset/count triple moves to arrival; the .jsonl side re-keys to SET MEMBERSHIP, since a mergeable projection has no stable byte offset. merge_store/receive_store rewritten to append into arrival and let both projections re-derive — never direct index INSERTs. reanchor (jsonl_store.py:152-156) becomes a PERMANENT REFUSAL: arrival is never rewound, which retires the queued log-rewrite ceremony item.\nC ORDERING — declared projection order; arrival | by KEY; id as totalizer. _receipt_order (libs/store/src/store/jsonl.py:104-126) DISSOLVES — it exists only because there is no durable receipt ordinal, and arrival supplies one. Extend generate_lens.py from ts-only to arbitrary declared keys. CAS per above.\nD SURFACES — canonical_audit.py is the one place that FIGHTS BACK: respecifying only the deep check is insufficient, because the L1 default gate is order-dependent too; the whole offset/prefix custody model moves to arrival and the jsonl comparison becomes set-membership. Blast radius contained to one call site. preflight.py survives UNTOUCHED — its pure-reader contract ("repair destroys the evidence verification exists to inspect") and the Check.beyond_offset scope-not-verdict discipline are the cleanest things in the audited surface; only the artifact pair changes. Seals re-base on arrival position. Aggregation keeps WitnessAggregateUnsupported and A10 verbatim.\n\n=== THE ONE MIGRATION — WHERE THE REMAINING SKEPTICISM GOES ===\n\nTemplate is `rebirth` (fully receipted, precedent fact 01KTY5RNA96DSC1FW9R7NC69RT with source hashes and counts, sealed by a genesis tick), NOT the JSONL flip, which left NO receipt in the fact stream at all and whose only trace is store_meta plus a manual .pre-jsonl snapshot — a convention appearing nowhere in code.\n\nRATIFIED CONSTRAINT — DO NOT MANUFACTURE HISTORICAL PRECISION. _receipt_order carries a documented LOSSY heuristic for ticks with null or unresolvable fact_cursor (jsonl.py:35-40), and a heuristic written into an append-only arrival log is PERMANENT epistemic history. Where a legacy store does not contain enough information to reconstruct exact historical receipt order, the migration MUST mint an explicit legacy-adoption genesis marker — basis = imported legacy set, historical receipt UNAVAILABLE before genesis — with exact receipt semantics from that boundary onward. A named incomplete state over a convenient lie, which is the conceptual model's own stance. The migration spec must ESTABLISH which stores permit exact migration rather than letting the heuristic silently become history. THIS IS THE THING TO ADVERSARIALLY TEST NEXT.\nPopulation: locally ONE jsonl-canonical store (project.jsonl, 156MB, 3720 facts/92 ticks) where arrival is a LOSSLESS re-encode of existing line order, and six sqlite-canonical config vertices whose fact/tick interleave must go through _receipt_order and therefore inherit the heuristic.\nIDEMPOTENCE AND RESUMABILITY ARE RELEASE BLOCKERS, not nice-to-haves: every migration writer today refuses a pre-existing target, so an interrupted run on 150MB+ artifacts restarts from zero and errors on retry; rebirth assembles across two connections and two commits, and a crash between them leaves a receipt with no sealing tick that the never-overwrite guard makes un-retryable — annoying for rebirth, UNRECOVERABLE for an append-only arrival. Arrival is append-only, so resume-from-offset is natural: DESIGN IT IN. Carry both non-determinism carve-outs (receipt and genesis tick) explicitly, or derive them deterministically from source content.\n\n=== WHAT THIS DELETES FROM THE RECORD ===\nunion/ceremony discipline; the mergeability rollup and its construction ratchet; the S3 asymmetric override (no substrate asymmetry remains — a receipt fold is witness-relative BY DEFINITION, not a stronger ask); two CAS species; two merge legalities; "attestation grade is part of the store type" (custody substrate is uniform, so custody attestation is uniformly AVAILABLE); the positions law (now trivially true); the D7 rewind/residence question (a checkout dropping admitted facts is a DIVERGENT PROJECTION repaired by re-projecting from arrival — nothing rewinds, and FACTS DO NOT BELONG TO BRANCHES); and the trilemma as a store-level choice.\nSURVIVES: the three-clock ontology; receipt stamps, now universal; minted identity; admission as a distinct custody act; witness-relative derivation publishing TESTIMONY ABOUT A DERIVATION (a tick remains a published conclusion reached through a fold; portability does not retroactively make its production a raw observation); declaration-generation pinning in ticks. TICK = conclusion + declaration generation + witness basis + provenance/attestation.\n\n=== OPEN, CARRIED FORWARD ===\nUnknowns the audit named and could not settle: whether promoting own_lineage into arrival collides with existing _decl.genesis lineage semantics; WHETHER A REBUILD INVALIDATES OUTSTANDING WITNESS POSITIONS (rowids are reassigned; nobody traced whether a previously-issued seq: handle silently names a different fact after rebuild — the natural next question); the loops-go conformance oracle and siftd are NOT IN THIS TREE, so a mirrored CAS or ordering implementation there is unaudited (flagged independently by three of five audits, the most consistently raised blind spot); rebirth's source_content_sha256 witness-order derivation; libs/sign and the observer-key registry untraced for other bindings to file position; the arrival suffix name is undecided and unchecked for collision; the 216 ticks that re-entered as tick.* facts in the 2026-06-12 rebirth need a semantic ruling.\nMETHODOLOGICAL CAVEATS: no audit ran tests, so test-coverage claims come from diff text; two-process concurrency against one jsonl-canonical store was never exercised empirically; NO GIT MERGE OF A JSONL LOG WAS EVER PERFORMED; and one verification pass ran against main instead of the branch worktree and produced a FALSE REFUTED, corrected in synthesis — branch-scoped citations require the worktree at /Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/receipt-order-fold.\n\nDISPOSITION: architecture RATIFIED and closed to redesign absent implementation evidence contradicting an invariant. Next work is ratification residue (propagate into log-and-index-roles, rewrite memo and plan FROM this fact) and implementation proof, with migration exactness as the first adversarial target.
01M086FMFACWV6CCQ6VPEX56WC	design/shared-projection-transport			RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Opus 5, cross-family with GPT 5.6 "Sol"). Where the git-facing shared projection lives, and why the answer is not "wherever the code is".\n\nFORCING CONSUMER, and it is a real person rather than a hypothetical: Kyle's boss, who drove the JSONL work in the first place. He wants to share what he assembles in repos — guidance, best practices, investigations — across a set of per-repo curated vertices plus a COMBINATORIAL vertex over them. Git is the sensible transport. That workflow, not aesthetics, decides this.\n\n=== THE TWO SHAPES ===\n\nBRANCH-TRAVEL      the projection is a tracked file in the working tree; it moves with\n                   checkout; a PR carries its facts alongside its code.\nMONOTONIC REF      the projection lives on its own append-only line of history,\n                   decoupled from feature branches; it publishes on push.\n\n=== RULING: BUILD THE MONOTONIC REF DRIVER. LEAVE BRANCH-TRAVEL LEGAL AND UNBUILT. ===\n\nFour independent arguments, one conceptual, one workflow, one mechanical, one that dissolves the case for branch-travel entirely.\n\n1. A FACT'S SURVIVAL MUST NOT DEPEND ON A CODE-REVIEW OUTCOME. An observation made on feat/auth is true whether or not the branch merges. If the branch is abandoned the observation is MORE valuable — it is the record of a path not taken. Branch-travel makes evidence retention contingent on a decision that was about code.\n\n2. THE PROJECTION SHOULD OBEY THE SAME LAW AS WHAT IT PROJECTS. Arrival is append-only and never rewound. Under a monotonic ref so is the projection, and the two artifacts then differ only in ordering and in whether they carry custody — which is what "the degenerate case where they coincide" should mean at the sync layer too. Under branch-travel the projection is freely movable while its source is monotonic, and the whole of cut B's merge apparatus exists to paper over that mismatch.\n\n3. BRANCH-TRAVEL LOSES ITS OWN MOTIVATING BENEFIT. This is the argument that settles it. Amendment #4 ruled FACTS DO NOT BELONG TO BRANCHES: a checkout dropping admitted facts is a divergent projection, repaired by re-projecting from arrival. So Alice emits on feat/auth, checks out main, and the repair APPENDS HER FACTS BACK INTO MAIN'S COPY. Every branch's version of the file converges to the local union of everything she witnessed. Branch-travel therefore does not deliver PR-scoped facts. It delivers a perpetually dirty 157MB tracked file, churned on every checkout, converging on exactly the content a monotonic ref would have held — plus a merge driver to keep it consistent across replicas. It is the general case with churn, not an alternative to it.\n\n4. THE COMBINATORIAL VERTEX BREAKS UNDER BRANCH-TRAVEL. Each member's fact set becomes whatever branch is checked out in that clone, so the aggregate's answer depends on the checkout state of N repositories on whichever machine runs the combine. Two people with identical evidence get different answers. Aggregation can refuse to fabricate a cross-store witness order (WitnessAggregateUnsupported, A10) but it cannot refuse to be perturbed by MEMBERSHIP wobble. Under a monotonic ref each member's shared set only grows, so the aggregate only grows.\n\n=== WHAT THIS DEFERS OUT OF THE REWRITE ===\n\nTHE SEMANTIC MERGE DRIVER IS NO LONGER CUT-B WORK. Under a monotonic ref there is nothing to textually merge: FAST-FORWARD IS THE SUPERSET CHECK, and a REJECTED PUSH IS THE CONFLICT, resolved by re-project-and-push — machinery the model already requires for divergence repair. So .gitattributes, the ours/base/theirs union codec, and the CI-enforced merge-boundary invariant family all become what a BRANCH-TRAVEL driver would need IF someone configures one. Do not prepay for it. Amendment #4 designed for branch-travel implicitly (merge driver, "git remains the PR/concurrency workflow") without ever recording that call, even though the facts-do-not-belong-to-branches ruling argued against it in the same fact — one unrecorded decision sitting underneath cut B's largest piece of new work.\n\n=== THE CHEAP WATERMARK COMES BACK ON A MONOTONIC TRANSPORT ===\n\ndecision:design/projection-driver-model removes reconcile() and notes the O(1) offset check cannot survive on a set-keyed projection. It comes back at the TRANSPORT layer when the transport is monotonic: LAST-FETCHED COMMIT IS THE WATERMARK, and "what is new" is a diff between two commits — cheap and exact, with no content comparison of a 157MB materialization. Under branch-travel it does not work, because the ref can move among incomparable histories and a commit id no longer bounds what has been seen. So the cheap watermark was never lost to the authority inversion; it is lost to NON-MONOTONIC TRANSPORT specifically.\n\n=== TRANSPORT PROGRESS IS NOT CUSTODY PROGRESS ===\n\nSol's catch, and it stands regardless of how the disposition question resolves. If commit C->D introduces five candidates and one is not given a terminal disposition, advancing last_fetched=D drops it from consideration forever, since the next discover() only sees diff(D,E). Two cursors exist and must not be conflated:\n\n    transport cursor   "I have fetched through commit C."\n    custody state      "these candidates have terminal disposition."\n\nBoth can advance monotonically; they are not the same monotone. What holds non-terminal dispositions is exactly the question at thread:admission-disposition, and it is NOT ratified here.\n\n=== WHAT REMAINS OPEN, AND WHAT DOES NOT ===\n\nNOT open: whether the projection travels with feature branches. It does not, by default.\nOPEN: the concrete ref shape. refs/loops/facts as a custom namespace is tidier; an orphan branch is browsable in a forge UI and uses ordinary fetch/push/protection. Kyle's stated preference is to let the data flow decide rather than a UI limitation, and under the driver model this choice sits BENEATH the store contract — a transport parameter, changeable without touching anything above it. Deliberately not ratified.\n\nBRANCH-TRAVEL REMAINS A LEGAL CONFIGURATION. The driver model makes it expressible and it should stay expressible. It is not a peer on the merits, and nothing should be built for it speculatively.
01M08EMX3MYQQ5BB6K5AZ6DZHG	design/migration-genesis-attestation			RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable). Two rulings, one ceremony.\n\n1. REBIRTH DISSOLVES UNDER 1.0. Its function — replay a corpus into a new custody context, receipted, sealed — is the composition of ratified arrival primitives: lineage genesis + driver-proposed candidates + custodian admission + classification facts. Release-scope ruling 3 already reshaped adopt into the lineage genesis ceremony; a standalone rebirth verb beside that is a two-mode residue. ONE re-custody ceremony exists under 1.0, with two instances: the frozen 0.x->1.0 sidecar (one-time, pinned) and arrival-native re-custody through the ordinary admission path. What survives is rebirth's epistemic TEMPLATE (receipt fact with source hashes/counts, sealing genesis tick) — the tool dies, the discipline is inherited. RESIDUE SWEEP when cut D lands: store/rebirth.py and its CLI surface die with residence.py.\n\n2. KEYLESS MIGRATION OF A SIGNED SOURCE REQUIRES EXPLICIT --allow-unsigned (option 2 of the attestation-drop question). Hard refusal (option 1) punishes exactly the user the frozen uvx sidecar exists for — arriving years later from any 0.x, possibly without custody. Silent proceed (option 3, rebirth's current posture) is ruled out by classification-as-fact: era transitions are recorded, never incidental. Under option 2 the downgrade is deliberate at ceremony time (the flag) and loud permanently (classification fact: signature era UNSIGNED opening a lineage whose source was signed). verify_chain's era-monotonicity break applies within a chain; a migration genesis is a new lineage, so the downgrade is legal there — it must merely be loud.\n\nWith rebirth dissolved, the keyless question has exactly one home; rebirth and the sidecar can no longer be ruled differently because only the sidecar remains.
01M08J0C1BBJM7NNGKSM1J8JEK	arrival-migration-arc	open		ARRIVAL-LOG DESIGN SESSION (2026-08-17, Kyle + Fable) — the ruled entry point, substantially advanced. Rulings converged in-session (ratified conversationally; this entry records them for the arc):\n\n1. GRAMMAR DISSOLVES. The arrival log is the EXISTING JSONL codec — fact/tick/batch line shapes unchanged, genesis-first, line position as witness order, tick chain re-based from rowid to line order (spec-text change, not byte change). No new file type, no per-record envelope. Unsealed-span posture accepted: order between seals is asserted by custody, committed by the next seal — seal density is the ruled integrity lever (per admission-disposition). Retroactive win: one interleaved file records the fact/tick interleave _receipt_order had to reconstruct.\n\n2. THE LOG CONTAINS EVERYTHING THAT IS EVIDENCE (Kyle's conception, census-verified against ~/.config/loops + .loops): genesis, declarations (vertex definition INCLUDED — the loops/kinds block already rides as _decl batch lines), observer introductions, grants, assertions, seals. EXCLUDED, exactly four categories: secrets (private keys), code (lenses), transport (driver config/credentials/cursors, store locator), and its own address. The .vertex FILE becomes a folded-out PROJECTION — editable for iteration, re-absorbed via absorb_edit CAS (Edit 2 doctrine applied; observers{} block joins the declaration document set).\n\n3. VERTEX REGISTRATION relocates into the AGGREGATOR'S OWN lineage as first-class facts (membership assertions, admitted like anything else); discover globs degrade from authority to a discovery DRIVER proposing membership candidates — Law 3 verbatim. Cross-lineage topology never enters a member's log (Law 4).\n\n4. GENESIS IS SELF-CERTIFYING. Founding observer-introduction fact carries the pubkey and is signed BY it — TOFU at line 1; attests possession, never identity (signatures attest claims, not external truth; names are lineage-local; cross-lineage identity = vouch arc, deferred). Later observers introduced by facts signed by already-introduced observers; grants/rotations/revocations are ordinary signed facts. Verification becomes POSITION-DEPENDENT against the in-log registry (arrival restatement of internal-table-meta-schema's historized-keys ruling) — fixes today's timeless .vertex registry (retroactive validation + rotation-breaks-history defects) and the Relay cross-vertex unverifiability (thread:cross-vertex-observer-key-reuse's demand "trust decision is itself a fact" satisfied structurally). Keyless genesis stays coherent: --allow-unsigned = no TOFU anchor, era UNSIGNED classification, introduction may open the signed era later.\n\n5. TAINTED-SPAN ruled at decision:design/key-revocation-taint-disposition — default leave-in-place + projection policy; content-destruction = re-custody ceremony, never in-place rebuild.\n\nloops init reshapes into a three-movement genesis ceremony: lineage genesis, declaration absorption, observer introduction — sealed before first ordinary admission; a fresh 1.0 log is self-describing and self-verifying from line 1.\n\nNEXT: review of the full decision chain + consolidated arrival-log shape (in progress this session), then the sidecar spec (must ref 01M070N0 directly), migration verifier, memo correction.
01M08M4WX608FVQTSY75PC1CC7	design/aggregation-membership-as-declaration			RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; arrival-log design session). VERTEX REGISTRATION DISSOLVES INTO DECLARATION STATE IN THE AGGREGATOR'S OWN LINEAGE.\n\nCorrected from the session's first phrasing ("membership assertions, admitted like anything else") — membership is NOT an admission: it is the custodian's interpretive commitment about which lineages participate in this vertex's answers, i.e. DECLARATION state, changed through the declaration ceremony (custodian-authored batch, CAS'd) in the aggregator's own arrival log. This is the arrival restatement of design/internal-table-meta-schema (2026-07-01), whose CONSTITUTION vocabulary already names member-defined/member-removed as historized combine-constituent events.\n\nTHE SPLIT, on the four-exclusions line:\n- IN the aggregator's log: membership declarations naming members BY LINEAGE ID (stable, minted at member genesis, machine-independent). Historized, so "what did this aggregation consist of when that answer was given" is a fold over CONSTITUTION events — aggregated-read provenance is incomplete without it, which is what earns log residence. (Today this is unanswerable: config globs + combine blocks appear in no receipt.)\n- OUTSIDE, as driver config: the locator map (lineage id -> current path/remote/schedule). Paths are transport — a log naming filesystem paths lies the moment anything moves, same reason it cannot contain its own address.\n- discover globs DEGRADE from authority to a DISCOVERY DRIVER: scans, reports "lineage X found at path P", drafts a membership declaration edit for the custodian to absorb. Law 3 shape, through the declaration ceremony rather than admission.\n\nBOUNDARY DELIBERATELY UNMOVED: ad-hoc combine (read over arbitrary stores) stays a pure read-path operation, registration-free. Membership declarations are for STANDING aggregation where the composition is part of what answers mean; exploratory reads carry no membership provenance, honestly.
01M08MD6Y51BS2RJ8136J5DGFV	design/arrival-cas-two-scopes			RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; arrival-log design session). cas(head) IS CONDITIONAL APPEND ON A KIND-SCOPED WITNESS POSITION, WITH EXACTLY TWO SANCTIONED SCOPES.\n\nThe verb from log-and-index-roles (append->stamp, records_from, cas(head)) is specified: "append this batch iff no record of kind-class K admitted since position N." Two scopes only: K=everything (the ARRIVAL head — transport, backup boundaries) and K=declarations (the DECLARATION head — the absorb ceremony's guard, what _declaration_head_in_txn already does). CAS against the arrival head alone would be spuriously strict for declaration edits: any ordinary admission between fold-out and re-absorb would fail an edit with no actual conflict.\n\nNO PREDICATE GENERALIZATION: "append-if no record matching P" is a query language growing inside the custody boundary; admission stays too dumb to evaluate semantics. Kind-scoping is the entire vocabulary — structural, one indexed lookup in the single-writer transaction.\n\n_decl.* PROMOTES FROM CONVENTION TO CONTRACT-LEVEL NAMESPACE (binds forever under the one-break budget — said out loud). It already exists de facto: _decl.genesis + the frozen *-defined/*-retired edit vocabulary, _meta.own_lineage, _topology. Structural, not semantic: the custodian distinguishes declaration records the way it distinguishes fact lines from tick lines, without knowing what any declaration means. Residue under arrival: _meta.own_lineage moves from store_meta (index-side, derived) into the genesis fact.\n\nFROZEN AT TWO WITH A SHRINK-ONLY BAR: a third scope requires demonstrating a ceremony that is structurally neither ordinary admission nor a declaration edit. The extensibility question dissolved on inspection — every ceremony named in this arc (observer introduction/grant/rotation/revocation, membership edits, epoch/registry mutations) is declaration-shaped, because the observers block and aggregation membership were both ruled into the declaration document set. Ratchet-test pattern applied to the verb surface.\n\nRIDER, forced not chosen — window_hash SCOPE: windows stay FACTS-ONLY under the single interleaved file. Migration exactness decides it: signed history migrates exactly iff committed bytes are unchanged, and historical windows commit to fact rows between id-resolved cursor bounds; including tick lines would change every window input and force re-signing. Nothing lost: window_hash pins fact order, prev_hash pins tick order, fact_cursor pins each tick's position among facts (ties among cursor-sharing ticks break by chain order) — jointly the entire line interleave is committed.
01M08MPF247VX7YR9GZVQK9XB7	arrival-migration-arc	open		ARTIFACT STOOD UP: "The Arrival Log" — https://claude.ai/code/artifact/a70ab076-a5c0-4d18-96bd-5fb0829a0963 — sibling to The Arrival Substrate memo, laying out the artifact itself: JSONL format ruling + riders, line grammar and (lineage, ordinal) position, contents boundary (four exclusions, .vertex-as-projection), three-movement genesis, position-dependent verification + self-certifying genesis, rotation/revocation/taint two-arm ruling, membership-as-declaration, cas two-scopes + _decl contract namespace, facts-only windows + seal-density posture, migration touchpoints, deferred ledger. Colophon carries all backing fact ids. Carries the memo rowid correction inline (sect. 10). NEXT: sidecar contract spec (ref 01M070N08HX69QAEQ3TRPY72CQ directly).
01M08N9H33H3X06A9ZR9X00V1Q	design/arrival-batch-ordinals			RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; Sol review contract 1). ORDINAL IS PER-RECORD: witness order is line order with batch lines expanding in row order. Forced by the code, not chosen: deserialize_records expands rows in array order and _index_lines INSERTs in that order — each fact in a batch gets its own rowid today, and arrival witness order must be order-isomorphic to legacy rowid order or class (b) migration verification (window hashes recomputed over carried order) breaks; one-ordinal-per-batch would make a migrated store's fact counts and window membership disagree with its own signed history. A batch occupies a CONTIGUOUS ordinal range. Atomicity is an ADMISSION property (the line commits whole or truncates whole), never an addressing property: a read basis may land mid-batch, exactly as a fact-id address can name a mid-ceremony fact today. (lineage, ordinal) addresses a RECORD; the entry (line) is the atomicity unit. Sol's coherent alternative (batch = one custody act = one position) rejected as the new-machinery branch of the dissolution test.
01M08N9H8GT4WQXMPGJN3ADWW4	design/arrival-genesis-bootstrap			RATIFIED 2026-08-17 (Kyle, in-session with Fable; Sol review contract 2 — Sol caught a real ordering bug in the first three-movement sequence: lines preceding the key introduction were either unsigned inside a signed lineage or needed a retroactive-verification exception). THE GENESIS FACT IS THE FOUNDING INTRODUCTION. Line 1 (_decl.genesis) carries lineage id, format-version, and the founding PUBLIC KEY, self-signed by that key — the TOFU anchor at ordinal 0. Then the declaration batch, signed by the now-introduced key; then the genesis seal. The three movements become: SELF-CERTIFYING GENESIS, DECLARATION ABSORPTION, SEAL.\n\nVERIFIER RULE, one explicit clause instead of an exception: a key is valid at position N iff introduced at position < N, OR N is the genesis position and the record is self-certifying — SELF-CERTIFICATION IS LEGAL AT ORDINAL 0 AND NOWHERE ELSE. No retroactive verification anywhere.\n\nKeyless genesis unchanged: same line 1, no key field, unsigned, classification era UNSIGNED; a later introduction opens the signed era (that introduction is itself self-certifying-shaped but arrives through ordinary custodian admission, era transition recorded per classification-as-fact).\n\nRIDERS ACCEPTED FROM THE SAME REVIEW PASS: (a) the self-verification claim scopes to CRYPTOGRAPHICALLY self-verifying — TOFU genesis means self-verifying ≠ externally authenticated; names stay lineage-local, identity is the vouch arc. (b) INTERLEAVE UNIQUENESS becomes a stated rule + conformance-vector obligation: a tick's cursor assigns it to the gap immediately after fact F; ticks sharing a gap order by chain; chain continuity (verify_chain) makes assignment monotone — unique total interleave, and a claim that can be falsified automatically must be (loops-go vector family candidate). (c) MIGRATION spells out: legacy physical position != 1.0 witness ordinal even for order-VERIFIED stores; preserved = relative order, record bytes, tick relationships — never receipt-number identity. (d) SDK SURFACE for the two-scope CAS: distinct coordinate types (ArrivalHead / DeclarationHead), never generic position + flag — the frozen scope set lives in the type system, not review vigilance; verb renames to guarded_append (cas(head) under-describes its own semantics; canon two-scope ruling unchanged).
01M08NCZENDSXQPD407RTFVZR7	arrival-migration-arc	open		SOL REVIEW PASS FOLDED IN (2026-08-17, GPT 5.6 Sol, artifact-only read — no code access). Verdict: "the first implementation discussion that makes me more confident the collapse was real" — dissolution held (existing codec/grammar/ceremonies under one new authority: physical line order = minted witness order). Three contracts identified; all settled:\n\n1. BATCH ORDINALS — ruled at decision:design/arrival-batch-ordinals @ 01M08N9H33H3X06A9ZR9X00V1Q: per-record ordinals (batch expands in row order, contiguous range, atomicity = admission property not addressing property). Forced by code Sol couldn't see: _index_lines gives each batch row its own rowid today, and class (b) migration verification requires order-isomorphism.\n\n2. GENESIS BOOTSTRAP — ruled at decision:design/arrival-genesis-bootstrap @ 01M08N9H8GT4WQXMPGJN3ADWW4: Sol caught a REAL ordering bug in the artifact's first draft (declarations preceded the key that signs them). Fix: genesis fact IS the founding introduction (lineage id + format-version + founding key, self-signed); movements become self-certifying genesis / declaration absorption / seal; verifier gains one explicit clause (self-certification legal at ordinal 0, nowhere else), no retroactive verification. Riders in same fact: "cryptographically self-verifying" scope qualifier; interleave-uniqueness stated rule + conformance-vector obligation (loops-go queue candidate); legacy-position != ordinal migration disclaimer; SDK typed heads (ArrivalHead/DeclarationHead) + guarded_append rename.\n\n3. CUSTODIAN CONTINUATION — Sol concurs with the deferral and sharpened the articulation ("possessing bytes claiming lineage L" vs "authorized to continue L"); remains the named next custody discussion.\n\nArtifact updated in place (same URL, version label sol-review-folded): six edits + colophon review record. The arrival-log design session is now CLOSED pending the sidecar spec.
