01M09GNGW7VTSKDPYMJ027HEPR	design/arrival-slice0-record-grammar			RATIFIED (Kyle, 2026-08-17 session with Fable — the slice-0 ratify gate per plan:arrival-libs-slice-0 is now OPEN for implementation). The arrival log record grammar + suffix design fact, proposal doc: docs/dev/arrival-slice0-record-grammar-2026-08-17.md (authored by a Claude design agent over an agy-explorer ledger; all citations spot-verified).\n\nCORE: suffix .arrival (companions .arrival.lock / .arrival.tmp); JSON-lines framing inheriting the ensure_ascii/allow_nan=False encoder discipline; record fields in order v, lin, ord, prev, at, k, observer, origin, body, sig?, rh; coordinate (lin, ord) WRITTEN INTO the record — append validates, never assigns; rh = sha256(JCS(record-without-rh)); prev chains rh from slice 0 (deferring to slice D would leave a permanent chain hole); torn tail truncates ONLY under the append lock, corrupt interior always refuses; genesis is ordinary record at ord=0, k=genesis, sig REQUIRED, O_EXCL staging + atomic rename + directory fsync; append under fcntl.flock on .arrival.lock (mutual exclusion forced by ordinal assignment), reads lock-free; resume mark = (arrival_lineage, arrival_offset, arrival_ordinal), all three validated, counts custody DISSOLVES. NAMED DEPARTURE, ratified as such: body is a JSON object, not verbatim TEXT — the verbatim-payload invariant retires with the two-custody-holders condition that created it; JCS defines canonical bytes.\n\nKYLE'S THREE RULINGS: (1) sig covers CONTENT ONLY (k, at, observer, origin, body — field-for-field the existing commitment envelope) — coordinate-covering signatures would make identity store-local; portable single identity across many stores is the point. Coordinate integrity rides rh/prev. (2) Genesis body MINIMAL in slice 0 — protocol version + lineage claim; document set and migration pins are slice A's, where a genesis has real history behind it. (3) Suffix .arrival over .lineage after vocabulary workshop — lineage is a PROPERTY of the records; the logs are the arrival of observations. Axis name stays continuous across filesystem, SDK (ArrivalHead), and meta keys (arrival_*).\n\nVOCABULARY: seed denylist EMBEDDED per plan:arrival-vocabulary-ratchet (jsonl_canonical + jsonl_* meta family, receipt_order/receipt_mode/receipt-as-custody, event-as-ordering, reanchor-as-operation, merge-touches-custody, rewind, mergeability/union-discipline, two-CAS-species names — the last as a pointer slice C resolves against the ruled list). Glossary ratified: arrival log, record, lineage, ordinal, coordinate, genesis, head, append, resume mark, torn tail, projection, body. Named adjacency: witness.py late_arrivals is a different (witness-time) sense; slice A decides its rename.\n\nGATE (slice-0, empirical): six tests in proposal §3.5, headlined by 4 real OS processes x 250 appends asserting dense gapless ordinals + intact prev chain + recomputing rh. Real processes, not threads — the gate is not passed otherwise.
01M09MMZ7BFGM2BF5ZTWAR3E0X	test/arrival-slice0-review-ledger			SLICE-0 DISPOSITION LEDGER — ROUND 2 CLOSED (supersedes the round-1 entry; branch feat/arrival-libs @ f07bfb90). Running totals: 7 findings in, 7 dispositions out, ZERO dropped. Rounds 1-2 both found real defects; not yet converged. Round 3 dispatched.\n\nROUND 2 (gemini-3.7-flash-high, pointed at BREAKING round-1's fixes): verdict NOT_CONVERGED, 3 findings, all confirmed, all FIXED @ f07bfb90.\nF1-R2 BLOCKING — resume path accepted an INVALID INTERIOR GENESIS as anchor and consumed past a record walk() refuses. F2-R2 BLOCKING — append validated the CANDIDATE's placement but never the HEAD's, so a log whose ordinal-0 record is unsigned/forged kept accepting appends (arbiter reproduced independently). F3-R2 MAJOR — Rule 18 missed __all__ exports, string forward-ref annotations, punctuation-separated dict keys.\n\nTHE ROOT CAUSE, and the reason this arc is worth receipting: a PROXY SHAPE. resume_offset validated an anchor that walk_from then INDEPENDENTLY RE-READ — the checks did not live at the point the record actually became an authority. That single shape produced round-1 F4 AND both round-2 blockers. Fixed as the general form, not the instances: _authority_fault(record, lineage) states what makes an existing on-disk record adoptable AS A PREMISE (decodes + rh recomputes + _placement_fault at its claimed ordinal + lineage matches), and there is now ONE adoption site each — _anchor_for(mark) for the resume anchor, _tail_record for the append head (reads genesis first to establish the true lineage). EVIDENCE THE GENERAL FORM WAS THE RIGHT UNIT OF REPAIR: writing it caught a THIRD instance no review reported — a tail re-chained onto a foreign lineage accepted appends, because the candidate copies its lineage FROM the head and the head was never compared to genesis. Point-fixing the two reported instances would have left that for round 3.\n\nDISTINCTION NOW LOAD-BEARING IN THE DESIGN: reading a record forward and adopting one as a premise are DIFFERENT ACTS. A rule enforced on the way past a record says nothing about a record you never walked to. The lazy/eager split is why: walk() is a generator that validates nothing until consumed (now docstring'd + test-pinned), and the O(1) eager paths that adopt authorities were skipping what the consumed read path performs.\n\nTHREE ARBITER RULINGS overnight, all overturnable by Kyle: (1) multi-word denylist terms are IDENTIFIER bans not prose bans; (2) sense-qualified bans (event/merge/receipt) deliberately NOT mechanized, named in _NOT_MECHANIZED; (3) the O(n) residual ACCEPTED at its stated width — an adopted authority is not proven to chain back to genesis nor that its claimed ordinal is its physical position; both need the whole-prefix walk these O(1) paths exist to avoid, matching ratified §3.2 ("the mark is a cheap boundary check; walk is the integrity statement"). Round 3 is asked to test whether the residual is WIDER than stated, not to re-report it.\n\nQUEUED FOR SIMPLIFY (not defects): _tail_record reads genesis on EVERY append — the genesis lineage is immutable for the file's life, so it is memoizable; pyright nits (_bad lacks NoReturn so callers show possibly-unbound; unused names).\n\nGATE (arbiter, independent, round 2): both exploits re-run by hand and confirmed closed — F2-R2 refuses with GenesisRefused leaving bytes BYTE-IDENTICAL, F1-R2 discards the mark (resume_offset 0) and walk_from raises ArrivalCorrupt at ordinal 1; 84 arrival + 98 arch + 1620 engine green; one power proof re-broken by hand (placement half of _authority_fault) with liveness asserted, two tests caught it; production diff empty; review worktree swept clean all three dispatches.
